events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lasp/adamant-skills/commit/d15dea3a33e3407336e89012d1fb1d611499da6b","node_id":"C_kwDOUHIrOdoAKGQxNWRlYTNhMzNlMzQwNzMzNmU4OTAxMmQxZmIxZDYxMTQ5OWRhNmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lasp/adamant-skills/commit/9c903043d660e7dab3abdc4cc82a51fbf4812627","sha":"9c903043d660e7dab3abdc4cc82a51fbf4812627","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/9c903043d660e7dab3abdc4cc82a51fbf4812627"}],"sha":"d15dea3a33e3407336e89012d1fb1d611499da6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/d15dea3a33e3407336e89012d1fb1d611499da6b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90524106?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jbsco","id":90524106,"login":"Jbsco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTI0MTA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/9c903043d660e7dab3abdc4cc82a51fbf4812627/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-30T02:07:43Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T17:32:49Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"message":"formal-verification: add proof-mechanics reference (loop restriction, nonlinearity, discharge ladder)\n\nThree proof-mechanics gotchas, each reproduced against the Adamant GNATprove\ntoolchain before writing (verbatim symptoms in the reference):\n\n- The \"non-scalar object declared before loop-invariant is not yet supported\"\n  hard error, its remedies (hoist the declaration; better, ask whether a\n  domain-fixed iteration count means the loop should be unrolled away), and the\n  meta-lesson that a tool restriction can be diagnostic.\n- Variable exponentiation as a nonlinearity trap, with a sharper finding than the\n  source report: a bare `D / 2**Shift` proves, but a product `X * (2**Shift)`\n  raises \"cannot prove upper bound\" even when the result obviously fits; the\n  failure surfaces in dependents rather than at the cause; prefer a divisor\n  parameter (linear) or a static exponent.\n- The compile-time-first ladder for discharging a fact (compile-time > prover >\n  run-time > comment), using `Compile_Time_Error` over derived constants to make\n  single-source-of-truth enforced, plus the verified caveat that\n  `gnatprove --mode=check` does NOT evaluate the pragma (must compile to fire it).\n  Confirmed both the satisfied (clean) and violated (build error) paths.\n\nAlso two reproducibility notes (version-control the proof switches; pin the\nprover version for proof-product work) and a fixed-point amendment: bound the\naccumulator from the format parameters and pin it with Compile_Time_Error.\nSelector routes \"a proof will not discharge / times out / loop-invariant error\"\nhere. Worked example stays public-hardware-generic; no project content.","tree":{"sha":"26f2e3f5ec1efc2eab3582bc8247af65542ba26c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/trees/26f2e3f5ec1efc2eab3582bc8247af65542ba26c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/commits/9c903043d660e7dab3abdc4cc82a51fbf4812627","verification":{"payload":"tree 26f2e3f5ec1efc2eab3582bc8247af65542ba26c\nparent 741fba0ff5f46c7c991799f6e54e25acaab71372\nauthor Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1785377263 -0600\ncommitter Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1785519169 -0600\n\nformal-verification: add proof-mechanics reference (loop restriction, nonlinearity, discharge ladder)\n\nThree proof-mechanics gotchas, each reproduced against the Adamant GNATprove\ntoolchain before writing (verbatim symptoms in the reference):\n\n- The \"non-scalar object declared before loop-invariant is not yet supported\"\n  hard error, its remedies (hoist the declaration; better, ask whether a\n  domain-fixed iteration count means the loop should be unrolled away), and the\n  meta-lesson that a tool restriction can be diagnostic.\n- Variable exponentiation as a nonlinearity trap, with a sharper finding than the\n  source report: a bare `D / 2**Shift` proves, but a product `X * (2**Shift)`\n  raises \"cannot prove upper bound\" even when the result obviously fits; the\n  failure surfaces in dependents rather than at the cause; prefer a divisor\n  parameter (linear) or a static exponent.\n- The compile-time-first ladder for discharging a fact (compile-time > prover >\n  run-time > comment), using `Compile_Time_Error` over derived constants to make\n  single-source-of-truth enforced, plus the verified caveat that\n  `gnatprove --mode=check` does NOT evaluate the pragma (must compile to fire it).\n  Confirmed both the satisfied (clean) and violated (build error) paths.\n\nAlso two reproducibility notes (version-control the proof switches; pin the\nprover version for proof-product work) and a fixed-point amendment: bound the\naccumulator from the format parameters and pin it with Compile_Time_Error.\nSelector routes \"a proof will not discharge / times out / loop-invariant error\"\nhere. Worked example stays public-hardware-generic; no project content.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEw4OO+fgBg9dPCrHf5dlyl7D/NcoFAmqTLZUACgkQ5dlyl7D/\nNcoiJBAA0Ilh0RUSo9bxeEKlAc0X5ECZudQZ4j13XWX2sNFNfXvDpTIqWg+JGELL\nPkpheVLSGwODekgcSIySdzn5/8c87d+l49vDgyZENAaYeAfq/R/f1lkSAMLhkwhy\n7LrB6Q1k+iy8b9u+3+VoD6uCqGQCOdkVFShpwVvLPnknHNSs73MpdpRjlSZh0uxS\n78W8+6eidaRWmENYvXsH48kPunPizlh0+qCptBhzmm8KZjWsueJTQGHCBe/aS8FH\nEsImkPonyTpPPLgZ1dn9djD7zrZA7ONP2y8v7otNfvGbYwXbW6zxUNOkj2dK1Hhz\nw+UyNx/MwmS4217EBWk9KWknfw+QodTX5HUmCI7zto+wQ7SinATYaU9AWZA1D9zN\njhNk/2v3ZF9VC0+Nqc8VtJZKnKk0bhmN0bkHpDrE/1r5pGOlOZGR2xQBvUJ+L/b9\nK5Yw4i2eQ37YWfKNxcbr/Au0D2/bAOIGdlLVC8LdU8EXVVCnPDRCHbMIPfnLE67s\no/sXBaIoKLKam7Gx1sjCCAFVI9yONaAtUSqUXycpiEEd7FGsclOPaf1rpNJ55glN\nGgd7EG1tyDyskZ5kb5To6yt2Q6sBOUrJkd7r1SyuBsMRTm5u74d+Panjjehp49ty\n389o613PSH61pdUllx/ZxRT2ysx0AWn1Ok2zggwepYCjvQ9/RA8=\n=9SI2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-29T19:09:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90524106?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jbsco","id":90524106,"login":"Jbsco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTI0MTA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lasp/adamant-skills/commit/9c903043d660e7dab3abdc4cc82a51fbf4812627","node_id":"C_kwDOUHIrOdoAKDljOTAzMDQzZDY2MGU3ZGFiM2FiZGM0Y2M4MmE1MWZiZjQ4MTI2Mjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lasp/adamant-skills/commit/741fba0ff5f46c7c991799f6e54e25acaab71372","sha":"741fba0ff5f46c7c991799f6e54e25acaab71372","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/741fba0ff5f46c7c991799f6e54e25acaab71372"}],"sha":"9c903043d660e7dab3abdc4cc82a51fbf4812627","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/9c903043d660e7dab3abdc4cc82a51fbf4812627"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90524106?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jbsco","id":90524106,"login":"Jbsco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTI0MTA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/741fba0ff5f46c7c991799f6e54e25acaab71372/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-30T00:35:51Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T17:32:49Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"message":"formal-verification: add fixed-point proof reference; high-assurance: parameterisation coverage\n\nCloses the fixed-point gap the earlier queue flagged (S1): a reference that\nteaches fixed-point as the tractable alternative to proof-hostile float, since\nscaled-integer obligations lower to linear integer arithmetic.\n\nEvery mechanical claim is grounded in a worked package proved with GNATprove\n(silver, level 2, checks-as-errors): declaring a type that means a hardware\nformat (delta, explicit Small, Size, shown on a 16-bit 1.3.12 coprocessor\nformat); the universal_fixed conversion requirement on * and /; widening\noperands into a wider fixed type before multiplying; saturation-with-flag as a\nproved multi-branch postcondition (the fixed-point instance of the specified-\nsaturation carve-out). The load-bearing finding, hit and fixed during that\nproof: a fixed-point product named in a POSTCONDITION needs the same widening as\nthe body -- a bare X * C raises \"medium: overflow check might fail\" -- which\nforces the wide intermediate type into the visible part of the spec. Also folds\nin two device-modelling patterns (per-operation scale selectors and selector-\nparameterised operations belong in the contract, not a global constant), under\nthe rule that an operation''s identity is not fully given by its name.\n\nThe worked example uses publicly documented consumer-hardware fixed-point\nformats, so the reference carries no project or controlled content; it is\ndescribed generically (a fixed-point geometry coprocessor) rather than branded.\n\nhigh-assurance-design gains the parameterisation-coverage obligation: replacing\nN specialisations with one parameterised implementation requires an argument\nthat the parameter space covers every specialisation''s behaviour, discharged by\nenumeration and per-specialisation correspondence -- a design-review question\nbefore a proof question.\n\nSelector and SKILL.md routing updated for both (fixed-point-vs-float as an\nentry point, and the new reference in the References list).","tree":{"sha":"89b1f989fc3a770466d52906ae4d62fac71e501e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/trees/89b1f989fc3a770466d52906ae4d62fac71e501e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/commits/741fba0ff5f46c7c991799f6e54e25acaab71372","verification":{"payload":"tree 89b1f989fc3a770466d52906ae4d62fac71e501e\nparent 33988d2551aa1c4dce9e390d6ec8391e6c22a185\nauthor Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1785371751 -0600\ncommitter Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1785519169 -0600\n\nformal-verification: add fixed-point proof reference; high-assurance: parameterisation coverage\n\nCloses the fixed-point gap the earlier queue flagged (S1): a reference that\nteaches fixed-point as the tractable alternative to proof-hostile float, since\nscaled-integer obligations lower to linear integer arithmetic.\n\nEvery mechanical claim is grounded in a worked package proved with GNATprove\n(silver, level 2, checks-as-errors): declaring a type that means a hardware\nformat (delta, explicit Small, Size, shown on a 16-bit 1.3.12 coprocessor\nformat); the universal_fixed conversion requirement on * and /; widening\noperands into a wider fixed type before multiplying; saturation-with-flag as a\nproved multi-branch postcondition (the fixed-point instance of the specified-\nsaturation carve-out). The load-bearing finding, hit and fixed during that\nproof: a fixed-point product named in a POSTCONDITION needs the same widening as\nthe body -- a bare X * C raises \"medium: overflow check might fail\" -- which\nforces the wide intermediate type into the visible part of the spec. Also folds\nin two device-modelling patterns (per-operation scale selectors and selector-\nparameterised operations belong in the contract, not a global constant), under\nthe rule that an operation''s identity is not fully given by its name.\n\nThe worked example uses publicly documented consumer-hardware fixed-point\nformats, so the reference carries no project or controlled content; it is\ndescribed generically (a fixed-point geometry coprocessor) rather than branded.\n\nhigh-assurance-design gains the parameterisation-coverage obligation: replacing\nN specialisations with one parameterised implementation requires an argument\nthat the parameter space covers every specialisation''s behaviour, discharged by\nenumeration and per-specialisation correspondence -- a design-review question\nbefore a proof question.\n\nSelector and SKILL.md routing updated for both (fixed-point-vs-float as an\nentry point, and the new reference in the References list).\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEw4OO+fgBg9dPCrHf5dlyl7D/NcoFAmqTLZUACgkQ5dlyl7D/\nNcpwhQ/5AdEO5u5EZ/ToPQ5PuUbrPqpD2zJRq/n+y4b4nK+Kg4sRBdNLJ/R5hg9A\noC5Hnfk2Os1Qub7hEYRcFm/21BT7TJbLoApaM5mQQ/0JpIKtdZ3CL2MkWzJ9lSNx\nItgFscabj+382cX2B3eIatYQNVNMhzBIRxUVaMHLrhZntypDP1hHJR/ns7tw+A3F\nzDe6eCXNf2a/riTGmk/l/71GM5amRNDIpL3yHF+akL8qTmSBiPDED0vWra85BumZ\nTNOSX4Yj6T3LcXkYZUOfYJ6kdj5U/KSSYF/+eJ1pND8lsQuMcDv5YPWwVlcKytfJ\nIupJJJwyxa34lj+jBJBUYNU1osIs6pGC3eEmqrGkAeWbVjQC/vJyp+2MQspCplX0\nTTLybKq0XEn7kTCwPuPR30Uay4WismvBE3h4YFwp0Lh1myq0hmprBxSE8jkxMI5o\ny/0b5LzmywzlcIf1XMhNKQkFWWAuo0Dj9jH9CLNyEIxnQllGpT9bUZPYX6G9kJDk\nZLK3SUCp4vrwj3QwzNP/Zw83TjtV3EOa5fuOvQSD4eMJirAa7eBWTmZ1krljj+fP\ns1Huy1/dl5nrMAYYQfJuSfB+3RYtoVBUaa5G2AKKTyuD89Gh9ksVKtGHKmnIeC0Z\n3AEdk8dekOZEGSJhNq1uPgE71i7vaK/BfOPPy7Nn9mKdF+2FuoE=\n=kr+y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-29T19:09:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90524106?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jbsco","id":90524106,"login":"Jbsco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTI0MTA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lasp/adamant-skills/commit/741fba0ff5f46c7c991799f6e54e25acaab71372","node_id":"C_kwDOUHIrOdoAKDc0MWZiYTBmZjVmNDZjN2M5OTE3OTlmNmU1NGUyNWFjYWFiNzEzNzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lasp/adamant-skills/commit/33988d2551aa1c4dce9e390d6ec8391e6c22a185","sha":"33988d2551aa1c4dce9e390d6ec8391e6c22a185","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/33988d2551aa1c4dce9e390d6ec8391e6c22a185"}],"sha":"741fba0ff5f46c7c991799f6e54e25acaab71372","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/741fba0ff5f46c7c991799f6e54e25acaab71372"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90524106?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jbsco","id":90524106,"login":"Jbsco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTI0MTA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/33988d2551aa1c4dce9e390d6ec8391e6c22a185/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-29T23:37:37Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T17:32:49Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"message":"formal-verification: add the integer-logic conversion reference\n\nWritten from a conversion performed end to end: pulling an integer allocation\nout of a component body into a Pure SPARK logic package, proving it, and\nrewiring the caller. Every rule in the reference either discharged a proof or\ncaught a defect during that work, per the no-invented-patterns rule.\n\nThe substantive content is what modular register types do to a conversion.\nGenerated register types are modular, so the language raises no overflow\nobligations at all: the real obligations are range checks on conversions plus\nwhatever the postconditions state, and wraparound is invisible unless a\npostcondition forbids it. Three consequences are documented with the forms that\nfail. Widening after an addition rather than before wraps in the narrow domain\n(Wider (A + B) instead of Wider (A) + Wider (B)) and was a live defect in the\nconverted code. Signed-arithmetic guard idioms such as ''Max (X - Y, 0) are dead\ncode on a modular type. And an assert written in the same wrapped domain as the\nbug validates the bug instead of catching it, which is why a converted assert\nmust restate the property rather than transcribe the expression.\n\nAlso records clamp-then-narrow (taking the min in the wider type makes the\nnarrowing obligation unconditional and deletes the assert that documented the\nconditional form), how to draw the extraction boundary so the logic package\nimports nothing generated, how to write postconditions as properties rather\nthan restatements of the body, and the four verification fronts a conversion\nneeds, with the differential sweep called out as the only one that reveals\nwhere the original was wrong.\n\nMain skill gains the second admt prove failure signature, the note that a\nframework-free logic package needs only its own directory on SOURCE_DIRS, and\nan instruction to read the gnatprove summary rather than trusting exit status,\nincluding where a relative OBJECT_DIR actually writes it.","tree":{"sha":"b8342a1589711b3cc3189727f09f67b44ef8a484","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/trees/b8342a1589711b3cc3189727f09f67b44ef8a484"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/commits/33988d2551aa1c4dce9e390d6ec8391e6c22a185","verification":{"payload":"tree b8342a1589711b3cc3189727f09f67b44ef8a484\nparent cafbbe710c6ca97816d4d626cd876dfa9bd10272\nauthor Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1785368257 -0600\ncommitter Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1785519169 -0600\n\nformal-verification: add the integer-logic conversion reference\n\nWritten from a conversion performed end to end: pulling an integer allocation\nout of a component body into a Pure SPARK logic package, proving it, and\nrewiring the caller. Every rule in the reference either discharged a proof or\ncaught a defect during that work, per the no-invented-patterns rule.\n\nThe substantive content is what modular register types do to a conversion.\nGenerated register types are modular, so the language raises no overflow\nobligations at all: the real obligations are range checks on conversions plus\nwhatever the postconditions state, and wraparound is invisible unless a\npostcondition forbids it. Three consequences are documented with the forms that\nfail. Widening after an addition rather than before wraps in the narrow domain\n(Wider (A + B) instead of Wider (A) + Wider (B)) and was a live defect in the\nconverted code. Signed-arithmetic guard idioms such as ''Max (X - Y, 0) are dead\ncode on a modular type. And an assert written in the same wrapped domain as the\nbug validates the bug instead of catching it, which is why a converted assert\nmust restate the property rather than transcribe the expression.\n\nAlso records clamp-then-narrow (taking the min in the wider type makes the\nnarrowing obligation unconditional and deletes the assert that documented the\nconditional form), how to draw the extraction boundary so the logic package\nimports nothing generated, how to write postconditions as properties rather\nthan restatements of the body, and the four verification fronts a conversion\nneeds, with the differential sweep called out as the only one that reveals\nwhere the original was wrong.\n\nMain skill gains the second admt prove failure signature, the note that a\nframework-free logic package needs only its own directory on SOURCE_DIRS, and\nan instruction to read the gnatprove summary rather than trusting exit status,\nincluding where a relative OBJECT_DIR actually writes it.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEw4OO+fgBg9dPCrHf5dlyl7D/NcoFAmqTLZUACgkQ5dlyl7D/\nNcrUhg//US/kxQDAzRUxDFbHF5CsddHZMef9no4ZcU8aC6FLdTVGtHTpxW1AWJI9\nuc1lNY0kkUxSiuhQuRgohKWytJY1qt7TKQQrwItOzaHHI6xSCjc+D7mh+u10UADm\nS0cpIGQCyTZmxJXM+MO1ANmmWrL7pTqIScellCBLVRGqQFpTBxSrVsDviq2iX2+N\nuI26sVPt9K7BsncqyuTG+txyoaCOpxcKW0QdSqArx/BV/HiHsxuZVnDU/zoQZCwB\ne6T+ak0181/mvIm6o5IFDcJ4bs/cYdIVbFtlM8cco1PAh07o5scCWsz8SAbHYxJi\nh35/LXh5PGHeP4UV7Co5C0qyuFJzUC9XGcllpx1EMd+perDDgoMb2PPGhp3E3ZwJ\nQeja7edsxPXhzCxd2Y7BjRp0IBKhtnZDD7SZVycAlRt5skX+t7U1RWLcUd3elVfZ\nNc0MigkLIkfNMe6ZNfQW4mRRa4JrPH/8PJEY1jNt7athWNPto9AEUBkvhMGCVP1v\nzBO9lb65G+BqZ0TZ9EIwd8ldTBRykfTm4yembeNF53exbDMhqgW6mnTNjW262eS9\nx9nrUl7q60sK5XI2oinHcvWJlW7z4ZkoHVDwtCYTaliY3hP9Noxw+kKz+qKV1QlT\nQ3bFvuTLHW97DRPWHCYYndOA0nVQR4khSSZymCpF+pRZrS65/k4=\n=7kX2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-29T19:09:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90524106?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jbsco","id":90524106,"login":"Jbsco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTI0MTA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lasp/adamant-skills/commit/33988d2551aa1c4dce9e390d6ec8391e6c22a185","node_id":"C_kwDOUHIrOdoAKDMzOTg4ZDI1NTFhYTFjNGRjZTllMzkwZDZlYzgzOTFlNmMyMmExODU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lasp/adamant-skills/commit/cafbbe710c6ca97816d4d626cd876dfa9bd10272","sha":"cafbbe710c6ca97816d4d626cd876dfa9bd10272","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/cafbbe710c6ca97816d4d626cd876dfa9bd10272"}],"sha":"33988d2551aa1c4dce9e390d6ec8391e6c22a185","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/33988d2551aa1c4dce9e390d6ec8391e6c22a185"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90524106?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jbsco","id":90524106,"login":"Jbsco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTI0MTA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/cafbbe710c6ca97816d4d626cd876dfa9bd10272/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-29T23:27:05Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T17:32:49Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"message":"formal-verification: route to the vendor gnatprove skill and carve out specified saturation\n\nAdds the missing routing statement between this skill and a toolchain vendor''s gnatprove skill: the vendor skill is authoritative for tool mechanics and SPARK idioms, this one for how they meet Adamant. States the one override that applies at the point of routing.\n\nThe override is the clamping rule. General SPARK guidance treats an introduced Min/Max as a proof smell, which is right for application logic and wrong for anything modelling a register, device, protocol field, or configured limit, where the bound IS the specification. An agent following the vendor rule cold gets steered away from the construct such a model requires. Gives the discriminating question, the two-case table, and the multi-branch postcondition that turns a specified clamp into a proved case split.\n\nAlso adds the assume-count proof gate: report ''pragma Assume'' occurrences alongside unproved subprograms on every run, so Silver-to-Gold drift is visible rather than asserted. Selector gains routing for logic-package conversion and the vendor cross-link.","tree":{"sha":"4ebecc197dd8c2b7f70d2346a1914d829e8a687a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/trees/4ebecc197dd8c2b7f70d2346a1914d829e8a687a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/commits/cafbbe710c6ca97816d4d626cd876dfa9bd10272","verification":{"payload":"tree 4ebecc197dd8c2b7f70d2346a1914d829e8a687a\nparent 44483107b70a582fcb39333df18b3df3a73dc72d\nauthor Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1785367625 -0600\ncommitter Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1785519169 -0600\n\nformal-verification: route to the vendor gnatprove skill and carve out specified saturation\n\nAdds the missing routing statement between this skill and a toolchain vendor''s gnatprove skill: the vendor skill is authoritative for tool mechanics and SPARK idioms, this one for how they meet Adamant. States the one override that applies at the point of routing.\n\nThe override is the clamping rule. General SPARK guidance treats an introduced Min/Max as a proof smell, which is right for application logic and wrong for anything modelling a register, device, protocol field, or configured limit, where the bound IS the specification. An agent following the vendor rule cold gets steered away from the construct such a model requires. Gives the discriminating question, the two-case table, and the multi-branch postcondition that turns a specified clamp into a proved case split.\n\nAlso adds the assume-count proof gate: report ''pragma Assume'' occurrences alongside unproved subprograms on every run, so Silver-to-Gold drift is visible rather than asserted. Selector gains routing for logic-package conversion and the vendor cross-link.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEw4OO+fgBg9dPCrHf5dlyl7D/NcoFAmqTLZQACgkQ5dlyl7D/\nNcpxbxAAqP4aQ4Lb3wBdJnhBdzG+l/V0tWAqiKX088bdIv7UZfYbHTDtj1TAwEEn\nMS+FQczBQ6W0b8x9IQaJxVKGwR7EkfoS4S/7v4bnCHWQgPDfQY8kNvdTm3eRvPBe\nkt2FyUZXkZqPTGt9Qy9d0R7WUsACFnmOWnig4zxvGXxLZ38vtzI1toAjCUFIeJsm\nfUfdccdI0M+sPaeyzGGzmVBp68kVW58Gg5opOslHKx/Swr3o7Eh12TWx3+2LXr3i\nFtEZXa3dcqerOcp2m7maLWk3uecWS0BiVUMKxkYCmYx+86RslZI