:"https://github.com/Jbsco","id":90524106,"login":"Jbsco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTI0MTA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/7d700ee2c4f5e30d524448210e2fb6ad397572ff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-29T15:50:31Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-29T15:50:31Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"message":"docs: order project selection by agent preference (Jbsco/adamant-agent-skills#21 review)\n\nReview: the section was ordered by resolution mechanics (terminal ->\nheadless -> per-command), but the reader is an agent choosing what to\ndo. Reorder by preference and say so up front: (1) pin the session via\nthe auto-detected harness id (`env use` once), (2) ADMT_ENV as the\nper-command override when needed. The interactive-terminal path drops\nto a one-line completeness note carrying the caveat that a tty is not\nusually available inside an agent session, and the mechanical-precedence\npreamble goes away -- \"outranks the pin\" in the override bullet is the\nonly precedence fact an agent needs.","tree":{"sha":"a49f1d14cbd58943a778ada3f702592899890967","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/trees/a49f1d14cbd58943a778ada3f702592899890967"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/commits/7d700ee2c4f5e30d524448210e2fb6ad397572ff","verification":{"payload":"tree a49f1d14cbd58943a778ada3f702592899890967\nparent b492c9c942e7afc748180