ite_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/b492c9c942e7afc74818029c1c0b4cded19002ec/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T14:17:55Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T14:17:55Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"message":"docs: fold Codex into the auto-detected harness set (lockstep with Jbsco/admt#37)\n\nJbsco/admt#37''s reviewed harness list grew from Claude Code alone to Claude\nCode + Codex (both on the normal shell path) -- so \"others map onto\nADMT_SESSION_KEY\" understated it. Name both auto-detected harnesses;\nanything else still maps onto ADMT_SESSION_KEY. (Gemini''s hook-only var\nis omitted here: it does not fire on the shell path agents use, so it\nwould mislead in agent-facing guidance -- admt''s own docs carry that\ncaveat.)\n\nStill gated on Jbsco/admt#37 shipping.","tree":{"sha":"d03e5a6e63ccb7dd2b7f010803325b8405d74ebe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/trees/d03e5a6e63ccb7dd2b7f010803325b8405d74ebe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/commits/b492c9c942e7afc74818029c1c0b4cded19002ec","verification":{"payload":"tree d03e5a6e63ccb7dd2b7f010803325b8405d74ebe\nparent 7e423d0e609a434451998e3cea3dc7562812e998\nauthor Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1785248275 -0600\ncommitter Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1785248275 -0600\n\ndocs: fold Codex into the auto-detected harness set (lockstep with Jbsco/admt#37)\n\nJbsco/admt#37''s reviewed harness list grew from Claude Code alone to Claude\nCode + Codex (both on the normal shell path) -- so \"others map ont