pos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/38583385707151fa66bbcd1d5d0ef27b32538879/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-11T20:59:14Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T13:19:13Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"message":"Encourage in-situ skill updates from novel debugging work\n\nThe campaign''s most valuable content came from field falsifications and\ngaps hit in practice, but nothing told an agent doing ordinary debugging\nwork to feed those observations back. New section: when a task exceeds\nwhat is written or a documented move fails as described, capture it --\nheld to the skill''s own demonstrated-not-inferred standard, kept generic\n(placeholders, no project identifiers or naming motifs), extending\nexisting sections rather than duplicating, with a routing cue so the\naddition is findable. Tasks that forbid skill edits report the proposed\nchange verbatim instead; version control stays with the orchestrator\nor maintainer.","tree":{"sha":"03c44727efd0959d679b8a782c90ad0e1c9f26fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/trees/03c44727efd0959d679b8a782c90ad0e1c9f26fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/commits/38583385707151fa66bbcd1d5d0ef27b32538879","verification":{"payload":"tree 03c44727efd0959d679b8a782c90ad0e1c9f26fe\nparent 050c0c18396d8614e4cf4ab86c48df2076be3cb6\nauthor Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1783803554 -0600\ncommitter Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1785071953 -0600\n\nEncourage in-situ skill updates from novel debugging work\n\nThe campaign''s most valuable content came from field falsifications and\ngaps hit in practice, but nothing told an agent doing ordinary debugging\nwork to feed those observations back. New section: when a task exceeds\nwhat is written or a documented move fails as described, capture it --\nheld to the skill''s own demonstrated-not-inferred standard, kept generic\n(placeholders, no project identifiers or naming motifs), extending\nexisting sections rather than duplicating, with a routing cue so the\naddition is findable. Tasks that forbid skill edits report the proposed\nchange verbatim instead; version control stays with the orchestrator\nor maintainer.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEw4OO+fgBg9dPCrHf5dlyl7D/NcoFAmqTLZIACgkQ5dlyl7D/\nNcpKTA/8C+tM4OeBAIVPGS1Zu8Zd3X/Rc162jlJnbVymOd5SR5yPiQsJIoe8FIwL\nzIFW0FMunx+2VLwU07iTlJuHD8MwyQt8e4lBXmpEdS09FuRGKNcJLESrL7wRdYE9\n1eSEajruP+dVY0Z9NqBEzEJ553ZzpYR2+fQ2pfbX7+F8FC4+Y/myxhXkifhW8cBv\nCBbRpx2cUh8kzTZJNtd839N2psVwekv26FAx69xXrS0cbk5BZhd5QNHzUnY6sGGs\ni5yW3631px4OKvN7PSGStFL0SmjOWxyQLMS+1WHkz42ZZCXyCff8Lb+hv+ZNPC+K\nKROErpMx52RxxJocZbY2slBY3enzTgCTCMy0CP4erckTFbOTI4TTNH0HFNvxBzXI\ngbhOng/Wpfi70NX6InDeB+i5NqQ+nJmWd/MCjMOSsvF/dHU0XB9E4+Cz7ch5dzM+\nicRUFTnGTQJ8rWDzk1q6q1pwwt9ztQ2DaCTLyTdBVIYvzG0113Mg0QVPlNb/9W4v\n5vuoS52BX356lio0Q7zriTGMT7vze9pzIRVfe6EjYEHvHaQyVcGBiWHMX7uwWBAh\n0tTQXEW6JnH3nu5kjPJps8bgGzu+uaEDvlkrchEqZSFpmd0ka45LySfnVJ9hOU27\nu3PLuLUQ1rhx2RWU2OlT+QU59Fd0QrpKvo4E3Z7dDrRRzL+qcgY=\n=p2R3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-29T19:09:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90524106?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jbsco","i