type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/050c0c18396d8614e4cf4ab86c48df2076be3cb6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-11T20:49:56Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T13:19:12Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"message":"Cross-link and scope the new headless-emulator sections\n\nThree skill-review coherence catches (adversarially verified). The\nbench-operations runbook and the Renode-stub watchpoint section each\nstated the batch-continue limitation and the emulator-native-hook\nworkaround without pointing at each other -- added reciprocal see-also\npointers so a reader landing in either file finds the other half. The\nbench-ops section read as crash-reproduction-only despite applying to\nevery headless Renode session (interactive cross debugging,\ntest_renode) -- added a scoping sentence. SKILL.md''s reference pointer\nfor post-mortem-and-lch.md predated the new sections, leaving the\nraw-capture extraction recipe and the bench-ops runbook invisible to\nthe routing read -- pointer updated with a read-before-scripted-\nemulator-session cue.","tree":{"sha":"646d217533b370d35ee4581ac428257aaf95dc99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/trees/646d217533b370d35ee4581ac428257aaf95dc99"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/commits/050c0c18396d8614e4cf4ab86c48df2076be3cb6","verification":{"payload":"tree 646d217533b370d35ee4581ac428257aaf95dc99\nparent 78f26ab5ed7f75f9fe3957f8192b5e22b92d1d1c\nauthor Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1783802996 -0600\ncommitter Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1785071952 -0600\n\nCross-link and scope the new headless-emulator sections\n\nThree skill-review coherence catches (adversarially verified). The\nbench-operations runbook and the Renode-stub watchpoint section each\nstated the batch-continue limitation and the emulator-native-hook\nworkaround without pointing at each other -- added reciprocal see-also\npointers so a reader landing in either file finds the other half. The\nbench-ops section read as crash-reproduction-only despite applying to\nevery headless Renode session (interactive cross debugging,\ntest_renode) -- added a scoping sentence. SKILL.md''s reference pointer\nfor post-mortem-and-lch.md predated the new sections, leaving the\nraw-capture extraction recipe and the bench-ops runbook invisible to\nthe routing read -- pointer updated with a read-before-scripted-\nemulator-session cue.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEw4OO+fgBg9dPCrHf5dlyl7D/NcoFAmqTLZIACgkQ5dlyl7D/\nNcpDMw/9Gl6RZ2b6vsQuipYH2obgjQGcpWM5kK+/4sJHM0kFVUEk0KzkuiJXnHmc\n4XonBP1/EvcTbyadfjJ+ihA4vB+ndxYC/MW9rTvD2SOJncTEnU4Ha3Ei8pJ+C9Ii\nTTqpwEp8zu3jzjXXLv0vFeCAKX2M5hEhN401MYCiIIuht0wvMQQuNN7cdm7iUCPb\nYZujgViAbwGNAIVjZJ4u6fLpOcwr4pzYmgkA9KROvojzP2NvO7rPTkBjIAq8/c+e\nSxUeTsr223WhXVEK0QwFcjeAa751vuzM+BxgHLaKMJvfCBeLFZ0tllVAl/Yv9xtu\nifzO9WZkhGWRrcdQflOY25u/Vcic5zzfz0ZiQE56Af1aDLhKXaYjU7owHaNs6LCn\n9fa9imPqmytxW3ed2G9SMNUa6fcR4SwEv3lZzCsdZ2rfyVbkkJLrMX4GHSBxJlx+\nttbKmtIzI8grNAa8U2TRbqgjy58JeurSR/WOTnTRnB98uiv+iNJYTlk+zw9dvn+8\nfnNCPmtEQ2icmhzN83Z3JAsGbwoX3wyEW8NK5sSN2IXrc9zLBbFT73PB2t73nBLL\n+gSjZt0u3Q5gk6Pg4NbiwOHIA0Ifxjli8Pi3lJlVq1N5ZvbQDaq7OYUirxaSTrns\nZxZbaweiG+fiiqux3N946aRqRYyXIwvHPhsOWmrHHE3Z8hxP0o8=\n=TJJH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-29T19:09:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90524106?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jbsco","id":90524106,"login":"Jbsco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTI0MTA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lasp/adamant-skills/commit/050c0c18396d8614e4cf4ab86c48df2076be3cb6","node_id":"C_kwDOUHIrOdoAKDA1MGMwYzE4Mzk2ZDg2MTRlNGNmNGFiODZjNDhkZjIwNzZiZTNjYjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lasp/adamant-skills/commit/78f26ab5ed7f75f9fe3957f8192b5e22b92d1d1c","sha":"78f26ab5ed7f75f9fe3957f8192b5e22b92d1d1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/78f26ab5ed7f75f9fe3957f8192b5e22b92d1d1c"}],"sha":"050c0c18396d8614e4cf4ab86c48df2076be3cb6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/050c0c18396d8614e4cf4ab86c48df2076be3cb6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90524106?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jbsco","id":90524106,"login":"Jbsco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTI0MTA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/78f26ab5ed7f75f9fe3957f8192b5e22b92d1d1c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-11T20:48:37Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T13:19:12Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"message":"Correct mcause legend and catch-assert rationale\n\nTwo skill-review factual catches (adversarially verified). (1) The\nRISC-V trap table lumped mcause 5/6/7 as load/store access faults,\nmislabeling code 6 -- store/AMO ADDRESS MISALIGNED -- as an access\nfault; it is the store-side analog of code 4, the exact fault class\nFamily 1 teaches, so a reader hitting mcause=6 during alignment\ndebugging would misdiagnose it as a bus fault. Split the legend per the\nISA and added code 0. (2) The catch-assert note claimed AUnit Assert\ncalls record failures without raising; verified against AUnit and\nAdamant sources, the procedure-form Assert DOES raise Assertion_Error.\nThe correct reason catch assert stays silent is that it hooks GNAT''s\nassert-failure routine, not ordinary raises -- and catch exception\ntherefore DOES stop at test assertions. Conclusion unchanged, rationale\nfixed.","tree":{"sha":"82b1f4e8dae8c4d69bde0a97b44cc8d984578a21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/trees/82b1f4e8dae8c4d69bde0a97b44cc8d984578a21"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/commits/78f26ab5ed7f75f9fe3957f8192b5e22b92d1d1c","verification":{"payload":"tree 82b1f4e8dae8c4d69bde0a97b44cc8d984578a21\nparent 2ca1bdf8753697ddc429ab1872be1b8dfaef3d6e\nauthor Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1783802917 -0600\ncommitter Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1785071952 -0600\n\nCorrect mcause legend and catch-assert rationale\n\nTwo skill-review factual catches (adversarially verified). (1) The\nRISC-V trap table lumped mcause 5/6/7 as load/store access faults,\nmislabeling code 6 -- store/AMO ADDRESS MISALIGNED -- as an access\nfault; it is the store-side analog of code 4, the exact fault class\nFamily 1 teaches, so a reader hitting mcause=6 during alignment\ndebugging would misdiagnose it as a bus fault. Split the legend per the\nISA and added code 0. (2) The catch-assert note claimed AUnit Assert\ncalls record failures without raising; verified against AUnit and\nAdamant sources, the procedure-form Assert DOES raise Assertion_Error.\nThe correct reason catch assert stays silent is that it hooks GNAT''s\nassert-failure routine, not ordinary raises -- and catch exception\ntherefore DOES stop at test assertions. Conclusion unchanged, rationale\nfixed.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEw4OO+fgBg9dPCrHf5dlyl7D/NcoFAmqTLZIACgkQ5dlyl7D/\nNcrTUA/9H5qLa4sgLaCzf2dP2esClppQVUpR7C7yVDvfrOWesYGkMkSezjS4c3K1\n2Hjl3BHuNX14i2LDTdIr3JH/eoSjLxUUGCT8Si54bplBicfu/C8W3FDJeSxQOo7R\nSJmuqD8jtMzl8xNELMBKLRPK9luP5+MiV0lXBogsSmO1P2n8AZci59fSsCxQgoGt\nbnYxi9cz6/PFiWRrzt/sa1oX447KevdmjdXMa0DYRUPKPM/Yl/Zpxj8wm3/kdFsS\nXpwa0uIFrlgJsoVSdz2XaywAsVEXvRZHikHgBZz2s3pwDRiZOs+q9PPbclOC+xeq\nVceQmrA3DJZ4OmgeBcWB1DYFkRhTeY0AU5MKF2+VMprFcqN95hVWhnM9oUkM/d1h\nHcGzGmL53kt/QpxAdTIKM5vqvdrqboHPrzSabEn1zfQirT+hnIh7M2olO4h2riHu\nM//EscA8clEvqr8G42i5/1i4AFEv1pcG2KFqpJ8AqSFfAeZSy4QrI5Q/5nbD39rO\noAxDNGKtdBgX8l9vG2PXsZ7Cw0zzyMpE13BwHMmaXIaYz9Rc8szY0ujzU3MqXsvX\nObuPNQrjx+dMUhABTXk8byYLYCRJdVBBsHvW5fWd6WnPMj3Nbsi0Vk0NXjm9lJGJ\nS0sE2Mmy+WOL8fbdZXFpMXyp+dnijkczzgyNDL12N0+D5gNMnMI=\n=Fpj6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-29T19:09:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90524106?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jbsco","id":90524106,"login":"Jbsco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTI0MTA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lasp/adamant-skills/commit/78f26ab5ed7f75f9fe3957f8192b5e22b92d1d1c","node_id":"C_kwDOUHIrOdoAKDc4ZjI2YWI1ZWQ3Zjc1ZjlmZTM5NTdmODE5MmI1ZTIyYjkyZDFkMWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lasp/adamant-skills/commit/2ca1bdf8753697ddc429ab1872be1b8dfaef3d6e","sha":"2ca1bdf8753697ddc429ab1872be1b8dfaef3d6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/2ca1bdf8753697ddc429ab1872be1b8dfaef3d6e"}],"sha":"78f26ab5ed7f75f9fe3957f8192b5e22b92d1d1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/78f26ab5ed7f75f9fe3957f8192b5e22b92d1d1c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90524106?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jbsco","id":90524106,"login":"Jbsco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTI0MTA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/2ca1bdf8753697ddc429ab1872be1b8dfaef3d6e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-11T20:48:04Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T13:19:12Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"message":"Remove project-derived C++ termination hook name from LCH anatomy\n\nSkill-review leak catch (adversarially verified): the C++-termination\nclause in the LCH anatomy named a hook symbol derived from a closed\nproject''s private naming rather than a standard runtime identifier. The\ngenuine mechanism is a project-installed std::terminate handler feeding\nthe same last-chance path; restated generically. Sole occurrence in the\nrepo (grep-verified).","tree":{"sha":"1717d79585b8b28777d9cf0374a20471cabfa7b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/trees/1717d79585b8b28777d9cf0374a20471cabfa7b4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/commits/2ca1bdf8753697ddc429ab1872be1b8dfaef3d6e","verification":{"payload":"tree 1717d79585b8b28777d9cf0374a20471cabfa7b4\nparent 6159624e5751647602c209a7ce8c01bad8ab6cc4\nauthor Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1783802884 -0600\ncommitter Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1785071952 -0600\n\nRemove project-derived C++ termination hook name from LCH anatomy\n\nSkill-review leak catch (adversarially verified): the C++-termination\nclause in the LCH anatomy named a hook symbol derived from a closed\nproject''s private naming rather than a standard runtime identifier. The\ngenuine mechanism is a project-installed std::terminate handler feeding\nthe same last-chance path; restated generically. Sole occurrence in the\nrepo (grep-verified).\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEw4OO+fgBg9dPCrHf5dlyl7D/NcoFAmqTLZEACgkQ5dlyl7D/\nNcrnWxAAlCxt5t8fTpMLK8xxu8o5YyvZjCdPcJGT57K7HUvQ/x3gJfy3BJ/H75tY\nx68I8JJHeN7akBQnurZnzk0BmGW26oZXVcqSDMKTk/9vFE7VvgUTR8XTF3Z1UsLF\nU4Z0V2cmTZ83TQG3Jf2TsTmwOMQnX082Hx1/PuLGY7L+NPBpb52dGD/LLZymreAS\nMPVGVZ7beIFHTGhFbxyfujKtS9OFgHxOFL339LJFvVu6OJjKAgDB54ftV9OPtr6A\nAOaiZGgPZLuL6YMnluzvd8MajiEENY5zgXcaSVYva6eZFwQnioQM9wqzqo5nMI3r\npiCuA7wjtj9ClydHb7VBGcip04gfoKZKEaMlYDAFKnbTmpSOUUoaocdW0JAttTRO\nmiNN2jbMvNo7xRfROiSl/qYdkz4/vlbMPa7Bnqf+7jo943P/ArM63Lux8JkzxHMG\n4QOPU3Qxgy1pU+ycNj0b+e+4YpRP41ZTMNLQ7FMdde+2Sd/o9M9A6RGFY7lR1Em+\n+D7Sk5hjoX46JtnoaRVMRc7XgXV6hBT4cpMlJkPa4F6efLGVKD680t9abAPbySMS\n/wy3b7hX5E+A9U3VfJSN26fZiuV6TUgJhILHUYOuLcVV1GSKITv70WSmjW9cMzYD\nwWL7825q/BlHG1HP8+GpEesHAK3GXZCQ31+p1HPl5/YYfu/8bOE=\n=nWNV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-29T19:09:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90524106?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jbsco","id":90524106,"login":"Jbsco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTI0MTA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lasp/adamant-skills/commit/2ca1bdf8753697ddc429ab1872be1b8dfaef3d6e","node_id":"C_kwDOUHIrOdoAKDJjYTFiZGY4NzUzNjk3ZGRjNDI5YWIxODcyYmUxYjhkZmFlZjNkNmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lasp/adamant-skills/commit/6159624e5751647602c209a7ce8c01bad8ab6cc4","sha":"6159624e5751647602c209a7ce8c01bad8ab6cc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/6159624e5751647602c209a7ce8c01bad8ab6cc4"}],"sha":"2ca1bdf8753697ddc429ab1872be1b8dfaef3d6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/2ca1bdf8753697ddc429ab1872be1b8dfaef3d6e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90524106?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jbsco","id":90524106,"login":"Jbsco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTI0MTA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/6159624e5751647602c209a7ce8c01bad8ab6cc4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-11T20:11:15Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T13:19:12Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"message":"Sharpen fixture-opacity rule and add prompt-technique-leak rule\n\nE3 tier ran to a 5-clean streak that the catches exposed as hollow: the\nwatchpoint DP (never genuinely earned) was still not earned. Two causes,\nboth campaign-methodology gaps. (1) The fixture was labelled corruption\n-- which the opacity rule lists as runtime-opaque -- but its off-by-one\nindex was source-visible, so agents read the one writing procedure and\nlocalized it with no watchpoint. Clarified that the label is not the\ntest: opacity requires that which location gets hit is not derivable from\nthe writer''s source (runtime-computed address, stray pointer, no textual\nreach to the victim). (2) The debug prompt named the exact guard address\nand framed the watchpoint, scaffolding the behavior under test -- so the\nDP measured the prompt, not the skill. Added the symptom-in/technique-out\nrule for runtime-technique DPs, generalizing the E1a demotion.","tree":{"sha":"5bebb900e7f983a7fe346fda6bfdfb2a0521eee6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/trees/5bebb900e7f983a7fe346fda6bfdfb2a0521eee6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/commits/6159624e5751647602c209a7ce8c01bad8ab6cc4","verification":{"payload":"tree 5bebb900e7f983a7fe346fda6bfdfb2a0521eee6\nparent d1fc2884ed518845e1fa7547945a73f54cdaac2a\nauthor Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1783800675 -0600\ncommitter Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1785071952 -0600\n\nSharpen fixture-opacity rule and add prompt-technique-leak rule\n\nE3 tier ran to a 5-clean streak that the catches exposed as hollow: the\nwatchpoint DP (never genuinely earned) was still not earned. Two causes,\nboth campaign-methodology gaps. (1) The fixture was labelled corruption\n-- which the opacity rule lists as runtime-opaque -- but its off-by-one\nindex was source-visible, so agents read the one writing procedure and\nlocalized it with no watchpoint. Clarified that the label is not the\ntest: opacity requires that which location gets hit is not derivable from\nthe writer''s source (runtime-computed address, stray pointer, no textual\nreach to the victim). (2) The debug prompt named the exact guard address\nand framed the watchpoint, scaffolding the behavior under test -- so the\nDP measured the prompt, not the skill. Added the symptom-in/technique-out\nrule for runtime-technique DPs, generalizing the E1a demotion.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEw4OO+fgBg9dPCrHf5dlyl7D/NcoFAmqTLZEACgkQ5dlyl7D/\nNcrs4hAA0DE9vX/S7J2CgRnTKiB3RLYemhzFEa28JR9BDcv8YmLQCFKWtZxuXBoA\nZUPlJEKLekfGCisqfP9vt2tHb0y1+OgCnl5EVVbpFjLfK2fLEF/FhKkDSuOhJxo4\njBFOV3arqzqmoMtwSoqSB2UAmvqP5wAteJLBW9QYhTS4etun8+dVEUBfqBHD2r5K\n6ImTEU82I9tTnkR5bCWoFcU/3idI1S6NSbBkUa7N3Ej9MeB/sqlc4QJsleuYus2C\nFAFsGYVWMdUDmPXzlSuu+3u2n9vE7Wz0hLXSEFok9G7HxP9lBfYqBJ3FBNLrkCNI\ndrLS4ZNZ30NXJo4J5PzvlVxT6eu+/v3x/zm8BdKVvjQT1bZrZJAdsQCB7Av+qr1q\ndI4/eU1cEmCftbk0qatBqH+hlK+MS+WV1+cvgy2rUctc6L4CTC8KxtnxL6Elm8qC\nVT43zi8frgjIYqYxym/GwNtqFG7LpaCqFbLmtZFMO2n0FHHpnnqxg/UTrVEXTBt5\ncRgyvRIpg2WsLh8tQgu+zEmJo8KEkb17msixo8MAkrpQIzu7QohSIDY+wfchZ+S8\nvqZayBH8HgnpsboLkIle0mTF71HmznHKgwzPIu3vCLC5YY1ylpPtNj9hpQZAwblM\nvJXUd2jzgE5/NjW27+wlQnj2uBzd7G/PPA0k5PZ9LSDFe77im30=\n=qvft\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-29T19:09:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90524106?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jbsco","id":90524106,"login":"Jbsco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTI0MTA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lasp/adamant-skills/commit/6159624e5751647602c209a7ce8c01bad8ab6cc4","node_id":"C_kwDOUHIrOdoAKDYxNTk2MjRlNTc1MTY0NzYwMmMyMDlhN2NlOGMwMWJhZDhhYjZjYzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lasp/adamant-skills/commit/d1fc2884ed518845e1fa7547945a73f54cdaac2a","sha":"d1fc2884ed518845e1fa7547945a73f54cdaac2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/d1fc2884ed518845e1fa7547945a73f54cdaac2a"}],"sha":"6159624e5751647602c209a7ce8c01bad8ab6cc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/6159624e5751647602c209a7ce8c01bad8ab6cc4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90524106?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jbsco","id":90524106,"login":"Jbsco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTI0MTA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/d1fc2884ed518845e1fa7547945a73f54cdaac2a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-11T20:10:31Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T13:19:12Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"message":"Route mystery-write/silent-corruption symptom to debugging watchpoints\n\nE3 campaign catch (iterations 3, 4): the Common Task Combinations table\nhad no row for the ''a value is wrong at runtime and no source assignment\nexplains it'' symptom, so agents navigating by the table did not route to\nthe debugging skill''s watchpoint content -- they source-inferred the\nwriter instead. Added a row mapping the mystery-write / corruption /\ncanary-flip symptom to debugging (advanced-inspection watchpoints).","tree":{"sha":"3ebf4511c20aa417cb8e696178b6e3606c0751bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/trees/3ebf4511c20aa417cb8e696178b6e3606c0751bc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/commits/d1fc2884ed518845e1fa7547945a73f54cdaac2a","verification":{"payload":"tree 3ebf4511c20aa417cb8e696178b6e3606c0751bc\nparent e5714290e587191736cf6bac214a0022a6508309\nauthor Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1783800631 -0600\ncommitter Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1785071952 -0600\n\nRoute mystery-write/silent-corruption symptom to debugging watchpoints\n\nE3 campaign catch (iterations 3, 4): the Common Task Combinations table\nhad no row for the ''a value is wrong at runtime and no source assignment\nexplains it'' symptom, so agents navigating by the table did not route to\nthe debugging skill''s watchpoint content -- they source-inferred the\nwriter instead. Added a row mapping the mystery-write / corruption /\ncanary-flip symptom to debugging (advanced-inspection watchpoints).\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEw4OO+fgBg9dPCrHf5dlyl7D/NcoFAmqTLZEACgkQ5dlyl7D/\nNcrVYg//TzEwR+e8GO+7gMQn60sS7JEBXOdSzMQnYRMBGRyGXhKQrpqOUaZtSAg3\n7ilBxCXhfO2GVTXFYOU7cY4cC479+kvjkqeXDe/puNTVshOSE6hb1dhOp1/s5ImC\n/Thiv9/dvj6gb2syu2ZTWiRnJZTkDPvgniuE6LR001LNx7CBXP4gLlN6exSbDHld\nJiU5k26uU7rrXkUpdIUSPBsrq2g/RpZqjheeqae+EFdjaGzMMoQybBEC/l3yjQzB\n1f2U1j+RTT7XskRm99k30Gojk63vDSwCr3ditQOUasT8fPbAzTQKgcpFH2Hg0GdJ\nTWkuVtEhe4Q1lrbgCvmrAPRum3hUlgk/M3wQIA8huBp3KYrZvUTggP5SUoHuqUM