owing{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jbsco","id":90524106,"login":"Jbsco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTI0MTA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/74e8886472e68d14337a95b193d004c18896448d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-11T05:16:09Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T13:19:10Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"message":"Add cross-target test-failure row to selector combos table\n\nE1 campaign catch (2/3 agents): a ''passes on Linux, fails on the flight\ntarget'' task has no row in Common Task Combinations, so agents that\nnavigate by the table fall through and never open adamant-debugging.\nThe Debugging section header covers target-only bugs, but transcript\nverification showed both missing agents consulted the table and stopped.\nRoute the task shape explicitly to debugging (target-pitfalls ref) with\nbuild-system secondary.","tree":{"sha":"9c85154ebdeab59e55c47e3dd84dd9291b86fb7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/trees/9c85154ebdeab59e55c47e3dd84dd9291b86fb7b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/commits/74e8886472e68d14337a95b193d004c18896448d","verification":{"payload":"tree 9c85154ebdeab59e55c47e3dd84dd9291b86fb7b\nparent 6234fb17bff3206100461ee738403289bc9adcce\nauthor Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1783746969 -0600\ncommitter Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1785071950 -0600\n\nAdd cross-target test-failure row to selector combos table\n\nE1 campaign catch (2/3 agents): a ''passes on Linux, fails on the flight\ntarget'' task has no row in Common Task Combinations, so agents that\nnavigate by the table fall through and never open adamant-debugging.\nThe Debugging section header covers target-only bugs, but transcript\nverification showed both missing agents consulted the table and stopped.\nRoute the task shape explicitly to debugging (target-pitfalls ref) with\nbuild-system secondary.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEw4OO+fgBg9dPCrHf5dlyl7D/NcoFAmqTLZAACgkQ5dlyl7D/\nNcpNJA/9FcUqo3nCKd5zWI6vYlCqekZ5Op21Zou9OHN468dArQGt8PCV3YmshhYq\nDAWjYfN+ZVE9p50nP78NKmYvKmqYAmrrz0NBGjOG+LopuA1gKbjBIazEItFNxape\nvlJ1WiFIIjxQB4bezsNVzYvLKd2tGCiuqSLJ4NaSsE8hMW7T8hKDPYvym4C3DcZN\nNoCaiVEG/iuiH6vHps/ZVdnFc4vb6ZTU8nmJ3pR0+fmg6tnXqCnvGL4eEP/tCygy\ngmc2ZB91EYmH8iKr1idXSygvx6fQSJMuLh7VIpwi2y2J01fdDRuQSy8e94pOn0MA\n1cSKI1BDvo2UNBFmxCfJVYwRKeWT97QDGGNLl/W3KYV+1b5slkJTa3/ZYgTIUawW\nbb0SEl+VrKc/N+4aINhv1hjPFejlTy9rPk1yQg5nULBNHuacS6gKY52xerH9rqGO\nR9ULZoWqbb7JfvGjkTbSxXVon+woqc4DBtwoMp4CzWDn3AF3fL3zB+y6x1s8luJe\n8SrNhnHAGbie+v/TFGRYLPPJzcQ5AgPw0sWh/2N702x/P3Z2UcERauLsRYgNWj1K\nPfnX372xAhymm8Kq58NOmAAgE0MGStIuGo4XcHcUptPrVfdje8OkZJbgTPzzSBSa\njNrSJGiXChg6Yfpyu8h6biNqLao7z6nQFkI3K14rG5rizBN3MQ8=\n=ViUZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-29T19:09:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90524106?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jbsco","id":90524106,"login":"Jbsco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTI0MTA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lasp/adamant-skills/commit/74e8886472e68d14337a95b193d004c18896448d","node_id":"C_kwDOUHIrOdoAKDc0ZTg4ODY0NzJlNjhkMTQzMzdhOTViMTkzZDAwNGMxODg5NjQ0OGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lasp/adamant-skills/commit/6234fb17bff3206100461ee738403289bc9adcce","sha":"6234fb17bff3206100461ee738403289bc9adcce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/6234fb17bff3206100461ee738403289bc9adcce"}],"sha":"74e8886472e68d14337a95b193d004c18896448d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/74e8886472e68d14337a95b193d004c18896448d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90524106?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jbsco","id":90524106,"login":"Jbsco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTI0MTA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/6234fb17bff3206100461ee738403289bc9adcce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-11T04:12:42Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T13:19:10Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"message":"Note SPARK contracts as runtime assertions in the debug loop\n\nUser raised GNAT/SPARK env differences for mission_fsw. Verified the\ninteractive-gdb layer transfers (ema linux_test.gpr extends the same\na_linux_debug_base.gpr the target table came from; -gnata on, 471 asserts)\nand the cross/post-mortem layers are ema-native already. The one boundary\nthe skill omitted: SPARK pre/postconditions behave as assertions at\nruntime on Debug/Test targets, so catch exception/assert catches a failing\ncontract like a pragma Assert; static proof is a separate GNATprove\nanalyze target (see adamant-formal-verification), not the gdb loop. Added\nas Ada-specific move #3.","tree":{"sha":"cef9d6364b9ae0f34a5d5eeee578a6e09028b9a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/trees/cef9d6364b9ae0f34a5d5eeee578a6e09028b9a9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/commits/6234fb17bff3206100461ee738403289bc9adcce","verification":{"payload":"tree cef9d6364b9ae0f34a5d5eeee578a6e09028b9a9\nparent 8c8da90149a8fa869e3fe4124c21448c9fae9caf\nauthor Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1783743162 -0600\ncommitter Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1785071950 -0600\n\nNote SPARK contracts as runtime assertions in the debug loop\n\nUser raised GNAT/SPARK env differences for mission_fsw. Verified the\ninteractive-gdb layer transfers (ema linux_test.gpr extends the same\na_linux_debug_base.gpr the target table came from; -gnata on, 471 asserts)\nand the cross/post-mortem layers are ema-native already. The one boundary\nthe skill omitted: SPARK pre/postconditions behave as assertions at\nruntime on Debug/Test targets, so catch exception/assert catches a failing\ncontract like a pragma Assert; static proof is a separate GNATprove\nanalyze target (see adamant-formal-verification), not the gdb loop. Added\nas Ada-specific move #3.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEw4OO+fgBg9dPCrHf5dlyl7D/NcoFAmqTLY8ACgkQ5dlyl7D/\nNcr1ww//csxye/afWC44M+WZfb/9+LXa8nLoRntDCG0oEwZv2RPffaDRY7+tZ5YV\nVWm/WaGc9OnwdALCaFXR1D+ZQO97LOnY5InGJdVH5BCiVksnsagI5CgucYeY7XRL\nIRK7IWa2dfn34+eCqmKsUNeoiZZuLU4H7XvXMnO37zP/sbzE60tP8kDcD4cqIN+/\nY8y5j4DMV80CGIjJ+Si31uzoEvSo8HUEx+fzPWG6m0kGH3SsexUvwiCfGKBkNifx\n4+obCkUSpVuQfJ2m8u1SO2r43+2x1AShzLBctX0rMLsShufwDGjyl17IK4X6ZZbq\nYrWCcpktECvFGLokM74SC88W2RFbECaN7WDN5oIpRVSvdnpmhtevSmtcktKofttM\nW+6hBR8cq/AzTPKHkplxjaVAokhU6h5SGJgJuXANT8pduM+U5j0ORZLjwx2/8+vN\nmMXxrZt295dR2+hlsNPTl5k2A3BVseUrbnyqdnZKERO0RlRCzxD74193VauuaT3k\n4K89Jo4wiR+vejVU3EJiX+DtU6YhdiTVkH3Bc9I5bExU0MthG6YhTXvIsnOL6Tt8\n05ew6UbkeMdiu8+d35TW1KOSr1k7B9Z0PNGFE/hi4f5sB14xhJ3A6Eu/vh0t+GMZ\nNWr9JPbX7PXQqo6tSj044BgqRpdNW4MsR8JxS6YDTEtTTddNrSw=\n=OgE/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-29T19:09:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90524106?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jbsco","id":90524106,"login":"Jbsco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTI0MTA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lasp/adamant-skills/commit/6234fb17bff3206100461ee738403289bc9adcce","node_id":"C_kwDOUHIrOdoAKDYyMzRmYjE3YmZmMzIwNjEwMDQ2MWVlNzM4NDAzMjg5YmM5YWRjY2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lasp/adamant-skills/commit/8c8da90149a8fa869e3fe4124c21448c9fae9caf","sha":"8c8da90149a8fa869e3fe4124c21448c9fae9caf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/8c8da90149a8fa869e3fe4124c21448c9fae9caf"}],"sha":"6234fb17bff3206100461ee738403289bc9adcce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/6234fb17bff3206100461ee738403289bc9adcce"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90524106?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jbsco","id":90524106,"login":"Jbsco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTI0MTA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/8c8da90149a8fa869e3fe4124c21448c9fae9caf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-11T03:48:23Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T13:19:10Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"message":"Correct hung-task triage: thread apply all bt over info tasks\n\nCampaign catch (D1A-S3 deadlock, the fixture built to genuinely require\nlive attach; 3/3 transcript-verified): the skill claimed `info tasks`\nmaps the blocked Ada task to its component as THE hang answer, but on a\nreal Adamant Linux assembly `info tasks` returned only main_task /\n\"does not use any Ada tasks\" -- the per-component rate-group tasks do\nnot register with GNAT''s task table gdb reads. `thread apply all bt` is\nwhat actually revealed the suspended tasks. Guidance inverted: lead with\nthread apply all bt and map the parked thread to its component by the\nTick handler frame; info tasks demoted to unreliable-bonus. Also added\n(same practical session): finding the attach PID when the assembly runs\nbehind a launch wrapper ($!/bare pgrep grab the wrapper, not the ELF) --\nan agent burned ~5 attempts and once attached to the wrong process.\n\nSelector-routing shadow recurred once (1/3) despite a0b5a19 -- logged,\nbelow re-fix threshold. Fixture semi-opacity (both handshakes readable\ntogether => static-solvable) is a fixture refinement, not a skill gap.","tree":{"sha":"31cc0791ce6eae1924e5d5fb21544125e424d7fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/trees/31cc0791ce6eae1924e5d5fb21544125e424d7fa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/commits/8c8da90149a8fa869e3fe4124c21448c9fae9caf","verification":{"payload":"tree 31cc0791ce6eae1924e5d5fb21544125e424d7fa\nparent 5303d2758f1d04a40dbf1931dd9abbedee68951a\nauthor Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1783741703 -0600\ncommitter Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1785071950 -0600\n\nCorrect hung-task triage: thread apply all bt over info tasks\n\nCampaign catch (D1A-S3 deadlock, the fixture built to genuinely require\nlive attach; 3/3 transcript-verified): the skill claimed `info tasks`\nmaps the blocked Ada task to its component as THE hang answer, but on a\nreal Adamant Linux assembly `info tasks` returned only main_task /\n\"does not use any Ada tasks\" -- the per-component rate-group tasks do\nnot register with GNAT''s task table gdb reads. `thread apply all bt` is\nwhat actually revealed the suspended tasks. Guidance inverted: lead with\nthread apply all bt and map the parked thread to its component by the\nTick handler frame; info tasks demoted to unreliable-bonus. Also added\n(same practical session): finding the attach PID when the assembly runs\nbehind a launch wrapper ($!/bare pgrep grab the wrapper, not the ELF) --\nan agent burned ~5 attempts and once attached to the wrong process.\n\nSelector-routing shadow recurred once (1/3) despite a0b5a19 -- logged,\nbelow re-fix threshold. Fixture semi-opacity (both handshakes readable\ntogether => static-solvable) is a fixture refinement, not a skill gap.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEw4OO+fgBg9dPCrHf5dlyl7D/NcoFAmqTLY8ACgkQ5dlyl7D/\nNcrWNRAAxm0DinRKO14mBPliDsM7kTdqeAX5Oo0NqQvxzGyjXYYLNKX863xB7//o\n8FqICYU3mNfeidc7MF9iOa6Br2z2GU/4jPszf0HgvWUiaJUer47gwjXZxrloqwkF\nyH75tW50yhmnXOrhdBi428cpNMsl4UorM3/Qx1c4NfNSGBUmKupdD6w84yK8INW1\nYX6XZquPbEGnpl36zAtkdVKyx8cX76j6fXvOBjnk5GL2NsOdQmoWPYkFbGPDzgOz\nwQR7FtETVNJuQCGzx5Pup5Ruaon9TabLrCIgzCOuog2psLnUL95c5yl66i3yw1y2\nrMIJ47edHj0K1zQMXP6F5x5bSgeiY883vmrLkbYPsXfxTSfTzaCP4iC7N5HY4YUL\nVS3qVoZExlGE/qLtj6c8oElRFR9CUSPJMnXRAuNeV7RXanygo30KS3Az3nmjucQv\nP6azM5qOt6geJGrCIJ3Jcvo+ZCTPi+7IeB76N/QkEIFfAIy8/8V7mCQXRJeEJELa\nGV2f1wqo3CDgZ0ihvIAWkINPPxDxVfI64GJ7FNnnmAlL8TP6LF5eQzjH58gB3QlW\n5vNGmD7Rdoz9XMsNEa+Gw5+pt+5Yowi1nyVTJX1h/XwjmramtVE3ZqIbgxUdOOHl\nSVAeKEv/OGmcT+Fl34pgYMvLXA4ZItjvYHAO0OWzaJ+/yf1Qve0=\n=1Vex\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-29T19:09:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90524106?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jbsco","id":90524106,"login":"Jbsco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTI0MTA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lasp/adamant-skills/commit/8c8da90149a8fa869e3fe4124c21448c9fae9caf","node_id":"C_kwDOUHIrOdoAKDhjOGRhOTAxNDlhOGZhODY5ZTNmZTQxMjRjMjE0NDhjOWZhZTljYWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lasp/adamant-skills/commit/5303d2758f1d04a40dbf1931dd9abbedee68951a","sha":"5303d2758f1d04a40dbf1931dd9abbedee68951a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/5303d2758f1d04a40dbf1931dd9abbedee68951a"}],"sha":"8c8da90149a8fa869e3fe4124c21448c9fae9caf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/8c8da90149a8fa869e3fe4124c21448c9fae9caf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90524106?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jbsco","id":90524106,"login":"Jbsco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTI0MTA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/5303d2758f1d04a40dbf1931dd9abbedee68951a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-11T02:41:21Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T13:19:10Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"message":"Add general audit rules + a fault-injection campaign archetype\n\nFrom running the adamant-debugging validation campaign, critically\nfiltered for generality:\n\nGENERAL (all campaigns):\n- Behavioral DPs (skill loaded? tool run? in what order?) leave no file\n  artifact -- score them from the run transcript, not the agent summary,\n  which routinely claims steps the transcript does not show. Sharpens the\n  existing \"audit artifacts not self-report\" rule.\n- New Common Error: scoring a DP the scenario cannot exercise (faulting an\n  agent for skipping a technique the task never required). Fix the fixture\n  to earn the DP; the cheapest sufficient method is the right answer.\n\nSCOPED to diagnose/fix skills (a distinct archetype from build campaigns):\nnew \"Campaigning a diagnose/fix skill (fault injection)\" section --\ndeployed-system/no-archaeology framing (committed seeds are recoverable\nfrom git history), fixture opacity matched to the DP (source-visible bug\ntests reading, not the runtime tool), in-fiction commit messages AND\nbranch names, end-to-end fixture validation. Explicitly gated to\ndiagnose/fix skills, NOT presented as general build-campaign guidance.\n\nDebug-campaign-specific fixture doctrine and per-run tracking stay in the\ncampaign roadmap, not the skill.","tree":{"sha":"2fc20a8d674ac4c55c9aaf8d2c2f54eeef4c3867","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/trees/2fc20a8d674ac4c55c9aaf8d2c2f54eeef4c3867"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/commits/5303d2758f1d04a40dbf1931dd9abbedee68951a","verification":{"payload":"tree 2fc20a8d674ac4c55c9aaf8d2c2f54eeef4c3867\nparent e0cbb1114a4fd5039ac5ee4ad6ce38ab3f84fbe7\nauthor Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1783737681 -0600\ncommitter Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1785071950 -0600\n\nAdd general audit rules + a fault-injection campaign archetype\n\nFrom running the adamant-debugging validation campaign, critically\nfiltered for generality:\n\nGENERAL (all campaigns):\n- Behavioral DPs (skill loaded? tool run? in what order?) leave no file\n  artifact -- score them from the run transcript, not the agent summary,\n  which routinely claims steps the transcript does not show. Sharpens the\n  existing \"audit artifacts not self-report\" rule.\n- New Common Error: scoring a DP the scenario cannot exercise (faulting an\n  agent for skipping a technique the task never required). Fix the fixture\n  to earn the DP; the cheapest sufficient method is the right answer.\n\nSCOPED to diagnose/fix skills (a distinct archetype from build campaigns):\nnew \"Campaigning a diagnose/fix skill (fault injection)\" section --\ndeployed-system/no-archaeology framing (committed seeds are recoverable\nfrom git history), fixture opacity matched to the DP (source-visible bug\ntests reading, not the runtime tool), in-fiction commit messages AND\nbranch names, end-to-end fixture validation. Explicitly gated to\ndiagnose/fix skills, NOT presented as general build-campaign guidance.\n\nDebug-campaign-specific fixture doctrine and per-run tracking stay in the\ncampaign roadmap, not the skill.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEw4OO+fgBg9dPCrHf5dlyl7D/NcoFAmqTLY8ACgkQ5dlyl7D/\nNcrGXw/8D8B5gBre329BES9J5Hi2MmHTNMUUhEhwu1oZXVpxtX/wJ+CpoeY