url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/e0cbb1114a4fd5039ac5ee4ad6ce38ab3f84fbe7"}],"sha":"5303d2758f1d04a40dbf1931dd9abbedee68951a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/5303d2758f1d04a40dbf1931dd9abbedee68951a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90524106?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jbsco","id":90524106,"login":"Jbsco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTI0MTA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/e0cbb1114a4fd5039ac5ee4ad6ce38ab3f84fbe7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T23:56:29Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T13:19:10Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"message":"Route hung-task/advanced scenarios to the reference explicitly\n\nCampaign catch at 3-mention threshold (D1A-S2 i1/i2/i3, all clean but\nrecurring): agents ran generic thread backtraces and NEVER read\nreferences/gdb-advanced-inspection.md, even on the fixture built to\nrequire it -- so they missed info tasks (the Ada task -> Adamant\ncomponent-instance mapping that is the actual answer for a hang) and\nmapped via assembly YAML instead. Two edits: (1) SKILL.md checklist\nitem 3 now names the trigger conditions (hung/parked task, mystery\nwrite, packed mismatch) and says READ the reference, not improvise;\n(2) the reference elevates `info tasks` to the first move for a hang,\nwith thread apply all bt as fallback. Behavior was already correct\n(3/3 PASS post routing-fix); this converts \"got the answer via generic\ngdb\" into \"used the Ada-aware move the skill prescribes.\"","tree":{"sha":"fdedac0cbff3061ff8c2c270b4d6bc4e33b8ec85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/trees/fdedac0cbff3061ff8c2c270b4d6bc4e33b8ec85"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/commits/e0cbb1114a4fd5039ac5ee4ad6ce38ab3f84fbe7","verification":{"payload":"tree fdedac0cbff3061ff8c2c270b4d6bc4e33b8ec85\nparent 1bd3f1cb1e973b80e9262478a9b72887b25c0141\nauthor Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1783727789 -0600\ncommitter Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1785071950 -0600\n\nRoute hung-task/advanced scenarios to the reference explicitly\n\nCampaign catch at 3-mention threshold (D1A-S2 i1/i2/i3, all clean but\nrecurring): agents ran generic thread backtraces and NEVER read\nreferences/gdb-advanced-inspection.md, even on the fixture built to\nrequire it -- so they missed info tasks (the Ada task -> Adamant\ncomponent-instance mapping that is the actual answer for a hang) and\nmapped via assembly YAML instead. Two edits: (1) SKILL.md checklist\nitem 3 now names the trigger conditions (hung/parked task, mystery\nwrite, packed mismatch) and says READ the reference, not improvise;\n(2) the reference elevates `info tasks` to the first move for a hang,\nwith thread apply all bt as fallback. Behavior was already correct\n(3/3 PASS post routing-fix); this converts \"got the answer via generic\ngdb\" into \"used the Ada-aware move the skill prescribes.\"\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEw4OO+fgBg9dPCrHf5dlyl7