A2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/934d53fc6391fd0bbbec79cd4b03177be5ff8899/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T21:12:16Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T13:19:09Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"message":"Add OpenOCD/Debug Probe variant to the JTAG section\n\nadamant_example (open source) documents a complete OpenOCD + Raspberry\nPi Debug Probe flow for its Pico assembly -- citable verbatim, unlike\nthe closed-project J-Link scripts. The JTAG section now distinguishes\nthe two server variants by their differing monitor bring-up syntax\n(OpenOCD ''reset init'' vs J-Link ''reset''+''halt''), cites the example''s\ndebug.sh/config.gdb/program.sh as the discoverable open reference, adds\nthe one-shot program-verify-reset-exit flash command, and notes the\nserial/UART cable as capture path vs debug transport. Orthogonal to the\nD1A decision points under active convergence testing (touches only the\ncross-target section).","tree":{"sha":"0c6de44676e3d47edd88a63b13d909f29e62e738","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/trees/0c6de44676e3d47edd88a63b13d909f29e62e738"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/commits/934d53fc6391fd0bbbec79cd4b03177be5ff8899","verification":{"payload":"tree 0c6de44676e3d47edd88a63b13d909f29e62e738\nparent bd4d8c5c87e33394021c4578b0896099c13d59a5\nauthor Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.n