acob Seman"},"message":"Add advanced GDB inspection reference to adamant-debugging\n\nreferences/gdb-advanced-inspection.md: the beyond-breakpoints layer,\neach pattern carrying its Ada/GNAT/Adamant-specific wrinkle (the part\ngeneric GDB knowledge gets wrong): watchpoints incl. -l location\nwatching and the hardware-budget/Renode-slowness rules; Ravenscar task\ntriage (info tasks maps blocked tasks to Adamant component instance\nnames; live attach without restart); packed-record logical view vs\nx/xb wire view as a serialization-defect localizer; type overlays on\nraw memory; conditional/scripted stops with Ada expressions; signals\nvs cross-target traps (catch signal fires before catch exception;\nRenode traps vector, not signal); generate-core-file as the Linux\nanalogue of the LCH NV dump; Renode monitor passthrough + halted-time\nwatchdog note vs real hardware. SKILL.md: reference pointer + checklist\nescalation line. Counts 682 -> updated.\n\nCampaign context: content lands ahead of campaign tier D1A which will\nstress these patterns with fixtures unsolvable by breakpoints alone\n(mystery-write watchpoint scenario, hung-task triage, packed-layout\nmismatch).","tree":{"sha":"8f6b8dd39305f69a353bd174320434bdbee48555","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/trees/8f6b8dd39305f69a353bd174320434bdbee48555"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/commits/8592fe477828ef468f5af078b6871beb318fee71","verification":{"payload":"tree 8f6b8dd39305f69a353bd174320434bdbee48555\nparent 5e0312ba5aa54bf026bfbd6d96da45f505d60864\nauthor Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1783715704 -0600\ncommitter Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1785071949 -0600\n\nAdd advanced GDB inspection reference to adamant-debugging\n\nreferences/gdb-advanced-inspection.md: the beyond-breakpoints layer,\neach pattern carrying its Ada/GNAT/Adamant-specific wrinkle (the part\ngeneric GDB knowledge gets wrong): watchpoints incl. -l location\nwatching and the hardware-budget/Renode-slowness rules; Ravenscar task\ntriage (info tasks maps blocked tasks to Adamant component instance\nnames; live attach without restart); packed-record logical view vs\nx/xb wire view as a serialization-defect localizer; type overlays on\nraw memory; conditional/scripted stops with Ada expressions; signals\nvs cross-target traps (catch signal fires before catch exception;\nRenode traps vector, not signal); generate-core-file as the Linux\nanalogue of the LCH NV dump; Renode monitor passthrough + halted-time\nwatchdog note vs real hardware. SKILL.md: reference pointer + checklist\nescalation line. Counts 682 -> updated.\n\nCampaign context: content lands ahead of campaign tier D1A which will\nstress these patterns with fixtures unsolvable by breakpoints alone\n(mystery-write watchpoint scenario, hung-task triage, packed-layout\nmismatch).\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEw4OO+fgBg9dPCrHf5dlyl7D/NcoFAmqTLY4ACgkQ5dlyl7D/\nNcpZ+Q/+JN6af9eNQ3qE03G5n/nAHEKL4+TsdbRRiOCUutrHiiTXPg6cwegqk3K+\nLr4S3qMAGvSdeIm3kfqGEkxxEgO4HbqbF/UEk8ATOY7cLSDre/4rL2llMpBXhuRi\nF1FKN6f4gsJaJc1VkvTgtdfS/38plRndZjwGWulDHxOEdRuf+xkcR9b3jHApwzES\nTcjy7vrg8lbV1YV7eitume8+CqrpmDlIeHJFVEYXd62sbU7hD3gPCJ2jth4S0h2I\nGYR+xsZVqfvIkaU4YX6WOGh9YhJvEY0EKC5+AveNySwHPtSo15HMJfwWuMhUcEP3\naHUq1J28FrfXujwQl6g8p6uhZoR03zLF6Sv/2xx7IjibT+z+VXheOxQGJR9HrgtT\nDFLq7SiZZJwqUMWT7wQB3uBbDBFKOIWPaL7+zM4Bd5tcRhCHpN1gOEMXrauDCwVv\n0+QV1n+CZRQ2P8U+3oChv0qjGUfQ+JcGvWFzJRxELb2Wu08ok/F2ZysVXCoshIX2\nKit657Ij+cRjtvQ6iyUIpQXWKjut28gk+oT04goW6PowBkgESLiaQZMyCcuYXIEQ\nmNW5jX57QhDKN8rp9X9mnwarN12wMuBQx+6lqajghqrQ2mps3WH49fe/EiGsmGlj\npUux/SxX/dj5qGv48YkkYCipNAtIne6kMPQGKpHg+uEPq0Q57IE=\n=JB4q\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-29T19:09:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90524106?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jbsco","id":90524106,"login":"Jbsco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTI0MTA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lasp/adamant-skills/commit/8592fe477828ef468f5af078b6871beb318fee71","node_id":"C_kwDOUHIrOdoAKDg1OTJmZTQ3NzgyOGVmNDY4ZjVhZjA3OGI2ODcxYmViMzE4ZmVlNzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lasp/adamant-skills/commit/5e0312ba5aa54bf026bfbd6d96da45f505d60864","sha":"5e0312ba5aa54bf026bfbd6d96da45f505d60864","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/5e0312ba5aa54bf026bfbd6d96da45f505d60864"}],"sha":"8592fe477828ef468f5af078b6871beb318fee71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/8592fe477828ef468f5af078b6871beb318fee71"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90524106?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jbsco","id":90524106,"login":"Jbsco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTI0MTA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/5e0312ba5aa54bf026bfbd6d96da45f505d60864/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T19:17:45Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T13:19:09Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"message":"Expand adamant-debugging to three layers with references and a symbolizer\n\nScope grows from GDB-only to the three levels a debugging agent actually\nmeets, sourced from a 4-searcher sweep of ~/cs reports, the lasp-design\nLogseq graph, cross-project session memories, and the framework +\nproject tooling inventories:\n\n- SKILL.md (249 lines): adds post-mortem/LCH layer (framework fault\n  components table: zero_divider, last_chance_manager, stack/cpu/queue\n  monitors, memory_dumper, logger + gnd/bin decoders -- all open-source\n  framework content), target/compiler layer pointer, project-tooling\n  discovery pattern (closed-source helpers referenced generically as\n  \"look in gnd/bin\"), 4 new Common Errors (same-build symbol rule,\n  hang-is-a-crash, one-frame interrupt traces, never-disable-assertions).\n- references/post-mortem-and-lch.md (192): LCH anatomy raise->telemetry,\n  4 capture paths incl. batch-gdb attach to the spinning target, generic\n  nm/addr2line symbolization + same-build rule, interrupt-context trap\n  recovery (paused start + hbreak), RISC-V trap-register decoding table,\n  proven crash root-cause checklist (unseeded dependencies first,\n  systemic assert-grep, tick-disconnect binary search), suite sentinel\n  strings, post-mortem event-log decode via framework gnd/bin.\n- references/target-pitfalls.md (130): erroneous-execution families\n  (alignment overlays, SSO codegen) with transferable proof techniques\n  (bit-pattern analysis, disassembly at faulting PC), workaround-pinning\n  rule, post-rebase stale-codegen signature table, runtime debug-variant\n  builds, bare-board unstaged-parameter flake, monitor-component-first\n  resource debugging.\n- scripts/symbolize_traceback.py (111, stdlib-only, clean-room):\n  addresses (argv/stdin, hex/decimal, pasted trace text) -> nearest\n  symbol via nm dump bisect and/or file:line via addr2line. All three\n  modes verified against a real test binary (exact offsets, correct\n  file:line resolution).\n\nDisclosure rule applied throughout: adamant/adamant_example content is\nnamed and detailed; closed-project tooling appears only as generic\ndiscovery patterns and technique descriptions.\n\nSelector entry and combinations rows widened; index counts refreshed\n(232 -> 682 lines).","tree":{"sha":"26a4a05e41b93766adbac2201abd84afa934e730","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/trees/26a4a05e41b93766adbac2201abd84afa934e730"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/commits/5e0312ba5aa54bf026bfbd6d96da45f505d60864","verification":{"payload":"tree 26a4a05e41b93766adbac2201abd84afa934e730\nparent 8eec235d9ac8e0bbd09264eef85efd4d8763eb07\nauthor Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1783711065 -0600\ncommitter Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1785071949 -0600\n\nExpand adamant-debugging to three layers with references and a symbolizer\n\nScope grows from GDB-only to the three levels a debugging agent actually\nmeets, sourced from a 4-searcher sweep of ~/cs reports, the lasp-design\nLogseq graph, cross-project session memories, and the framework +\nproject tooling inventories:\n\n- SKILL.md (249 lines): adds post-mortem/LCH layer (framework fault\n  components table: zero_divider, last_chance_manager, stack/cpu/queue\n  monitors, memory_dumper, logger + gnd/bin decoders -- all open-source\n  framework content), target/compiler layer pointer, project-tooling\n  discovery pattern (closed-source helpers referenced generically as\n  \"look in gnd/bin\"), 4 new Common Errors (same-build symbol rule,\n  hang-is-a-crash, one-frame interrupt traces, never-disable-assertions).\n- references/post-mortem-and-lch.md (192): LCH anatomy raise->telemetry,\n  4 capture paths incl. batch-gdb attach to the spinning target, generic\n  nm/addr2line symbolization + same-build rule, interrupt-context trap\n  recovery (paused start + hbreak), RISC-V trap-register decoding table,\n  proven crash root-cause checklist (unseeded dependencies first,\n  systemic assert-grep, tick-disconnect binary search), suite sentinel\n  strings, post-mortem event-log decode via framework gnd/bin.\n- references/target-pitfalls.md (130): erroneous-execution families\n  (alignment overlays, SSO codegen) with transferable proof techniques\n  (bit-pattern analysis, disassembly at faulting PC), workaround-pinning\n  rule, post-rebase stale-codegen signature table, runtime debug-variant\n  builds, bare-board unstaged-parameter flake, monitor-component-first\n  resource debugging.\n- scripts/symbolize_traceback.py (111, stdlib-only, clean-room):\n  addresses (argv/stdin, hex/decimal, pasted trace text) -> nearest\n  symbol via nm dump bisect and/or file:line via addr2line. All three\n  modes verified against a real test binary (exact offsets, correct\n  file:line resolution).\n\nDisclosure rule applied throughout: adamant/adamant_example content is\nnamed and detailed; closed-project tooling appears only as generic\ndiscovery patterns and technique descriptions.\n\nSelector entry and combinations rows widened; index counts refreshed\n(232 -> 682 lines).\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEw4OO+fgBg9dPCrHf5dlyl7D/NcoFAmqTLY4ACgkQ5dlyl7D/\nNcryYw//R60KSw6A60fHwdrn9E+mZS4RfEzerhKRuSHV+S9drXxyirs/fw4Ip9Ow\n2AbqNLke3k