s/Jbsco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/commits/8e1e0cde9a97292c2251ed4fc389f17836a9b590/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T16:58:55Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-24T19:57:40Z","email":"90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jacob Seman"},"message":"Apply audit fixes: accuracy, convention, and enforcement corrections\n\nFixes the A (accuracy), B (repo-convention), and C (enforcement) findings\nfrom the skill audit, incorporating the validation round against real\ngenerated plugin dictionaries, OpenC3 7.2.0 source, and the framework.\n\nAccuracy:\n- Group setup/teardown comments: run ONCE per group, not per test\n  (OpenC3 suite.py Group.run()).\n- CCSDS items: removed the false \"COSMOS auto-exposes CCSDS_SEQ_COUNT/...\"\n  claim; header items are dictionary-defined (framework emits field-named\n  items; naming layers may rename, e.g. Primary_Header_sequence_count).\n  Copy-ready snippets now use a <Seq_Count_Item> placeholder (documented in\n  the placeholder list) and RECEIVED_COUNT (genuinely COSMOS-derived) for\n  first contact.\n- Event-capture snippet: bind the module-level event-id import to a local\n  before check_expression(..., locals()) -- locals() cannot see module-level\n  names (was a NameError as written).\n- Scoped the \"standing contracts\": command-response is every-project; CCSDS\n  framing applies to projects using the framework packetizer/depacketizer,\n  with the XOR-8 command checksum (seed 0xFF, write-protocol-computed) and\n  telemetry-only CRC-16 trailer stated precisely.\n- Corrected the check-API rationale (bare asserts DO reach the report via\n  the runner''s exception handling; the real reasons are formatted context\n  and disconnect-mode behavior) and the wait* return-value claim (plain\n  wait returns elapsed time, not a bool).\n- Naming-transform text no longer asserts lowercased/dashed as the rule;\n  the join/case is naming-layer-dependent and the dictionary is\n  authoritative.\n\nConventions:\n- Removed project-specific leakage: \"(softsim-style)\", the unexplained \"IR\"\n  abbreviation, gnd/cosmos/<TARGET> asserted as universal (now introduced\n  once as \"commonly ...; confirm against the project tree\"), and verbatim\n  project helper names (sim_util/wait_check_st/... -> neutral descriptive\n  names).\n- Grounded \"the generated dictionary\" in cmd.txt/tlm.txt at first mention;\n  reworded the renamed suite-results cross-references to the stream +\n  exit-code framing; paired the counter-delta imperative with its reason.\n\nEnforcement:\n- Hook wiring now uses ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR} (a cwd-relative path that\n  fails to resolve exits 2 == BLOCK, wedging every matched tool call).\n- Deny-rule anchors corrected: /**-anchored rules are project-root-relative,\n  not filesystem-wide; scoping note rewritten (other mounts need their own\n  // or ~/ rules); Edit/Write rows now cover all nine extensions.\n- Exit-code contract stated precisely (exit 2 is the only blocking code;\n  fail-closed hardening must exit 2, not 1).\n- Layer-1 gap description updated to current Claude Code semantics (deny\n  rules also cover Grep/Glob and recognized Bash file commands; the residual\n  is arbitrary subprocesses and unrecognized shapes).\n- Residual gaps disclosed honestly (recursive grep, shell globs, git\n  history, Grep content-mode; over-broad Bash matching) with by-design\n  pass-through examples in the verify list; threat model stated once\n  (reflexive access, not determined exfiltration; sandboxing for hard\n  boundaries); Layer 2 retitled.\n- Hook: NotebookEdit added to the documented matcher; Grep brace/class\n  globs (*.{adb,ads}, *.[ch], *.ad[bs]) expanded and blocked; REASON says\n  \"names a source file\" (accurate for prose/incidental matches).\n\nHook behavior validated by execution: 14-case battery (block/allow/residual\n/fail-open) all passing.","tree":{"sha":"5720684d4857b0d959f12e91093e25cfac5c6a72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/trees/5720684d4857b0d959f12e91093e25cfac5c6a72"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasp/adamant-skills/git/commits/8e1e0cde9a97292c2251ed4fc389f17836a9b590","verification":{"payload":"tree 5720684d4857b0d959f12e91093e25cfac5c6a72\nparent 39c2b986fc39d8d89ece4a8dde836f446c5fce32\nauthor Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1783011535 -0600\ncommitter Jacob Seman <90524106+Jbsco@users.noreply.github.com> 1784923060 -0600\n\nApply audit fixes: accuracy, convention, and enforcement corrections\n\nFixes the A (accuracy), B (repo-convention), and C (enforcement) findings\nfrom the skill audit, incorporating the validation round against real\ngenerated plugin dictionaries, OpenC3 7.2.0 source, and the framework.\n\nAccuracy:\n- Group setup/teardown comments: run ONCE per group, not per test\n  (OpenC3 suite.py Group.run()).\n- CCSDS items: removed the false \"COSMOS auto-exposes CCSDS_SEQ_COUNT/...\"\n  claim; header items are dictionary-defined (framework emits field-named\n  items; naming layers may rename, e.g. Primary_Header_sequence_count).\n  Copy-ready snippets now use a <Seq_Count_Item> placeholder (documented in\n  the placeholder list) and RECEIVED_COUNT (genuinely COSMOS-derived) for\n  first contact.\n- Event-capture snippet: bind the module-level event-id import to a local\n  before check_expression(..., locals()) -- locals() cannot see module-level\n  names (was a NameError as written).\n- Scoped the \"standing contracts\": command-response is every-project; CCSDS\n  framing applies to projects using the framework packetizer/depacketizer,\n  with the XOR-8 command checksum (seed 0xFF, write-protocol-computed) and\n  telemetry-only CRC-16 trailer stated precisely.\n- Corrected the check-API rationale (bare asserts DO reach the report via\n  the runner''s exception handling; the real reasons are formatted context\n  and disconnect-mode behavior) and the wait* return-value claim (plain\n  wait returns elapsed time, not a bool).\n- Naming-transform text no longer asserts lowercased/dashed as the rule;\n  the join/case is naming-layer-dependent and the dictionary is\n  authoritative.\n\nConventions:\n- Removed project-specific leakage: \"(softsim-style)\", the unexplained \"IR\"\n  abbreviation, gnd/cosmos/<TARGET> asserted as universal (now introduced\n  once as \"commonly ...; confirm against the project tree\"), and verbatim\n  project helper names (sim_util/wait_check_st/... -> neutral descriptive\n  names).\n- Grounded \"the generated dictionary\" in cmd.txt/tlm.txt at first mention;\n  reworded the renamed suite-results cross-references to the stream +\n  exit-code framing; paired the counter-delta imperative with its reason.\n\nEnforcement:\n- Hook wiring now uses ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR} (a cwd-relative path that\n  fails to resolve exits 2 == BLOCK, wedging every matched tool call).\n- Deny-rule anchors corrected: /**-anchored rules are project-root-relative,\n  not filesystem-wide; scoping note rewritten (other mounts need their own\n  // or ~/ rules); Edit/Write rows now cover all nine extensions.\n- Exit-code contract stated precisely (exit 2 is the only blocking code;\n  fail-closed hardening must exit 2, not 1).\n- Layer-1 gap description updated to current Claude Code semantics (deny\n  rules also cover Grep/Glob and recognized Bash file commands; the residual\n  is arbitrary subprocesses and unrecognized shapes).\n- Residual gaps disclosed honestly (recursive grep, shell globs, git\n  history, Grep content-mode; over-broad Bash matching) with by-design\n  pass-through examples in the verify list; threat model stated once\n  (reflexive access, not determined exfiltration; sandboxing for hard\n  boundaries); Layer 2 retitled.\n- Hook: NotebookEdit added to the documented matcher; Grep brace/class\n  globs (*.{adb,ads}, *.[ch], *.ad[bs]) expanded and blocked; REASON says\n  \"names a source file\" (accurate for prose/incidental matches).\n\nHook behavior validated by execution: 14-case battery (block/allow/residual\n/fail-open) all passing.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEw4OO+fgBg9dPCrHf5dlyl7D/NcoFAmqTLY0ACgkQ5dlyl7D/\nNcpovA/+N5nTDl4ln1GCT9SNItdmkYg+7NwasEBMhcrFJmYegTxqrsFyf4tXLvDN\nYCUZYQ+CihbGLLdXpp2fB9cUooBHhAOGQJ4+lG8H+m6QHIsaaKCMSWz5sJpUgogU\nPnnItgPwDbnPNDdvciE2tg9+MTlc4NWHh1BU8PR5hY5/FO/yVfcgX8a4RcDQmcj2\nV5CQmDtxPu1v6k/QnqSLI/bATuFjaBCr8QtSpScVqF0cKMuXhCnYTsvOlcWWP2AG\ngtpjlD1etV6BIoY2u9xEKc9axGLIvbv9mSLScSItlOs02ak24m6PY/Y1s8EVyQFy\n8CWx9pYYXQXHUJyPsqcQTsnijSNB8QgL3RfOQJh6UPJn9Foi5ky6qfiLZ+/NmTiQ\nVISQLhyvLtrKoMEISMwwPt5CvjnzjBJ4pApfbv1JvIflNaUulDvv51aNc/0X3fxT\nmZGT5IpaU7EHS7BrqBFefMVR/L0eemfT0Ar5B5bJjgQo9uzz7LBkFn/tG2iIfTCz\naLqYYWEF3YXiMsVwvJNT5HrhBU7D2ngomg85sbIe1pMNXoSx0IqfD7pNE1dk9Frh\nDshlooyhESwrWafqAb7K9P5dQDflUhcFlqqB/0/6ovbkPvnNaSk8uwKwLKdjYVIB\nyfp36FEMMuaHhp9KvnFxj5OAywRXlblr78uzX0sgIpEMFB96PX8=\n=Vy6L\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-29T19:09:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90524106?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jbsco","id":90524106,"login":"Jbsco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTI0MTA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jbsco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/us