 Forms submissions at /api/form-submit\n\nOptimizely Forms stores nothing — SubmitUrl is authored and the endpoint\nbehind it is ours. Adds a KV-backed store and a public receiver with body,\nfield and per-IP rate caps, and corrects the FormWrapper error text that\nclaimed the CMS mints the endpoint.","tree":{"sha":"d4d08c513263d5b01a349257069d233bde40e9be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/d4d08c513263d5b01a349257069d233bde40e9be"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/ca81aaac3774b2a00668e4fd7d44b921bd4ddde2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/ca81aaac3774b2a00668e4fd7d44b921bd4ddde2","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKGNhODFhYWFjMzc3NGIyYTAwNjY4ZTRmZDdkNDRiOTIxYmQ0ZGRkZTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/a5247d47e518a5a60c0d0e0c2590a754e650a2a1","sha":"a5247d47e518a5a60c0d0e0c2590a754e650a2a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/a5247d47e518a5a60c0d0e0c2590a754e650a2a1"}],"sha":"ca81aaac3774b2a00668e4fd7d44b921bd4ddde2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/ca81aaac3774b2a00668e4fd7d44b921bd4ddde2"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/a5247d47e518a5a60c0d0e0c2590a754e650a2a1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T06:37:24Z","email":"mdtarek.rahman@optimizely.com","name":"Md Tarek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T06:37:24Z","email":"mdtarek.rahman@optimizely.com","name":"Md Tarek"},"message":"docs: how a form container is referenced from an experience, and the nested POST /v1/content shape","tree":{"sha":"f885096ae94ada08fa08958a84ba2ab3a4913194","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/f885096ae94ada08fa08958a84ba2ab3a4913194"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/a5247d47e518a5a60c0d0e0c2590a754e650a2a1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/a5247d47e518a5a60c0d0e0c2590a754e650a2a1","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKGE1MjQ3ZDQ3ZTUxOGE1YTYwYzBkMGUwYzI1OTBhNzU0ZTY1MGEyYTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/aa00c0514ceacdec37c8cdd0dbe1adb115c5e3f8","sha":"aa00c0514ceacdec37c8cdd0dbe1adb115c5e3f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/aa00c0514ceacdec37c8cdd0dbe1adb115c5e3f8"}],"sha":"a5247d47e518a5a60c0d0e0c2590a754e650a2a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/a5247d47e518a5a60c0d0e0c2590a754e650a2a1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/aa00c0514ceacdec37c8cdd0dbe1adb115c5e3f8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T06:17:33Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T06:17:33Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"feat(forms): reference the form container from /contact over REST\n\nIt can be done, and the CMS says how if you read the right error. Embedding\nthe form inline gets:\n\n    A section with layout type ''form'' cannot be embedded in an experience,\n    it must be referenced.\n\nA reference is a COMPONENT node carrying the form''s dashed guid and its content\ntype, with no inner nodes:\n\n    { \"nodeType\": \"component\",\n      \"id\": \"f408a2d2-f3c7-45fe-85e7-8416d3c66344\",\n      \"component\": { \"contentType\": \"OptiFormsContainerData\" } }\n\nNot `nodeType: \"section\"`, even though the form''s own root node is a section —\nthe API infers any node with an `id` to be a component and rejects the rest\nwith \"is of type ''component'' but does not have the required ''component''\nproperty\". Six plausible field names (reference, contentReference, contentLink,\nlink, sharedContent, referenceKey) are all rejected with \"does not exist on\ntype ''CompositionNode''\", which turns out to be a fast way to probe what the\nschema accepts.\n\n/contact now carries the form between the title and the emergency callout, and\nis published. Written up in Optimizely.md so the next person does not spend an\nafternoon on it.","tree":{"sha":"5052e90c7e94f24c6623b96887665235cee585a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/5052e90c7e94f24c6623b96887665235cee585a9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/aa00c0514ceacdec37c8cdd0dbe1adb115c5e3f8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/aa00c0514ceacdec37c8cdd0dbe1adb115c5e3f8","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKGFhMDBjMDUxNGNlYWNkZWMzN2M4Y2RkMGRiZTFhZGIxMTVjNWUzZjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/f3bb6267f2db39ce5bcb3383b18711d7954f64d4","sha":"f3bb6267f2db39ce5bcb3383b18711d7954f64d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/f3bb6267f2db39ce5bcb3383b18711d7954f64d4"}],"sha":"aa00c0514ceacdec37c8cdd0dbe1adb115c5e3f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/aa00c0514ceacdec37c8cdd0dbe1adb115c5e3f8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/f3bb6267f2db39ce5bcb3383b18711d7954f64d4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T05:57:10Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T05:57:10Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"feat(forms): render Optimizely Forms — verified query, real field names\n\nGraph finished indexing, all twelve OptiForms types check out against the live\nschema, and the gate is open locally.\n\nThe container adapter was rewritten because the old one could not have worked.\nIt asked Graph for SingleChoice, Step, Feed and a Validators on the range\nelement — five fields that do not exist on this instance, so the query would\nhave 400''d — and read elements from `composition.grids`, which is not the shape\nGraph returns. Every field in the new query was checked against the schema, and\nthe walk matches what a real form returns: composition → step → row → column →\ncomponent. `step`, not `section`.\n\nThe seven input adapters now submit under SubmissionFieldName. They were using\nthe content key, which would have posted a GUID as the field name.\n\nFormWrapper no longer reports success when there is no SubmitUrl. It used to\nskip the fetch and set ''submitted'', telling a visitor their message was\nreceived when nothing was sent. It now fails visibly and logs what to do.\n\n/contact was left broken by the previous commit — its composition still named\nOT_ContactForm, which that commit deleted from the registry. The section is\nremoved, so the page renders again: title, emergency callout, other ways to\nreach us.\n\nEverything learned by trying is in Optimizely.md, including the two things REST\nwould not do: persist Validators, and reference a form container from an\nexperience. Both want the CMS UI, which is also the documented flow.","tree":{"sha":"2eb78cdf339a62cf928cb9f7444f29c708a095dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/2eb78cdf339a62cf928cb9f7444f29c708a095dd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/f3bb6267f2db39ce5bcb3383b18711d7954f64d4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/f3bb6267f2db39ce5bcb3383b18711d7954f64d4","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKGYzYmI2MjY3ZjJkYjM5Y2U1YmNiMzM4M2IxODcxMWQ3OTU0ZjY0ZDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/be8ef7c48f2207c2faf19eb3a7fbd846ade25244","sha":"be8ef7c48f2207c2faf19eb3a7fbd846ade25244","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/be8ef7c48f2207c2faf19eb3a7fbd846ade25244"}],"sha":"f3bb6267f2db39ce5bcb3383b18711d7954f64d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/f3bb6267f2db39ce5bcb3383b18711d7954f64d4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/be8ef7c48f2207c2faf19eb3a7fbd846ade25244/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T05:04:34Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T05:04:34Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"refactor(forms): drop the custom contact form, match OptiForms to the live schema\n\nForms has been activated on the instance — 85 content types became 98, and the\ntwelve OptiForms* types arrived with source: _server. So the hand-built\ncontact form is the wrong answer now, and it is gone: the block, the content\ntype, /api/contact, the KV store, the admin view, the showcase entry.\n\nWhat replaces it is the CMS''s own Forms, which needs the repo''s twelve type\ndefinitions to be RIGHT before the gate opens. They were not:\n\n  - SubmissionFieldName was missing from all seven input elements. That field\n    is the key each answer arrives under; without it the generated query never\n    asks for it and the only way to identify a field is its Label, which\n    breaks the moment an editor rewords it.\n  - OptiFormsDependencyRule was missing AfterStep, JumpToStep and TargetStep.\n  - OptiFormsContainerData declared no compositionBehaviors; the server says\n    sectionEnabled.\n\nAll twelve are now generated from GET /v1/contenttypes, with one divergence\nwritten into every file rather than hidden: the server declares\n`formsElementEnabled`, these say `elementEnabled`, because cms-sdk 2.2.0\npredates Forms and its union has only two members. The value has one job here\n— a non-empty list is what makes the SDK emit an _IComponent fragment — and\nwhere an editor may place an element is decided by the CMS from its own value.\n\nVerified every declared field against the live Graph schema before touching\nthe gate, because this is the change that took the whole site down last time.\nEleven of twelve are clean. OptiFormsContainerData is not in Graph yet, which\nis why the gate stays SHUT in this commit.\n\nTwo things learned by trying, both worth writing down:\n  - A form container can be created over REST, composition and all —\n    layoutType \"form\", then step > row > column > element, not section.\n  - A validator is { name, message }. { type, message } is rejected with\n    ''Error message of \"\" is required'', which names the element''s Label rather\n    than the field, so it reads like a missing label.","tree":{"sha":"3a162dfa82438a16ad8b03267408ca6b1bd371b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/3a162dfa82438a16ad8b03267408ca6b1bd371b7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/be8ef7c48f2207c2faf19eb3a7fbd846ade25244","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/be8ef7c48f2207c2faf19eb3a7fbd846ade25244","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKGJlOGVmN2M0OGYyMjA3YzJmYWYxOWViM2E3ZmJkODQ2YWRlMjUyNDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/7790697405c19b8e36f20224477a10ec7512394d","sha":"7790697405c19b8e36f20224477a10ec7512394d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/7790697405c19b8e36f20224477a10ec7512394d"}],"sha":"be8ef7c48f2207c2faf19eb3a7fbd846ade25244","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/be8ef7c48f2207c2faf19eb3a7fbd846ade25244"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/7790697405c19b8e36f20224477a10ec7512394d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T04:47:34Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T04:47:34Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"feat(contact): a working contact form, and the page at /contact\n\nThis instance has no Optimizely Forms. Checked rather than assumed: of 85\ncontent types and the whole Graph schema, nothing Forms-related exists — the\nonly match for \"Form\" is this repo''s own OT_QuoteForm. The twelve OptiForms*\ntypes here stay gated and unpushed; enabling them without the add-on fails\nevery page query.\n\nSo the form is ours.\n\n  cms/content-types/OT_ContactForm.ts   labels are CMS properties\n  components/blocks/ContactForm.tsx     a real <form>, four fixed fields\n  app/api/contact/route.ts              validation, rate limit, storage\n  lib/contactStore.ts                   KV, thirty-day expiry\n  app/opti-admin/(dashboard)/contact    where messages are read\n\nAn editor changes what the form SAYS, not what it collects. The fields are\nfixed in the component, so the endpoint knows exactly what arrives, and no\neditor can add a field that quietly starts collecting a personal number into a\nstore never designed to hold one. Less flexible than Optimizely Forms, and\nmuch harder to misuse.\n\nBecause this holds personal data it is built to hold as little as possible:\neverything expires after thirty days, enforced by the store rather than by\nanyone remembering; the IP is never stored, only a salted hash, and only to\nrate-limit; field values are never logged, only counts and outcomes; nothing\nis written into the content tree, because content is published and a\nstranger''s message is not content. The message renders as text in the admin\nview, never as markup. A honeypot answers 200 so a bot learns nothing.\n\nThe rate limiter fails OPEN — a contact form that stops accepting messages\nbecause a cache blinked is worse than one that briefly accepts too many, and\nthe cap is about abuse, not security.\n\nTwo things learned getting the content type in, both now in Optimizely.md:\n`yarn cms:push` is blocked on this instance but POST /v1/contenttypes is not,\nand the property field is `isLocalized`, not `localized`.\n\nPage created and published under Root as /contact — title, form, an emergency\ncallout telling people NOT to use the form for an accident in progress, and\nthe other ways to reach us. Showcase demo and nav entry ship with it, as\nCLAUDE.md requires. Coverage stays at 100%: all nine label properties carry\ndata-epi-edit.\n\ntsc and eslint clean. NOT exercised end to end — the sandbox cannot reach the\ndeployment, so the submit path needs a real POST after deploy.","tree":{"sha":"7d1d8e92e0ba8cf685fa8a0235c1d2576dcd33e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/7d1d8e92e0ba8cf685fa8a0235c1d2576dcd33e9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/7790697405c19b8e36f20224477a10ec7512394d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/7790697405c19b8e36f20224477a10ec7512394d","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKDc3OTA2OTc0MDVjMTliOGUzNmYyMDIyNDQ3N2ExMGVjNzUxMjM5NGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/75e8734906d15a63f097a0d89fb1ba3a2881b62d","sha":"75e8734906d15a63f097a0d89fb1ba3a2881b62d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/75e8734906d15a63f097a0d89fb1ba3a2881b62d"}],"sha":"7790697405c19b8e36f20224477a10ec7512394d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/7790697405c19b8e36f20224477a10ec7512394d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/75e8734906d15a63f097a0d89fb1ba3a2881b62d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T03:40:17Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T03:40:17Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"docs: the three pieces of live preview, and what pa() can and cannot mark\n\nThree gotchas from making every block editable in place: the pieces that are\nsilent when missing, the two shapes of pa() and why a client component cannot\ntake it, and the four categories of property that can never carry\ndata-epi-edit. The last one matters most — without it the coverage number\nlooks like a failure instead of a ceiling.","tree":{"sha":"c424b2bb315ad166967c665020b429773c15814b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/c424b2bb315ad166967c665020b429773c15814b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/75e8734906d15a63f097a0d89fb1ba3a2881b62d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/75e8734906d15a63f097a0d89fb1ba3a2881b62d","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKDc1ZTg3MzQ5MDZkMTVhNjNmMDk3YTBkODlmYjFiYTNhMjg4MWI2MmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/bb82acb2bd095fb35e44e36e594e6079609bc6d2","sha":"bb82acb2bd095fb35e44e36e594e6079609bc6d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/bb82acb2bd095fb35e44e36e594e6079609bc6d2"}],"sha":"75e8734906d15a63f097a0d89fb1ba3a2881b62d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/75e8734906d15a63f097a0d89fb1ba3a2881b62d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/bb82acb2bd095fb35e44e36e594e6079609bc6d2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T03:40:01Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T03:40:01Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"feat(preview): every block property that can be edited in place now is\n\n86/86, 32 of 32 blocks. An editor typing in Visual Builder sees the change in\nthe canvas as they type, on every block, instead of waiting for the refetch.\n\nTwo patterns, chosen by the block rather than by taste:\n\n  - Server components take `pa` and call pa(''heading'') at the render site.\n  - Client components cannot — `pa` is a function and does not cross the\n    boundary — so the adapter computes the attributes and passes plain objects.\n    QuoteForm carries them per field, because its fields render through a map\n    and there is no element for \"field1Label\" until the row exists.\n\nThe denominator moved a long way, 174 → 86, and every reduction is a property\nthat CANNOT carry the attribute rather than one being excused:\n\n  - Attributes, not content: alt text, input placeholders, a video iframe''s\n    title. data-epi-edit marks an element whose CONTENT is the property.\n  - Configuration: enums, booleans, numbers, ids, layout and colour settings.\n    Decided from the declared type rather than a name list, so it does not rot.\n  - Arrays: N elements behind one property name.\n  - Computed values: firstName and lastName render as one display name, bio as\n    a truncated preview, languages as a joined list. Patching one in place\n    would replace the whole composite — \"Anna Berg\" becoming \"Anna\".\n\nAll of these still update through NextPreviewComponent''s refetch.\n\nThe coverage tool under-reported four separate ways before it was right, and\neach was found by disbelieving a zero and opening the file:\n\n  - named imports (`import X, { type Y } from …`)\n  - a server wrapper whose render sites live in the sibling .client file\n  - components outside components/blocks/ — OT_PractitionerProfile renders\n    through components/practitioner/PractitionerHeader\n  - `pa?.(''x'')`, the optional form used when the factory is an optional prop\n\nEach made a finished block read as untouched. A tool that under-reports sends\nyou to rewrite work that was already done.\n\ntsc clean. eslint unchanged: 96 pre-existing errors before and after.","tree":{"sha":"21d2351b38d5067835656a87996457f8ada85991","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/21d2351b38d5067835656a87996457f8ada85991"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/bb82acb2bd095fb35e44e36e594e6079609bc6d2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/bb82acb2bd095fb35e44e36e594e6079609bc6d2","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKGJiODJhY2IyYmQwOTVmYjM1ZTQ0ZTM2ZTU5NGU2MDc5NjA5YmM2ZDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/c8998fa38cc7b5b612f41a7112a6eacc149a8ac1","sha":"c8998fa38cc7b5b612f41a7112a6eacc149a8ac1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/c8998fa38cc7b5b612f41a7112a6eacc149a8ac1"}],"sha":"bb82acb2bd095fb35e44e36e594e6079609bc6d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/bb82acb2bd095fb35e44e36e594e6079609bc6d2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/c8998fa38cc7b5b612f41a7112a6eacc149a8ac1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T03:28:44Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T03:28:44Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"feat(preview): property overlays for callout, FAQ, button and divider\n\nFour of the blocks the LF pages actually use now carry data-epi-edit on every\ntext property, so an editor''s keystroke patches the DOM instead of waiting for\nthe refetch. Coverage 43/174 → 61/141.\n\nTwo patterns, and which one applies is decided by the block, not by taste:\n\n  - A server block takes `pa` and calls pa(''heading'') inline. QuoteBlock and\n    PrimaryTextBlock already worked this way.\n  - A client block cannot: `pa` is a function and does not cross the boundary.\n    The adapter computes the attributes and passes plain objects, the shape\n    LaserSignature already took as `epiProps`. CalloutBlock and FaqAccordion\n    go this way.\n\nThe denominator moved because two kinds of property were being counted that\ncan never carry the attribute:\n\n  - URLs. data-epi-edit marks an element whose CONTENT is the property; an\n    href has no such element and is edited in the panel.\n  - Arrays. They render as N elements and the attribute names one property, so\n    there is nothing to point at — FaqBlock''s questions/answers are fifteen\n    rows behind two property names. These update through the refetch like any\n    structural change.\n\nCounting either as missing put a ceiling on the metric and made it useless as\na signal, which is the only thing it is for.","tree":{"sha":"f2dd98e5c3d952e3ce5fe129573d56f3babc8ae5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/f2dd98e5c3d952e3ce5fe129573d56f3babc8ae5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/c8998fa38cc7b5b612f41a7112a6eacc149a8ac1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/c8998fa38cc7b5b612f41a7112a6eacc149a8ac1","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKGM4OTk4ZmEzOGNjN2I1YjYxMmY0MWE3MTEyYTZlYWNjMTQ5YThhYzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/09b9d17754ff0badf8e9ec22332f823860b8d700","sha":"09b9d17754ff0badf8e9ec22332f823860b8d700","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/09b9d17754ff0badf8e9ec22332f823860b8d700"}],"sha":"c8998fa38cc7b5b612f41a7112a6eacc149a8ac1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/c8998fa38cc7b5b612f41a7112a6eacc149a8ac1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/09b9d17754ff0badf8e9ec22332f823860b8d700/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T03:25:40Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T03:25:40Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"fix(preview): coverage tool under-reported by missing named imports\n\nblocksFor matched the module path only after a bare default-import identifier,\nso it skipped\n\n    import QuoteBlock, { type QuoteStyleOptions } from ''@/components/blocks/QuoteBlock''\n\nand reported OT_QuoteBlock as 0/3 while the component calls pa(''quote'') three\ntimes. Matching on the module path alone lifts the real figure from 43/174 to\n54/174, and moves five blocks out of the ''none'' column.\n\nA coverage tool that under-reports is worse than no tool: it sends you to\nrewrite files that were already finished.","tree":{"sha":"c08ca91ad6666328b021927398d21a77280b1046","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/c08ca91ad6666328b021927398d21a77280b1046"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/09b9d17754ff0badf8e9ec22332f823860b8d700","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/09b9d17754ff0badf8e9ec22332f823860b8d700","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKDA5YjlkMTc3NTRmZjBiYWRmOGU5ZWMyMjMzMmY4MjM4NjBiOGQ3MDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/29302a9e6210f88a388761a1ae53c776d12363c6","sha":"29302a9e6210f88a388761a1ae53c776d12363c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/29302a9e6210f88a388761a1ae53c776d12363c6"}],"sha":"09b9d17754ff0badf8e9ec22332f823860b8d700","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/09b9d17754ff0badf8e9ec22332f823860b8d700"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/29302a9e6210f88a388761a1ae53c776d12363c6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T03:24:32Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T03:24:32Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"feat(preview): measure which block properties are editable in place\n\nLive editing has to be added per property, per block — pa(''headline'') spread\nonto the element that renders `headline` — so it is exactly the kind of work\nthat gets half-finished and looks done. `yarn preview:coverage` counts it.\n\nThe first honest number: 43 of 174 properties across 33 blocks, 25%. Eighteen\nblocks have none at all, including OT_HeroBlock, OT_FaqBlock, OT_QuoteBlock,\nOT_CalloutBlock and OT_CompareTable — all of which the LF pages use.\n\nTwo things the script had to learn the hard way, both now in comments: the\nalignment of `baseType:` varies between content-type files, so a literal\n\"baseType: ''_component''\" match silently skipped nine blocks; and OptiForms\nelements and the theme/token singletons are noise here — third-party and gated,\nor configuration nobody edits on a page.\n\nIt reports absence, not misplacement: a property counts as covered when\npa(''name'') appears in the block or its adapter. That catches the common\nfailure. Whether the attribute landed on the right element still needs eyes.","tree":{"sha":"484479b60e6fe3ca595d9c5211d76630436dd729","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/484479b60e6fe3ca595d9c5211d76630436dd729"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/29302a9e6210f88a388761a1ae53c776d12363c6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/29302a9e6210f88a388761a1ae53c776d12363c6","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKDI5MzAyYTllNjIxMGY4OGEzODg3NjFhMWFlNTNjNzc2ZDEyMzYzYzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/bb0fcdcca96779fac7c10667ef95c253e4339b44","sha":"bb0fcdcca96779fac7c10667ef95c253e4339b44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/bb0fcdcca96779fac7c10667ef95c253e4339b44"}],"sha":"29302a9e6210f88a388761a1ae53c776d12363c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/29302a9e6210f88a388761a1ae53c776d12363c6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/bb0fcdcca96779fac7c10667ef95c253e4339b44/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T03:22:49Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T03:22:49Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"fix(preview): the in-place edit path had never run — wrong attribute, wrong route\n\nTwo independent faults, either of which alone was enough to stop live editing\nfrom feeling live.\n\n1. OnPageEdit matched `[data-epi-property-name=\"…\"]`. Nothing emits that.\n   The SDK''s getPreviewUtils().pa(''headline'') returns\n   `{ ''data-epi-edit'': ''headline'' }` — that is the documented attribute and the\n   one the CMS looks for when placing property overlays. The selector never\n   matched, every save silently fell through to the refetch, and the fast path\n   was dead code that read as working.\n\n2. OnPageEdit was mounted only in the `(draft)` route group, which covers a\n   single-block route. Real page previews go through `(site)/[...slug]` and\n   `/preview`, where it was absent. So even with the right attribute it would\n   not have run where it matters.\n\nLive preview is three pieces — the CMS bridge script, NextPreviewComponent''s\nrefetch, and the in-place patch — and a page with two of them is not two-thirds\nlive, it is broken in a way nobody notices. They were spread across seven\nhand-written pairs in three routes plus a fourth copy in the draft layout, and\nthe third piece was in none of them.\n\ncomponents/preview/PreviewBridge.tsx now renders all three together, and every\npreview route uses it. They cannot drift apart again.\n\nAlso narrowed what the patch will write: strings only, as textContent. A\nrich-text property arrives as a node tree, so innerHTML would have written\n\"[object Object]\" into the page, and writing editor markup straight to the DOM\nis an injection the rest of this codebase routes through sanitizeCmsHtml.\nAnything not a string is left to the refetch, which renders it through the\nnormal component path.\n\ntsc clean. eslint unchanged: the 14 pre-existing `any` warnings in the slug\nroute are the same 14, verified by linting the file at HEAD.","tree":{"sha":"8dfb44490a77e167b66c8bd25a1bc96d7858d79a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/8dfb44490a77e167b66c8bd25a1bc96d7858d79a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/bb0fcdcca96779fac7c10667ef95c253e4339b44","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/bb0fcdcca96779fac7c10667ef95c253e4339b44","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKGJiMGZjZGNjYTk2Nzc5ZmFjN2MxMDY2N2VmOTVjMjUzZTQzMzliNDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/28ecb753493835d6fe21e0586bb378b7f0efc16e","sha":"28ecb753493835d6fe21e0586bb378b7f0efc16e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/28ecb753493835d6fe21e0586bb378b7f0efc16e"}],"sha":"bb0fcdcca96779fac7c10667ef95c253e4339b44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/bb0fcdcca96779fac7c10667ef95c253e4339b44"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/28ecb753493835d6fe21e0586bb378b7f0efc16e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T19:54:01Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T19:54:01Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"docs: write down the blog, the Opal tools, and what they cost to learn\n\nEverything added over this session had lived only in commit messages and code\ncomments. Now:\n\n- docs/blog-and-opal.md — how an article is stored and why it is a\n  BlankExperience rather than OT_BlogPage, the /blog index and why it is a code\n  route, both Opal tools, the fifteen section types and what each renders as,\n  the skill, setup and a verification table keyed by status code.\n- Optimizely.md — ten new gotchas, each one something that cost real time here:\n  Graph rejecting limit > 100 rather than clamping it, DAM references needing\n  the DamImageSource segment, the CMS dropping empty strings from string arrays,\n  cms:push failing on content types while display templates go through, Opal\n  caching a manifest at registration, Opal serialising list parameters as JSON\n  strings, and auth_requirements meaning an identity provider.\n- README.md — a Blog/Opal section, the new routes and env vars, four gotchas\n  worth surfacing above the detail, and the Opal row in the integration table\n  moved from \"not started\".\n- CLAUDE.md — a pointer, plus the three files that must change together when a\n  section type is added. The manifest''s SECTIONS_DOC string is easy to forget,\n  and forgetting it means the model never learns the type exists.\n\nA subagent fact-checked every claim against the source and found six wrong ones,\nall now fixed: the endpoints described as failing closed are the two that do,\nnot the public discovery route; the OT_LandingSection gotcha said `article` was\nundeclared when that push has since landed; a README that pointed at the wrong\nfolder; a 503 row that named one of its two causes; a stats cap of \"n\" that is\n4; and an env block presented as complete while omitting\nCMP_BLOG_CONTAINER_KEY, which /api/cmp-publish cannot run without and which is\none character from CMS_BLOG_CONTAINER_KEY.\n\nSwept the repo afterwards for env vars read by code but documented nowhere —\nfive, all pre-existing, now in .env.example. That check is worth repeating:\ngrep process.env across app/ and lib/ and diff against the template.","tree":{"sha":"c347d17830783141a0274555274d0a42e0871f74","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/c347d17830783141a0274555274d0a42e0871f74"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/28ecb753493835d6fe21e0586bb378b7f0efc16e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/28ecb753493835d6fe21e0586bb378b7f0efc16e","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKDI4ZWNiNzUzNDkzODM1ZDZmZTIxZTA1ODZiYjM3OGI3ZjBlZmMxNmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/49436d2dda81cbd9733b7c41ffbfed75c45a34cf","sha":"49436d2dda81cbd9733b7c41ffbfed75c45a34cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/49436d2dda81cbd9733b7c41ffbfed75c45a34cf"}],"sha":"28ecb753493835d6fe21e0586bb378b7f0efc16e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/28ecb753493835d6fe21e0586bb378b7f0efc16e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/49436d2dda81cbd9733b7c41ffbfed75c45a34cf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T19:15:53Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T19:15:53Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"fix(opal): accept `sections` as a JSON string, which is how Opal sends it\n\nThe skill is doing its job — Opal called list_dam_images, looked at the\npreviews, declined to attach a misleading image, and refused to route around\nour tool with a generic CMS one. It then failed on our own validation:\n\n    {\"error\":\"`sections` must be a non-empty array.\"}\n\nthree times, on a payload that was a perfectly well-formed array. Opal said as\nmuch in passing: \"the section payload needs to go over as compact JSON\". It\ndeclares the parameter as type `list` and then serialises it, so what arrived\nwas a STRING containing an array.\n\nRejecting that is pedantry. The content was right, only the wrapping differed,\nand a caller cannot change how its runtime encodes a parameter. asArray() now\nparses a JSON string into an array, and unwraps each element the same way,\nsince a list of JSON strings is the other shape this arrives in. Applied to\n`sections` and `breadcrumb`. Checked against nine input shapes including empty\nstrings, garbage and objects — all either coerce correctly or return null.\n\nThe 400 log now prints field TYPES, not just names: \"sections=string\" would\nhave said this in one line instead of three round trips. Types only, never\nvalues.","tree":{"sha":"5556b3c2f606ba7b47837bc84400cdd244403398","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/5556b3c2f606ba7b47837bc84400cdd244403398"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/49436d2dda81cbd9733b7c41ffbfed75c45a34cf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/49436d2dda81cbd9733b7c41ffbfed75c45a34cf","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKDQ5NDM2ZDJkZGE4MWNiZDk3MzNiN2M0MWZmYmZlZDc1YzQ1YTM0Y2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/bf5496e348ca109550f01bfa1c2fd09ef56dd78c","sha":"bf5496e348ca109550f01bfa1c2fd09ef56dd78c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/bf5496e348ca109550f01bfa1c2fd09ef56dd78c"}],"sha":"49436d2dda81cbd9733b7c41ffbfed75c45a34cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/49436d2dda81cbd9733b7c41ffbfed75c45a34cf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/bf5496e348ca109550f01bfa1c2fd09ef56dd78c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T19:05:33Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T19:05:33Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"fix(opal): SKILL.md name must be a slug, not a title\n\nThe importer refused it:\n\n    SKILL.md frontmatter is invalid: name must be lowercase alphanumeric\n    with hyphens\n\n`name` is an identifier, matching the folder — lf-stockholm-blog-articles —\nand the readable title belongs in the body''s heading, where it now is and where\nskill.json picks it up as `title`.\n\nThe generator asserts the slug pattern, so this fails locally next time rather\nthan at import. Noted in the README too, since the rule is not obvious from a\nfield called \"name\".","tree":{"sha":"5557536efd5e26678b97bcaca6f8643c72dbf206","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/5557536efd5e26678b97bcaca6f8643c72dbf206"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/bf5496e348ca109550f01bfa1c2fd09ef56dd78c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/bf5496e348ca109550f01bfa1c2fd09ef56dd78c","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKGJmNTQ5NmUzNDhjYTEwOTU1MGYwMWJmYTFjMmZkMDllZjU2ZGQ3OGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/a41a6293ca7c0e28bbff0ed7417633799fceadea","sha":"a41a6293ca7c0e28bbff0ed7417633799fceadea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/a41a6293ca7c0e28bbff0ed7417633799fceadea"}],"sha":"bf5496e348ca109550f01bfa1c2fd09ef56dd78c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/bf5496e348ca109550f01bfa1c2fd09ef56dd78c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/a41a6293ca7c0e28bbff0ed7417633799fceadea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T18:56:55Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T18:56:55Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"docs(opal): ship the blog skill as an importable SKILL.md, not prose\n\nOpal''s importer takes SKILL.md, skill.json, a zip, or a GitHub URL pointing at\na skill folder — and skills use the SKILL.md format, agentskills.io compatible.\nSo the skill is now an actual importable artifact instead of a page of\ninstructions to retype:\n\n  docs/opal-skills/lf-stockholm-blog-articles/SKILL.md\n  docs/opal-skills/lf-stockholm-blog-articles/skill.json\n  docs/opal-skills/README.md\n\nThe GitHub-URL import path is also the honest answer to \"why does this belong\nin the repo\": the skill drives create_blog_article, and when the section types\nin lib/blogComposition.ts change the skill text has to change with them.\nKeeping them in one repo makes that drift visible, and Opal can import the\nfolder directly.\n\nskill.json is generated from SKILL.md rather than written by hand, so the two\ncannot disagree. Its field names come from Opal''s own skill editor, but the\nexport schema is not published, so the README says plainly that SKILL.md is the\nformat to trust and that exporting an existing skill from Opal is how to learn\nthe authoritative shape.\n\nTwo things SKILL.md cannot carry, both noted in the README because they are the\ndifference between the skill working and doing nothing: \"Where to use\", which\nbinds it to CMS / lans01saas: Production1, and \"Activation Trigger\", which must\nbe keyword and intent matching — the tool-based trigger fires only once a tool\nis already in use, too late to influence which tool gets chosen.\n\nReplaces the earlier prose version of the same content.","tree":{"sha":"468aa54b4273da7a3b814ce810e136d689f38573","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/468aa54b4273da7a3b814ce810e136d689f38573"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/a41a6293ca7c0e28bbff0ed7417633799fceadea","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/a41a6293ca7c0e28bbff0ed7417633799fceadea","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKGE0MWE2MjkzY2E3YzBlMjhiYmZmMGVkNzQxNzYzMzc5OWZjZWFkZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/8003d0c9f9682bdf84fd5c7202e6f411a28751d7","sha":"8003d0c9f9682bdf84fd5c7202e6f411a28751d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/8003d0c9f9682bdf84fd5c7202e6f411a28751d7"}],"sha":"a41a6293ca7c0e28bbff0ed7417633799fceadea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/a41a6293ca7c0e28bbff0ed7417633799fceadea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/8003d0c9f9682bdf84fd5c7202e6f411a28751d7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T18:50:46Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T18:50:46Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"docs(opal): an Opal skill that pins blog writing to our tool, on our instance\n\nVerified that create_blog_article puts articles in the Blog folder — posted\none through the live endpoint and read its container back from the CMS: it\nmatches. So the pages appearing elsewhere are not from this tool. Opal is\nchoosing its own built-in CMS tools instead.\n\nTwo changes, aimed at the choice rather than the symptom.\n\n1. docs/opal-skill-lf-blog.md — the text of an Optimizely Opal skill, ready to\n   paste. Skills are Optimizely''s mechanism for exactly this: reusable\n   instructions applied at runtime. The important field is \"Where to use\",\n   which scopes a skill to one product and one instance, so this stays out of\n   the way everywhere else. Set as an Organization skill so it covers everyone.\n\n   The skill tells Opal to use create_blog_article and no other CMS tool for\n   blog content here; to call list_dam_images and never invent an image key; to\n   stop and say so rather than substitute a tool if ours is unavailable; and to\n   report the `container` from the response, which is the fingerprint proving\n   which tool ran.\n\n2. The manifest description now claims the territory instead of just describing\n   the capability. That string is what an assistant reads when choosing between\n   this tool and its built-ins, and the previous polite version kept losing. It\n   now says outright that only this tool places the article in the Blog folder\n   and that a page made any other way does not display.\n\nThe description works without the skill; the skill works without the\ndescription. Together they cover the case where one is missed.","tree":{"sha":"81569972a0b6fd49ee815e602949fdbc46a77f3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/81569972a0b6fd49ee815e602949fdbc46a77f3b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/8003d0c9f9682bdf84fd5c7202e6f411a28751d7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/8003d0c9f9682bdf84fd5c7202e6f411a28751d7","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKDgwMDNkMGM5Zjk2ODJiZGY4NGZkNWM3MjAyZTZmNDExYTI4NzUxZDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/310e80976a7128a474e8c0de582847a10b6eaa3e","sha":"310e80976a7128a474e8c0de582847a10b6eaa3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/310e80976a7128a474e8c0de582847a10b6eaa3e"}],"sha":"8003d0c9f9682bdf84fd5c7202e6f411a28751d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/8003d0c9f9682bdf84fd5c7202e6f411a28751d7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/310e80976a7128a474e8c0de582847a10b6eaa3e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T18:43:58Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T18:43:58Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"chore(opal): report which container an article was created in\n\n\"Opal made the page outside the Blog folder\" should not need a hunt through\nthe content tree to confirm or refute.\n\nThis endpoint always posts `container: BLOG_FOLDER`, which is\nCMS_BLOG_CONTAINER_KEY or, unset, the Blog folder''s own key. So an article\nlanding anywhere else means one of exactly two things: that variable is set\nto the wrong key on the deployment, or the article was not made by this tool\nat all. The response now carries `container`, and the log says whether the\nbuilt-in default was used, which tells those two apart on sight.\n\nChecked against the CMS first: the Blog folder holds one child, Root holds\nsix, and no content anywhere in the instance is newer than the renovation\narticle — so nothing Opal has produced has reached this CMS. That points at\nthe second case, but the log will settle it on the next run rather than\nleaving it as my inference.\n\nCould not exercise the live endpoint from here: this sandbox''s proxy allows\napi.cms.optimizely.com and cg.optimizely.com only, and refuses the Vercel\nhost. tsc and eslint clean.","tree":{"sha":"930515f04cd7b7a1d147eec416259824b310e080","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/930515f04cd7b7a1d147eec416259824b310e080"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/310e80976a7128a474e8c0de582847a10b6eaa3e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/310e80976a7128a474e8c0de582847a10b6eaa3e","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKDMxMGU4MDk3NmE3MTI4YTQ3NGU4YzBkZTU4Mjg0N2ExMGI2ZWFhM2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/2ed8edcb232ca4666c1cc006c6fa412b0b67a9ff","sha":"2ed8edcb232ca4666c1cc006c6fa412b0b67a9ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/2ed8edcb232ca4666c1cc006c6fa412b0b67a9ff"}],"sha":"310e80976a7128a474e8c0de582847a10b6eaa3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/310e80976a7128a474e8c0de582847a10b6eaa3e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/2ed8edcb232ca4666c1cc006c6fa412b0b67a9ff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T18:24:50Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T18:24:50Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"chore(opal): log every discovery fetch, so a stale registry is visible\n\nThe manifest on production has served two tools since the last deploy —\nverified by reading the live endpoint. Opal keeps answering from the copy it\ncached when the registry was first created, and reports, correctly for what\nit can see, that list_dam_images does not exist.\n\nFrom outside there was no way to separate \"Opal never re-read the manifest\"\nfrom \"Opal read it and something else is wrong\". Now each GET logs the caller\nand the tool count, so the absence of a line is itself the answer.\n\nInfo level, user-agent truncated, nothing sensitive: this endpoint is public\nby design.","tree":{"sha":"697d020239a79ecfb8d534cb25add213e678d4b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/697d020239a79ecfb8d534cb25add213e678d4b6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/2ed8edcb232ca4666c1cc006c6fa412b0b67a9ff","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/2ed8edcb232ca4666c1cc006c6fa412b0b67a9ff","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKDJlZDhlZGNiMjMyY2E0NjY2YzFjYzAwNmM2ZmE0MTJiMGI2N2E5ZmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/b25c3d3826743a66fd29e338b1a68f18228c6deb","sha":"b25c3d3826743a66fd29e338b1a68f18228c6deb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/b25c3d3826743a66fd29e338b1a68f18228c6deb"}],"sha":"2ed8edcb232ca4666c1cc006c6fa412b0b67a9ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/2ed8edcb232ca4666c1cc006c6fa412b0b67a9ff"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/b25c3d3826743a66fd29e338b1a68f18228c6deb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T18:14:27Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T18:14:27Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"fix(blog): back to narrow — 896px was the right measure after all\n\nTried the middle width on a real article and it read too loose. 896px puts\nbody text at roughly the measure it wants, and that matters more here than\ngiving a gallery or a table extra room: this is an article, and most of it\nis prose.\n\nThe \"article\" width (1024px) stays in place — the class in\ncms/compositions/Section.tsx and the choice in the pushed OT_LandingSection\ntemplate — just not as the default. Two reasons not to rip it out:\n\n  - It is already live in the CMS, so an editor sees it in the Visual Builder\n    width dropdown. A choice offered there with no matching class silently\n    falls back to `default` (1440px), which is a worse trap than an unused\n    entry in a lookup table.\n  - Per-section width is a legitimate editorial decision; what was wrong was\n    letting it fall out of which block a section happened to use.\n\nOne constant still moves the whole article. Probe rebuilt and republished at\n/blog/section-probe, all 18 sections back at narrow.","tree":{"sha":"8c8f89405462459b69647157acc302e12ad97a40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/8c8f89405462459b69647157acc302e12ad97a40"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/b25c3d3826743a66fd29e338b1a68f18228c6deb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/b25c3d3826743a66fd29e338b1a68f18228c6deb","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKGIyNWMzZDM4MjY3NDNhNjZmZDI5ZTMzOGIxYTY4ZjE4MjI4YzZkZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/bc2e2e1523cfaf7bac56798dc21a67a8229d7429","sha":"bc2e2e1523cfaf7bac56798dc21a67a8229d7429","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/bc2e2e1523cfaf7bac56798dc21a67a8229d7429"}],"sha":"b25c3d3826743a66fd29e338b1a68f18228c6deb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/b25c3d3826743a66fd29e338b1a68f18228c6deb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/bc2e2e1523cfaf7bac56798dc21a67a8229d7429/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T18:06:42Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T18:06:42Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"fix(blog): one content width for the whole article, and a size that fits it\n\nSections were choosing their own width: prose, quotes and callouts at\n\"narrow\", cards, galleries, tables, video and the lead image at \"default\".\nThose are max-w-4xl (896px) and max-w-[90rem] (1440px) — a 500px jump — so\nthe left edge moved every few sections and a long article read as three\ndocuments stacked on top of each other. Visible immediately once the tool\nstarted emitting nine more section types.\n\nEvery section now takes one width, set by a single constant.\n\nThat width is new. The four presets left nothing between 896px and 1440px:\nnarrow reads well for prose but cramps a three-up gallery or a comparison\ntable, and default is far too wide to read a paragraph in. So widthClasses\ngains \"article\" at max-w-5xl (1024px) — text stays near its comfortable\nmeasure while the wider blocks get somewhere to breathe.\n\nChecked that the CMS accepts a setting value the display template does not\ndeclare: it does, 201. But the front end falls back to `default` for an\nunknown width, so the Section component needed the class before this could\nmean anything, and OT_LandingSection needs a `yarn cms:push` before the\noption appears in the Visual Builder dropdown. Until that push, an editor\nopening the width control on one of these sections sees no matching choice.\n\nFull-bleed moments are still a real editorial device. They just have to be\nchosen deliberately for a design rather than falling out of which block a\nsection happens to use — hence one constant to move, not nine call sites.\n\nThe section probe was rebuilt, posted and published at /blog/section-probe\nwith all 18 sections at the new width. The rendered result is NOT verified:\nthat needs this commit deployed, since the class does not exist in the\nrunning build.","tree":{"sha":"e892ce3059747862d371dd3da6a3a61f4aafd91b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/e892ce3059747862d371dd3da6a3a61f4aafd91b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/bc2e2e1523cfaf7bac56798dc21a67a8229d7429","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/bc2e2e1523cfaf7bac56798dc21a67a8229d7429","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKGJjMmUyZTE1MjNjZmFmN2JhYzU2Nzk4ZGMyMWE2N2E4MjI5ZDc0Mjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/8f10876af89a1a74ccc9969b6f88189062faf13f","sha":"8f10876af89a1a74ccc9969b6f88189062faf13f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/8f10876af89a1a74ccc9969b6f88189062faf13f"}],"sha":"bc2e2e1523cfaf7bac56798dc21a67a8229d7429","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/bc2e2e1523cfaf7bac56798dc21a67a8229d7429"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/8f10876af89a1a74ccc9969b6f88189062faf13f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T17:56:39Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T17:56:39Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"feat(opal): nine more section types, and a DAM image tool to feed them\n\nThe blog tool could write six kinds of section and no pictures. It can now\nwrite fifteen, and choose images from the DAM.\n\nNEW TOOL — list_dam_images\n    Returns each image''s key, title and CDN preview URL. Opal calls it first\n    and passes the key it picks as `imageKey`. Called a listing rather than a\n    search on purpose: Graph does index cmp_Asset with _fulltext, but the\n    library''s titles are Unsplash filenames, so \"house\" matches nothing and\n    returning everything is the more useful answer at this size. Behind the\n    same bearer check as create_blog_article — an open endpoint enumerating a\n    customer''s media library is an inventory of it.\n\nNEW SECTIONS\n    image, imageText, gallery — imageText leans on OT_ImageBlock''s own\n      two-column layout rather than building columns here, so it survives an\n      editor resizing things afterwards.\n    steps  — an <ol>, not a stack of cards. Numbered steps are a list, and the\n      numbering then stays right for screen readers and for reordering.\n    table  — OT_CompareTable.\n    divider, stats, banner, video.\n\n    stats renders as cards, NOT OT_StatBlock. That type declares only\n    `sectionEnabled` and holds an array of components, making it unplaceable in\n    a column: the CMS accepts it and it renders nothing. A card with the figure\n    as its heading is the honest approximation available.\n\n    A video URL that is not YouTube or Vimeo is dropped rather than posted —\n    the content type''s pattern would reject it and take the whole article down\n    with it.\n\nTHREE BUGS FOUND BY ACTUALLY POSTING THIS\n    Verified by building an article that uses every section type and putting it\n    through the real CMS, not by reading the types and hoping.\n\n    1. DAM references were being written as `cms://content/<key>`. Reading the\n       published home page''s composition shows the CMS stores a DAM asset as\n       `cms://content/DamImageSource/<key>`. The old form yields an image block\n       with no image. This had been sitting in the hero-image path since the\n       tool was written, unexercised because nobody had passed an image.\n    2. OT_CompareTable.intro is a plain string, not richText. Posting\n       { html: … } is rejected outright: \"requires an element of type ''String'',\n       but the target element has type ''Object''\".\n    3. The CMS DROPS empty strings from a string array. A table row of [\"No\"]\n       against two columns came back with five cells instead of six, shifting\n       every later value into the wrong column — silently. Short rows are now\n       padded with an em dash, which is both non-empty and honest: it reads\n       \"not stated\", where \"no\" would assert the feature is absent.\n\nProbe article posted, read back, and checked section by section: 18 sections,\nall three DAM references stored with the DamImageSource segment, table grid\n2x3 = 6 cells intact. scripts/emit_section_probe.mts keeps the probe around so\nthe next person can repeat it.\n\nAlso extracted the bearer check into lib/opalAuth.ts so the second tool cannot\ndrift from the first.","tree":{"sha":"8434fa565975247f77fe2a9a31d6446f3d36a62f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/8434fa565975247f77fe2a9a31d6446f3d36a62f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/8f10876af89a1a74ccc9969b6f88189062faf13f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/8f10876af89a1a74ccc9969b6f88189062faf13f","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKDhmMTA4NzZhZjg5YTFhNzRjY2M5OTY5YjZmODgxODkwNjJmYWYxM2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/5b05a30a8e575bb0cd30ba6d8322f2e540a85d51","sha":"5b05a30a8e575bb0cd30ba6d8322f2e540a85d51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/5b05a30a8e575bb0cd30ba6d8322f2e540a85d51"}],"sha":"8f10876af89a1a74ccc9969b6f88189062faf13f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/8f10876af89a1a74ccc9969b6f88189062faf13f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/5b05a30a8e575bb0cd30ba6d8322f2e540a85d51/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T17:37:02Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T17:37:02Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"fix(opal): unwrap the { parameters: … } envelope Opal actually posts\n\nAuth is solved — the 401 is gone and Opal now reaches the handler. It fails\none step later, with our own 400:\n\n    {\"error\":\"`title` is required.\"}\n\non a call that carried a title. Opal does not post a tool''s arguments at the\ntop level; it wraps them the way the Opal tools SDK expects, so a handler\nreceives its typed `parameters` object:\n\n    { \"parameters\": { \"title\": …, \"sections\": [ … ] }, \"auth\": { … } }\n\nvalidate() read body.title straight off the root and found nothing.\n\nBoth shapes are accepted now: if `parameters` is an object, that is the\npayload; otherwise the body is. curl and scripts post flat, Opal posts\nwrapped, and neither has to know about the other. `auth` is ignored — this\ntool authenticates on the Authorization header, not on forwarded credentials.\n\nA 400 now also logs the top-level KEYS of what arrived. Names only, no values.\nA rejected payload is nearly always the wrong envelope rather than the wrong\ncontent, and the keys say which without another round trip.\n\ntsc and eslint clean. The flat shape stays covered by the curl smoke test; the\nwrapped shape needs Opal to confirm.","tree":{"sha":"6c4491c744d4030338a44aeaeb513945a294dd20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/6c4491c744d4030338a44aeaeb513945a294dd20"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/5b05a30a8e575bb0cd30ba6d8322f2e540a85d51","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/5b05a30a8e575bb0cd30ba6d8322f2e540a85d51","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKDViMDVhMzBhOGU1NzViYjBjZDMwYmE2ZDgzMjJmMmU1NDBhODVkNTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/b3fa3ee32d2e20222b7816302de01df50384b128","sha":"b3fa3ee32d2e20222b7816302de01df50384b128","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/b3fa3ee32d2e20222b7816302de01df50384b128"}],"sha":"5b05a30a8e575bb0cd30ba6d8322f2e540a85d51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/5b05a30a8e575bb0cd30ba6d8322f2e540a85d51"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/b3fa3ee32d2e20222b7816302de01df50384b128/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T14:38:18Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T14:38:18Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"fix(opal): accept a scheme-less Authorization value, and log which headers arrived\n\ncurl with the same token Opal holds returns 200 and creates the draft, so the\nsecret on Vercel is right and the endpoint works. Opal is therefore not\nsending that token — or not sending it the way we parse it.\n\nTwo changes, both aimed at telling those apart on the next attempt:\n\n- A bare Authorization value with no scheme is now accepted. Some callers put\n  the raw token in the header; rejecting that buys nothing, since the value\n  still has to equal the secret, and it fails identically to a wrong secret.\n- On a missing header the log now lists the header NAMES that did arrive.\n  Names only, never values. If Opal sends its token as x-api-key or anything\n  else, that line says so immediately instead of costing another round trip.\n\ntsc and eslint clean. Verified only via curl; the Opal path still needs Opal.","tree":{"sha":"2ffe2d4d1de21898d6d3ee3c0467fbe51a1bd08b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/2ffe2d4d1de21898d6d3ee3c0467fbe51a1bd08b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/b3fa3ee32d2e20222b7816302de01df50384b128","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/b3fa3ee32d2e20222b7816302de01df50384b128","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKGIzZmEzZWUzMmQyZTIwMjIyYjc4MTYzMDJkZTAxZGY1MDM4NGIxMjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/c1c674c9b6a8535f8acdb703be2ab685964a0a85","sha":"c1c674c9b6a8535f8acdb703be2ab685964a0a85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/c1c674c9b6a8535f8acdb703be2ab685964a0a85"}],"sha":"b3fa3ee32d2e20222b7816302de01df50384b128","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/b3fa3ee32d2e20222b7816302de01df50384b128"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/c1c674c9b6a8535f8acdb703be2ab685964a0a85/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T14:34:53Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T14:34:53Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"fix(seo): sitemap advertised /en/ URLs the site does not treat as canonical\n\nWith the limit fixed, the sitemap finally emitted URLs — and they were the\nwrong ones:\n\n    https://…/en/product/home-insurance/\n    https://…/en/blog/the-road-to-a-successful-renovation/\n\nGraph returns the default locale as a path segment. lib/i18n/config is\nexplicit that the default locale carries NO prefix, and every link the site\nrenders points at /blog/x. Both forms resolve, and each declares ITSELF\ncanonical — verified in the browser: /blog/x says canonical /blog/x, and\n/en/blog/x says canonical /en/blog/x. So the sitemap was handing crawlers a\nsecond URL for every page and splitting the signal between the two.\n\ntoSiteUrl now drops a leading default-locale segment and the trailing slash,\nmatching the canonical the page itself declares. Non-default locales keep\ntheir prefix, because there the prefix IS the URL. The home page keeps its\nslash to avoid a pointless redirect.\n\nChecked against /, /en/, /en/product/x/, /fr/x/, /product/x and a path that\nmerely starts with the letters \"en\" — only a whole \"en\" segment is stripped.\n\nNot addressed here: /en/blog/x is still reachable and still self-canonical.\nNothing links to it and the sitemap no longer names it, so crawlers should not\nfind it, but the real cure is lib/metadata.ts normalising the canonical for\nevery page. That touches every route and deserves its own change.","tree":{"sha":"c49b4fc97140803ae1b316b09737cee739f8cbc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/c49b4fc97140803ae1b316b09737cee739f8cbc2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/c1c674c9b6a8535f8acdb703be2ab685964a0a85","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/c1c674c9b6a8535f8acdb703be2ab685964a0a85","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKGMxYzY3NGM5YjZhODUzNWY4YWNkYjcwM2JlMmFiNjg1OTY0YTBhODU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/23e366ac4ea9c5edff0a5ab7a70730d69e722974","sha":"23e366ac4ea9c5edff0a5ab7a70730d69e722974","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/23e366ac4ea9c5edff0a5ab7a70730d69e722974"}],"sha":"c1c674c9b6a8535f8acdb703be2ab685964a0a85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/c1c674c9b6a8535f8acdb703be2ab685964a0a85"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/23e366ac4ea9c5edff0a5ab7a70730d69e722974/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T14:26:09Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T14:26:09Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"fix(seo): limit 200 was the empty sitemap — Graph caps it at 100\n\nThe build log finally said it out loud, once the previous commit stopped\nswallowing the error:\n\n    Invalid ''limit'' (value: 200, expected: [0-100])\n\nGraph does not clamp an over-large limit, it rejects the document. The old\nsitemap query asked for 200, so every request failed, and `catch { return [] }`\nturned that into a valid, empty <urlset> that robots.txt kept advertising to\ncrawlers. My rewrite split the query and added logging but carried the 200\nstraight over, which is why it still came back empty.\n\nNow 100, named and explained so nobody raises it again. That is per type, so\nthe real ceiling is 100 x PAGE_TYPES.length — far above this site. Page with\n`skip` if it is ever reached.\n\nSwept the rest of the repo for literal limits over 100: none.\n\nVerified from the user''s own build output, which is the first time this query\nhas been seen to run.","tree":{"sha":"a2c9d08ff043ced9e3a6ecceb934ccf0010f05ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/a2c9d08ff043ced9e3a6ecceb934ccf0010f05ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/23e366ac4ea9c5edff0a5ab7a70730d69e722974","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/23e366ac4ea9c5edff0a5ab7a70730d69e722974","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKDIzZTM2NmFjNGVhOWM1ZWRmZjBhNWFiN2E3MDczMGQ2OWU3MjI5NzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/3a5717c3379a4bdf870f29f8401968965a48c3af","sha":"3a5717c3379a4bdf870f29f8401968965a48c3af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/3a5717c3379a4bdf870f29f8401968965a48c3af"}],"sha":"23e366ac4ea9c5edff0a5ab7a70730d69e722974","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/23e366ac4ea9c5edff0a5ab7a70730d69e722974"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/3a5717c3379a4bdf870f29f8401968965a48c3af/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T14:21:17Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T14:21:17Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"fix(opal): accept a lowercase bearer scheme, trim both sides, say why a 401 happened\n\nOpal reached the endpoint and got 401. The chain works — manifest read, tool\nmatched, POST delivered — so the only thing left is the token, and the handler\ngave no way to tell which kind of token problem it was.\n\nTwo ways it could 401 on a CORRECT secret:\n\n- `header.startsWith(''Bearer '')` is case-sensitive. RFC 7235 makes the auth\n  scheme case-insensitive, so a client sending \"bearer <token>\" was rejected\n  before the comparison ran, producing a 401 identical to a wrong secret.\n  Now parsed with /^bearer\\s+(.+)$/i.\n- Neither side was trimmed. A secret pasted into a dashboard field picks up a\n  trailing newline routinely, and the resulting mismatch is invisible in both\n  UIs. Both the header value and the env var are trimmed now.\n\nAnd the 401 now logs WHY: no token at all, or a mismatch with the two lengths.\nLengths only — enough to separate \"wrong secret\" from \"truncated paste\"\nwithout writing either value to a log.\n\ntsc and eslint clean. Not exercised against Opal from here.","tree":{"sha":"32af425f944ff471b5fee30bc9e1b939a68bab7e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/32af425f944ff471b5fee30bc9e1b939a68bab7e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/3a5717c3379a4bdf870f29f8401968965a48c3af","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/3a5717c3379a4bdf870f29f8401968965a48c3af","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKDNhNTcxN2MzMzc5YTRiZGY4NzBmMjlmODQwMTk2ODk2NWE0OGMzYWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/5d7930bdc2cf82752c8398932123dd60cd1de0a2","sha":"5d7930bdc2cf82752c8398932123dd60cd1de0a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/5d7930bdc2cf82752c8398932123dd60cd1de0a2"}],"sha":"3a5717c3379a4bdf870f29f8401968965a48c3af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/3a5717c3379a4bdf870f29f8401968965a48c3af"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/5d7930bdc2cf82752c8398932123dd60cd1de0a2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T13:26:36Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T13:26:36Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"fix(blog): match the article path wherever \"blog\" sits, and log when nothing does\n\n/blog rendered \"No articles have been published yet\" over a blog that has an\narticle in it. The query was fine — the path filter was not. It required\nurl.default to start with \"/blog/\", and Graph returns a locale prefix on this\ninstance, so \"/en/blog/the-road-to-a-successful-renovation\" failed the test\nand the page reported an empty blog. Same class of bug as the empty sitemap:\na silent zero that reads as \"nothing here\" rather than \"I looked wrong\".\n\nNow the check splits the path and looks for a \"blog\" segment with something\nafter it, wherever that segment sits. That handles a locale prefix without\nhard-coding which locales exist, and still excludes the index itself, whose\npath ends at \"blog\".\n\nAlso: when Graph returns experiences and none of them survive the filter, the\npaths it DID return are logged. That is the entire diagnosis, and last time it\ncost a round trip through the user to find out.\n\ntsc and eslint clean. Still unverified against Graph from here — the sandbox\ngets 403 from both Graph and the CMS API.","tree":{"sha":"a393e225c85cf88eed82809d28bfc35e3987869d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/a393e225c85cf88eed82809d28bfc35e3987869d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/5d7930bdc2cf82752c8398932123dd60cd1de0a2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/5d7930bdc2cf82752c8398932123dd60cd1de0a2","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKDVkNzkzMGJkYzJjZjgyNzUyYzgzOTg5MzIxMjNkZDYwY2QxZGUwYTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/dff7d4fb77ec09a365cf6c095ed3db5f8a05180c","sha":"dff7d4fb77ec09a365cf6c095ed3db5f8a05180c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/dff7d4fb77ec09a365cf6c095ed3db5f8a05180c"}],"sha":"5d7930bdc2cf82752c8398932123dd60cd1de0a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/5d7930bdc2cf82752c8398932123dd60cd1de0a2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/dff7d4fb77ec09a365cf6c095ed3db5f8a05180c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T13:23:28Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T13:23:28Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"feat(blog): a /blog index, so published articles are reachable at all\n\n/blog answered 404. Articles live in a CMS folder, and a folder lends its\nsegment to a child''s URL without being a page itself, so every article the\nOpal tool writes was findable only by already knowing its exact URL. For a\ntool whose whole point is \"ask Opal for an article and it appears\", that is\nmost of the feature missing.\n\nBuilt as a code route rather than a CMS experience carrying OT_BlogFeedBlock,\nfor two reasons:\n\n- That block queries OT_BlogPage. These articles are BlankExperience\n  documents, because they are composition pages that must stay editable in\n  Visual Builder. Dropping the block on a page would have listed nothing,\n  and looked like an empty blog rather than a type mismatch.\n- A listing derived from Graph needs no authoring step, so an article Opal\n  writes shows up the moment it is published.\n\nThe trade-off, written into the file: this index is not VB-editable. The\narticles it links to still are.\n\nlib/blogIndex.ts asks Graph for nothing unproven. Every field is copied from\nbuildBlankExperienceQuery in app/api/search/route.ts, which the site search\nexercises against the live index. Omitted on purpose: `noIndex` (declared on\nthe type, but app/sitemap.ts requests it and returns an empty urlset in\nproduction, so it is the prime suspect for a field Graph has not indexed —\nand one unknown field fails the whole document), `orderBy` and\n`url { hierarchical }` (only used in this repo inside catch blocks that hide\ntheir own failures), and site scoping on `url.base` (search builds it as\nhttps://${domain} while getRequestBaseUrl returns the request''s scheme —\nhttp on localhost — and a mismatch there is silent). Sorting and the /blog/\npath filter run in JS, where they cannot 400.\n\nA failed query returns null and the page says the list could not load; an\nempty result says no articles yet. Distinguishing them is the point: an\nempty grid that means \"broken\" is how the sitemap went unnoticed.\n\ntsc and eslint clean. NOT run against Graph or rendered — this sandbox gets\n403 (Cloudflare 1010) from both Graph and the CMS API, and cannot build\n(no SWC binary for linux/arm64). Needs `yarn dev` or a deploy to confirm the\nquery shape is right.","tree":{"sha":"a2d5b827d31582c64cc238798d523cc68957c772","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/a2d5b827d31582c64cc238798d523cc68957c772"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/dff7d4fb77ec09a365cf6c095ed3db5f8a05180c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/dff7d4fb77ec09a365cf6c095ed3db5f8a05180c","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKGRmZjdkNGZiNzdlYzA5YTM2NWNmNmMwOTVlZDNkYjVmOGEwNTE4MGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/8bc35c166f8698c1873eaa575ef0a2590b973a6f","sha":"8bc35c166f8698c1873eaa575ef0a2590b973a6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/8bc35c166f8698c1873eaa575ef0a2590b973a6f"}],"sha":"dff7d4fb77ec09a365cf6c095ed3db5f8a05180c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/dff7d4fb77ec09a365cf6c095ed3db5f8a05180c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/8bc35c166f8698c1873eaa575ef0a2590b973a6f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T13:13:49Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T13:13:49Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"fix(seo): stop the sitemap failing silently into an empty urlset\n\n/sitemap.xml on production is a valid, completely empty <urlset> — and\nrobots.txt sends every crawler to it. Three things conspired:\n\n- One GraphQL document asked for BlankExperience and OT_BlogPage together.\n  GraphQL is all-or-nothing, so one bad field on one type discards the\n  other type''s results as well. Each type is now queried separately and a\n  failing type is skipped instead of taking the rest down with it.\n\n- `catch { return [] }` logged nothing. An empty sitemap is not an error\n  anyone trips over, so the real message never reached a human. Failures\n  now name the type and go to the server log, and an all-empty result says\n  so explicitly.\n\n- No revalidate, so Next built this exactly once at deploy time. A Graph\n  timeout or re-index during that single build freezes an empty sitemap\n  until the next deploy. Now revalidated hourly: a transient failure costs\n  an hour instead of a release.\n\nAlso hardened the entry mapping — an unparseable lastModified used to\nbecome an Invalid Date and serialize as garbage; it is now dropped.\n\nI could not reproduce the underlying Graph error from here (Graph answers\n403 to this sandbox), so this makes the failure VISIBLE rather than\nclaiming to fix its cause. If the urlset is still empty after deploy, the\nreason will be in the Vercel function log under [sitemap].\n\ntsc and eslint clean.","tree":{"sha":"3c69f1dbdd91437b1bf3cbb75dc4055b9bfaff19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/3c69f1dbdd91437b1bf3cbb75dc4055b9bfaff19"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/8bc35c166f8698c1873eaa575ef0a2590b973a6f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/8bc35c166f8698c1873eaa575ef0a2590b973a6f","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKDhiYzM1YzE2NmY4Njk4YzE4NzNlYWE1NzVlZjBhMjU5MGI5NzNhNmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/4d4f2ba8680dba12356593d2cc586eef986cb847","sha":"4d4f2ba8680dba12356593d2cc586eef986cb847","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/4d4f2ba8680dba12356593d2cc586eef986cb847"}],"sha":"8bc35c166f8698c1873eaa575ef0a2590b973a6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/8bc35c166f8698c1873eaa575ef0a2590b973a6f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/4d4f2ba8680dba12356593d2cc586eef986cb847/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T13:00:43Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T13:00:43Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"fix(opal): manifest Opal will actually accept — drop the fake auth provider\n\nRegistering the registry returned 400. That is not the bearer token being\nwrong (a wrong token reaches our handler and comes back 401); it is Opal\nrefusing to parse the discovery document. Two things in it were invented\nrather than checked against Opal''s own SDK:\n\n- auth_requirements declared {provider: \"bearer\"}. In the Opal tools SDK\n  `provider` names an IDENTITY provider whose credentials Opal resolves\n  for the user and forwards to the tool — \"google\", \"microsoft\", Opti ID.\n  There is no \"bearer\" provider. The token entered on the tool registry\n  is a different mechanism entirely: Opal puts it in the Authorization\n  header of every call, and needs no declaration in the manifest. So the\n  array is now empty, and /api/opal/create-blog still checks the header.\n\n- Two parameters were typed \"array\". Opal''s ParameterType enum is\n  string | integer | number | boolean | list | dictionary. Now \"list\".\n\ntsc and eslint clean. Registration itself not re-tested from here — that\nneeds the Opal UI.","tree":{"sha":"e81b520558cd7764a84a3c6b93b95d9161cb33df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/e81b520558cd7764a84a3c6b93b95d9161cb33df"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/4d4f2ba8680dba12356593d2cc586eef986cb847","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/4d4f2ba8680dba12356593d2cc586eef986cb847","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKDRkNGYyYmE4NjgwZGJhMTIzNTY1OTNkMmNjNTg2ZWVmOTg2Y2I4NDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/bcdc6ab0200f36eb6b389f11c8933c91b3d59f72","sha":"bcdc6ab0200f36eb6b389f11c8933c91b3d59f72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/bcdc6ab0200f36eb6b389f11c8933c91b3d59f72"}],"sha":"4d4f2ba8680dba12356593d2cc586eef986cb847","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/4d4f2ba8680dba12356593d2cc586eef986cb847"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/bcdc6ab0200f36eb6b389f11c8933c91b3d59f72/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T12:33:30Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T12:33:30Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"fix(opal): advertise the host that fetched the manifest, not NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL\n\nThe deployed manifest was handing Opal this endpoint:\n\n    \"endpoint\": \"http://localhost:3000/api/opal/create-blog\"\n\nbecause NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL is set to localhost on Vercel. Opal would\nhave called localhost and failed, and a discovery document that parses\nproduces no error anyone sees — Opal just quietly ends up with a tool it\ncannot reach.\n\nNEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL is a canonical-URL setting for SEO, and pointing it\nat localhost while developing is reasonable. A manifest is different: it\nis a set of live addresses. So derive the origin from the request that\narrived — whatever host fetched this document can, by definition, be\nreached — preferring Vercel''s x-forwarded-* over req.nextUrl.origin.\n\nThis does NOT fix the env var. robots.txt still emits\n\"Sitemap: http://localhost:3000/sitemap.xml\", and canonical hrefs, JSON-LD\npageUrl and llms.txt read the same variable. Set it to the deployed origin\nin Vercel and redeploy.\n\ntsc and eslint clean.","tree":{"sha":"aea053d1994ca5cb664186c8d7996a6f45bf6e49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/aea053d1994ca5cb664186c8d7996a6f45bf6e49"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/bcdc6ab0200f36eb6b389f11c8933c91b3d59f72","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/bcdc6ab0200f36eb6b389f11c8933c91b3d59f72","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKGJjZGM2YWIwMjAwZjM2ZWI2YjM4OWYxMWM4OTMzYzkxYjNkNTlmNzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/16714ae0ad2717e814d1ab61363179cf75cc0add","sha":"16714ae0ad2717e814d1ab61363179cf75cc0add","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/16714ae0ad2717e814d1ab61363179cf75cc0add"}],"sha":"bcdc6ab0200f36eb6b389f11c8933c91b3d59f72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/bcdc6ab0200f36eb6b389f11c8933c91b3d59f72"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/16714ae0ad2717e814d1ab61363179cf75cc0add/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T12:01:41Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T12:01:41Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"fix(cmp): let CMP frame the site, and stop the webhooks failing open\n\nTwo problems, both of which only show up once CMP is actually wired to\nthis deployment.\n\n1. CSP blocked CMP''s preview pane.\n\n   next.config.ts allowed `frame-ancestors ''self'' https://*.cms.optimizely.com`\n   — the Visual Builder canvas and nothing else. CMP embeds the completed\n   preview URL in an iframe of its own, so an editor requesting a preview\n   would have got a blank pane and a console error they never see. Added\n   *.cmp.optimizely.com and *.welcomesoftware.com, both of which Optimizely\n   lists in its own domain allowlist; a `*` matches one label, so the three\n   entries do not overlap.\n\n2. The CMP webhooks skipped verification when their secret was missing.\n\n   Both handlers wrapped the check in `if (expectedSecret)`, so an unset\n   CMP_CALLBACK_SECRET turned authentication off rather than turning the\n   endpoint off. /api/cmp-publish writes to the CMS, so that left content\n   creation reachable by anyone who found the URL — and nothing about the\n   running system looked wrong, which is the part that makes this worth\n   fixing rather than documenting.\n\n   lib/webhookAuth.ts now holds one verifier for both: no secret is 503\n   (refused, and logged with the variable name to set), a wrong secret is\n   401, and the comparison is constant-time so response timing does not\n   leak the secret''s length or prefix. /api/opal/create-blog already failed\n   closed and now shares the same comparison instead of its own copy.\n\n   Operationally this means CMP_CALLBACK_SECRET must be set in Vercel\n   BEFORE the CMP webhooks are registered, or the first delivery answers\n   503 and CMP marks the webhook failed. .env.example says so now.\n\ntsc and eslint clean. Not exercised against a live CMP delivery — the\nround trip needs the deployed URL.","tree":{"sha":"3cbd955b0bd22650c745eec58aadac168c24c34c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/3cbd955b0bd22650c745eec58aadac168c24c34c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/16714ae0ad2717e814d1ab61363179cf75cc0add","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/16714ae0ad2717e814d1ab61363179cf75cc0add","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKDE2NzE0YWUwYWQyNzE3ZTgxNGQxYWI2MTM2MzE3OWNmNzVjYzBhZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/7594af3c20fc5a677c52d1b4da8cd41ad9f3a0d5","sha":"7594af3c20fc5a677c52d1b4da8cd41ad9f3a0d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/7594af3c20fc5a677c52d1b4da8cd41ad9f3a0d5"}],"sha":"16714ae0ad2717e814d1ab61363179cf75cc0add","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/16714ae0ad2717e814d1ab61363179cf75cc0add"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/7594af3c20fc5a677c52d1b4da8cd41ad9f3a0d5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T11:19:44Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T11:19:44Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"feat(blog): Blog folder, article builder, and an Opal tool to write into it\n\nAnyone — Opal, a form, curl — can now create an article by describing it, without\nknowing anything about Optimizely compositions.\n\n    Root > Blog > the-road-to-a-successful-renovation\n\nArticles are BlankExperience, same as the product pages, so every section and\nblock is selectable and editable in Visual Builder.\n\nlib/blogComposition.ts turns a flat list of sections into a composition. It\nexists so the traps live in tested code rather than in a caller''s prompt:\nlayoutType \"outline\", the experience > section > row > column > component nesting\nVB needs, displayName on every section, OT_FaqBlock instead of the unplaceable\nOT_AccordionBlock, and \"#\" never reaching a url property.\n\nSection types: text, accordion, quote, callout, cards, links. A section type it\ndoes not recognise is skipped rather than throwing — a slightly-wrong payload\nfrom a model should still produce a page.\n\nField limits are enforced by truncating at a word boundary. This was not\ntheoretical: the first publish attempt failed with\n\n    Property ''Body'' must not be more than 200 characters.\n    Property ''CTA Label'' must not be more than 40 characters.\n\nand the CMS rejects the WHOLE article for one long field. A model writing prose\nwill overrun these constantly, so losing a few words beats losing the page.\n\nPOST /api/opal/create-blog validates, builds and creates. Two deliberate calls:\n\n  - It FAILS CLOSED. With OPAL_TOOL_SECRET unset it refuses every request. The\n    CMP webhooks in this repo do the opposite — they skip verification entirely\n    when their secret is missing, which leaves them open to anyone with the URL.\n    Comparison is constant-time.\n  - Articles are created as DRAFTS. Anything a language model can trigger should\n    land where a person confirms it before the public sees it; publishing stays a\n    human action in the CMS.\n\nGET /api/opal/discovery is the manifest Opal reads. Register it under\nOpal > Tools > Registries > Discovery URL. It is unauthenticated on purpose —\nit describes the interface; using it still needs the bearer token.\n\nVerified by building the renovation article through the real builder and\npublishing it: 13 sections, two accordions, three cards, both callouts.","tree":{"sha":"6a8de330b6dc5c95f17ff5107fff174847017cec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/6a8de330b6dc5c95f17ff5107fff174847017cec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/7594af3c20fc5a677c52d1b4da8cd41ad9f3a0d5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/7594af3c20fc5a677c52d1b4da8cd41ad9f3a0d5","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKDc1OTRhZjNjMjBmYzVhNjc3YzUyZDFiNGRhOGNkNDFhZDlmM2EwZDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/6f00036e8272467c8562ce25cddc7b5dfd32c5c7","sha":"6f00036e8272467c8562ce25cddc7b5dfd32c5c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/6f00036e8272467c8562ce25cddc7b5dfd32c5c7"}],"sha":"7594af3c20fc5a677c52d1b4da8cd41ad9f3a0d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/7594af3c20fc5a677c52d1b4da8cd41ad9f3a0d5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/6f00036e8272467c8562ce25cddc7b5dfd32c5c7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T13:40:00Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T13:40:00Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"fix: revert the OT_QuoteForm schema change that took the whole site down\n\nAdding `headline` and `intro` to OT_QuoteForm broke every page, not just the one\nusing the block:\n\n    Cannot query field \"headline\" on type \"OT_QuoteForm\".\n    GET /   500\n\nThe SDK builds one composition fragment per registered content type and sends it\non every request, so the moment the repo declares a property Graph has not\nindexed, every page''s query is rejected. Graph still had not picked the two\nfields up nine minutes later. That is my mistake — I treated a content-type\nchange as cheap because the CMS accepted it instantly, and never checked what it\ndoes to the query the app issues.\n\nThe rule worth keeping: a PROPERTY is a schema change and takes Graph minutes,\nduring which the site is down. A display SETTING lives in the composition, never\ntouches Graph''s schema, and applies immediately.\n\nSo the hero spacing is a setting instead. OT_PrimaryTextDefault gains\n`spacing` (default / small / none) exactly like OT_ImageDefault did, overriding\nthe size-derived vertical padding. The hero sets both the heading block and the\nillustration to `none`, which closes the gap between copy and ticks and lines the\nillustration''s top edge up with the heading — the same result the merged block\nwas for, with no schema risk.\n\nVerified with the app''s own query shape: the composition returns the QuoteForm\nwith three ticks, both fields and the CTA, and no GraphQL errors.\n\nv65 car-insurance, v66 home-insurance.\n\nThe two properties remain on the CMS type — content types have no PUT, so they\ncannot be removed, and they are harmless now that nothing queries them.","tree":{"sha":"aff0db3c0d59edccf08d85d7be0884cd008f4806","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/aff0db3c0d59edccf08d85d7be0884cd008f4806"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/6f00036e8272467c8562ce25cddc7b5dfd32c5c7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/6f00036e8272467c8562ce25cddc7b5dfd32c5c7","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKDZmMDAwMzZlODI3MjQ2N2M4NTYyY2UyNWNkZGM3YjVkZmQzMmM1Yzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/15ffa928c4e89f19d79c9506b68f6ed262f37e6f","sha":"15ffa928c4e89f19d79c9506b68f6ed262f37e6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/15ffa928c4e89f19d79c9506b68f6ed262f37e6f"}],"sha":"6f00036e8272467c8562ce25cddc7b5dfd32c5c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/6f00036e8272467c8562ce25cddc7b5dfd32c5c7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/15ffa928c4e89f19d79c9506b68f6ed262f37e6f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T13:31:46Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T13:31:46Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"fix(product): close the hero gaps — one block per column, not three\n\nThe gap between the copy and the ticks, and the illustration sitting a step\nbelow the heading, had the same cause: every block carries its own vertical\npadding, and a composition cannot reach inside a block to close it. Three blocks\nstacked in the left column meant the spacing was whatever the sum of their\npadding happened to be — PrimaryText alone contributes py-lg top and bottom.\n\nLeft column is now ONE block. OT_QuoteForm takes `headline` and `intro`, so the\nheading, copy, ticks and panel are laid out together and every gap is set in one\nplace instead of being emergent.\n\nRight column: OT_ImageDefault gains a `spacing` setting (default / small / none)\nand the hero illustration uses `none`. Its wrapper was hard-coded to py-xl,\nwhich is right for a standalone band and 64px too much beside a heading — that\nis exactly the offset in the screenshot. The setting is general, so any image in\na column can now sit flush without touching the component again.\n\nv64. Hero is col6 QuoteForm | col6 Image + Card, matching the reference.","tree":{"sha":"8b85262f47e3b3c73d00da4dcee426dd58552020","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/8b85262f47e3b3c73d00da4dcee426dd58552020"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/15ffa928c4e89f19d79c9506b68f6ed262f37e6f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/15ffa928c4e89f19d79c9506b68f6ed262f37e6f","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKDE1ZmZhOTI4YzRlODlmMTlkNzljOTUwNmI2OGY2ZWQyNjJmMzdlNmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/63db73230e6bade7bcb2d8fc08b5d43667f09908","sha":"63db73230e6bade7bcb2d8fc08b5d43667f09908","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/63db73230e6bade7bcb2d8fc08b5d43667f09908"}],"sha":"15ffa928c4e89f19d79c9506b68f6ed262f37e6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/15ffa928c4e89f19d79c9506b68f6ed262f37e6f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/63db73230e6bade7bcb2d8fc08b5d43667f09908/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T13:23:44Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T13:23:44Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"feat(cms): OT_QuoteForm — the hero quote panel, as a form\n\nYou were right that it is a form. I had built it as two bordered callouts in a\nseparate strip below the hero, which is neither the right element nor the right\nplace.\n\nThe hero now matches the reference:\n\n    col6  PrimaryText + QuoteForm      copy, ticks, the panel\n    col6  Image + Card                 illustration, adviser card beneath it\n\nQuoteForm renders the light-blue panel: two labelled inputs, the Swedish plate\nbadge on the registration field, the privacy link under it, help text under the\npersonal number, and the \"See price & subscribe\" button.\n\nIt also carries the tick list, and that is why it exists rather than being three\n`<li>`s in the hero copy: rich-text `ul` is hard-set to `list-style-type: disc`,\nso a list of typed tick characters renders a bullet AND a tick on every row —\nvisible in the screenshot as \"• ✓ 10 percent discount\". The ticks are now real\nicons.\n\nTHE PANEL COLLECTS NOTHING, deliberately. One field asks for a social security\nnumber, so:\n  - no <form> element, so there is nothing to submit and Enter does nothing\n  - no `name` on the inputs, so even inside a form they would serialise nothing\n  - autoComplete=\"off\"\n  - the button is a link to a quote journey, not a submit control\n\nA GET form would have put a personal number in the URL, in browser history and\nin every access log on the way. Making this real needs a POST endpoint over TLS\nand a retention decision — a backend call, not a block setting. The block is\nshaped so that wiring it up later is additive.\n\nPublished v63, 15 sections. The separate \"Get a quote\" strip is gone; it existed\nonly because the panel was not a block yet.","tree":{"sha":"195609d17470b066e0d650f2d29525f7d46f442b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/195609d17470b066e0d650f2d29525f7d46f442b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/63db73230e6bade7bcb2d8fc08b5d43667f09908","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/63db73230e6bade7bcb2d8fc08b5d43667f09908","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKDYzZGI3MzIzMGU2YmFkZTdiY2IyZDhmYzA4YjVkNDM2NjdmMDk5MDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/2523365a92781edb3b95767f81db9eb1da4dc297","sha":"2523365a92781edb3b95767f81db9eb1da4dc297","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/2523365a92781edb3b95767f81db9eb1da4dc297"}],"sha":"63db73230e6bade7bcb2d8fc08b5d43667f09908","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/63db73230e6bade7bcb2d8fc08b5d43667f09908"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/2523365a92781edb3b95767f81db9eb1da4dc297/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T13:17:00Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T13:17:00Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"feat(product): the rest of the Car insurance page, section for section\n\nFills in everything I had left out of the reference rather than only the parts\nthat mapped cleanly onto existing blocks.\n\nAdded:\n  - quote strip under the hero: registration number and social security number\n    panels plus the adviser card, then the CTA\n  - wide editorial photograph after the comparison table\n  - \"Compare and choose the right car insurance\" with its \"More about car\n    insurance\" link\n  - quick guide: the two side-by-side boxes, the right one carrying the quiz CTA\n  - \"Our brand insurances\" (Toyota / Lexus / Suzuki)\n  - \"Are you planning to park your car?\"\n\nv62: 16 sections, 30 blocks, all 7 images from DAM.\n\nThe CTA moved out of the hero and under the quote strip, which is where the\nreference puts it — the hero itself is heading, copy and ticks only.\n\nTwo things still differ from the screenshot and are worth naming rather than\nleaving to be spotted:\n  - the 4.5 rating is a callout, not the circled score panel the reference draws\n  - the FAQ has no \"Show more\"; all fifteen questions render\nBoth need components of their own. Say the word and I will build them the same\nway as OT_CompareTable.","tree":{"sha":"9ffb09ed77b7d559cbde9fb441f10aeeb779573d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/9ffb09ed77b7d559cbde9fb441f10aeeb779573d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/2523365a92781edb3b95767f81db9eb1da4dc297","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/2523365a92781edb3b95767f81db9eb1da4dc297","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKDI1MjMzNjVhOTI3ODFlZGIzYjk1NzY3ZjgxZGI5ZWIxZGE0ZGMyOTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/82ac0f35c1898544eed0585115034e0dd0db313e","sha":"82ac0f35c1898544eed0585115034e0dd0db313e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/82ac0f35c1898544eed0585115034e0dd0db313e"}],"sha":"2523365a92781edb3b95767f81db9eb1da4dc297","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/2523365a92781edb3b95767f81db9eb1da4dc297"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/82ac0f35c1898544eed0585115034e0dd0db313e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T13:13:02Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T13:13:02Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"feat(cms): OT_CompareTable — the car page gets the real comparison matrix\n\nI substituted three cards for the comparison table and called it an\napproximation. That was the wrong call: the table is the point of that section,\nand swapping it changed the design you specified rather than building it.\n\nOT_ComparisonTableBlock is the block that should do this and cannot be placed —\none of the seven array-of-component types with no legal position in a\ncomposition. OT_CompareTable is the same idea in the shape that actually works,\nthe one OT_FaqBlock established: `_component` + elementEnabled, with the grid\nheld as flat string arrays because an elementEnabled type may hold arrays of\nscalars but not of components.\n\n`cells` is row-major and `columnLabels.length` reconstitutes the grid. The\nbuilder takes rows as (label, [cells]) and refuses a row whose width does not\nmatch the column count — with a flat array, one short row silently shifts every\nlater cell into the wrong column, which is a wrong table rather than a broken\none, and far harder to notice.\n\nCells render as a tick for \"yes\", a dash for \"no\", and as plain text otherwise,\nso \"Optional\" works without another content type. Marks carry screen-reader text;\nthe header row''s corner cell is deliberately empty rather than captioned, since\nan invented \"Feature\" heading would show in every table summary. Horizontal\nscroll sits on the table wrapper, not the page — a twelve-row matrix cannot\nreflow on a phone.\n\nVerified through Graph exactly as the app queries it, four levels deep:\n\n    columns: 3   rows: 12   cells: 36   OK\n    Traffic injury                    yes / yes / yes\n    Collision damage to your own car  no  / no  / yes\n\nPublished v61.","tree":{"sha":"59e125ff1980904d1534893c1e864800fc512416","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/59e125ff1980904d1534893c1e864800fc512416"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/82ac0f35c1898544eed0585115034e0dd0db313e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/82ac0f35c1898544eed0585115034e0dd0db313e","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKDgyYWMwZjM1YzE4OTg1NDRlZWQwNTg1MTE1MDM0ZTBkZDBkYjMxM2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/769ab85604db2c3750fb6e6c5b322fa5f5037300","sha":"769ab85604db2c3750fb6e6c5b322fa5f5037300","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/769ab85604db2c3750fb6e6c5b322fa5f5037300"}],"sha":"82ac0f35c1898544eed0585115034e0dd0db313e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/82ac0f35c1898544eed0585115034e0dd0db313e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/769ab85604db2c3750fb6e6c5b322fa5f5037300/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T12:56:28Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T12:56:28Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"feat(product): Car insurance experience\n\nSecond product page, same structure as Home insurance and built by the same\nscript — a PRODUCTS entry plus a build function, no new machinery.\n\n    Root > Product > Car insurance    /product/car-insurance\n\nv60: 11 sections, 20 blocks, 19 FAQ rows across two accordions, all 8 images\nfrom DAM.\n\nTwo accordions rather than one. \"Motor, semi- or full insurance — what''s the\ndifference?\" is a real accordion in the reference, not four stacked text blocks,\nso it uses OT_FaqBlock the same way the FAQ does. That is the first reuse of the\nblock outside the page it was built for, and it needed no changes.\n\nThe cover-level comparison is three cards, one per level, rather than a table.\nOT_ComparisonTableBlock is the natural fit and is one of the seven array-based\nblocks with no legal position in a composition — same trap as the accordion. The\ncards carry the same information and each one is editable in Visual Builder,\nwhich a table built from unplaceable parts would not be. Worth revisiting with\nthe parallel-array shape if a real matrix is wanted.\n\nCTA placeholders resolve: the CMS turns \"/\" into a reference to the home\nexperience, so the links work rather than rendering disabled the way \"#\" did.","tree":{"sha":"2cb861797b719e5b5eb93558389faf16d59231aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/2cb861797b719e5b5eb93558389faf16d59231aa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/769ab85604db2c3750fb6e6c5b322fa5f5037300","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/769ab85604db2c3750fb6e6c5b322fa5f5037300","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKDc2OWFiODU2MDRkYjJjMzc1MGZiNmU2YzViMzIyZmE1ZjUwMzczMDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/ca2e1b6a121d25ecacf0087d34a9353d06a12835","sha":"ca2e1b6a121d25ecacf0087d34a9353d06a12835","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/ca2e1b6a121d25ecacf0087d34a9353d06a12835"}],"sha":"769ab85604db2c3750fb6e6c5b322fa5f5037300","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/769ab85604db2c3750fb6e6c5b322fa5f5037300"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/ca2e1b6a121d25ecacf0087d34a9353d06a12835/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T12:46:16Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T12:46:16Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"fix(product): CTA links were empty, which is why the hero button was disabled\n\nThe pale \"Get an offer\" button was not a styling accident. ButtonBlock renders\nitself disabled when it has a label but no URL — deliberately, so a\nmisconfigured button is visible to an editor rather than being a dead clickable\ncontrol. It had no URL.\n\nCause: `url`-typed properties will not store \"#\". The CMS discards it as invalid\nand Graph returns an empty string, so every \"#\" placeholder in the builder\nbecame nothing:\n\n    ButtonBlock  label=''Get an offer''  url=''''\n    CardBlock    ctaLabel=''Read more''  ctaUrl=''''\n\nThat also explains the home page''s card links rendering with empty hrefs — the\nsame placeholder, the same silent discard, just less visible there because a card\nwith a dead link still looks like a card.\n\nAll CTA placeholders now point at PLACEHOLDER_URL (\"/\") instead. Verified\nagainst Graph after publishing: the button has a real URL and all nine card CTAs\nresolve, none empty.\n\nHero also loses a deep empty band under the button — section spacing medium ->\nsmall and the row''s vertical padding to none. Residual height comes from\nImageBlock''s own py-xl on its standalone layout, which the composition cannot\nreach; say the word if that should be trimmed for in-column use.\n\nPublished v58.","tree":{"sha":"13f4ea4222cac09ff43de9fe56191d199d1cba9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/13f4ea4222cac09ff43de9fe56191d199d1cba9a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/ca2e1b6a121d25ecacf0087d34a9353d06a12835","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/ca2e1b6a121d25ecacf0087d34a9353d06a12835","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKGNhMmUxYjZhMTIxZDI1ZWNhY2YwMDg3ZDM0YTkzNTNkMDZhMTI4MzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/b5c782431ded2cd862a43daa34a13ef32ca9fb4f","sha":"b5c782431ded2cd862a43daa34a13ef32ca9fb4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/b5c782431ded2cd862a43daa34a13ef32ca9fb4f"}],"sha":"ca2e1b6a121d25ecacf0087d34a9353d06a12835","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/ca2e1b6a121d25ecacf0087d34a9353d06a12835"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/b5c782431ded2cd862a43daa34a13ef32ca9fb4f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T12:37:19Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T12:37:19Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"fix(faq): OT_FaqBlock — the shape that both the CMS places and the SDK queries\n\nThe questions were in Properties and the block still rendered empty. That was\nnot a styling problem, and my last two attempts were aimed at the wrong layer.\n\nThe cause, found in the SDK rather than guessed at:\n\n    // node_modules/@optimizely/cms-sdk/dist/esm/util/queryUtils.js\n    export const isExperienceComponent = (contentType) =>\n      contentType.baseType === ''_component'' && ...\n\ncreateQuery.js builds the composition''s `_IComponent` fragments from exactly\nthat filter. OT_FaqSection was `_section`, so the SDK never generated a fragment\nfor it, never selected its fields, and handed the adapter a component with no\nitems — while the CMS accepted the type and Graph returned all fifteen rows when\nasked directly. Valid in the CMS, correct in Graph, blank on the page.\n\nSo the type must be `_component` + elementEnabled, and that forbids an array of\ncomponents (\"The property ''items'' is not allowed when content type has\nElementEnabled\"). Arrays of STRINGS are permitted — verified against the live\ninstance — so OT_FaqBlock holds two parallel arrays and the adapter zips them,\npairing row N with answer N. Zipping to the shorter array is deliberate: a\nhalf-finished edit shows fewer complete rows rather than a question with an\nempty answer.\n\nVerified this time by querying the composition exactly as the app does, four\nlevels deep through section > row > column > component:\n\n    OT_FaqBlock\n      questions: 15\n      answers  : 15\n\nThat check is the thing I should have run two attempts ago; the earlier \"it\nrenders\" assumptions were never tested against the query the front end actually\nissues.\n\nReplaces OT_FaqSection, whose display template is deleted. The content type\nitself returns 409 on delete because published version 56 still references it —\nharmless, and it will drop out once that version is no longer the newest for any\nlocale.\n\nThe header comment in the builder is corrected too: it claimed `_section` was\nthe way out for all seven array-based blocks. It is not. Parallel scalar arrays\nare, absent an SDK change.\n\nPublished v57.","tree":{"sha":"b9b9f6c659335817c1ff022cb94af805e4f963a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/b9b9f6c659335817c1ff022cb94af805e4f963a2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/b5c782431ded2cd862a43daa34a13ef32ca9fb4f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/b5c782431ded2cd862a43daa34a13ef32ca9fb4f","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKGI1Yzc4MjQzMWRlZDJjZDg2MmE0M2RhYTM0YTEzZWYzMmNhOWZiNGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/20e0e031cc0744d3597ba81e56ce4c54adf4d909","sha":"20e0e031cc0744d3597ba81e56ce4c54adf4d909","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/20e0e031cc0744d3597ba81e56ce4c54adf4d909"}],"sha":"b5c782431ded2cd862a43daa34a13ef32ca9fb4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/b5c782431ded2cd862a43daa34a13ef32ca9fb4f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/20e0e031cc0744d3597ba81e56ce4c54adf4d909/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T12:17:43Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T12:17:43Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"feat(faq): purpose-built FaqAccordion, and the FAQ section back on the page\n\nNew component rather than another AccordionBlock variant. That block''s three\nborder styles all draw a bordered box around dark-on-light text; the LF pattern\nis a white card per question on a grey band, brand-blue bold question text, and\na brand rule between an open question and its answer. Reaching that through\nAccordionBlock would have meant a fourth border style plus colour overrides on\nevery part, for a look its other three styles never want.\n\nBuilt on Radix Accordion for the same reason AccordionBlock is — roving focus,\nHome/End, and the trigger/panel ARIA wiring are easy to get subtly wrong by hand.\n\nNo item cap. AccordionBlock stops at twelve and drops the rest silently, which\nwould have lost three of the fifteen questions without saying so.\n\nTwo Tailwind details that would have shipped broken:\n  - `-rotate-135` does not exist. 135deg is not in the rotate scale and there is\n    no negative variant, so the chevron would simply never have turned. Uses\n    arbitrary values.\n  - the chevron''s optical centring was a margin flip between states, which would\n    have jumped rather than eased, and moves a layout property on interaction.\n    Dropped; the rotation alone carries it.\n\nOT_FaqSection''s adapter now renders FaqAccordion. `borderStyle` from the display\ntemplate is deliberately not forwarded — this component has one row treatment by\ndesign, so there is nothing to switch.\n\nFAQ section restored to the Home insurance page: v56, 15 questions, back in\nposition between \"If something happens\" and \"Articles\". The Inspection strip\ncame back with it — reverting to v51 had removed both.","tree":{"sha":"158028c8644f4281a5de592f54eb6372f0dff3c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/158028c8644f4281a5de592f54eb6372f0dff3c6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/20e0e031cc0744d3597ba81e56ce4c54adf4d909","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/20e0e031cc0744d3597ba81e56ce4c54adf4d909","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKDIwZTBlMDMxY2MwNzQ0ZDM1OTdiYTgxZTU2Y2U0YzU0YWRmNGQ5MDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/f6a274a640d2341d50139f8f1e66eff021460570","sha":"f6a274a640d2341d50139f8f1e66eff021460570","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/f6a274a640d2341d50139f8f1e66eff021460570"}],"sha":"20e0e031cc0744d3597ba81e56ce4c54adf4d909","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/20e0e031cc0744d3597ba81e56ce4c54adf4d909"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/f6a274a640d2341d50139f8f1e66eff021460570/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T11:55:34Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T11:55:34Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"feat(cms): OT_FaqSection — a real accordion that can actually be placed\n\nThe FAQ is now the AccordionBlock component: question cards that stay collapsed\nuntil clicked, one open at a time.\n\nWHY THE RICH TEXT VERSION COULD NEVER HAVE WORKED\nOT_RichTextBlock does not render HTML. It renders through the SDK''s <RichText>,\nwhich walks a structured node tree and knows a fixed set of node types, so the\n<details>/<summary> markup I was posting as {\"html\": ...} was flattened to its\ntext before it reached the page. It looked correct in the payload and in the\nsanitiser, and no amount of CSS could have rescued it — I was styling elements\nthat never existed in the DOM. Two rounds of \"fix the FAQ design\" were spent on\nthat, and the answer was to stop pushing markup through a tree renderer.\n\nWHY A NEW CONTENT TYPE\nOT_AccordionBlock cannot be placed on a page at all:\n  - a column accepts only elementEnabled components;\n  - elementEnabled cannot be granted to it — \"The property ''items'' is not\n    allowed when content type has ElementEnabled\", and `items` is what makes it\n    an accordion;\n  - a section''s component must have baseType _section, so a _component is\n    refused with \"The component type is not based on section base type.\"\n\n`_section` is the way out, and it is a real one: verified against the live\ninstance that a _section type may hold an array of components, because the\nElementEnabled restriction simply does not apply to it. OT_FaqSection is the\naccordion re-declared with that baseType and rendered by the SAME AccordionBlock\ncomponent, so this is a placement fix, not a second implementation to keep in\nstep.\n\nThe same move would rescue the other six blocks stuck in this trap —\nFeatureGrid, StatBlock, Tabs, ComparisonTable, Disclosure, TrustRail — all of\nwhich currently exist, render, and cannot be added to a page by any editor.\n\nShips: content type, display template (cards by default, one-at-a-time), adapter,\nand all four registry entries. Pushed to the CMS via REST, so the section is\nselectable in Visual Builder and its rows editable there.\n\nRemoved the dead .ot-faq CSS and the presentational \"Did this answer help you?\"\nrow, which only existed because rich text could not host a real control. The\nsanitiser keeps details/summary for hand-authored asides, with a comment saying\nplainly that it is not what the FAQ uses.\n\nPublished v55: OT_FaqSection, 15 questions.","tree":{"sha":"da5cdbcba740593a3b7a51810656e8f3ecb23e26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/da5cdbcba740593a3b7a51810656e8f3ecb23e26"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/f6a274a640d2341d50139f8f1e66eff021460570","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/f6a274a640d2341d50139f8f1e66eff021460570","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKGY2YTI3NGE2NDBkMjM0MWQ1MDEzOWY4ZjFlNjZlZmYwMjE0NjA1NzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/2aa129929e79a572ac4a9cb7147c575c6a44a1ec","sha":"2aa129929e79a572ac4a9cb7147c575c6a44a1ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/2aa129929e79a572ac4a9cb7147c575c6a44a1ec"}],"sha":"f6a274a640d2341d50139f8f1e66eff021460570","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/f6a274a640d2341d50139f8f1e66eff021460570"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/2aa129929e79a572ac4a9cb7147c575c6a44a1ec/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T11:45:20Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T11:45:20Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"fix(product): rebuild the FAQ to match the reference\n\nThe previous pass got the container right and the rows wrong — one card with\nhairlines through it, which is why it still read as text rather than as a list.\n\nEach question is now its own white card on the grey band, with a gap between\nthem:\n\n  - question in brand blue at headline weight, chevron right-aligned\n  - the open row keeps a 2px brand rule under its header, separating question\n    from answer\n  - answer body drops back to normal prose weight and foreground colour\n  - answers split on a blank line, so a reply can run to more than one paragraph\n    as the reference does\n  - overflow hidden on the row, or the open header''s fill escapes the radius\n\nStill native <details>/<summary>: open and close, keyboard operation and the\naccessible name come from the browser, no JS. The chevron is the only restyled\npart, and its rotation is a transform that is dropped under reduced motion.\n\n\"Did this answer help you? Yes / No\" is PRESENTATIONAL. The sanitiser allows no\n<button> and there is nothing behind it, so these are spans that match the\nreference rather than controls that pretend to work. Making it real needs its own\nblock with a handler — say the word and I will build one rather than leave a\ndecoration.\n\nAll the styling is scoped to .ot-faq. The earlier version styled\n`[data-rich-text] details` generally, which would have reached every rich text\nblock on the site.\n\nVerified the sanitiser passes the whole structure — wrapper div, details,\nsummary, and the class attributes the pattern depends on — through unchanged.\n\nPublished v53: 15 rows, 15 helper rows, multi-paragraph answer rendering.","tree":{"sha":"877eb56c32bd3035b4b669670f0802c0285b8017","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/877eb56c32bd3035b4b669670f0802c0285b8017"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/2aa129929e79a572ac4a9cb7147c575c6a44a1ec","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/2aa129929e79a572ac4a9cb7147c575c6a44a1ec","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKDJhYTEyOTkyOWU3OWE1NzJhYzRhOWNiNzE0N2M1NzVjNmE0NGExZWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/adba82bd7df742eeb65f4fb471d46003875d45d0","sha":"adba82bd7df742eeb65f4fb471d46003875d45d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/adba82bd7df742eeb65f4fb471d46003875d45d0"}],"sha":"2aa129929e79a572ac4a9cb7147c575c6a44a1ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/2aa129929e79a572ac4a9cb7147c575c6a44a1ec"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/adba82bd7df742eeb65f4fb471d46003875d45d0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T11:30:03Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T11:30:03Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"fix(product): give the FAQ its card treatment\n\nThe FAQ was rendering as full-width prose with hairlines through it rather than\nas the list the design shows.\n\nThree changes:\n\n  - The section is `narrow` and centred instead of running the full container\n    width. Fifteen rows spanning 1440px read as a wall of text, not a list.\n  - The rows sit in a card: white ground, hairline, radius, padding, on the grey\n    band. The wrapper is `<div class=\"ot-faq\">` inside the rich text — `class`\n    is on the sanitiser''s attribute allowlist, which is what lets editor-authored\n    content adopt a named pattern at all.\n  - The block''s own background drops to \"none\". The card supplies the ground, so\n    a block background would have sat behind it as a second, slightly larger\n    panel.\n\nScoping the card to .ot-faq rather than styling the generic coloured rich-text\ncontainer was deliberate: the latter would have restyled every coloured rich text\nblock on the site to fix one section.\n\nTwo dead style hooks fixed along the way, both mine:\n\n  - I had written `var(--ot-border)`, which does not exist. The repo''s hairline\n    convention is fg at low alpha, as AccordionBlock does with `border-fg/10`,\n    so both rules now derive it that way.\n  - MenuDrawer''s row separators used `border-border`. `--color-border` is not\n    declared in the @theme block, so the class produced nothing and the drawer''s\n    Menu and Shortcuts rows have been running without their dividers since they\n    were added. Now `border-fg/10`.\n\nPublished v52: 15 rows, narrow, card wrapper present.","tree":{"sha":"483fc4eaff9b55f95a183275289cf54a891b779b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/483fc4eaff9b55f95a183275289cf54a891b779b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/adba82bd7df742eeb65f4fb471d46003875d45d0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/adba82bd7df742eeb65f4fb471d46003875d45d0","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKGFkYmE4MmJkN2RmNzQyZWViNjVmNGZiNDcxZDQ2MDAzODc1ZDQ1ZDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/accd1e391a5c149d244255217f0f92166fe8c4b7","sha":"accd1e391a5c149d244255217f0f92166fe8c4b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/accd1e391a5c149d244255217f0f92166fe8c4b7"}],"sha":"adba82bd7df742eeb65f4fb471d46003875d45d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/adba82bd7df742eeb65f4fb471d46003875d45d0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/accd1e391a5c149d244255217f0f92166fe8c4b7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T11:20:58Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T11:20:58Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"style: trim the heading scale and shorten the product hero\n\nHeadings were too large everywhere, and the Home insurance hero was several\nscreens deep.\n\nType scale — roughly a fifth off every heading tier:\n\n    display   clamp(3rem, 8vw, 6rem)        -> clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem)\n    hero      clamp(2.5rem, 6.25vw, 4.5rem) -> clamp(2.25rem, 5.5vw, 3.5rem)\n    headline  clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.75rem)  -> clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.25rem)\n    subhead   1.5rem                        -> 1.375rem\n    title     1.25rem                       -> 1.125rem\n\nBody and label are untouched, so the gap between heading and prose narrows\nrather than the whole page shrinking. Ordering is preserved at BOTH ends of every\nclamp — title < subhead < headline < hero < display — which is the thing a\ncareless edit here breaks, since a clamp can invert at one viewport and look\nfine at another. Checked rather than eyeballed.\n\nProduct hero: the height came from the headline, not the image. It was rendering\nat `display` (up to 6rem) because OT_PrimaryTextBlock has no hero tier; it now\nuses `headline`, and the section drops from large to medium spacing.\n\nThe image ratio is now stated as r16_9 rather than left at `auto`. That changes\nnothing visually — `auto` is absent from RATIO_MAP in cms/styling, so it fell\nthrough to undefined and ImageBlock''s 16:9 default — but the height is now\nchosen rather than inherited from a lookup miss. I had first written this up as\nthe cause of the tall hero; it was not, and the comment says so.\n\nAlso fixes the builder reading its content key from /tmp, which stopped working\nas soon as the shell was recycled. Keys are stable CMS identifiers and now live\nin the script.\n\nPublished v50.","tree":{"sha":"318d339299ec98c72bdaf34cf01a61861c6c998c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/318d339299ec98c72bdaf34cf01a61861c6c998c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/accd1e391a5c149d244255217f0f92166fe8c4b7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/accd1e391a5c149d244255217f0f92166fe8c4b7","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKGFjY2QxZTM5MWE1YzE0OWQyNDQyNTUyMTdmMGY5MjE2NmZlOGM0Yjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/1bf5cf7a2da4ca766be3585b0ee521d7f4e956e9","sha":"1bf5cf7a2da4ca766be3585b0ee521d7f4e956e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/1bf5cf7a2da4ca766be3585b0ee521d7f4e956e9"}],"sha":"accd1e391a5c149d244255217f0f92166fe8c4b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/accd1e391a5c149d244255217f0f92166fe8c4b7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/1bf5cf7a2da4ca766be3585b0ee521d7f4e956e9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T08:06:49Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T08:06:49Z","email":"tareksabbir4599@gmail.com","name":"Md. Tarek Rahman"},"message":"feat(product): Product folder plus the Home insurance experience\n\nSets up the structure for one experience per product and builds the first one.\n\n    Root\n      Product/              OT_FolderPage     /product\n        Home insurance/     BlankExperience   /product/home-insurance\n\nscripts/lf_product_page.py is the builder. Adding the next product is a PRODUCTS\nentry and a run; the page shape is shared, only the copy differs.\n\n12 sections, 27 blocks, all nested experience > section > row > column >\ncomponent so every one is selectable in Visual Builder. All 12 images resolve\nfrom DAM (placeholders for now).\n\nThree things the design could not be built the obvious way, each worth recording:\n\nEvery array-based block in this repo is unplaceable.\n  OT_AccordionBlock, OT_FeatureGridBlock, OT_StatBlock, OT_TabsBlock,\n  OT_ComparisonTableBlock, OT_DisclosureBlock and OT_TrustRail all carry an\n  array-of-component property, and that boxes them in completely:\n    - a column accepts only elementEnabled components;\n    - elementEnabled cannot be granted to them — \"The property ''items'' is not\n      allowed when content type has ElementEnabled\";\n    - and a section''s component must have baseType _section, so offering a\n      _component is refused with \"The component type is not based on section\n      base type.\"\n  There is no legal position for any of them. They exist, they render, and no\n  editor can add one to a page. I tried the section route and then tried adding\n  elementEnabled before the third error made the shape clear.\n\n  The FAQ is therefore native <details>/<summary> inside a rich text block —\n  browser-supplied open/close, keyboard operation and accessible name, no JS.\n  It also lifts the accordion block''s silent 12-item cap (MAX_ITEMS in\n  AccordionBlock.tsx drops the rest without warning), so all 15 questions from\n  the design are there. `details` and `summary` are added to the sanitiser\n  allowlist: both are inert structure, and the existing attribute allowlist\n  still limits them to class/id/data-*, so content cannot force `open`.\n\nNo block renders a tick list.\n  OT_HeroBlock.body is a plain 300-char string and rich-text `ul` is hard-set to\n  disc, so the hero is composed by hand from PrimaryText + Button + Image rather\n  than OT_HeroBlock, with literal tick characters in the rich text.\n\nThere is no breadcrumb block.\n  The trail is a small rich text line, so it is not semantic nav. Worth a real\n  block later if product pages multiply.\n\nTwo CMS API shapes learned here, both after a rejection:\n  - create is POST /v1/content with an `initialVersion` object; displayName,\n    locale, routeSegment and properties all live inside it, not at the top level\n  - `composition` is a TOP-LEVEL field on a version, a sibling of `properties`,\n    not a property — nesting it gives \"The field ''nodeType'' does not exist on\n    type ''PropertyData''\"\n\nPublished v49, indexed at /en/product/home-insurance/ — the same locale-prefix\narrangement the home page has, which getLocalizedContentByPath already falls back\nthrough.","tree":{"sha":"bbc6a3219a916209649c7ccf7200510fc1a530b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/trees/bbc6a3219a916209649c7ccf7200510fc1a530b9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/git/commits/1bf5cf7a2da4ca766be3585b0ee521d7f4e956e9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/1bf5cf7a2da4ca766be3585b0ee521d7f4e956e9","node_id":"C_kwDOUHNwENoAKDFiZjVjZjdhMmRhNGNhNzY2YmUzNTg1YjBlZTUyMWQ3ZjRlOTU2ZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commit/c46d32f122cc3aa02eb962800743daa01989847e","sha":"c46d32f122cc3aa02eb962800743daa01989847e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/c46d32f122cc3aa02eb962800743daa01989847e"}],"sha":"1bf5cf7a2da4ca766be3585b0ee521d7f4e956e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tareksabbir/Lnsfrskringar-Demo/commits/1bf5cf7a2da4ca766be3585b0ee521d7f4e956e9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83573232?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tareksabbir","id":83573232,"login":"tareksabbir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTczMjMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tareksabbir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.c