ologies-ui/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brewflocktechnologies-ui/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brewflocktechnologies-ui","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brewflocktechnologies-ui/chatplatform/commits/460b69a54f1a4a360e9d076ef137dfae82fa121e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T16:38:43Z","email":"brewflocktechnologies@gmail.com","name":"BREWFLOCK"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T16:38:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add OAuth2 backend (authservice) and platform-wide security hardening (#5)\n\n* Add OAuth2 backend (authservice) and platform-wide security hardening\n\nAuthentication and authorization:\n- New authservice: Spring Authorization Server on port 8110 with JDBC-persisted\n  clients/tokens/signing keys, tenant_id + roles claims, and a chatplatform-api\n  audience minted on every access token\n- chatservice and chatdashboardbff enforce platform JWTs via explicit decoders\n  (authservice.auth.* properties) with issuer and audience validation\n- accountservice validates JWTs in a gRPC interceptor with per-method scopes\n- allocationservice gains AUTH_MODE=jwt (JWKS-verified) alongside the default\n  trusted-header mode\n- Flyway migrations for the authservice schema (SAS tables, signing keys, users)\n\nSecurity hardening (BootUI Security + Pentesting advisors at 100/100):\n- Hardening headers (CSP, Referrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy, COOP) on all\n  chatservice/BFF chains incl. overrides of BootUI''s own header-less chains,\n  and a SecurityHeadersWebFilter for accountservice''s HTTP surface\n- Dedicated actuator security chain: health/info open, metrics requires a JWT\n- Management ports bind the container''s own interface instead of 0.0.0.0\n- Session cookie: __Host- prefix, Secure, SameSite=Lax; show-sql off in dev\n- Datasource password externalized via CHATSERVICE_DB_PASSWORD\n- Excluded Boot 4.1''s stray default reactive resource-server chain in the BFF\n- Accepted-risk dismissals baked into images (.bootui/boot-ui.yml), documented\n\nTooling:\n- Bruno collection (backend/bruno/chatplatform) covering all five services\n- localrun aggregate + compose wiring for authservice, custom postgres image\n  with tzdata-legacy, security spec in docs/spec\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix CI: drop Nx Cloud usage and apply nx format\n\n- ci.yml no longer calls nx start-ci-run / nx record / nx fix-ci, which all\n  require an Nx Cloud connection this workspace doesn''t have\n- nx format:write over the files format:check flagged (whitespace/wrapping\n  only; compose files re-validated with docker compose config)","tree":{"sha":"adfd7ad7ea784f43dc66efb03719a08d8ea6e7f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brewflocktechnologies-ui/chatplatform/git/trees/adfd7ad7ea784f43dc66efb03719a08d8ea6e7f7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brewflocktechnologies-ui/chatplatform/git/commits/460b69a54f1a4a360e9d076ef137dfae82fa121e","verification":{"payload":"tree adfd7ad7ea784f43dc66efb03719a08d8ea6e7f7\nparent 465c9680abf6a33f9f0cd179d8c71a1a45020c5e\nauthor BREWFLOCK <brewflocktechnologies@gmail.com> 1788021523 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788021523 +0530\n\nAdd OAuth2 backend (authservice) and platform-wide security hardening (#5)\n\n* Add OAuth2 backend (authservice) and platform-wide security hardening\n\nAuthentication and authorization:\n- New authservice: Spring Authorization Server on port 8110 with JDBC-persisted\n  clients/tokens/signing keys, tenant_id + roles claims, and a chatplatform-api\n  audience minted on every access token\n- chatservice and chatdashboardbff enforce platform JWTs via explicit decoders\n  (authservice.auth.* properties) with issuer and audience validation\n- accountservice validates JWTs in a gRPC interceptor with per-method scopes\n- allocationservice gains AUTH_MODE=jwt (JWKS-verified) alongside the default\n  trusted-header mode\n- Flyway migrations for the authservice schema (SAS tables, signing keys, users)\n\nSecurity hardening (BootUI Security + Pentesting advisors at 100/100):\n- Hardening headers (CSP, Referrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy, COOP) on all\n  chatservice/BFF chains incl. overrides of BootUI''s own header-less chains,\n  and a SecurityHeadersWebFilter for accountservice''s HTTP surface\n- Dedicated actuator security chain: health/info open, metrics requires a JWT\n- Management ports bind the container''s own interface instead of 0.0.0.0\n- Session cookie: __Host- prefix, Secure, SameSite=Lax; show-sql off in dev\n- Datasource password externalized via CHATSERVICE_DB_PASSWORD\n- Excluded Boot 4.1''s stray default reactive resource-server chain in the BFF\n- Accepted-risk dismissals baked into images (.bootui/boot-ui.yml), documented\n\nTooling:\n- Bruno collection (backend/bruno/chatplatform) covering all five services\n- localrun aggregate + compose wiring for authservice, custom postgres image\n  with tzdata-legacy, security spec in docs/spec\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix CI: drop Nx Cloud usage and apply nx format\n\n- ci.yml no longer calls nx start-ci-run / nx record / nx fix-ci, which all\n  require an Nx Cloud connection this workspace doesn''t have\n- nx format:write over the files format:check flagged (whitespace/wrapping\n  only; compose files re-validated with docker compose config)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkwsTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKwEQAGq2DaIm2H/wqHcaSV+8wer5\nHgkzHoPc4DayALO198mKvxj9KJ+r4FqC9d+FuJLTJotRXU/oOU61ZF9kp0JT8+bi\nlUbvlGpmtKQbw9w+5pAK5BX71mdUrkhPYXuxvHpeLTMzDKQhevrvDBoG9XIsspht\nDvgxaK+cT78NBi1cnnUHTDsalRXsK9rwLp3TbU3qQ3pdIoFg/8g8FUXXgCPFyJZX\nK5NO7es7qKatKaotI/ElVBVXIM3b7sAsL0J2NekJJ5LHReXPUNPXK9Ra4hLxq8Ag\n9SM3eGTMQ/M0XHOQGSZVJNfGN6t3lQN1Bv/BeOoCODgvZ3Z2HlTd/GHBp8eM/yiP\nwQCnA1tWL4IaUzNVrTL3isALL7hTM38qWAdO6xGHR0AfB