n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T17:39:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commit/c49911c0bf13f3c3b38bc5b0ae3adfa405c46832","node_id":"C_kwDOUHx5BtoAKGM0OTkxMWMwYmYxM2YzYzNiMzhiYzViMGFlM2FkZmE0MDVjNDY4MzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commit/ad4906c5cddfd87891731abe9e56a9b8e2b3e851","sha":"ad4906c5cddfd87891731abe9e56a9b8e2b3e851","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/ad4906c5cddfd87891731abe9e56a9b8e2b3e851"}],"sha":"c49911c0bf13f3c3b38bc5b0ae3adfa405c46832","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/c49911c0bf13f3c3b38bc5b0ae3adfa405c46832"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1575723?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa","id":1575723,"login":"juusimaa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NzU3MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/ad4906c5cddfd87891731abe9e56a9b8e2b3e851/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:12:26Z","email":"jouni.uusimaa@gmail.com","name":"Jouni Uusimaa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:12:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fold the add form and Import & export; explain a renewal of today (#84)\n\nCritique issue 5. Below the list, every visit ended with two always-open\nsections: the full add form and two columns of backup controls. Adding is\nalready one click away in the list header and on `n`, and a backup is\nsomething done now and then.\n\n- \"Add a subscription\" (desktop) and \"Import & export\" (both widths) are\n  now headings that fold open, with a chevron and aria-expanded. Bodies\n  stay mounted under `hidden`, so typed text survives closing.\n- The list''s Add button and `n` open the add form before focusing it.\n  Once open it stays open for adding several in a row.\n- With Started = today the suggested Next renewal is also today, which\n  read like a mistake. The field now says \"The first charge, on the day\n  it starts.\" This is the honest date (the plan charges the day it\n  starts), so it is explained rather than pushed a cycle ahead.\n- The Import & export hint says what it is for in plain words.\n\nBaselines regenerated in the Playwright Linux container with CI=1 and one\nworker. The full suite passes with --repeat-each=3.\n\nFrom the 2026-10-05 dashboard critique, priority issue 5.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uu@icloud.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f5ac993506855b5b0b939e843846366e2eca4082","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/git/trees/f5ac993506855b5b0b939e843846366e2eca4082"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/git/commits/ad4906c5cddfd87891731abe9e56a9b8e2b3e851","verification":{"payload":"tree f5ac993506855b5b0b939e843846366e2eca4082\nparent aec181a44806d2572a139e93e6f0712c34aacb8d\nauthor Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uusimaa@gmail.com> 1791220346 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791220346 +0300\n\nFold the add form and Import & export; explain a renewal of today (#84)\n\nCritique issue 5. Below the list, every visit ended with two always-open\nsections: the full add form and two columns of backup controls. Adding is\nalready one click away in the list header and on `n`, and a backup is\nsomething done now and then.\n\n- \"Add a subscription\" (desktop) and \"Import & export\" (both widths) are\n  now headings that fold open, with a chevron and aria-expanded. Bodies\n  stay mounted under `hidden`, so typed text survives closing.\n- The list''s Add button and `n` open the add form before focusing it.\n  Once open it stays open for adding several in a row.\n- With Started = today the suggested Next renewal is also today, which\n  read like a mistake. The field now says \"The first charge, on the day\n  it starts.\" This is the honest date (the plan charges the day it\n  starts), so it is explained rather than pushed a cycle ahead.\n- The Import & export hint says what it is for in plain words.\n\nBaselines regenerated in the Playwright Linux container with CI=1 and one\nworker. The full suite passes with --repeat-each=3.\n\nFrom the 2026-10-05 dashboard critique, priority issue 5.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uu@icloud.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw9p6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAE88QAC5Yd8AJbZjkB3AO18vA8cXw\nak1VqOtDMRWpHNewHBYEZs7d+a0xD8Fta/LJN6FdpL2jndrhdvsMLDByVd6wveWM\nu5Qeg7PTTpsXPD3D6KBTeILwd7eL2i0OQpGopXjb5fSq4KsKBG6OzUMEWptbWiWq\nbvDkotURUxrBU9lzDriv6Zz31XHaR5NNXScOj3F7Yo/IQ7g319T6rQgeeSDpLYrr\ntwiJxCdi8acJ/qtZxUydAEpAvEb+0WkWidev48WbuFdmPdlXGtyH64/zjIX3/NYs\n626DkuAI8pUrB4PpdweaumfHc+6LaXnctIWQANAckPGYd/7y8plrwTbuU/B29Yk+\nIF4Ct8VWNQbdEZdK1C9ruGhBpCT8OVKJYY0/KAvOt0fmoL1WhcG82pEzN8ZjjX3M\nIfkskJ/aAZqpAJjj4hug8NkOP/ViHthBM4iLUpCMLdgCsGZ6LdUvPb4AxwxdRJfy\nnZZlNwqLqcSUDI91LnnesI+gci4iYn+3hIr9lVMnCsa2yx20kt7LS5qXtOGDALSS\ncSXZOiADv7UDeGlwjqgHOtmVsE2EXHuvQVdxHTXHEGjwWLnyZCQfyXicZjZuki3S\nsdT8zzvDnVkVXHJQbb8AQqs/sWswGZ8McwuI2JqIxxRLHKE7Ki18chXf8y/tHWbp\npIhaPs3xghtvUY0MWB8J\n=u4ng\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T17:12:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commit/ad4906c5cddfd87891731abe9e56a9b8e2b3e851","node_id":"C_kwDOUHx5BtoAKGFkNDkwNmM1Y2RkZmQ4Nzg5MTczMWFiZTllNTZhOWI4ZTJiM2U4NTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commit/aec181a44806d2572a139e93e6f0712c34aacb8d","sha":"aec181a44806d2572a139e93e6f0712c34aacb8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/aec181a44806d2572a139e93e6f0712c34aacb8d"}],"sha":"ad4906c5cddfd87891731abe9e56a9b8e2b3e851","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/ad4906c5cddfd87891731abe9e56a9b8e2b3e851"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1575723?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa","id":1575723,"login":"juusimaa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NzU3MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/aec181a44806d2572a139e93e6f0712c34aacb8d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T13:45:29Z","email":"jouni.uusimaa@gmail.com","name":"Jouni Uusimaa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T13:45:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Keep red for the view, quiet the trial list, slim the mobile bar (#83)\n\n* Keep red for the view, quiet the trial list, slim the mobile bar\n\nCritique issue 4. Signal Red had spread to choices that cost nothing, the\ntrial banner repeated the next-charge strip at full volume, and on mobile\nthe two-button fixed bar sat over \"Cancel before it charges\" as it\nscrolled past.\n\n- Selected segments fill with Ink. Plan type, export format and conflict\n  mode are form answers; only the Monthly/Yearly period (.seg-view) keeps\n  Signal Red Deep, because it names the view the page is showing.\n- The trial banner becomes a ruled section on the page ground with Ink\n  text. Its 2px Signal Red top rule replaces the divider under the split\n  instead of stacking under it, and it closes with a 2px rule.\n- The mobile bar holds only \"Add subscription\". \"Show ended\" was a\n  duplicate of the list''s own toggle. scroll-padding-bottom keeps a\n  focused control clear of the bar.\n- DESIGN.md updated to match; visual baselines regenerated in the\n  Playwright Linux container.\n\nFrom the 2026-10-05 dashboard critique, priority issue 4.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Drop scroll-padding under the mobile bar; it made a capture flaky\n\nWith 72px of bottom scroll padding the 655px subscription list no longer\nfits the scrollport on an iPhone 13 viewport, so where Playwright scrolls\nit, and whether the runs toggle tap lands, depended on timing:\ngrouped-runs-open-mobile failed in CI on every run and passes 15/15\nwithout it. The bar is the same 72px tall it was on main, so removing the\npadding regresses nothing; keeping focus clear of it can come back as its\nown change with a test that pins the scroll position.\n\nBaselines regenerated with CI=1 and one worker, as CI runs them, and the\nfull suite passes three times over.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uu@icloud.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c37c8ce998c0767792a1822203bdf020bc269399","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/git/trees/c37c8ce998c0767792a1822203bdf020bc269399"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/git/commits/aec181a44806d2572a139e93e6f0712c34aacb8d","verification":{"payload":"tree c37c8ce998c0767792a1822203bdf020bc269399\nparent 0ed86627e755596e798483975be705f23adac1eb\nauthor Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uusimaa@gmail.com> 1791207929 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791207929 +0300\n\nKeep red for the view, quiet the trial list, slim the mobile bar (#83)\n\n* Keep red for the view, quiet the trial list, slim the mobile bar\n\nCritique issue 4. Signal Red had spread to choices that cost nothing, the\ntrial banner repeated the next-charge strip at full volume, and on mobile\nthe two-button fixed bar sat over \"Cancel before it charges\" as it\nscrolled past.\n\n- Selected segments fill with Ink. Plan type, export format and conflict\n  mode are form answers; only the Monthly/Yearly period (.seg-view) keeps\n  Signal Red Deep, because it names the view the page is showing.\n- The trial banner becomes a ruled section on the page ground with Ink\n  text. Its 2px Signal Red top rule replaces the divider under the split\n  instead of stacking under it, and it closes with a 2px rule.\n- The mobile bar holds only \"Add subscription\". \"Show ended\" was a\n  duplicate of the list''s own toggle. scroll-padding-bottom keeps a\n  focused control clear of the bar.\n- DESIGN.md updated to match; visual baselines regenerated in the\n  Playwright Linux container.\n\nFrom the 2026-10-05 dashboard critique, priority issue 4.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Drop scroll-padding under the mobile bar; it made a capture flaky\n\nWith 72px of bottom scroll padding the 655px subscription list no longer\nfits the scrollport on an iPhone 13 viewport, so where Playwright scrolls\nit, and whether the runs toggle tap lands, depended on timing:\ngrouped-runs-open-mobile failed in CI on every run and passes 15/15\nwithout it. The bar is the same 72px tall it was on main, so removing the\npadding regresses nothing; keeping focus clear of it can come back as its\nown change with a test that pins the scroll position.\n\nBaselines regenerated with CI=1 and one worker, as CI runs them, and the\nfull suite passes three times over.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uu@icloud.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw6n5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALYEQAA1Q6HIkbCFrBSbX3OH58Gv1\nCysLtJIATuWy+a05/+2Lh+F1/R+mt7VZKOD22oYHrzykWmF6CcwlSs8k2bjAG54v\npqORdbPHmNMcOT11cqYAtrNScjjI1+BihILETxiRNivwx2CDKJuIGHFN2F6DMIpw\nD1rzJUBpoHk9gzDPSloxZt+95PCqQ8Z17/U1hEutWIqSAgbIrtG0cinnDnLmKQoG\ndYao9P/H0dAE61vuQMNCGrckJi2bo+1PupAco6Mpd7kuD2BY3+tuZmH06EhWNCoi\nHhzAsb6AEgeU0pNWiSVAfyXT8lnRJhqnwRG5lZ69Pii/0a5OVujqiSvFIx9jt/S2\nszPs7yEd0YOaQ4bcrp25egzVesbQYZ8LlnEzyivgCgQvIWPrsMGYcRUekn4rpCiE\n5YV5MnOIO/UINcfl3Q19W54TDOeFRDyQs0QRX1yTqR+mZ2V3iff2tr1q+1dYHepT\n6tE+VuewhgMzreZoM3D1R0TTgwRAjSSJ7Uc3qzrTw0BoH3YZUg0Rp4HldIMwtqG2\nRh6cRmfSG4y3/QCGWgvcdyyncigR6H+caIV2L/nnrsmRdiBUExdJ6SVqaM5ebQ3j\nVDgVt1bbZSZdJ3Gkn+nA19yvsQevkCTQIYrVOFYZIRk2g1ud8aB6cXtw+SZck2Ut\n0rKdC6S6iIuDaGLwyVdX\n=gtbt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T13:45:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commit/aec181a44806d2572a139e93e6f0712c34aacb8d","node_id":"C_kwDOUHx5BtoAKGFlYzE4MWE0NDgwNmQyNTcyYTEzOWU5M2U2ZjA3MTJjMzRhYWNiOGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commit/0ed86627e755596e798483975be705f23adac1eb","sha":"0ed86627e755596e798483975be705f23adac1eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/0ed86627e755596e798483975be705f23adac1eb"}],"sha":"aec181a44806d2572a139e93e6f0712c34aacb8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/aec181a44806d2572a139e93e6f0712c34aacb8d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1575723?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa","id":1575723,"login":"juusimaa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NzU3MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/0ed86627e755596e798483975be705f23adac1eb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T13:24:11Z","email":"jouni.uusimaa@gmail.com","name":"Jouni Uusimaa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T13:24:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Say what went wrong and what to do, not the HTTP status (#82)\n\nError copy printed raw codes (\"Request failed: 500\", \"503 — the server\ndidn''t respond.\", \"(422)\"). Those mean nothing to the reader, and the load\nbanner said \"didn''t respond\" for any status, even when the server had\nanswered with a refusal.\n\n- A response with no server message now gets a plain cause by status\n  (server problem, too many requests, no permission, no longer exists).\n- describeWriteError adds the next step: check the connection when the\n  request never arrived, try again in a moment for 5xx/429, and nothing\n  extra for a refusal, since the server''s own message says what to fix.\n  It takes an outcome (\"Nothing was imported\") so every write site uses it.\n- The load banner, account dialog, import/export, add form and row editor\n  go through it instead of putting the status in the copy themselves.\n- Login catches network failures instead of showing \"Failed to fetch\".\n\nFrom the 2026-10-05 dashboard critique, priority issue 3.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uu@icloud.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f0fffadc44d4769b3bb8ad35d0be081c93a826fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/git/trees/f0fffadc44d4769b3bb8ad35d0be081c93a826fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/git/commits/0ed86627e755596e798483975be705f23adac1eb","verification":{"payload":"tree f0fffadc44d4769b3bb8ad35d0be081c93a826fd\nparent 4568f0ae9aa99afe8e216531aa132cbec63ec7cb\nauthor Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uusimaa@gmail.com> 1791206651 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791206651 +0300\n\nSay what went wrong and what to do, not the HTTP status (#82)\n\nError copy printed raw codes (\"Request failed: 500\", \"503 — the server\ndidn''t respond.\", \"(422)\"). Those mean nothing to the reader, and the load\nbanner said \"didn''t respond\" for any status, even when the server had\nanswered with a refusal.\n\n- A response with no server message now gets a plain cause by status\n  (server problem, too many requests, no permission, no longer exists).\n- describeWriteError adds the next step: check the connection when the\n  request never arrived, try again in a moment for 5xx/429, and nothing\n  extra for a refusal, since the server''s own message says what to fix.\n  It takes an outcome (\"Nothing was imported\") so every write site uses it.\n- The load banner, account dialog, import/export, add form and row editor\n  go through it instead of putting the status in the copy themselves.\n- Login catches network failures instead of showing \"Failed to fetch\".\n\nFrom the 2026-10-05 dashboard critique, priority issue 3.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uu@icloud.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw6T7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFk0QAAK4aVpH3+A95rjmIg69VoBl\nMLPl3UVMAF/SIR0uuj4nQyEuwEaSJLMndadrojmhkTrsd/JSj6jLT2Ojw1TEDXq9\nUyZ6smSKGsoC2Kwe3DIncdF7IPxWkkqg34JWY+uRzJy6r3YZUaBYjQfDU6mA1Mo8\nO67tKURwkPzRBNbw/i8e+qwJ2pCoGCg/pxI7GboDDYAR0TqTcO/zWdfb89SfqDNO\ngkz6xM7tClPIgnzSwOJipAW0kl0ImZS/8RIk/MrFJZvKg19A6sGGi4YVAMEIUcR/\nbSb1YiHExI4IOkkiDMhGqHXlKzMWf7M+7ncaKnCVqK1CKvngo+4gSwkqjykoWMQX\nN7f90nSujnGfPAsV4hwrlttqDG9GbJxgA3ahiW33XtMs63GKub0BeRidvaMwrdLO\ndYlc7eMVE7tY71BFeilG3omfUcJuuGFqkL7xXlVYSo12JlVLSlleDolNYGdgXNmM\nYBls7pQUa7hi5SkGl+VbyS4vxn7Ksg+2oivLRnIhsMdGT8sWJ3HBKadirMzGvM+g\nJJpshvF7sEfL52IV9ZSVcXPLfB8Iu8rMRKo5MaeX/83TYcg3BmXKkXIfNIMfpV2u\nF