}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa","id":1575723,"login":"juusimaa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NzU3MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/fa14df288217c5a96c5fb7171ba7ba44877171bc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T08:03:10Z","email":"jouni.uusimaa@gmail.com","name":"Jouni Uusimaa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T08:03:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Write up TODO items 13-15 as fixed (#41)\n\nAll three landed on 2026-09-08. Moves them out of the open list into the\n\"Fixed on 2026-09-08\" section, in the file''s existing style, and rewrites\nthe intro paragraph that described them as open.\n\nEach note records what the fix was and why it took the shape it did -- for\nitem 14 in particular, which fields deliberately kept a plain `str`:\ncurrent_password, AccountDelete.password and POST /token all verify an\nexisting password rather than setting a new one, so a byte limit on any of\nthem would have locked out exactly the accounts whose stored password is\nover 72 bytes.\n\nAlso written up, without a number because it was never a gap in the API:\nthe backend''s .env lookup escaping the backend directory and loading\nCompose''s root .env instead. It landed the same day and out of the same\nwork, and the failure it produces is far enough from its cause to be worth\nrecording.\n\nItem 12''s existing note is updated where item 15 changed the test it cites,\nso the cross-reference stays accurate.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uu@icloud.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2b59009101a52c388b0b428364c821020c1172fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/git/trees/2b59009101a52c388b0b428364c821020c1172fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/git/commits/fa14df288217c5a96c5fb7171ba7ba44877171bc","verification":{"payload":"tree 2b59009101a52c388b0b428364c821020c1172fe\nparent 0906b82ea5210e144e51b094c835f65d37217f6d\nauthor Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uusimaa@gmail.com> 1788854590 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788854590 +0300\n\nWrite up TODO items 13-15 as fixed (#41)\n\nAll three landed on 2026-09-08. Moves them out of the open list into the\n\"Fixed on 2026-09-08\" section, in the file''s existing style, and rewrites\nthe intro paragraph that described them as open.\n\nEach note records what the fix was and why it took the shape it did -- for\nitem 14 in particular, which fields deliberately kept a plain `str`:\ncurrent_password, AccountDelete.password and POST /token all verify an\nexisting password rather than setting a new one, so a byte limit on any of\nthem would have locked out exactly the accounts whose stored password is\nover 72 bytes.\n\nAlso written up, without a number because it was never a gap in the API:\nthe backend''s .env lookup escaping the backend directory and loading\nCompose''s root .env instead. It landed the same day and out of the same\nwork, and the failure it produces is far enough from its cause to be worth\nrecording.\n\nItem 12''s existing note is updated where item 15 changed the test it cites,\nso the cross-reference stays accurate.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uu@icloud.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqn8E+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7iIQAHfK+TOXdflK39V7rcuaGDYE\nLaKZb6VF06UkCZKaUtn7TRg+UnqBQAha70r1w87q2jVYlCYXrgInk/pcKLzC/tRW\nauUYvifNl9cHjFObyhash7a80OILo9y7nIjA6QpmldE03SyGbiLM0SfYEucUpfgi\nHbBpje3NIcLv1/JcO24ad/+bRt3eyvGQ/KgMv4KPc7gL/d11qgBDjfiERtw5iQyH\nGD0gcG+c7EvPCH3kopqOELrOTOPK8wfPHscJMXAzcr4bUS4Up0rbapQHFqkhqtRO\nYVgwOUb0XFDzXiCJDgHOeAw7UvEk301zvMfiumAWqiF6vSNopzJmWNai9xJGEF96\nVsOTKPPjDDlGCUt4FFZXWsmBz1lqf6HIbGbZ5AWQoYYGapPV7Pu/Zsw7SaEllmMI\nA264/SXGmgFMPS/OIH708A+zg6GsElWzoUpCNpWktEQ8xjBgdm00aeQq3fm2DP1z\nCj4TY/UBNLr8tQSLXeX6Lcgv3sYkgrXcUFlyJODCalrBRmqGEug12vj2PZiR0nDW\n/LyEthdTVYHc0UCZyQjWbVoxS0qFL59Gq8+7tH/+WQxfrLASenMRfc0W/okSlYFk\nxgjpt0hqY1+6+LnOzPF9GaqrenG2gUHSZYYGFAYzqidE0IPukcmVdYo/ky0erJxq\nYD3eiCDf0CG0JawDDVww\n=natG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T08:03:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commit/fa14df288217c5a96c5fb7171ba7ba44877171bc","node_id":"C_kwDOUHx5BtoAKGZhMTRkZjI4ODIxN2M1YTk2YzVmYjcxNzFiYTdiYTQ0ODc3MTcxYmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commit/0906b82ea5210e144e51b094c835f65d37217f6d","sha":"0906b82ea5210e144e51b094c835f65d37217f6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/0906b82ea5210e144e51b094c835f65d37217f6d"}],"sha":"fa14df288217c5a96c5fb7171ba7ba44877171bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/fa14df288217c5a96c5fb7171ba7ba44877171bc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1575723?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa","id":1575723,"login":"juusimaa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NzU3MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/0906b82ea5210e144e51b094c835f65d37217f6d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T07:53:07Z","email":"jouni.uusimaa@gmail.com","name":"Jouni Uusimaa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T07:53:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Pin the backend''s .env lookup to backend/.env (#40)\n\n`load_dotenv()` was called with no arguments in database.py and cache.py, so\ndotenv searched upward from the working directory and loaded the first .env\nit found. That reads backend/.env only when the process is started from\nbackend/. Started from anywhere else -- or from a git worktree, which has no\nbackend/.env of its own -- the search climbs past the backend directory and\nlands on the root .env.\n\nThose are two different files for two different jobs. backend/.env supplies\nthe variables the app reads when run directly on the host, and\nbackend/.env.example documents exactly that set. The root .env is Compose''s\n${VAR} substitution source, carrying values meant for containers -- among\nthem INVITE_CODE, which gates /register. Loading it into a test run turns\n~47 tests red at once, none of which are about invite codes, and the cause\nis a long way from the symptom.\n\nPin both calls to backend/.env, derived from __file__ rather than the\nworking directory. Inside the image this resolves to /app/.env, which does\nnot exist, so the call stays the no-op it already was there -- Compose\ninjects the real environment, and load_dotenv never overrode real variables\nanyway.\n\nAlso blank INVITE_CODE explicitly in the test suite. The pin stops a\nneighbouring file supplying one, but an exported shell variable still could,\nand load_dotenv would not have overridden that either. Blanked rather than\ndefaulted, since the value being defended against is one that is already\nset; an empty value reads as \"disabled\", which is what a deployment with\nopen signup runs. test_invite_code.py patches main.INVITE_CODE directly and\nis unaffected.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uu@icloud.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b98491ea41984b65ffed784f7c22b943b7cd76d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/git/trees/b98491ea41984b65ffed784f7c22b943b7cd76d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/git/commits/0906b82ea5210e144e51b094c835f65d37217f6d","verification":{"payload":"tree b98491ea41984b65ffed784f7c22b943b7cd76d8\nparent 95df66e7f2ac74030447d9db21dd2075b0fc980e\nauthor Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uusimaa@gmail.com> 1788853987 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788853987 +0300\n\nPin the backend''s .env lookup to backend/.env (#40)\n\n`load_dotenv()` was called with no arguments in database.py and cache.py, so\ndotenv searched upward from the working directory and loaded the first .env\nit found. That reads backend/.env only when the process is started from\nbackend/. Started from anywhere else -- or from a git worktree, which has no\nbackend/.env of its own -- the search climbs past the backend directory and\nlands on the root .env.\n\nThose are two different files for two different jobs. backend/.env supplies\nthe variables the app reads when run directly on the host, and\nbackend/.env.example documents exactly that set. The root .env is Compose''s\n${VAR} substitution source, carrying values meant for containers -- among\nthem INVITE_CODE, which gates /register. Loading it into a test run turns\n~47 tests red at once, none of which are about invite codes, and the cause\nis a long way from the symptom.\n\nPin both calls to backend/.env, derived from __file__ rather than the\nworking directory. Inside the image this resolves to /app/.env, which does\nnot exist, so the call stays the no-op it already was there -- Compose\ninjects the real environment, and load_dotenv never overrode real variables\nanyway.\n\nAlso blank INVITE_CODE explicitly in the test suite. The pin stops a\nneighbouring file supplying one, but an exported shell variable still could,\nand load_dotenv would not have overridden that either. Blanked rather than\ndefaulted, since the value being defended against is one that is already\nset; an empty value reads as \"disabled\", which is what a deployment with\nopen signup runs. test_invite_code.py patches main.INVITE_CODE directly and\nis unaffected.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uu@icloud.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqn77jCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAD8YQAK8JWdqpKgwZY/KMXKK2A1RL\nj6uzI7lrZhah63AJOSVXMt6KWiZFgcYO2EmZ6/wPI+pk2bPfwn2yTRnCPu4T6cJt\nYS3zIwpf9Zk6IwezK86yQUNalJ1/mHMgdGM/VnCwC2SgzjkaGjQK9EC+F/P+F3sG\nk0nwahKO6abcByU7tEA5nqbeawE6Zm7MnmNVW1113SCFZszmMW2bXlikbu5p83MG\n3T02nd74MlvSQh4X06083og+7ZGLxXXGNyUaHgjD4Uj0FIup3RMveni17W5Y96Ky\nVorzAwTZiFRA16wIatgWRNstmwYQty2kQ9ar/evCDop+hSPEnKtL+cPT++bpCikU\n7zZAAWFDgaq3tInaQic8YKsu5KuyIuj2uUzTRzHTM0haZRAUa15LjTBATPzD3wkQ\nnCsoBVTJCXtTSTRSJ81LbTgbyEsh9zLv3Lgrc7lHrrwVYf8VvXpSMOYP7RC30zwx\ncCif2i03HBXOgaB9upKd4gq81vXS32CAsvueXWbjrmBxAe5vMxC4SLXWjylXcQnc\n+5xNwnHbUPwQeqI2nTwxhjiMe1d+5ECjjbdJTQBBstRPOR+43NuN+zPjKfsbH60H\nuQIY4lD7h/dOUNy+tIUeCTOtq3qqcRajQozFpayUS/DBTmXUHX4mi9R5WtFqrFDn\ngCIOXZetFPK4cowF2xlW\n=AeE2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T07:53:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commit/0906b82ea5210e144e51b094c835f65d37217f6d","node_id":"C_kwDOUHx5BtoAKDA5MDZiODJlYTUyMTBlMTQ0ZTUxYjA5NGM4MzVmNjVkMzcyMTdmNmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commit/95df66e7f2ac74030447d9db21dd2075b0fc980e","sha":"95df66e7f2ac74030447d9db21dd2075b0fc980e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/95df66e7f2ac74030447d9db21dd2075b0fc980e"}],"sha":"0906b82ea5210e144e51b094c835f65d37217f6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/0906b82ea5210e144e51b094c835f65d37217f6d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1575723?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa","id":1575723,"login":"juusimaa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NzU3MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/95df66e7f2ac74030447d9db21dd2075b0fc980e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T07:41:20Z","email":"jouni.uusimaa@gmail.com","name":"Jouni Uusimaa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T07:41:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Enforce the password limit in bytes, not characters (TODO item 14) (#39)\n\nUserCreate.password and PasswordChange.new_password used\nField(max_length=72), which counts characters. bcrypt''s limit is 72\nbytes, and the pinned bcrypt 4.2.0 does not raise past it -- it\nsilently truncates before hashing. A password like 25 copies of \"€\"\n(75 bytes, 25 characters) passed the schema and was hashed short, with\nno error on either side.\n\nDeclares a shared Password alias (mirroring SubscriptionName and Cost\nabove it) that checks the UTF-8 encoded length instead, and applies it\nto both fields so the rule can''t be walked around by editing one of\nthem. Also corrects the docstring''s false claim that bcrypt raises on\noversized input.\n\n/token (OAuth2PasswordRequestForm) is untouched: existing users whose\nstored password already exceeds 72 bytes must keep authenticating,\nsince bcrypt truncates identically on hash and verify.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uu@icloud.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1e093ef08aee253ab977cfa7e8e6c285d08d1b04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/git/trees/1e093ef08aee253ab977cfa7e8e6c285d08d1b04"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/git/commits/95df66e7f2ac74030447d9db21dd2075b0fc980e","verification":{"payload":"tree 1e093ef08aee253ab977cfa7e8e6c285d08d1b04\nparent 637babae0ff6773237fd61bc3298304a5a99026d\nauthor Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uusimaa@gmail.com> 1788853280 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788853280 +0300\n\nEnforce the password limit in bytes, not characters (TODO item 14) (#39)\n\nUserCreate.password and PasswordChange.new_password used\nField(max_length=72), which counts characters. bcrypt''s limit is 72\nbytes, and the pinned bcrypt 4.2.0 does not raise past it -- it\nsilently truncates before hashing. A password like 25 copies of \"€\"\n(75 bytes, 25 characters) passed the schema and was hashed short, with\nno error on either side.\n\nDeclares a shared Password alias (mirroring SubscriptionName and Cost\nabove it) that checks the UTF-8 encoded length instead, and applies it\nto both fields so the rule can''t be walked around by editing one of\nthem. Also corrects the docstring''s false claim that bcrypt raises on\noversized input.\n\n/token (OAuth2PasswordRequestForm) is untouched: existing users whose\nstored password already exceeds 72 bytes must keep authenticating,\nsince bcrypt truncates identically on hash and verify.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uu@icloud.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqn7wgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3foQAE+zIgSSq/PZ0XAZ1fi0+Djg\nHfbXZuuY8BiLRpszWHIpKOAHnBzLFMlXwEIcSoV4/n7DoDVgegket7f8MJtDt20H\nSR/Gi6iUBm/u+YMt6sfswr2rzqJuac9rE7vptjQOsJGaYdQVSS4zf8SmyQ7W/gMk\nvwxl4NMYsxPiWDcNJvtHcIfAUz4kWch2xRcw6pOF/ZRV4wdjIta49pAPvOa1YqaI\nka+wICe69GliDeMLLBdAfNy6JKefudmLkN5Mx0B05iZTRuHv4Q9oR8VEqL5gVxeu\noF1TnQuhQHSSWU39p3UfkgtO2NMAdoMGbRV4oc4fSGf4XS5PSlsScTDEGu7oShL3\n4CWTVT8FleOKa4kCO5Opnj6vQBCL7+VkbBMsnFd4yrf1mLMXdu3WE6nT478YGQdP\naCtuveGcOnZ2rfcOszAdOeh2y1xLRHmkEK51boQaEiLqdN8tfQ4C0XtGHzaCvls4\nJ1JHCvLaKm6UJRGAQYrECgYm2H4f15q3oBSNn4He2CyX0gJW9Rvb8XUE33QdZQ0a\ncF4GG7RQbsEFytyHZ58DNBFU+NkttWDiklHpzJxBanEQRP4H4I0OtuY7bRu1aZbv\nbSwar1CV0pihIVd5+ROR4pn6LbzwHGm+MQdSycPl52EUJcHDmhDg6oMYld0G+Z/Y\nX1GrW9F/I3BRo17cjLhR\n=8isn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T07:41:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commit/95df66e7f2ac74030447d9db21dd2075b0fc980e","node_id":"C_kwDOUHx5BtoAKDk1ZGY2NmU3ZjJhYzc0MDMwNDQ3ZDlkYjIxZGQyMDc1YjBmYzk4MGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commit/637babae0ff6773237fd61bc3298304a5a99026d","sha":"637babae0ff6773237fd61bc3298304a5a99026d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/637babae0ff6773237fd61bc3298304a5a99026d"}],"sha":"95df66e7f2ac74030447d9db21dd2075b0fc980e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/95df66e7f2ac74030447d9db21dd2075b0fc980e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1575723?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa","id":1575723,"login":"juusimaa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NzU3MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/637babae0ff6773237fd61bc3298304a5a99026d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T07:37:23Z","email":"jouni.uusimaa@gmail.com","name":"Jouni Uusimaa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T07:37:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Reject costs with more than two decimal places (TODO item 13) (#38)\n\nCost bounded gt=0 and le=99999999.99 but not scale, so 0.001 passed\nvalidation and Numeric(10, 2) silently rounded it to 0.00 on commit --\na row that passed the positive-cost check ending up at the value that\ncheck exists to forbid, with every total computed over it short by the\ndifference. Adding decimal_places=2 to the shared Cost annotation\ncloses this on all three paths that accept a cost: POST /subscriptions,\nPUT /subscriptions/{id}, and POST /import.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uu@icloud.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9eb965ac64a4838fd9d06369add01763f72af933","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/git/trees/9eb965ac64a4838fd9d06369add01763f72af933"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/git/commits/637babae0ff6773237fd61bc3298304a5a99026d","verification":{"payload":"tree 9eb965ac64a4838fd9d06369add01763f72af933\nparent 0eb66883721e21d7973d051c7bf16eceab6b3a8e\nauthor Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uusimaa@gmail.com> 1788853043 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788853043 +0300\n\nReject costs with more than two decimal places (TODO item 13) (#38)\n\nCost bounded gt=0 and le=99999999.99 but not scale, so 0.001 passed\nvalidation and Numeric(10, 2) silently rounded it to 0.00 on commit --\na row that passed the positive-cost check ending up at the value that\ncheck exists to forbid, with every total computed over it short by the\ndifference. Adding decimal_places=2 to the shared Cost annotation\ncloses this on all three paths that accept a cost: POST /subscriptions,\nPUT /subscriptions/{id}, and POS