ps://github.com/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commit/75805aa9bbeb04f03a10e6957504d1c025bb84f9","sha":"75805aa9bbeb04f03a10e6957504d1c025bb84f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/75805aa9bbeb04f03a10e6957504d1c025bb84f9"}],"sha":"3b4a792e30c88b611bdbe0c70e679658ef6dda30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/3b4a792e30c88b611bdbe0c70e679658ef6dda30"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1575723?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa","id":1575723,"login":"juusimaa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NzU3MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/75805aa9bbeb04f03a10e6957504d1c025bb84f9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T04:52:44Z","email":"jouni.uusimaa@gmail.com","name":"Jouni Uusimaa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T04:52:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix check-then-insert races on register, categories and subscriptions (#27)\n\nregister and create_category checked \"does this exist?\" then inserted, so\ntwo concurrent identical requests could both pass the check and the second\nwould trip a unique constraint as a raw, unhandled IntegrityError (500)\ninstead of the clean 400/409 the sequential path returns. ensure_category\nhad the same shape, called from create_subscription and update_subscription.\n\nregister/create_category now catch IntegrityError around their commit and\nconvert it to the same 400/409 via a new crud.DuplicateError. ensure_category''s\nrace gets a different fix, since its sequential \"already exists\" branch isn''t\nan error at all: create_subscription/update_subscription retry once on\nIntegrityError, reusing whichever category spelling actually won instead of\nsurfacing an error for something that isn''t a conflict from that route''s\npoint of view.\n\nTODO.md item 5.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uu@icloud.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"61c01bd9ac6e33808c0ea920322f50212429c53a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/git/trees/61c01bd9ac6e33808c0ea920322f50212429c53a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/git/commits/75805aa9bbeb04f03a10e6957504d1c025bb84f9","verification":{"payload":"tree 61c01bd9ac6e33808c0ea920322f50212429c53a\nparent 651a59eb5e233899fe99067296a887d2465aa389\nauthor Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uusimaa@gmail.com> 1788843164 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788843164 +0300\n\nFix check-then-insert races on register, categories and subscriptions (#27)\n\nregister and create_category checked \"does this exist?\" then inserted, so\ntwo concurrent identical requests could both pass the check and the second\nwould trip a unique constraint as a raw, unhandled IntegrityError (500)\ninstead of the clean 400/409 the sequential path returns. ensure_category\nhad the same shape, called from create_subscription and update_subscription.\n\nregister/create_category now catch IntegrityError around their commit and\nconvert it to the same 400/409 via a new crud.DuplicateError. ensure_category''s\nrace gets a different fix, since its sequential \"already exists\" branch isn''t\nan error at all: create_subscription/update_subscription retry once on\nIntegrityError, reusing whichever category spelling actually won instead of\nsurfacing an error for something that isn''t a conflict from that route''s\npoint of view.\n\nTODO.md item 5.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uu@icloud.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqn5ScCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXzwQAAWjlFWH/jqLp0BqNebW09t2\ndNjOTXkqhrakfhPQnUX/KQyn/g4XVQPyG10cVT+3DE+5/smFzd/4KqhaPDimM4+N\niuYO/LvK3WS0cziPUrjPVMMa9nkFmmHAjC24nwrMqB0tF+oMVGzfU7hkg/9+H02Q\nPwfd1jdLH+KpachnUcPvtWj+N4vb8IZT8oxPQ6iqEljbDFVr/29WSZu9cZa1fLG/\nsfeAS6aJGVGTkvJ34GccXue4S5o6BncZElcilaDB/y9WkmuzVYzL74cz4tMWwbSl\nx2UHCHRaaLW6nD0beZHJlkuH2/V72lzOaFiafKPVCDSJ3Hb1T61MZrI8saM11D+r\nq0rhkw7DO8SWOng6A1ZRy8piseek36/isX+8UPC3jTkUC93YJrp2ZtztGc6Ozpkg\n/lwjbr9UudZA0/5h7KrFDCpXrUPLZV+a2VTaCLFgo00ZQTvKd7LDFMpl48p0dXAN\nNGz8tDbxuQYPYXrXVA5Wonx6xNzJA3nVc/nXJMPCBj0JKB88uBNgsyBZ2tJbib2k\nDOdWmA/hPpMzep9AVBPqPZ8rLAzgLS34WqNupaW5qzGRvm2v2GkIDG2qLCkQ1R+/\nTJkeqF8xd44d5K3IBwGwXt9XmreTuLusX2WmpIiHzhFIDEr9xS/IwdYfTriv60fp\nI7jj4tWa+/z/OoMHA5xf\n=oewl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T04:52:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commit/75805aa9bbeb04f03a10e6957504d1c025bb84f9","node_id":"C_kwDOUHx5BtoAKDc1ODA1YWE5YmJlYjA0ZjAzYTEwZTY5NTc1MDRkMWMwMjViYjg0Zjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commit/651a59eb5e233899fe99067296a887d2465aa389","sha":"651a59eb5e233899fe99067296a887d2465aa389","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/651a59eb5e233899fe99067296a887d2465aa389"}],"sha":"75805aa9bbeb04f03a10e6957504d1c025bb84f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/75805aa9bbeb04f03a10e6957504d1c025bb84f9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1575723?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa","id":1575723,"login":"juusimaa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NzU3MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/651a59eb5e233899fe99067296a887d2465aa389/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T16:14:50Z","email":"jouni.uusimaa@gmail.com","name":"Jouni Uusimaa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T16:14:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix blue subscription list text on iOS Safari (#26)\n\n* Disable iOS Safari data detection to fix blue list text\n\niOS Safari auto-wraps recognized text (dates, numbers) in subscription\nrows into native tel:/data-detector links, which pick up modernist.css''s\nglobal `a { color: var(--color-accent) }` rule and render blue -- instead\nof the normal text color used on desktop, where no such detection exists.\n\nFixes #25\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix actual cause of blue mobile list text: unset button color\n\nformat-detection didn''t fix it (confirmed on a real iPhone) -- and\ncouldn''t have, since this app''s accent color is red-orange, not blue.\nThe real cause: .mobile-row is a bare <button> that never gets the .btn\nclass, so it''s the only interactive element in the app without an\nexplicit `color`. iOS Safari''s UA stylesheet renders unstyled buttons in\nits system tint blue; desktop browsers default button text to black,\nwhich is why this only showed up on mobile.\n\nFixes #25\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uu@icloud.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fbfc8009cc02a83ffda5916db8d2c84ea911fced","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/git/trees/fbfc8009cc02a83ffda5916db8d2c84ea911fced"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/git/commits/651a59eb5e233899fe99067296a887d2465aa389","verification":{"payload":"tree fbfc8009cc02a83ffda5916db8d2c84ea911fced\nparent 566f1d38266673745b6b06b2abe8f0cbfee3b62d\nauthor Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uusimaa@gmail.com> 1788797690 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788797690 +0300\n\nFix blue subscription list text on iOS Safari (#26)\n\n* Disable iOS Safari data detection to fix blue list text\n\niOS Safari auto-wraps recognized text (dates, numbers) in subscription\nrows into native tel:/data-detector links, which pick up modernist.css''s\nglobal `a { color: var(--color-accent) }` rule and render blue -- instead\nof the normal text color used on desktop, where no such detection exists.\n\nFixes #25\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix actual cause of blue mobile list text: unset button color\n\nformat-detection didn''t fix it (confirmed on a real iPhone) -- and\ncouldn''t have, since this app''s accent color is red-orange, not blue.\nThe real cause: .mobile-row is a bare <button> that never gets the .btn\nclass, so it''s the only interactive element in the app without an\nexplicit `color`. iOS Safari''s UA stylesheet renders unstyled buttons in\nits system tint blue; desktop browsers default button text to black,\nwhich is why this only showed up on mobile.\n\nFixes #25\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uu@icloud.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnuL6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyxwQACKVBuSwW2suuyjtYTuWn7nT\nUmAff0XLFs0ZhAvBE+khQQI1FjtEvi5o18JI7m1Uo+mZYZpR18OVD0+rM7OZS/EV\nQVIva46FjyVBgBsNxH3ehruO+eNtZnFqHg6hKNkggD4mCA85uVHN1LC9CR/1pFs1\nFXYTPvwF6UIxpU5g31G4eJ1KNRnl+r+kpu8HEhmBiViR5IlNVx8qKhhh5NjMq3Ay\nMvLKFwfJThsZVuG/kI8+PAfZYZvPLbqmshDFJ+qaDNno37pHjX996KW3PH0LPc/B\n7zzhlA3nJskoNMjnI5oUaAMPLFIUMJEkRPJPzdA4HgJcW8puvYEBvPj8fBhfgZLD\n5B+1XGvRZNDjNGqjDS1/Jyby+Lv27wnNV2WTq0CGII0eJYl2rkE0QyvxYdpW7eLj\nfktxIUt55dxEiiAJwMJ0e455/s8q4uJIR91QpEimG/igE96Bc5rrX7kGuL7UegNj\nOnqyvlzcoVWRv/XGf2BuOhDWVkFxrBRHxx9mlBkrh/YcGJ4Hu1UerVV9QLKwqYCS\nYjDIY/+RiGosUk16uCr6aJsgnx+wljt9zS1F0bxUYmmF7cKceYv6lalomD+M3EPN\n/tX0hOFcTAaQFLFQfL37IzUf+0Ym4fZePFX3YCKaUEkNGbv6zi7oMIn//XYihl/9\nBYZualMrbhxDl1pSItHC\n=ebp3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T16:14:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commit/651a59eb5e233899fe99067296a887d2465aa389","node_id":"C_kwDOUHx5BtoAKDY1MWE1OWViNWUyMzM4OTlmZTk5MDY3Mjk2YTg4N2QyNDY1YWEzODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commit/566f1d38266673745b6b06b2abe8f0cbfee3b62d","sha":"566f1d38266673745b6b06b2abe8f0cbfee3b62d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/566f1d38266673745b6b06b2abe8f0cbfee3b62d"}],"sha":"651a59eb5e233899fe99067296a887d2465aa389","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/651a59eb5e233899fe99067296a887d2465aa389"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1575723?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa","id":1575723,"login":"juusimaa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NzU3MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/566f1d38266673745b6b06b2abe8f0cbfee3b62d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T06:43:57Z","email":"jouni.uusimaa@gmail.com","name":"Jouni Uusimaa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T06:43:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Name cancelled subscriptions in a category''s member list too (#24)\n\nsubscription_ids (added in the previous fix) already includes a\ncancelled plan for any month its historical charge still counts in --\nthat''s the whole point of /summary/spend not filtering by status. But\nthe category breakdown''s member list was still narrowing its candidate\nset to onTheBooks (non-cancelled) before checking chargedIds, so a\ncancelled plan could be counted in a category''s total and never named\nunder it -- reported as \"€14.99 for Sport in June, no name attached\"\nafter the subscription behind it was deleted... except the amount was\nactually coming from a *different*, cancelled Sport subscription this\nfiltering was hiding.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uu@icloud.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8f07928a851233cb212eddff1b99d5f81301d9af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/git/trees/8f07928a851233cb212eddff1b99d5f81301d9af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/git/commits/566f1d38266673745b6b06b2abe8f0cbfee3b62d","verification":{"payload":"tree 8f07928a851233cb212eddff1b99d5f81301d9af\nparent 0a6242aae6f4cef9bfb8d7498e443b5b20f0c787\nauthor Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uusimaa@gmail.com> 1788763437 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788763437 +0300\n\nName cancelled subscriptions in a category''s member list too (#24)\n\nsubscription_ids (added in the previous fix) already includes a\ncancelled plan for any month its historical charge still counts in --\nthat''s the whole point of /summary/spend not filtering by status. But\nthe category breakdown''s member list was still narrowing its candidate\nset to onTheBooks (non-cancelled) before checking chargedIds, so a\ncancelled plan could be counted in a category''s total and never named\nunder it -- reported as \"€14.99 for Sport in June, no name attached\"\nafter the subscription behind it was deleted... except the amount was\nactually coming from a *different*, cancelled Sport subscription this\nfiltering was hiding.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uu@icloud.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnl0tCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2UkQAImZhsjZwooPqsQQ46nrcBLS\ncJmqJGPh0t9/iHeYCQGGPphydlQiMPuCXaFjdwJ6l7xbajWNfVbngCIfMBHdzSG+\ne3ie3PmnCITtqKHOuUfuv5Ybfg8byFG0QkBOlGZQ3ayXdwvH2yXrl8mcEF8t7McD\n9d6d+FcFeNi8HqGDfdCJS9ljdRRSCfR9MCaFNPrEKf3t9D04H/CuIy35GSOFtlU4\n1TG98NH8T2BpSrfuwOokTyPHS1jnCrIGTIC4n7O44rAdQOH2KQnrwjiUJFhguLWW\nbYdnzcUZe2RRQjwi/LawjPXAkgH9fX195Zxc+3thOkF1vJk2xRVznzluvO9lHiHe\nJjRvWXPUpxXbnmM4RkxnKIYgzjGMoRrYOpdmzUEfwA1RfZFHYxoTAY47M87t6WnR\noSkHdCFSV53F01J6LYhqcN0fuZgGQW6b4loobSuRheJNbZoDlgQipwWvEQq/18sx\nK6jZNoh6buBzLitV1ifsyiR+mgbA3aDzPCqGQlGSRZo6n+GHgQ4dpyrOxKBnkwlE\n8N63aWpzVvBr1SkaYAbVboTP+RRlnXtH4H+IFlWIMJu4W3bJO5pkw0JLay6eLWqG\nO/N6gNfsYE5jn7fnYxyjk3va2wqUNIs/IhVTr3sqv9n8ZeSWyILUdLWJBznzM6v9\nwfAJMljFU7fewVs8KuO9\n=wwXv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T06:43:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commit/566f1d38266673745b6b06b2abe8f0cbfee3b62d","node_id":"C_kwDOUHx5BtoAKDU2NmYxZDM4MjY2NjczNzQ1YjZiMDZiMmFiZThmMGNiZmVlM2I2MmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commit/0a6242aae6f4cef9bfb8d7498e443b5b20f0c787","sha":"0a6242aae6f4cef9bfb8d7498e443b5b20f0c787","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/0a6242aae6f4cef9bfb8d7498e443b5b20f0c787"}],"sha":"566f1d38266673745b6b06b2abe8f0cbfee3b62d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/566f1d38266673745b6b06b2abe8f0cbfee3b62d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1575723?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa","id":1575723,"login":"juusimaa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NzU3MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/0a6242aae6f4cef9bfb8d7498e443b5b20f0c787/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T06:25:57Z","email":"jouni.uusimaa@gmail.com","name":"Jouni Uusimaa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T06:25:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix category breakdown listing subscriptions that didn''t bill that month (#23)\n\n* Fix category breakdown listing subscriptions that didn''t bill that month\n\nThe \"By category\" panel''s member list was every non-cancelled\nsubscription tagged with a category, whenever that category had any\nspend in the selected period -- not the subscriptions that actually\ncharged. A category with two differently-scheduled plans (e.g. a\nmonthly and a quarterly one sharing \"Sport\") would list both under\nevery month either one billed, even though only one of them charged.\n\n/summary/spend now reports subscription_ids per month (who is behind\nthat month''s total, from the same _charge_dates the total itself comes\nfrom), and the frontend filters category members against it instead of\nagainst category membership alone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Update dashboard visual baseline for the category-members fix\n\nWork''s March breakdown no longer lists Notion (a trial, never actually\ncharged) alongside Adobe -- the fixture''s subscription_ids now reflect\nwho actually billed, matching the /summary/spend response shape from\nthe previous commit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Regenerate dashboard visual baseline inside the CI Playwright container\n\nThe previous update ran on macOS via npm run test:visual:update, whose\nfont rendering doesn''t match the Linux container CI actually uses (see\ntests/visual/README.md) -- that made CI fail on drift unrelated to the\ncategory-members fix, at the same pixel-diff magnitude as the\nunrelated local drift already seen on this branch. Regenerated with\nthe documented `docker run ... mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:v1.63.0-noble`\ncommand instead; all 7 visual tests, including the previously-drifting\nfive, pass inside that container.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uu@icloud.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f243f91a145fb45fa47c7c322740bc0da9e461df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/git/trees/f243f91a145fb45fa47c7c322740bc0da9e461df"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/git/commits/0a6242aae6f4cef9bfb8d7498e443b5b20f0c787","verification":{"payload":"tree f243f91a145fb45fa47c7c322740bc0da9e461df\nparent 79d0f8e58d2a2c308511636ab3c48a4dc15bcee8\nauthor Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uusimaa@gmail.com> 1788762357 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788762357 +0300\n\nFix category breakdown listing subscriptions that didn''t bill that month (#23)\n\n* Fix category breakdown listing subscriptions that didn''t bill that month\n\nThe \"By category\" panel''s member list was every non-cancelled\nsubscription tagged with a category, whenever that category had any\nspend in the selected period -- not the subscriptions that actually\ncharged. A category with two differently-scheduled plans (e.g. a\nmonthly and a quarterly one sharing \"Sport\") would list both under\nevery month either one billed, even though only one of them charged.\n\n/summary/spend now reports subscription_ids per month (who is behind\nthat month''s total, from the same _charge_dates the total itself comes\nfrom), and the frontend filters category members against it instead of\nagainst category membership alone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Update dashboard visual baseline for the category-members fix\n\nWork''s March breakdown no longer lists Notion (a trial, never actually\ncharged) alongside Adobe -- the fixture''s subscription_ids now reflect\nwho actually billed, matching the /summary/spend response shape from\nthe previous commit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Regenerate dashboard visual baseline inside the CI Playwright container\n\nThe previous update ran on macOS via npm run test:visual:update, whose\nfont rendering doesn''t match the Linux container CI actually uses (see\ntests/visual/README.md) -- that made CI fail on drift unrelated to the\ncategory-members fix, at the same pixel-diff magnitude as the\nunrelated local drift already seen on this branch. Regenerated with\nthe documented `docker run ... mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:v1.63.0-noble`\ncommand instead; all 7 visual tests, including the previously-drifting\nfive, pass inside that container.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uu@icloud.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnlj1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXn8QABhrF/uFyCO4p9lMn4eg3uau\n5Q1MesQszLKtD9NShf9t127wy353I9qM+v7Q63iXx+d1gZ/m2sT2Hg4tCA9AbQjf\nREGibQyza5IrlIe7b4HpFGl3RyhmFGzKHM1KpV5v8q9CQFQDVGUC6tx/fUIzLDK2\nZ+KyKneqIzAHZOKN3okjjP7HR1ZeIlW920i23u6GLTKEWmvLxUlN7/r2qUrsBNkb\n/tQxOT6HYvASVo++