com/juusimaa","id":1575723,"login":"juusimaa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NzU3MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/9401385877c24b6db7ccce3e9b6721b4142eb9db/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T14:24:40Z","email":"jouni.uusimaa@gmail.com","name":"Jouni Uusimaa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T14:24:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix mobile view showing \"last charge\" for cancelled subscriptions (#13)\n\nMobile row meta and the detail sheet both said \"last charge <date>\" for\na cancelled subscription; desktop''s renewal column says \"access ends\"\nfor the same case. Align mobile with desktop''s wording.\n\nFixes #12\n\nCo-authored-by: Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uu@icloud.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b3e9646245122b0c8bb178edccef05a1267fe42e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/git/trees/b3e9646245122b0c8bb178edccef05a1267fe42e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/git/commits/9401385877c24b6db7ccce3e9b6721b4142eb9db","verification":{"payload":"tree b3e9646245122b0c8bb178edccef05a1267fe42e\nparent 4fb60dbcbbb0abdf0b5c2d079201637c8202b203\nauthor Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uusimaa@gmail.com> 1788704680 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788704680 +0300\n\nFix mobile view showing \"last charge\" for cancelled subscriptions (#13)\n\nMobile row meta and the detail sheet both said \"last charge <date>\" for\na cancelled subscription; desktop''s renewal column says \"access ends\"\nfor the same case. Align mobile with desktop''s wording.\n\nFixes #12\n\nCo-authored-by: Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uu@icloud.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnXeoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADLkQAAar7feWeGspnuyRcuWzHDH1\n7NTWrA/gdUzM9WAiDdG1AOvOyCKUxSAcgrDmhadhayUu5hyM2sbcpfP6laKbXCLp\nv1wU0vkWTRb9JpLmNp4KYifVTXoqqtxQjL0wzCJW8yHtMZ9s8BQ2ZqWCFbxBUmWS\nloGATJV4wV7y/5gpGlchNOJz7uTZ/iiuEdizP3aKhxrHpw6H9XNYhdr6xYzARS+J\nQMYumGpX4rfWzimWAzp0rxa0AoZ8WsU50vnAvHXbvjeg3cfLgABrlOksfi78fGoh\na20tu1v+SnjFgLg/xfycc5owlIuBxPk/ob3dTRrzcuodeDOfr0jG0hiWJKKWt/R6\n7GGa2xIn2zhCRFFkMIpnBIV3e9dKCvUKaJGhKf4lZKKd0I6lF7RhUhw4wwvGvxeR\nFMpBmKXqM8uwIkQH/7k1AxfRbdnzJW9GcUoisCzi0ycHWrvtzqVpB9QqX74bnMxh\nyfqrcKV2/1SwAMRSDlbCl0+0aFw5XZulfD5VLhXP50wKUxP8lwYN3A746T6kjmKC\nZb0uD3uCyKF2yhx+Qaug0Ke94cwviI/BvMp+HOyHSS0qwUCC/xlrB6NVfKGiKYCc\nmicvpdc9IdCePdsCJlnk7d3Ak1ZofaX3Ge1aPsLCIKAUUXqXGiDe/7iVjBMqHp48\nTTellNITJYI38rnjb1dY\n=YN/X\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-06T14:24:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commit/9401385877c24b6db7ccce3e9b6721b4142eb9db","node_id":"C_kwDOUHx5BtoAKDk0MDEzODU4NzdjMjRiNmRiN2NjY2UzZTliNjcyMWI0MTQyZWI5ZGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commit/4fb60dbcbbb0abdf0b5c2d079201637c8202b203","sha":"4fb60dbcbbb0abdf0b5c2d079201637c8202b203","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/4fb60dbcbbb0abdf0b5c2d079201637c8202b203"}],"sha":"9401385877c24b6db7ccce3e9b6721b4142eb9db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/9401385877c24b6db7ccce3e9b6721b4142eb9db"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1575723?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa","id":1575723,"login":"juusimaa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NzU3MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/4fb60dbcbbb0abdf0b5c2d079201637c8202b203/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T11:37:20Z","email":"jouni.uusimaa@gmail.com","name":"Jouni Uusimaa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T11:37:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Document the live subscriptionstrack.com deployment (#11)\n\nREADME and build-and-push.yml still described the Azure deploy as\nhypothetical (\"once milestone 8''s infra exists\", \"nothing deploys these yet\")\neven though it''s been live since 2026-09-04 and now has a custom domain\n(subscriptionstrack.com / api.subscriptionstrack.com) instead of just the\nazurecontainerapps.io URLs.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uu@icloud.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2466a244e165736a6560a2868e4535d9c32f3eb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/git/trees/2466a244e165736a6560a2868e4535d9c32f3eb9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/git/commits/4fb60dbcbbb0abdf0b5c2d079201637c8202b203","verification":{"payload":"tree 2466a244e165736a6560a2868e4535d9c32f3eb9\nparent c28dba549e90e6b59fb34e010f5f9acc398440dc\nauthor Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uusimaa@gmail.com> 1788694640 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788694640 +0300\n\nDocument the live subscriptionstrack.com deployment (#11)\n\nREADME and build-and-push.yml still described the Azure deploy as\nhypothetical (\"once milestone 8''s infra exists\", \"nothing deploys these yet\")\neven though it''s been live since 2026-09-04 and now has a custom domain\n(subscriptionstrack.com / api.subscriptionstrack.com) instead of just the\nazurecontainerapps.io URLs.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uu@icloud.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnVBwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWuMQAAVKpbl5As9+9HgZeaQ1L4vl\nzTqYquUSeVxabckRHt4yZ7VXw7IatAAZdgIKOZzX6dcEG4czHL9FRezIK3uSo5/5\nOYi5T1XtyMlIBtua76d0glpiC8b4lfCVKBcUQmMwWvDggtXhE7R5MRGQznp1AtkV\ntLx7vkJEC1nJ6aF31dLHbjGsYQOQxM933PgavqfKyVqqsBFoaGmKVgX/fbiRAsCI\nA3XaceF4QfIAKLtVc5kZik0yjWUMKVGzGWl30W37fzJCVHRGU+LVRS0zAvGebRom\nNLL20a413+tnpwZFwD+WEFCwLIbQ4hEsFo9Q2dTqDtf/LFlpvEgAwr1W9+/1UInw\nzuTK/wfDo39ErlnwVcJuy1OtJOrkjVP3XbssQGa3tPUAeNsb5TkCleZYwzDFw9QC\nkdMjRlNWOX9vHAwPua5iyK7f8U+mv+afkIgBDGey+5GWVXhqrlzvKLBtMsi8ufEr\nPPxBGlMa2DwuM5ZDLKnx74UvsWjg5kZkqLwWDyQIKslOIgKhP7bndJVSJ6W6OEf1\nOTPugH5okbRiCJuDRlxTPnZJ7pADa4mSbjnspDe33au+KwPIYW2e4ofN5/bfpU2S\nO2zYHhmOLbSISh9POYVZXcjhccpYrOviyReybMjpldcToiqLt2BSaEuLU37ntoCf\n9JyWnzK1QTToJ8/zFP83\n=Ri11\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-06T11:37:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commit/4fb60dbcbbb0abdf0b5c2d079201637c8202b203","node_id":"C_kwDOUHx5BtoAKDRmYjYwZGJjYmJiMGFiZGYwYjVjMmQwNzkyMDE2MzdjODIwMmIyMDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commit/c28dba549e90e6b59fb34e010f5f9acc398440dc","sha":"c28dba549e90e6b59fb34e010f5f9acc398440dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/c28dba549e90e6b59fb34e010f5f9acc398440dc"}],"sha":"4fb60dbcbbb0abdf0b5c2d079201637c8202b203","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/4fb60dbcbbb0abdf0b5c2d079201637c8202b203"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1575723?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa","id":1575723,"login":"juusimaa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NzU3MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/c28dba549e90e6b59fb34e010f5f9acc398440dc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T10:04:14Z","email":"jouni.uusimaa@gmail.com","name":"Jouni Uusimaa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T10:04:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix mobile form grids overflowing on real mobile Safari (#10)\n\n* Fix mobile form grids overflowing on real mobile Safari (#9)\n\n.sheet-row (mobile edit sheet) and the mobile .add-grid override used bare\n1fr tracks instead of minmax(0, 1fr). A native date/select control''s\ncontent-based minimum width can then blow out its track, overflowing the\nrow and squeezing the sibling column flush left with no visible gap. Only\nshows up on real mobile Safari, whose native controls run wider than\ndesktop Safari''s or Chromium''s emulation -- this codebase hit the same\nclass of bug in a flex layout before (issue #6).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Give input[type=date] the same appearance:none treatment as select (#9)\n\nThe earlier minmax(0, 1fr) grid fix turned out not to be the real cause --\nconfirmed via Web Inspector on a real iPhone that the grid gap and column\nwidths were already correct. getComputedStyle on the actual device showed\ninput[type=\"date\"] computing box-sizing: content-box (unlike every other\n.input element, which correctly computes border-box despite the universal\n* { box-sizing: border-box } reset) and ignoring min-height entirely, while\nevery other control on the same page honored both.\n\nPer the CSS appearance spec, a control that keeps its native rendering is\nallowed to disregard the author''s box model -- select.input already works\naround this (see the comment above it), just never got applied to date\ninputs since the symptom had no prior report. content-box adds padding and\nborder on top of the width the grid assigned instead of inside it, so the\ndate input paints wider than its column and overflows into its neighbor;\nthat''s the overflow and the \"zero\" gap #9''s screenshots show, and the\nignored min-height is the height mismatch. appearance:none hands sizing\nback to this stylesheet, same as it already does for select. Confirmed\nfixed on a real iPhone 17, including that the native calendar picker still\nopens on tap (::-webkit-calendar-picker-indicator is unaffected).\n\nRegenerated Playwright baselines in the Linux container -- no pixel diff,\nsince this is a WebKit-only behavior neither Chromium nor the iOS\nSimulator reproduces.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uu@icloud.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"45e5acf40ef680db7b5fdc5d982ec8f408505390","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/git/trees/45e5acf40ef680db7b5fdc5d982ec8f408505390"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/git/commits/c28dba549e90e6b59fb34e010f5f9acc398440dc","verification":{"payload":"tree 45e5acf40ef680db7b5fdc5d982ec8f408505390\nparent 2addd1429837cefe34b879412c4ea788c1f3cf64\nauthor Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uusimaa@gmail.com> 1788689054 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788689054 +0300\n\nFix mobile form grids overflowing on real mobile Safari (#10)\n\n* Fix mobile form grids overflowing on real mobile Safari (#9)\n\n.sheet-row (mobile edit sheet) and the mobile .add-grid override used bare\n1fr tracks instead of minmax(0, 1fr). A native date/select control''s\ncontent-based minimum width can then blow out its track, overflowing the\nrow and squeezing the sibling column flush left with no visible gap. Only\nshows up on real mobile Safari, whose native controls run wider than\ndesktop Safari''s or Chromium''s emulation -- this codebase hit the same\nclass of bug in a flex layout before (issue #6).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Give input[type=date] the same appearance:none treatment as select (#9)\n\nThe earlier minmax(0, 1fr) grid fix turned out not to be the real cause --\nconfirmed via Web Inspector on a real iPhone that the grid gap and column\nwidths were already correct. getComputedStyle on the actual device showed\ninput[type=\"date\"] computing box-sizing: content-box (unlike every other\n.input element, which correctly computes border-box despite the universal\n* { box-sizing: border-box } reset) and ignoring min-height entirely, while\nevery other control on the same page honored both.\n\nPer the CSS appearance spec, a control that keeps its native rendering is\nallowed to disregard the author''s box model -- select.input already works\naround this (see the comment above it), just never got applied to date\ninputs since the symptom had no prior report. content-box adds padding and\nborder on top of the width the grid assigned instead of inside it, so the\ndate input paints wider than its column and overflows into its neighbor;\nthat''s the overflow and the \"zero\" gap #9''s screenshots show, and the\nignored min-height is the height mismatch. appearance:none hands sizing\nback to this stylesheet, same as it already does for select. Confirmed\nfixed on a real iPhone 17, including that the native calendar picker still\nopens on tap (::-webkit-calendar-picker-indicator is unaffected).\n\nRegenerated Playwright baselines in the Linux container -- no pixel diff,\nsince this is a WebKit-only behavior neither Chromium nor the iOS\nSimulator reproduces.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uu@icloud.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnTqeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGisQAHZ3peY4EyrXu3ndWsESxyXc\n5TpFCMPxDrfdR5ixOMMijpTp+l3aFw3VEgdK52ET+sR0m/bfZWKL35i4zC+jdODX\nrawtzsjF/Fi+FWP0EaCzzymu/DHh2ESCbNRQTIHRH6j6BGw+NYDV3EHWEI1Iv+cB\noB6ERon5IkoUes6l8kyObLw0I5tUg1jShqrojXxyA9ybGqsIKCZ+PvC3QinudLtc\ndXoZgCGCHTlF+KsiKvNF2MiKJnblcQh9JAb4BoFJv6XSvEZJxYI7Cjz+kQvQa4n3\nKciRqNE6KCtY5LpJ+IC61ewqUZs5ycZDuF2HDPaKD6LVV3O7/g05iLq583NmVucm\n1wUroMMO1wXXVh2vU5PPqWKhhgCSA9tsxwX2qKu0ILktohriTlRXfn/JnZgC9sIW\njq5njXz5EYGR6mDSIYkWrGD03B1zWzGQP585IrMUQjKH/S08U5mXBg713OvDHLuQ\narX73tMHRPjl5zOPsZryaVjNObHQm/8/QSW5vwKZWYuYELpPyV9Z92/q/NrAwtzF\nPBNWmV3ACS3A483cCAoDRPBrrgRDkDvLc4OJFCI1oZj7ZgcHT3X/UnCTHIgsKnAI\nlSoILutLugwIy73Bao1HqCLMzQRppMA5uRBpn270X2so+ge0zj6b8IsIXnOxSEQQ\nUnwJ1aV1NcuPYGsFNLnc\n=SSUE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-06T10:04:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commit/c28dba549e90e6b59fb34e010f5f9acc398440dc","node_id":"C_kwDOUHx5BtoAKGMyOGRiYTU0OWU5MGU2YjU5ZmIzNGUwMTBmNWY5YWNjMzk4NDQwZGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commit/2addd1429837cefe34b879412c4ea788c1f3cf64","sha":"2addd1429837cefe34b879412c4ea788c1f3cf64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/2addd1429837cefe34b879412c4ea788c1f3cf64"}],"sha":"c28dba549e90e6b59fb34e010f5f9acc398440dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/c28dba549e90e6b59fb34e010f5f9acc398440dc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1575723?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/juusimaa","id":1575723,"login":"juusimaa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NzU3MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/juusimaa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/commits/2addd1429837cefe34b879412c4ea788c1f3cf64/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T11:07:53Z","email":"jouni.uusimaa@gmail.com","name":"Jouni Uusimaa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T11:07:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix required status checks getting stuck on path-filtered PRs (#8)\n\nmain''s branch protection requires \"sqlite\", \"postgres\" (test.yml) and\n\"visual\" (frontend-visual.yml) to pass before merging. All three\nworkflows only triggered on paths under backend/ or frontend/\nrespectively, so a PR touching just the other area (or neither, like\nPR #7''s workflow-only changes) never got those checks to report at\nall -- and a required check with no report blocks merging indefinitely\nrather than passing. That''s what forced the manual admin-bypass merge\nof #7.\n\nBoth workflows now always trigger; a paths-filter step determines\nwhether the real work is relevant and skips it when it isn''t, while the\njob still completes and reports success. frontend-visual.yml splits\nthis into its own \"changes\" job rather than a step inside \"visual\",\nsince \"visual\" runs entirely inside a container image that has no git\nhistory to diff against.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uu@icloud.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"13b695b85cea98f2c5317186300d92907f6fbff8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/git/trees/13b695b85cea98f2c5317186300d92907f6fbff8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juusimaa/subscription-tracker/git/commits/2addd1429837cefe34b879412c4ea788c1f3cf64","verification":{"payload":"tree 13b695b85cea98f2c5317186300d92907f6fbff8\nparent c52f5a18b98dc0f57c31e7ed835b7ae56231b188\nauthor Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uusimaa@gmail.com> 1788606473 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788606473 +0300\n\nFix required status checks getting stuck on path-filtered PRs (#8)\n\nmain''s branch protection requires \"sqlite\", \"postgres\" (test.yml) and\n\"visual\" (frontend-visual.yml) to pass before merging. All three\nworkflows only triggered on paths under backend/ or frontend/\nrespectively, so a PR touching just the other area (or neither, like\nPR #7''s workflow-only changes) never got those checks to report at\nall -- and a required check with no report blocks merging indefinitely\nrather than passing. That''s what forced the manual admin-bypass merge\nof #7.\n\nBoth workflows now always trigger; a paths-filter step determines\nwhether the real work is relevant and skips it when it isn''t, while the\njob still completes and reports success. frontend-visual.yml splits\nthis into its own \"changes\" job rather than a step inside \"visual\",\nsince \"visual\" runs entirely inside a container image that has no git\nhistory to diff against.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jouni Uusimaa <jouni.uu@icloud.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqm/gJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfLYQAITNKRxTqzwQdN923WE6mZLH\nwIGWAw+XeYvYWTZUkbJXKkdH8BeY4jKnkOSNqaBm1rhSrXPEzxKoNLLw/TNzFUjq\nyadEr4LKPj+tSMN/G8/O66GpasDUhELKDUzXEDikGSvnmyBnsgWhDCVTts927+v5\nP7CUM6+P5CNEuvzRcDesKKekdt/9gzx+xt5OrRneZrpo/NB3W1jKdoXaDpOBb8Q8\nzxEqDOR/UzRtEmTgA4XvqLayDsk/dBPGGubWP2Y5Tkna0un7L8ffXBPJrCshjqeO\n4OF+w+UijqtZAFat9Q1eGgiP8I0fYKAsQS2sJCJWd3QAaP7dRq86TpfRZ/F8tUAT\nULdgUJ00UXJvQ2Am26eRc8z3FFRQFtR8JDngIRk2nmW1vYvir1jECDE7ux6bmiqn\nAdpiAuUlXmSlM3jasOCyY3y6vvFZ352eVAcifiGfGTRXAidv/9tpdjHW1BXeWyUX\npSzQarVLDYcc7B6yOXjlzUlG35bIr0A6gkeWxefRKfwmB9k72Ihceo9hIDVydGv/\nW9xatHkX7WDg3p0Fjx+nolH1JOSLvlLs7uYvxPwAXha8vPbOHEBOf2+iXNwRp2v0\n6R6J/mG