B7j6cwh4h\n=6O+j\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T23:09:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-console/commit/f29b5d21316fc0685c3c8d09f51f59d2b1d6bb92","node_id":"C_kwDOUID9KNoAKGYyOWI1ZDIxMzE2ZmMwNjg1YzNjOGQwOWY1MWY1OWQyYjFkNmJiOTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-console/commit/a4cc062c20728b66b0e3cff115d6ee59b32bbe42","sha":"a4cc062c20728b66b0e3cff115d6ee59b32bbe42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-console/commits/a4cc062c20728b66b0e3cff115d6ee59b32bbe42"}],"sha":"f29b5d21316fc0685c3c8d09f51f59d2b1d6bb92","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-console/commits/f29b5d21316fc0685c3c8d09f51f59d2b1d6bb92"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-console/commits/a4cc062c20728b66b0e3cff115d6ee59b32bbe42/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:28:04Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:28:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: federate network-fulfillment remote + per-context Bounded Context Report screens (#43)\n\n* feat: federate network-fulfillment remote (netfulfil_mfe, port 5188)\n\n- vite.config.ts: add network_fulfillment_mfe to federation.remotes,\n  following the exact remoteEntry(name, port) pattern used by the other\n  eight remotes.\n- App.tsx: module-scope lazy() import + /network-fulfillment/* route,\n  mirroring facility_mfe''s RemoteBoundary wiring exactly.\n- ContextsScreen.tsx: new LaunchTile for network-fulfillment -- the ACL\n  to an external retail fulfillment network, observation-only from this\n  console.\n- README.md: add the new remote to the port table and route-ownership\n  description (nine remotes now, not eight).\n\n* feat: shared ContextReportScreen shell + reports config surface\n\n- config.ts: add REPORTS_BASE_URL, one entry per bounded context\n  (all 9), following the exact SERVICE_BASE_URL naming/resolution\n  pattern already used for the OLTP base URLs -- same runtime-config\n  override keys, same dev-port fallback shape. network-fulfillment''s\n  entry follows the same pattern for consistency even though its\n  backend /reports/... endpoint is still in an open PR upstream.\n- features/context-reports/types.ts: the shared ContextReportConfig<T>\n  contract + ReportFreshness shape every context''s /reports/.../freshness\n  endpoint answers.\n- features/context-reports/reportWindow.ts: the from/to RFC3339 query\n  window every /reports/... endpoint requires.\n- features/context-reports/ContextReportScreen.tsx: the ONE reusable\n  presentational shell -- loading / populated / whole-request-error\n  states, FreshnessBadge wired to the sibling /freshness endpoint,\n  ''never fabricate a number'' matching ReportDashboard.tsx''s philosophy.\n- features/context-reports/ContextReportRouteScreen.tsx +\n  registry.ts: the /reports/:context route, dispatching to each\n  context''s own config object.\n\n* feat: per-context report configs for all 9 bounded contexts\n\nOne adapter/config object per context mapping its OWN real\n/reports/... DTO (read directly from that service''s own\nreports_handler.go, not guessed) onto the shared ContextReportScreen\nshell''s ui-kit renderers. Endpoint path + DTO field names per context:\n\n- facility-layout: GET /reports/catalog-growth (day-bucketed rows:\n  sitesRegistered, zonesRegistered, aislesRegistered,\n  locationTypesRegistered, placementRulesDefined, slotsRegistered,\n  slotsDecommissioned, bulkImports, importRowsSubmitted/Imported/Rejected)\n- fulfillment-execution: GET /reports/throughput (hour-bucketed rows:\n  taskType, stationId, completions, avgClaimToCompleteSeconds,\n  leaseExpiries, weighCheckDiverts)\n- inventory-storage: GET /reports/flow-accuracy (rows: stage,\n  eventsIn/Out, accuracyPct, discrepancies)\n- labor-performance: GET /reports/performance (totals + byTaskType +\n  rows: associateId, taskType, standardSeconds, actualSeconds,\n  performancePct -- nullable when no standard exists yet)\n- order-management: GET /reports/funnel (stage counts: received,\n  allocated, released, shipped + medianSecondsPerStage rows)\n- process-path-management: GET /reports/catalog-growth (day-bucketed:\n  pathsDefined, pathsRevised, pathsDeactivated)\n- wes-work-planning: GET /reports/throughput (hour-bucketed:\n  released, completed, workPoolDepth, balancingActions)\n- workforce-management: GET /reports/staffing (rows: path,\n  plannedHeadcount, activeHeadcount, gap)\n- network-fulfillment: GET /reports/network-summary -- UNVERIFIED.\n  This context''s reports_handler.go does not exist yet on develop or\n  on its open feature branch as of this commit; the endpoint path and\n  DTO fields (ordersAcknowledged, ordersRejected, shipmentsConfirmed,\n  inventoryAdvertisements, syncLagSeconds) are a best-effort forward\n  guess based on its domain events, flagged in the config''s own header\n  comment, and MUST be reconciled against the real handler the moment\n  that PR merges.\n\nEvery /reports/... call also hits that context''s sibling\n/reports/.../freshness endpoint and renders it through FreshnessBadge,\nmatching the WMS/WES dashboards'' existing convention exactly.\n\n* test: ContextReportScreen shell + 2 per-context config tests\n\nTesting Library + MSW, following this repo''s existing\nsrc/features/*/*.test.tsx pattern:\n\n- ContextReportScreen.test.tsx: the shared shell''s own three\n  degradation states (loading, populated, whole-request error) plus\n  freshness-fetch failing independently of the report body, using a\n  synthetic config so every real per-context config inherits this\n  coverage for free.\n- facilityLayout.config.test.tsx: catalog-growth''s real DTO shape\n  (day-bucketed multi-metric rows) through the real shell.\n- fulfillmentExecution.config.test.tsx: throughput''s real DTO shape\n  (hour-bucketed task/station rows with lease-expiry and\n  weigh-check-divert counts) -- deliberately a different shape from\n  facility-layout''s, through the real shell.\n\n54/54 tests passing (8 test files).","tree":{"sha":"9a55558f510bb0a4ed85a3437292e8c066069d62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-console/git/trees/9a55558f510bb0a4ed85a3437292e8c066069d62"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-console/git/commits/a4cc062c20728b66b0e3cff115d6ee59b32bbe42","verification":{"payload":"tree 9a55558f510bb0a4ed85a3437292e8c066069d62\nparent 860449afba0b8cd7a38eb22ddec6035241205088\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790461684 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790461684 -0300\n\nfeat: federate network-fulfillment remote + per-context Bounded Context Report screens (#43)\n\n* feat: federate network-fulfillment remote (netfulfil_mfe, port 5188)\n\n- vite.config.ts: add network_fulfillment_mfe to federation.remotes,\n  following the exact remoteEntry(name, port) pattern used by the other\n  eight remotes.\n- App.tsx: module-scope lazy() import + /network-fulfillment/* route,\n  mirroring facility_mfe''s RemoteBoundary wiring exactly.\n- ContextsScreen.tsx: new LaunchTile for network-fulfillment -- the ACL\n  to an external retail fulfillment network, observation-only from this\n  console.\n- README.md: add the new remote to the port table and route-ownership\n  description (nine remotes now, not eight).\n\n* feat: shared ContextReportScreen shell + reports config surface\n\n- config.ts: add REPORTS_BASE_URL, one entry per bounded context\n  (all 9), following the exact SERVICE_BASE_URL naming/resolution\n  pattern already used for the OLTP base URLs -- same runtime-config\n  override keys, same dev-port fallback shape. network-fulfillment''s\n  entry follows the same pattern for consistency even though its\n  backend /reports/... endpoint is still in an open PR upstream.\n- features/context-reports/types.ts: the shared ContextReportConfig<T>\n  contract + ReportFreshness shape every context''s /reports/.../freshness\n  endpoint answers.\n- features/context-reports/reportWindow.ts: the from/to RFC3339 query\n  window every /reports/... endpoint requires.\n- features/context-reports/ContextReportScreen.tsx: the ONE reusable\n  presentational shell -- loading / populated / whole-request-error\n  states, FreshnessBadge wired to the sibling /freshness endpoint,\n  ''never fabricate a number'' matching ReportDashboard.tsx''s philosophy.\n- features/context-reports/ContextReportRouteScreen.tsx +\n  registry.ts: the /reports/:context route, dispatching to each\n  context''s own config object.\n\n* feat: per-context report configs for all 9 bounded contexts\n\nOne adapter/config object per context mapping its OWN real\n/reports/... DTO (read directly from that service''s own\nreports_handler.go, not guessed) onto the shared ContextReportScreen\nshell''s ui-kit renderers. Endpoint path + DTO field names per context:\n\n- facility-layout: GET /reports/catalog-growth (day-bucketed rows:\n  sitesRegistered, zonesRegistered, aislesRegistered,\n  locationTypesRegistered, placementRulesDefined, slotsRegistered,\n  slotsDecommissioned, bulkImports, importRowsSubmitted/Imported/Rejected)\n- fulfillment-execution: GET /reports/throughput (hour-bucketed rows:\n  taskType, stationId, completions, avgClaimToCompleteSeconds,\n  leaseExpiries, weighCheckDiverts)\n- inventory-storage: GET /reports/flow-accuracy (rows: stage,\n  eventsIn/Out, accuracyPct, discrepancies)\n- labor-performance: GET /reports/performance (totals + byTaskType +\n  rows: associateId, taskType, standardSeconds, actualSeconds,\n  performancePct -- nullable when no standard exists yet)\n- order-management: GET /reports/funnel (stage counts: received,\n  allocated, released, shipped + medianSecondsPerStage rows)\n- process-path-management: GET /reports/catalog-growth (day-bucketed:\n  pathsDefined, pathsRevised, pathsDeactivated)\n- wes-work-planning: GET /reports/throughput (hour-bucketed:\n  released, completed, workPoolDepth, balancingActions)\n- workforce-management: GET /reports/staffing (rows: path,\n  plannedHeadcount, activeHeadcount, gap)\n- network-fulfillment: GET /reports/network-summary -- UNVERIFIED.\n  This context''s reports_handler.go does not exist yet on develop or\n  on its open feature branch as of this commit; the endpoint path and\n  DTO fields (ordersAcknowledged, ordersRejected, shipmentsConfirmed,\n  inventoryAdvertisements, syncLagSeconds) are a best-effort forward\n  guess based on its domain events, flagged in the config''s own header\n  comment, and MUST be reconciled against the real handler the moment\n  that PR merges.\n\nEvery /reports/... call also hits that context''s sibling\n/reports/.../freshness endpoint and renders it through FreshnessBadge,\nmatching the WMS/WES dashboards'' existing convention exactly.\n\n* test: ContextReportScreen shell + 2 per-context config tests\n\nTesting Library + MSW, following this repo''s existing\nsrc/features/*/*.test.tsx pattern:\n\n- ContextReportScreen.test.tsx: the shared shell''s own three\n  degradation states (loading, populated, whole-request error) plus\n  freshness-fetch failing independently of the report body, using a\n  synthetic config so every real per-context config inherits this\n  coverage for free.\n- facilityLayout.config.test.tsx: catalog-growth''s real DTO shape\n  (day-bucketed multi-metric rows) through the real shell.\n- fulfillmentExecution.config.test.tsx: throughput''s real DTO shape\n  (hour-bucketed task/station rows with lease-expiry and\n  weigh-check-divert counts) -- deliberately a different shape from\n  facility-layout''s, through the real shell.\n\n54/54 tests passing (8 test files).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquEb0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAq2oQAH/Y5dHjptzy+DnBJQ6AVNwm\nnH/9VkF+NfEYSz3MvHZlWFowwL27nWJhyEZbR9Asbk/BD0qa8A1IvzgtneTIRXFg\nH1q4RGZt/s74jVVWs/WFuq1+vzlD/Jubm5jOgv1PHEsqTBYVTDwCZp4cLR60KPN/\nvCHQBBotIa2vbQac+txO9StzwYjtME2z4PgxyahWGnhg0XFlTCwNH2L8RyOvVRNj\n8zJ1+EJBAGQqR6w9fJ/