users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-console/commits/ec002e1e48ea97488821839bd03f80010413edc6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T02:25:10Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T02:25:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: refresh project documentation against develop (#38)\n\n* docs: refresh project documentation against develop\n\nBring README, the Docusaurus pages and .claude/rules/mfe-remotes.md in\nline with what develop actually does since the runtime-config / gateway\npath change (#22):\n\n- The \"known gap\" (build-time service URLs) is closed; describe\n  runtime /config.json, apiOrigin -> <apiOrigin>/api/<context> via Kong,\n  and the fact that npm run dev also needs a local public/config.json\n  (without it the shell refuses to start with a text/html error).\n- Module Federation: dev ports vs /mfes/<context>/remoteEntry.js in a\n  production build, served by the Nginx web gateway on http://localhost.\n- Cross-cutting screens: add Floor (GET /daily-brief), fix the lifecycle\n  route to GET /console/orders/{id}/lifecycle, and record which contexts\n  the BFF fans out to per screen.\n- Context map: add the two direct REST reads (Contexts launchpad badges\n  to fulfillment-execution and facility-layout).\n- Consuming the fleet: full checklist for adding a remote (vite remotes\n  entry, REMOTE_PREFIXES, LaunchTile, warehouse-infra frontend_remotes,\n  /mfes/<context>/ base, apiOrigin from window.__WAREHOUSE_CONFIG__).\n\n* docs(agents): refresh CLAUDE.md against develop\n\nBrings the agent entry point in line with the refreshed docs in this PR:\ncurrent binaries, ports/adapters, endpoint/event/ADR counts, env vars and\nCI jobs, verified against origin/develop code. AGENTS.md remains\nbyte-identical (symlink).\n\nAdds AGENTS.md as a symlink to CLAUDE.md, matching the rest of the fleet.","tree":{"sha":"7cf630e0509abc30128f95dd0fc5f4be1091d1fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-console/git/trees/7cf630e0509abc30128f95dd0fc5f4be1091d1fb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-console/git/commits/ec002e1e48ea97488821839bd03f80010413edc6","verification":{"payload":"tree 7cf630e0509abc30128f95dd0fc5f4be1091d1fb\nparent bd111c07bbb6f47d744ff8e27ca62acb21424c50\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790389510 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790389510 -0300\n\ndocs: refresh project documentation against develop (#38)\n\n* docs: refresh project documentation against develop\n\nBring README, the Docusaurus pages and .claude/rules/mfe-remotes.md in\nline with what develop actually does since the runtime-config / gateway\npath change (#22):\n\n- The \"known gap\" (build-time service URLs) is closed; describe\n  runtime /config.json, apiOrigin -> <apiOrigin>/api/<context> via Kong,\n  and the fact that npm run dev also needs a local public/config.json\n  (without it the shell refuses to start with a text/html error).\n- Module Federation: dev ports vs /mfes/<context>/remoteEntry.js in a\n  production build, served by the Nginx web gateway on http://localhost.\n- Cross-cutting screens: add Floor (GET /daily-brief), fix the lifecycle\n  route to GET /console/orders/{id}/lifecycle, and record which contexts\n  the BFF fans out to per screen.\n- Context map: add the two direct REST reads (Contexts launchpad badges\n  to fulfillment-execution and facility-layout).\n- Consuming the fleet: full checklist for adding a remote (vite remotes\n  entry, REMOTE_PREFIXES, LaunchTile, warehouse-infra frontend_remotes,\n  /mfes/<context>/ base, apiOrigin from window.__WAREHOUSE_CONFIG__).\n\n* docs(agents): refresh CLAUDE.md against develop\n\nBrings the agent entry point in line with the refreshed docs in this PR:\ncurrent binaries, ports/adapters, endpoint/event/ADR counts, env vars and\nCI jobs, verified against origin/develop code. AGENTS.md remains\nbyte-identical (symlink).\n\nAdds AGENTS.md as a symlink to CLAUDE.md, matching the rest of the fleet.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqty0GCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIsgQAKDjF4Kp5+4A2jC2MnNCmIJA\nXdNwR57HyWzWzMtIYk9b8YLvFzQFfaPmidc1WqmR7U7aVMPkglcJd8FPc3RCwKm/\nXeBQS1ePjER+qQY1BOuPKOtaUoMKMYoaVkkZhjCdABsDjnbbnJcBAB6RT2nZYNrj\nlE7x9VN63gAh3Vjm63NtWCN26ipBX5vnvM5I0biwJbaQbX0FHsF+CZ6vfphFdf40\no7dki4Av0qAqySn1hsxj/OdMK6T6BBGtYmF/DsnsLTJ9onswlvVQSnyiJwZcRlAz\nxYuHOclLr4ACPm5MYRqi+ZgE3YDpVE4gp92UOlyxAN6bMGGD06NU+TPLbAxxPXDL\nkqdbBXATmyRqtlnZebs3q4JP8EhFbuyK+jE3vNBP3q1CVwtyzs12ul/mEbsD3oA4\nPdK8k9MCLm9Uh7fb4rQnk4nrZoJkA2BQJRF/QM9k6gLsYxFnsFTMleuHAbfYTbLS\nqPffkXV4sQWi0XigOdaVsIJHDyE7gz8XutG0Isan4Sk6wm2SsOevHldM/VbyVsyP\nvaJRi3sphpCnACkA4lJW2uwc5Ep9RxDi035KVkXhfMZcMwfAvHrhMu1OeM489f+2\nB6qoxAHLu9rSXnllrsKjzH87bLkbA7TGRQhb/HeaPPMlOJY4skRtBzJoZeex2yXS\n47A50xA4VIDyUISUJEMw\n=Qg5D\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T02:25:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/s