66592618"}],"sha":"3355e2b2d010b553ffe365dbdae9dcce74bb97a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-console/commits/3355e2b2d010b553ffe365dbdae9dcce74bb97a1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","id":49699333,"login":"dependabot[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-console/commits/87b2bef6cca876c2c9153ce042d51b6066592618/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T12:41:27Z","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"dependabot[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T12:41:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"build(deps-dev): bump typescript from 5.6.3 to 7.0.2 in /docs (#15)\n\n* build(deps-dev): bump typescript from 5.6.3 to 7.0.2 in /docs\n\nBumps [typescript](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript) from 5.6.3 to 7.0.2.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/compare/v5.6.3...v7.0.2)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: typescript\n  dependency-version: 7.0.2\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-major\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\n\n* fix(docs): stop extending @docusaurus/tsconfig, TS7 rejects its baseUrl\n\ndocs/tsconfig.json extends @docusaurus/tsconfig, which still sets\nbaseUrl in its own config. TypeScript 7.0.2 removed baseUrl entirely\n(TS5102), and extends can''t drop an inherited option, so this bump\nbroke npm run typecheck.\n\nFix: inline the same settings @docusaurus/tsconfig provides, minus\nbaseUrl. paths alone (resolved relative to this tsconfig file) is\nsufficient for the @site/* alias. Verified: npm run typecheck and\nnpm run build both pass clean with typescript 7.0.2.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: claudioed <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"afe9db6b32fa3ad7f639ea1a8bf9a8cd63d348bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-console/git/trees/afe9db6b32fa3ad7f639ea1a8bf9a8cd63d348bd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-console/git/commits/87b2bef6cca876c2c9153ce042d51b6066592618","verification":{"payload":"tree afe9db6b32fa3ad7f639ea1a8bf9a8cd63d348bd\nparent defde4f0d58755df7cba8ca1ce3b8357092f4b16\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1789303287 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789303287 -0300\n\nbuild(deps-dev): bump typescript from 5.6.3 to 7.0.2 in /docs (#15)\n\n* build(deps-dev): bump typescript from 5.6.3 to 7.0.2 in /docs\n\nBumps [typescript](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript) from 5.6.3 to 7.0.2.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/compare/v5.6.3...v7.0.2)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: typescript\n  dependency-version: 7.0.2\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-major\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\n\n* fix(docs): stop extending @docusaurus/tsconfig, TS7 rejects its baseUrl\n\ndocs/tsconfig.json extends @docusaurus/tsconfig, which still sets\nbaseUrl in its own config. TypeScript 7.0.2 removed baseUrl entirely\n(TS5102), and extends can''t drop an inherited option, so this bump\nbroke npm run typecheck.\n\nFix: inline the same settings @docusaurus/tsconfig provides, minus\nbaseUrl. paths alone (resolved relative to this tsconfig file) is\nsufficient for the @site/* alias. Verified: npm run typecheck and\nnpm run build both pass clean with typescript 7.0.2.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: claudioed <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqppn3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAICYQADa4DyA7v5TUUwYVdENa38/k\nY1tag1LTlm+meQfc+yA8BGnVJRsIFatAmwaOGMDuwEs7Z+vsO6t9NhACV36TUDyg\nZ0j+OXnKSfT4mt2GeIbw5SXKi7hCI4bB0D1sCz1kZbCE/8AqnYyTBqlL66TbvMIk\nL1+8XnKhL7JlV4V3NiLA5EmOdASeI946w+kcZuO9lgMn97KQqmLNBAxqFik1NkF5\nRaUCWGGZhPPgLpDwS3gH/MfAx0BoOgZymRQEoTyZCLE5UfnZXXiJ7s62wRfrSySw\nQJKH9XQC9O9W2fkTF8mhS4srUkZ2fi4cw8N3xRpBRHgQcS51G4k5fxjoKZJysRgw\nnLbXpr/3rcXYtb57WQkcGfbW+ARnt/0iPH8xSYLaYQirj5vxPHPqOWFIwOMjQIeW\n5hNMNfjEs4y6yV2zoZHyGgmfGXzXaw4+YYpKR4QkV7fKBSg3KNybG2nZLppASZ30\nFRBEkFwStT7fPZT56KmHi2lMa5doUzdg7s1GFKwzE+WG9VfSpVzV96jru+PfKBfB\nvhVQrqlgZUTK/BzQoEtLIsIWum3JxaM2uXd9DdgSRQuqFVdB0UZm8q5dHwZ0S/Z1\ndG+b5O/UhCNWXxdwGlGr/NcG2SphUh+mnvC/kxFuzniOek00OIdB167T8brOBofw\nc/z5b9fgPeAw1V5I5abV\n=IX0w\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-13T12:41:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-console/commit/87b2bef6cca876c2c9153ce042d51b6066592618","node_id":"C_kwDOUID9KNoAKDg3YjJiZWY2Y2NhODc2YzJjOTE1M2NlMDQyZDUxYjYwNjY1OTI2MTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-console/commit/defde4f0d58755df7cba8ca1ce3b8357092f4b16","sha":"defde4f0d58755df7cba8ca1ce3b8357092f4b16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-console/commits/defde4f0d58755df7cba8ca1ce3b8357092f4b16"}],"sha":"87b2bef6cca876c2c9153ce042d51b6066592618","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-console/commits/87b2bef6cca876c2c9153ce042d51b6066592618"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-console/commits/defde4f0d58755df7cba8ca1ce3b8357092f4b16/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T17:43:03Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T17:43:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: resolve endpoints at runtime and address remotes by gateway path (#22)\n\nCloses the long-standing \"one image is only good for the environment it was\nbuilt for\" gap and makes the shell deployable behind the fleet''s Nginx web\ngateway, where frontend and API traffic use two independent host\nentrypoints and neither proxies to the other:\n\n  http://localhost      -> Nginx web gateway -> shell (/) + remotes (/mfes/*)\n  http://localhost:8000 -> Kong              -> every API (/api/<context>)\n\nKong must never serve HTML/JS/CSS; the web gateway must never proxy an API.\n\nruntime-config.ts (new):\n- fetches /config.json (mounted from a ConfigMap) and publishes the\n  validated contract on window.__WAREHOUSE_CONFIG__ for every remote.\n- validation is strict and fail-fast: non-object, missing/empty apiOrigin,\n  relative URL, non-HTTP scheme, or an origin carrying a path, query or\n  credentials are all rejected. A console pointed at nothing is worse than\n  one that refuses to start and says why.\n- rejects a non-OK response AND a non-JSON content type. nginx serves this\n  SPA with an index.html fallback, so a MISSING /config.json comes back as\n  HTML with a 200 rather than a 404; without the content-type check the app\n  would fail with a confusing JSON parse error instead of naming the real\n  problem.\n\nconfig.ts:\n- SERVICE_BASE_URL/BFF_BASE_URL are now resolved from the runtime origin as\n  <apiOrigin>/api/<context> instead of per-service localhost ports, and a\n  production build with no runtime config throws rather than silently\n  falling back to a developer port. Vite dev still uses the ports from\n  e2e-tests/env.sh.\n\nmain.tsx:\n- imports ./App DYNAMICALLY, after loadRuntimeConfig() resolves. A static\n  import would be hoisted and evaluated first, so config.ts (and every\n  remote''s own config module) would read an empty config and throw in\n  production. A failed load renders a plain error instead of mounting.\n\nvite.config.ts:\n- a production build addresses each remote at /mfes/<context>/remoteEntry.js\n  instead of its dev-server port. Kept as an object rather than the\n  ({command}) => ({}) callback form because vitest.config.ts does\n  mergeConfig() and Vite rejects a callback with \"Cannot merge config in\n  form of callback\", which breaks the whole suite.\n\nnginx.conf:\n- serves /config.json as an exact match with Cache-Control: no-store and an\n  explicit 404 (never the SPA fallback), no-cache on index.html, and a\n  single immutable Cache-Control on hashed assets -- `expires` is omitted\n  deliberately because it emits a SECOND Cache-Control header.\n\nchart:\n- runtime-config ConfigMap + subPath mount, and a checksum/runtime-config\n  pod annotation. subPath mounts are NOT live-updated by kubelet, so\n  without the checksum a changed apiOrigin would never reach the browser.\n  Fixed the annotation block, which was nested inside `with .podAnnotations`\n  and therefore skipped entirely under default values.\n\nDockerfile:\n- node:22-bookworm-slim and a lockfile-free install. The npm-10/macOS\n  lockfile has no linux entries for Vite 8''s native optional deps, so\n  node:26''s npm 11 rejects it outright and npm/cli#4828 leaves the binding\n  missing anyway -- `vite build` then dies with \"Cannot find native\n  binding\".\n\ntsconfig.test.json:\n- add vite/client types; the tests now import config.ts, which reads\n  import.meta.env.PROD.\n\nVerified: lint, typecheck, 42 tests, build, and helm lint all green; the\nbuilt bundle references all 8 remotes by gateway path with zero dev-port\nleakage. The image was then run behind a gateway harness and driven with a\nreal browser (Playwright): /config.json is fetched before mount,\nwindow.__WAREHOUSE_CONFIG__ is published, React renders, all 8 remoteEntry\nrequests go to /mfes/<context>/, zero requests hit a dev port, and\nnavigating to /order-management actually mounted that remote''s UI. Caught\nand fixed one real bug this way -- the nginx.conf header used C-style //\ncomments, which nginx rejects outright (\"unknown directive\"), so the\ncontainer would have crash-looped in the cluster.","tree":{"sha":"2546c14ec1cea7427be30a72c52adc0fdabb8820","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-console/git/trees/2546c14ec1cea7427be30a72c52adc0fdabb8820"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-console/git/commits/defde4f0d58755df7cba8ca1ce3b8357092f4b16","verification":{"payload":"tree 2546c14ec1cea7427be30a72c52adc0fdabb8820\nparent d2df2bc887d73e59dffc28da3bda20a130df71a0\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1789234983 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789234983 -0300\n\nfeat: resolve endpoints at runtime and address remotes by gateway path (#22)\n\nCloses the long-standing \"one image is only good for the environment it was\nbuilt for\" gap and makes the shell deployable behind the fleet''s Nginx web\ngateway, where frontend and API traffic use two independent host\nentrypoints and neither proxies to the other:\n\n  http://localhost      -> Nginx web gateway -> shell (/) + remotes (/mfes/*)\n  http://localhost:8000 -> Kong              -> every API (/api/<context>)\n\nKong must never serve HTML/JS/CSS; the web gateway must never proxy an API.\n\nruntime-config.ts (new):\n- fetches /config.json (mounted from a ConfigMap) and publishes the\n  validated contract on window.__WAREHOUSE_CONFIG__ for every remote.\n- validation is strict and fail-fast: non-object, missing/empty apiOrigin,\n  relative URL, non-HTTP scheme, or an origin carrying a path, query or\n  credentials are all rejected. A console pointed at nothing is worse than\n  one that refuses to start and says why.\n- rejects a non-OK response AND a non-JSON content type. nginx serves this\n  SPA with an index.html fallback, so a MISSING /config.json comes back as\n  HTML with a 200 rather than a 404; without the content-type check the app\n  would fail with a confusing JSON parse error instead of naming the real\n  problem.\n\nconfig.ts:\n- SERVICE_BASE_URL/BFF_BASE_URL are now resolved from the runtime origin as\n  <apiOrigin>/api/<context> instead of per-service localhost ports, and a\n  production build with no runtime config throws rather than silently\n  falling back to a developer port. Vite dev still uses the ports from\n  e2e-tests/env.sh.\n\nmain.tsx:\n- imports ./App DYNAMICALLY, after loadRuntimeConfig() resolves. A static\n  import would be hoisted and evaluated first, so config.ts (and every\n  remote''s own config module) would read an empty config and throw in\n  production. A failed load renders a plain error instead of mounting.\n\nvite.config.ts:\n- a production build addresses each remote at /mfes/<context>/remoteEntry.js\n  instead of its dev-server port. Kept as an object rather than the\n  ({command}) => ({}) callback form because vitest.config.ts does\n  mergeConfig() and Vite rejects a callback with \"Cannot merge config in\n  form of callback\", which breaks the whole suite.\n\nnginx.conf:\n- serves /config.json as an exact match with Cache-Control: no-store and an\n  explicit 404 (never the SPA fallback), no-cache on index.html, and a\n  single immutable Cache-Control on hashed assets -- `expires` is omitted\n  deliberately because it emits a SECOND Cache-Control header.\n\nchart:\n- runtime-config ConfigMap + subPath mount, and a checksum/runtime-config\n  pod annotation. subPath mounts are NOT live-updated by kubelet, so\n  without the checksum a changed apiOrigin would never reach the browser.\n  Fixed the annotation block, which was nested inside `with .podAnnotations`\n  and therefore skipped entirely under default values.\n\nDockerfile:\n- node:22-bookworm-slim and a lockfile-free install. The npm-10/macOS\n  lockfile has no linux entries for Vite 8''s native optional deps, so\n  node:26''s npm 11 rejects it outright and npm/cli#4828 leaves the binding\n  missing anyway -- `vite build` then dies with \"Cannot find native\n  binding\".\n\ntsconfig.test.json:\n- add vite/client types; the tests now import config.ts, which reads\n  import.meta.env.PROD.\n\nVerified: lint, typecheck, 42 tests, build, and helm lint all green; the\nbuilt bundle references all 8 remotes by gateway path with zero dev-port\nleakage. The image was then run behind a gateway harness and driven with a\nreal browser (Playwright): /config.json is fetched before mount,\nwindow.__WAREHOUSE_CONFIG__ is published, React renders, all 8 remoteEntry\nrequests go to /mfes/<context>/, zero requests hit a dev port, and\nnavigating to /order-management actually mounted that remote''s UI. Caught\nand fixed one real bug this way -- the nginx.conf header used C-style //\ncomments, which nginx rejects outright (\"unknown directive\"), so the\ncontainer would have crash-looped in the cluster.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpY8nCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAd9wQAJuLWbmfkXNg+4ZaMEEh97pg\nCAeRZ+IOkfFbRb+ljO3LSFOnc1Lgd8u/rVeMQXJ8W0kxu4OcDByG1VXjwKqkv3Qh\n7TY6GARx7LC+VQNNviHaU71EZw7rWLFczwgr8J2hEpw3TS4/28MWK8xrHEwfZPTu\ntI0znFn51h9On1GHYhs0f+8IKQIMbgmOheW471qveFTTqCL9BrMXikKM2D1U3h0S\n/V7CFjJjtKWGCe6TKBi83f2oG89UxeVZBz58oPoKxAx1r4yDXAGmCbTqOUY+rnWH\nqMuBU3nCXZMygIPhfa0bbDQXd8bqexpP/pJLWHaxxM