eira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T19:16:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(process-path): wire process-path-mfe as a new remote (#10)\n\nRebased/redone on top of PR #8''s Floor+Contexts nav restructure (the\noriginal branch this work was on predates that landing and would have\nconflicted). Adds process-path-mfe (process-path-management''s operator\nSPA, merged in process-path-management#4) as this shell''s seventh\nremote, following the CURRENT (post-#8) pattern: remotes are no longer\ntop-level nav items, they live behind the /contexts launchpad as\nLaunchTiles.\n\n- vite.config.ts: federation.remotes entry, dev port 5189 (matching\n  process-path-management''s own chart''s pre-reserved\n  corsAllowedOrigins value).\n- App.tsx: REMOTE_PREFIXES gains /process-path (so \"Contexts\" lights\n  up correctly while this remote is open), module-scope lazy() import,\n  and a /process-path/* route wrapped in the existing RemoteBoundary.\n- ContextsScreen.tsx: a new LaunchTile for process-path-management,\n  following the exact pattern the other six use.\n- README.md: added process-path-mfe to the local-dev port table.\n- scripts/verify-all-routes.cjs: added /process-path to the route list\n  (this script also changed materially in #8 -- routes now carry a\n  content assertion, not just an error check; the new entry follows\n  that same shape).\n\nVerified\n--------\n- npm run lint / npm run typecheck / npm run build / npm test: all\n  clean, 22/22 tests pass (the full suite added in #8).\n- Ran the real dev server (:5173) plus process-path-mfe''s own dev\n  server (:5189) and a scoped headless Playwright check:\n  - /contexts renders the new \"PROCESS-PATH-MANAGEMENT / Process\n    Paths\" tile alongside the other six, correct copy and href.\n  - /process-path resolves to the new remote and renders\n    ProcessPathsScreen''s full form + DataTable with correct headers.\n  - Zero page errors; remaining REQUEST FAILED noise is pre-existing\n    and unrelated (other remotes'' dev servers and backend services\n    were not running during this scoped check).","tree":{"sha":"18e9129af9497fd239a89dce263e8ee2cec45d17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-console/git/trees/18e9129af9497fd239a89dce263e8ee2cec45d17"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-console/git/commits/c9160109cf57475937c85842eb07e62db115e619","verification":{"payload":"tree 18e9129af9497fd239a89dce263e8ee2cec45d17\nparent f00791354176971b1f6ce538006064d4cb4a63b7\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1788722200 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788722200 -0300\n\nfeat(process-path): wire process-path-mfe as a new remote (#10)\n\nRebased/redone on top of PR #8''s Floor+Contexts nav restructure (the\noriginal branch this work was on predates that landing and would have\nconflicted). Adds process-path-mfe (process-path-management''s operator\nSPA, merged in process-path-management#4) as this shell''s seventh\nremote, following the CURRENT (post-#8) pattern: remotes are no longer\ntop-level nav items, they live behind the /contexts launchpad as\nLaunchTiles.\n\n- vite.config.ts: federation.remotes entry, dev port 5189 (matching\n  process-path-management''s own chart''s pre-reserved\n  corsAllowedOrigins value).\n- App.tsx: REMOTE_PREFIXES gains /process-path (so \"Contexts\" lights\n  up correctly while this remote is open), module-scope lazy() import,\n  and a /process-path/* route wrapped in the existing RemoteBoundary.\n- ContextsScreen.tsx: a new LaunchTile for process-path-management,\n  following the exact pattern the other six use.\n- README.md: added process-path-mfe to the local-dev port table.\n- scripts/verify-all-routes.cjs: added /process-path to the route list\n  (this script also changed materially in #8 -- routes now carry a\n  content assertion, not just an error check; the new entry follows\n  that same shape).\n\nVerified\n--------\n- npm