eef7bbb9b2544933062e9f627de8d9384","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-console/commits/5f908bfeef7bbb9b2544933062e9f627de8d9384"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-console/commits/c0eefbccc26397f4d4983c76d3256eeba8331171/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T17:25:36Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T17:25:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: apk upgrade in Dockerfile runtime stage to clear Trivy findings (#4)\n\n* feat: add Dockerfile and Helm chart for warehouse-console\n\nAdds fleet-standard packaging so warehouse-console can be built and\ndeployed like the Go services: a 3-stage Dockerfile (ui-kit sibling\nbuild -> app build -> nginx-unprivileged runtime on 8080), a matching\nHelm chart at charts/warehouse-console/, and CI parity (helm-lint,\nimage-based trivy-scan, docker-publish with cosign signing/SBOM\nattestation, and a release job that packages the chart to\noci://ghcr.io/claudioed).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FogYxqLgj896STU3QD8qKU\n\n* fix: apk upgrade in runtime stage to clear Trivy CRITICAL/HIGH findings\n\nnginx-unprivileged:1.27-alpine''s baked-in alpine 3.21.3 packages had\nfixed CVEs available in the same branch (openssl, libxml2, libpng,\nlibexpat, c-ares, etc.) that the trivy-scan CI job''s blocking gate\ncorrectly flagged. Runs `apk upgrade --no-cache` as root before\nswitching back to the non-root nginx user, matching the fleet''s Go\nservice runtime stages. Verified locally: 32 (2 CRITICAL/30 HIGH) -> 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FogYxqLgj896STU3QD8qKU\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4744868f5617c87afaedcff94adf6f8908f24dab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-console/git/trees/4744868f5617c87afaedcff94adf6f8908f24dab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-console/git/commits/c0eefbccc26397f4d4983c76d3256eeba8331171","verification":{"payload":"tree 4744868f5617c87afaedcff94adf6f8908f24dab\nparent 77209306695b0254409ad6c95c1ba960b4e90813\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1788629136 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788629136 -0300\n\nfix: apk upgrade in Dockerfile runtime stage to clear Trivy findings (#4)\n\n* feat: add Dockerfile and Helm chart for warehouse-console\n\nAdds fleet-standard packaging so warehouse-console can be built and\ndeployed like the Go services: a 3-stage Dockerfile (ui-kit sibling\nbuild -> app build -> nginx-unprivileged runtime on 8080), a matching\nHelm chart at charts/warehouse-console/, and CI parity (helm-lint,\nimage-based trivy-scan, docker-publish with cosign signing/SBOM\nattestation, and a release job that packages the chart to\noci://ghcr.io/claudioed).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FogYxqLgj896STU3QD8qKU\n\n* fix: apk upgrade in runtime stage to clear Trivy CRITICAL/HIGH findings\n\nnginx-unprivileged:1.27-alpine''s baked-in alpine 3.21.3 packages had\nfixed CVEs available in the same branch (openssl, libxml2, libpng,\nlibexpat, c-ares, etc.) that the trivy-scan CI job''s blocking gate\ncorrectly flagged. Runs `apk upgrade --no-cache` as root before\nswitching back to the non-root nginx user, matching the fleet''s Go\nservice runtime stages. Verified locally: 32 (2 CRITICAL/30 HIGH) -> 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FogYxqLgj896STU3QD8qKU\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnFCQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXSAQAEul9cB1rdCO8IQ3Db0A4dd5\nBxQFosd+bB+WBNm7i9L3K0z7GGmF+w1gn2aC/OZokPkZyw86q3wEP6V2RgqZCU3x\nURNhbkVnEnu1tssiZ7bpxjSs3ohyoxCLNX4r9goDeYzunllkY+ADFSDrYP0l89KO\n8Ighaae47tXD0P7Rz3jkLCjiea5wp3SLB9zrYBNpbpmo8bS6fcgV9u1Yit50YTnJ\nkFA9Y2JdcyN614D08tL4Gd7YRChIE/nRjcK5bdJIorOuj+kExyKi4Ugzn0QpaeTs\n1GXOg3Y1ZwTkUE6b0JPH2qvmTXDjxI1vJ+n5fQyzdUPSpZs4rVcxd96rIQt8b21t\ncGKdcAuM0iwBCzYW3lEmKE6smaNiBBUNz62jqxWO8abEEKg2TN86LW0PyNyVm6tl\nDjod5Ejas/HIWwqsIspmen+4AwjxpAiGzDR/hl6lYGr2jifsW6U51AGgoueB5JMC\nrcEITFBD1jitr7C6X65j1ti6fnJgq0OKNhLOtXBfTMzlVoUJ0nPRow+r2eZWWuez\nzn5es5sB3jEOD+ilStP9CXKiRSn1e9RdhM+5mAOLxcOwOnbg5M/vmZQ39tJ9Dls3\n+XZlo4x3p1WySRlUU8FhXsmNULDu+UyazKMAMyWxT1ke/C1MXnXqPl1VlbJ6it3Y\n87Oh2Gnvyyar4n0gv7PE\n=frdT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-05T17:25:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-console/commit/c0eefbccc26397f4d4983c76d3256eeba8331171","node_id":"C_kwDOUID9KNoAKGMwZWVmYmNjYzI2Mzk3ZjRkNDk4M2M3NmQzMjU2ZWViYTgzMzExNzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-console/commit/77209306695b0254409ad6c95c1ba960b4e90813","sha":"77209306695b0254409ad6c95c1ba960b4e90813","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-console/commits/77209306695b0254409ad6c95c1ba960b4e90813"}],"sha":"c0eefbccc26397f4d4983c76d3256eeba8331171","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-console/commits/c0eefbccc26397f4d4983c76d3256eeba8331171"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-console/commits/58826b4f568d181885d146f4e6c5f2b9f9e2f933/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T17:22:20Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T17:22:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Release: warehouse-console initial console shell (#3)\n\n* fix: correct trivy-action version tag (0.28.0 doesn''t exist, use v0.36.0)\n\n* feat: WMS and WES report dashboards (#1)\n\nTwo new shell-owned, cross-cutting screens backed by the console-bff''s\nsection-oriented report envelope (GET /console/reports/{wms,wes}):\n\n- /wms-dashboard -- what & where: order funnel (funnel), inventory flow\n  accuracy (bar), catalog growth (line).\n- /wes-dashboard -- when & in what order: planning throughput (line),\n  fulfillment throughput (bar), labor management (bar), labor\n  performance (bar).\n\nBoth consume the identical envelope, so the rendering rules live once in\nfeatures/reports/ReportDashboard.tsx and each screen is a thin wrapper\nnaming its title and endpoint. Chart primitive is chosen per section by\nthe payload''s own chartKind, so the BFF -- not the console -- decides how\na section reads.\n\nThese are eventually-consistent analytical projections, not live reads,\nso each card renders its freshnessLagSeconds through the ui-kit''s\nFreshnessBadge. Staleness is shown, never hidden.\n\nTwo failure modes kept deliberately distinct: a section arriving with\navailable:false is a routine, expected degradation of one upstream and\nrenders as one \"data unavailable\" card (the \"—\" convention Overview''s\nKPI tiles already use) while every other section still draws its real\nnumbers; only a whole-request failure produces a dashboard-level error\nstate. No number is ever fabricated to keep a card looking healthy.\n\nAlso adds scripts/verify-dashboards.cjs (npm run verify:dashboards),\nwhich stubs the report calls so all three states can be verified in a\nreal headless browser without a live warehouse-ops-agent.\n\nDepends on two upstream PRs before this is live end to end:\n  - warehouse-ui-kit#1 (feature/chart-primitives) -- BarChart, LineChart\n    and FunnelChart. Until it merges into ui-kit''s develop, this repo''s\n    CI typecheck/build jobs will fail, since they check the ui-kit out\n    at develop. No change is needed here once it merges: package.json\n    already points at file:../warehouse-ui-kit.\n  - warehouse-ops-agent (feature/console-reports-bff) -- the two report\n    endpoints themselves, which are not implemented yet.\n\n* feat: add Dockerfile and Helm chart for warehouse-console (#2)\n\nAdds fleet-standard packaging so warehouse-console can be built and\ndeployed like the Go services: a 3-stage Dockerfile (ui-kit sibling\nbuild -> app build -> nginx-unprivileged runtime on 8080), a matching\nHelm chart at charts/warehouse-console/, and CI parity (helm-lint,\nimage-based trivy-scan, docker-publish with cosign signing/SBOM\nattestation, and a release job that packages the chart to\noci://ghcr.io/claudioed).\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FogYxqLgj896STU3QD8qKU\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"655de89e29a2a79d1f0a0d4f0c8c31db05aa9aad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-console/git/trees/655de89e29a2a79d1f0a0d4f0c8c31db05aa9aad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-console/git/commits/58826b4f568d181885d146f4e6c5f2b9f9e2f933","verification":{"payload":"tree 655de89e29a2a79d1f0a0d4f0c8c31db05aa9aad\nparent 4aec5cce04a8a745f568a548118c7c29907af27b\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1788628940 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788628940 -0300\n\nRelease: warehouse-console initial console shell (#3)\n\n* fix: correct trivy-action version tag (0.28.0 doesn''t exist, use v0.36.0)\n\n* feat: WMS and WES report dashboards (#1)\n\nTwo new shell-owned, cross-cutting screens backed by the console-bff''s\nsection-oriented report envelope (GET /console/reports/{wms,wes}):\n\n- /wms-dashboard -- what & where: order funnel (funnel), inventory flow\n  accuracy (bar), catalog growth (line).\n- /wes-dashboard -- when & in what order: planning throughput (line),\n  fulfillment throughput (bar), labor management (bar), labor\n  performance (bar).\n\nBoth consume the identical envelope, so the rendering rules live once in\nfeatures/reports/ReportDashboard.tsx and each screen is a thin wrapper\nnaming its title and endpoint. Chart primitive is chosen per section by\nthe payload''s own chartKind, so the BFF -- not the console -- decides how\na section reads.\n\nThese are eventually-consistent analytical projections, not live reads,\nso each card renders its freshnessLagSeconds through the ui-kit''s\nFreshnessBadge. Staleness is shown, never hidden.\n\nTwo failure modes kept deliberately distinct: a section arriving with\navailable:false is a routine, expected degradation of one upstream and\nrenders as one \"data unavailable\" card (the \"—\" convention Overview''s\nKPI tiles already use) while every other section still draws its real\nnumbers; only a whole-request failure produces a dashboard-level error\nstate. No number is ever fabricated to keep a card looking healthy.\n\nAlso adds scripts/verify-dashboards.cjs (npm run verify:dashboards),\nwhich stubs the report calls so all three states can be verified in a\nreal headless browser without a live warehouse-ops-agent.\n\nDepends on two upstream PRs before this is live end to end:\n  - warehouse-ui-kit#1 (feature/chart-primitives) -- BarChart, LineChart\n    and FunnelChart. Until it merges into ui-kit''s develop, this repo''s\n    CI typecheck/build jobs will fail, since they check the ui-kit out\n    at develop. No change is needed here once it merges: package.json\n    already points at file:../warehouse-ui-kit.\n  - warehouse-ops-agent (feature/console-reports-bff) -- the two report\n    endpoints themselves, which are not implemented yet.\n\n* feat: add Dockerfile and Helm chart for warehouse-console (#2)\n\nAdds fleet-standard packaging so warehouse-console can be built and\ndeployed like the Go services: a 3-stage Dockerfile (ui-kit sibling\nbuild -> app build -> nginx-unprivileged runtime on 8080), a matching\nHelm chart at charts/warehouse-console/, and CI parity (helm-lint,\nimage-based trivy-scan, docker-publish with cosign signing/SBOM\nattestation, and a release job that packages the chart to\noci://ghcr.io/claudioed).\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FogYxqLgj896STU3QD8qKU\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnE/MCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWK8QAKdiHKd16zajzn3BA6YdXeWo\nn70ktK6g7FMAwqIlo44mCZqTpmiTNjZYBFQ3DPL/sMrAvIMtXZJLct5t7yNodaZI\ntbL7AHuXT6NGsYP6ba6BSiGSLvw54anLPdr86C+6RwkP4P3WKw/2HnuznLojpOTI\nI6DwwUqHnxZVRXBtUsPuye9QtEsbW/JAHTErFGBZpfsjjnk3mXd72vjZMYf1gMMK\nnpiH44JYzqw0f9TbQ48UEzivVzvwdEMu5XquuDsI5mUBZ9ryoOwqdwVzFsc4vmUO\nVGzbgVskRljDhN1pmrBCZwS4AlXzzSD5hQrmNiQofny5n14PQdKP1wBG89IPjcq0\nI0Cf/KG7lr6GMAvQua5+8HeQoUNeOLqwLMUD/KlG8NgUB427uWGsoytk0b6fKIxx\nWLv99XWAnAq6UIpgj+/bx/4VGptt1PzgEEx/z5gqyKN2veiU6l5yXXdUvmQd2uyK\nprTFD6kFs/sWTvZ3jNGIZBRtiMcpbtMDrlMnsoWAM/rj8MwD6pUVlTCA1B3NJBni\nuYZ4FiJR+rsSFi2MyyzwK1jbqW4inGu9LCGAprOXofS+tGNKhDDml+45fPRqe4Rz\nl8mr0LbtzuV77ECW347olkLUlTmzEvYDihhE0mHSoTQGUgz8V2IjIgor7kDuT14+\ncduyAFWS15ahn8tgHAh8\n=Pura\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"