m/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-console/commits/4aec5cce04a8a745f568a548118c7c29907af27b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T14:07:33Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"claudioed"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T14:07:33Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"claudioed"},"message":"feat: initial warehouse-console shell\n\nReact SPA shell hosting 6 Module Federation remotes (order-mgmt-mfe,\ninventory-mfe, planning-mfe, fulfillment-mfe, workforce-mfe,\nfacility-mfe), each owned by its own bounded-context repo.\n\nTwo cross-cutting screens live here since they''re not owned by any\nsingle context:\n- Order Lifecycle: cross-service order trace via the console-bff on\n  warehouse-ops-agent (order-management -> inventory-storage ->\n  wes-work-planning -> fulfillment-execution).\n- Operations Overview (new landing page): a KPI control-tower strip +\n  Fiori-style launchpad grid, applying established enterprise WMS/\n  ops-dashboard conventions (Manhattan Active WM, SAP Fiori, Grafana/\n  Datadog-style stat panels) with real numbers from each service''s own\n  REST endpoint -- no fabricated data.\n\nFixed a real render-time bug found while wiring this up: RemoteBoundary\nwas calling lazy() inside its own render body, which would remount\nevery federated remote (re-triggering its MF fetch) on every Shell\nre-render. Hoisted all 6 lazy() calls to module scope in App.tsx.","tree":{"sha":"6542c408e3be737c96eae13ef489f102cd813f1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-console/git/trees/6542c408e3be737c96eae13ef489f102cd813f1d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-console/git/commits/4aec5cce04a8a745f568a548118c7c29907af27b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar