,"events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/labor-performance/commit/dd26355a4f088481dddae488c39c910667dd3733","node_id":"C_kwDOUIGXYtoAKGRkMjYzNTVhNGYwODg0ODFkZGRhZTQ4OGMzOWM5MTA2NjdkZDM3MzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/labor-performance/commit/c098639ea22c5d48e49da1657352932af05a1cb6","sha":"c098639ea22c5d48e49da1657352932af05a1cb6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/c098639ea22c5d48e49da1657352932af05a1cb6"}],"sha":"dd26355a4f088481dddae488c39c910667dd3733","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/dd26355a4f088481dddae488c39c910667dd3733"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/c098639ea22c5d48e49da1657352932af05a1cb6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T10:59:48Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T10:59:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: resolve findings from the 2026-10-05 docs audit (#121)\n\n* fix(web): send Idempotency-Key from the labor_mfe define-standard form\n\napiPost sent only Content-Type, so against Postgres (RequireIdempotencyKey,\nADR 0016) POST /standards answered 400 idempotency-key-required. Send a\nfresh crypto.randomUUID() per submission; add a vitest; drop the README\nKnown-gap entry.\n\n* fix(kafka): make the analytics consumer''s claim+apply atomic and retry failures\n\nAnalyticsConsumer marked analytics_consumed_events before the projection\ntransaction and ReadMessage auto-committed the offset, so a failed apply\nwas logged and never retried (and the surviving claim hid a replay).\n\n- analyticsstore.UnitOfWork wraps the claim and the projection apply in one\n  Postgres transaction; ConsumedEventsRepo and PostgresProjection join the\n  ctx-carried tx (pgtx) when present.\n- Run uses FetchMessage + CommitMessages (after success only) and retries a\n  failing message with capped exponential backoff (200ms..5s).\n- Undecodable data payloads are deterministic: WARN + skip, not claimed.\n- Unit tests (rollback of the claim, fake reader commit ordering),\n  testcontainers Postgres UoW test and a Kafka+Postgres end-to-end test.\n- ADR 0031 + index, sequence-diagram/eventstorming updates, README gap closed.\n\n* fix(postgres): keep the shared tx usable after a one-open-standard 23505\n\nUnder RequireIdempotencyKey the use case''s UnitOfWork reuses the\nmiddleware''s transaction. A 23505 on\nidx_labor_standards_one_open_per_task_type aborted that transaction\n(SQLSTATE 25P02), so the middleware''s UPDATE idempotency_keys failed and the\nrequest returned 500 instead of 409 standard-conflict.\n\nStandardRepo.Save now runs its statement in a SAVEPOINT when a transaction\nis in the context, so only the failed INSERT is rolled back.\n\nTests (testcontainers): a repo-level test that the surrounding tx stays\nusable after both ErrOpenStandardConflict and ErrConcurrentModification, and\nan HTTP-level test where two requests with different keys race to open the\nfirst standard (one 201, one recorded 409 standard-conflict). Both failed\nbefore the fix (25P02 / 500).\n\n* docs: correct the task-type open-gap contract and refresh stale comments\n\nget_task_type_utilization and GET /task-types/{taskType}/utilization promised\nthe still-running open gap, but GetUtilization.ForTaskType has always\nreturned openGapSeconds 0: ADR 0014 defines the open gap per associate, and\nattributing it to a task type is a business rule the ADRs do not specify.\nThe MCP tool description, the OpenAPI descriptions (generated API reference\nregenerated like ci.yml''s docs-api-drift job) and the use-case comments now\nsay it is always 0 at task-type scope; tests pin both the use case and the\ntool description. The open-gap-per-task-type question is left for a product\ndecision.\n\nAlso: shared.DomainEvent and ports.EventPublisher no longer claim \"v1 ships a\nlog publisher only / not yet consumed\"; asyncapi.yaml contact URL -> IQVO\n(also openapi*.yaml) and the integration channel says workforce-management\nalready consumes it.","tree":{"sha":"7f171d438de4c26eee99264e457939c6f3ab2173","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/git/trees/7f171d438de4c26eee99264e457939c6f3ab2173"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/git/commits/c098639ea22c5d48e49da1657352932af05a1cb6","verification":{"payload":"tree 7f171d438de4c26eee99264e457939c6f3ab2173\nparent b4710a6c03d6feb672b3bf4b006be874eedc0636\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791284388 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791284388 -0300\n\nfix: resolve findings from the 2026-10-05 docs audit (#121)\n\n* fix(web): send Idempotency-Key from the labor_mfe define-standard form\n\napiPost sent only Content-Type, so against Postgres (RequireIdempotencyKey,\nADR 0016) POST /standards answered 400 idempotency-key-required. Send a\nfresh crypto.randomUUID() per submission; add a vitest; drop the README\nKnown-gap entry.\n\n* fix(kafka): make the analytics consumer''s claim+apply atomic and retry failures\n\nAnalyticsConsumer marked analytics_consumed_events before the projection\ntransaction and ReadMessage auto-committed the offset, so a failed apply\nwas logged and never retried (and the surviving claim hid a replay).\n\n- analyticsstore.UnitOfWork wraps the claim and the projection apply in one\n  Postgres transaction; ConsumedEventsRepo and PostgresProjection join the\n  ctx-carried tx (pgtx) when present.\n- Run uses FetchMessage + CommitMessages (after success only) and retries a\n  failing message with capped exponential backoff (200ms..5s).\n- Undecodable data payloads are deterministic: WARN + skip, not claimed.\n- Unit tests (rollback of the claim, fake reader commit ordering),\n  testcontainers Postgres UoW test and a Kafka+Postgres end-to-end test.\n- ADR 0031 + index, sequence-diagram/eventstorming updates, README gap closed.\n\n* fix(postgres): keep the shared tx usable after a one-open-standard 23505\n\nUnder RequireIdempotencyKey the use case''s UnitOfWork reuses the\nmiddleware''s transaction. A 23505 on\nidx_labor_standards_one_open_per_task_type aborted that transaction\n(SQLSTATE 25P02), so the middleware''s UPDATE idempotency_keys failed and the\nrequest returned 500 instead of 409 standard-conflict.\n\nStandardRepo.Save now runs its statement in a SAVEPOINT when a transaction\nis in the context, so only the failed INSERT is rolled back.\n\nTests (testcontainers): a repo-level test that the surrounding tx stays\nusable after both ErrOpenStandardConflict and ErrConcurrentModification, and\nan HTTP-level test where two requests with different keys race to open the\nfirst standard (one 201, one recorded 409 standard-conflict). Both failed\nbefore the fix (25P02 / 500).\n\n* docs: correct the task-type open-gap contract and refresh stale comments\n\nget_task_type_utilization and GET /task-types/{taskType}/utilization promised\nthe still-running open gap, but GetUtilization.ForTaskType has always\nreturned openGapSeconds 0: ADR 0014 defines the open gap per associate, and\nattributing it to a task type is a business rule the ADRs do not specify.\nThe MCP tool description, the OpenAPI descriptions (generated API reference\nregenerated like ci.yml''s docs-api-drift job) and the use-case comments now\nsay it is always 0 at task-type scope; tests pin both the use case and the\ntool description. The open-gap-per-task-type question is left for a product\ndecision.\n\nAlso: shared.DomainEvent and ports.EventPublisher no longer claim \"v1 ships a\nlog publisher only / not yet consumed\"; asyncapi.yaml contact URL -> IQVO\n(also openapi*.yaml) and the integration channel says workforce-management\nalready consumes it.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxNSkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZ2MQAEf6joL4nidAb0+OBy8SCh2a\n4PTDazfRJbf/bh6T6QQVDzGfdAwn9ZBEmLKEK0iPFzT7jLyprl/0xV2DFskSVNuM\ncZsoDyEdiOqyAplFNQ4t0veVC6bTc2FdzunGDk6pf96Z1VAFwS4P2CpcJtUif2uK\nd7GczfjmE3ZEnhWPPtlf29oPP6L+imQ5/IquCZjkK/VUjVhcvCSvA3BbqDboTV2A\nAwXmlxx9b1ayS22RI4kaWBzEsne/6Wa9XMlyF