ssage":"chore(harness): sync managed files from warehouse-harness-template","tree":{"sha":"0d007bf137acff42579afd517a6913af730741d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/git/trees/0d007bf137acff42579afd517a6913af730741d3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/git/commits/6ab6157998e055fd3cb9fd476499ae003e747e5d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/labor-performance/commit/6ab6157998e055fd3cb9fd476499ae003e747e5d","node_id":"C_kwDOUIGXYtoAKDZhYjYxNTc5OThlMDU1ZmQzY2I5ZmQ0NzY0OTlhZTAwM2U3NDdlNWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/labor-performance/commit/408fc276a8cd4ba755e6754c9e98a4184b543a5c","sha":"408fc276a8cd4ba755e6754c9e98a4184b543a5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/408fc276a8cd4ba755e6754c9e98a4184b543a5c"}],"sha":"6ab6157998e055fd3cb9fd476499ae003e747e5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/6ab6157998e055fd3cb9fd476499ae003e747e5d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/408fc276a8cd4ba755e6754c9e98a4184b543a5c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T09:49:13Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T09:49:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: ADR-conformance gaps (2026-10-04 audit): OCC+one-open-standard rollout, metrics coverage, docs drift, sweeper, DLQ writer (#114)\n\n* fix(standards): optimistic concurrency + one open standard per task type (ADR-0022)\n\n- migration 0006: labor_standards.version column + partial unique index\n  idx_labor_standards_one_open_per_task_type (task_type WHERE effective_to IS NULL)\n- StandardRepo.Save becomes a version-guarded upsert; RowsAffected()==0\n  maps to ports.ErrConcurrentModification; a 23505 on the partial index\n  maps to ports.ErrOpenStandardConflict\n- LaborStandard gains version/Version(); Rehydrate takes the row version\n- errors.go maps both sentinels to 409 concurrent-modification /\n  standard-conflict; openapi.yaml documents the header + 409 + /readyz\n- CORS AllowedHeaders adds Idempotency-Key (ADR-0016 preflight)\n- testcontainers conversion of the postgres repo suite: shared migrated\n  container via testDB(t), no DATABASE_URL skip gate; new race tests for\n  stale-version, concurrent close (exactly one winner) and the one-open-\n  standard backstop\n- ADR 0016''s ''no TTL job'' note now resolved by the sweeper (next commit)\n\n* feat(reports): serve tasksMeasured on every report layer + analyticsstore testcontainers coverage (ADR-0007)\n\n- report.Totals/TaskTypeBar gain TasksMeasured; reports_handler DTOs,\n  mapping and openapi-reports.yaml expose tasksMeasured on rows, bars and\n  totals (required) with the ADR-0006 measured-vs-scored distinction\n- fix ADR-0007''s stale line-161 claim (task_type IS on the wire since\n  fulfillment-execution ADR-0023) and the stale Deferred list (helm\n  wiring, labor-mfe remote, MCP adapter all shipped; the analytics\n  integration test now shipped too)\n- new postgres_integration_test.go: projection idempotency (double-apply),\n  commutative += upsert, UNCLASSIFIED normalisation, business-time\n  bucketing, filters, freshness watermark, consumed-events gate — against\n  a throwaway testcontainers analytics Postgres under migrations/analytics\n\n* feat(housekeeping): sweeper for idempotency keys + published outbox rows, outbox-lag gauge (ADR-0023, ADR-0010 follow-up)\n\n* fix(adr): close stale ADR text (0001/0003/0009/0014), align DLQ writer durability, regen openapi docs\n\n- ADR-0009: auth/scope sections superseded by ADR-0012; tool count 4; mcp.tool.outcome span attr; chart ships mcp-deployment.yaml disabled by default\n- ADR-0003/0014: task_type-on-the-wire gap closed by fulfillment-execution ADR-0023\n- ADR-0001: arch-go adopted (not deferred); 4 composition roots; GetUtilization in use-case list\n- fitness_test.go: TestMCPAdapterDependencyRule comment ADR-0008 -> ADR-0009\n- consumer.go: DLQ writer now sets RequiredAcks=RequireAll + Hash balancer, matching every outbound Kafka writer (ADR-0018); pinning unit test\n- openapi.yaml: 422 response documents idempotency-key-reused; regenerated docs/docs/api-reference (get-readyz + idempotency param drift)\n\n* docs(adr): short adoption ADRs for 7 undocumented features (0024-0030)\n\nlabor-mfe frontend remote, RFC 7807 problem details, arch-go fitness\nsuite, bootretry + startupProbe, Gateway API HTTPRoute, Kafka writer\ndurability (RequireAll + 10ms), MCP eval/governance gates. All added\nto about.md + sidebars.ts; docs build passes.","tree":{"sha":"c8fe536fab061333a3ea960b7af93533992c993b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/git/trees/c8fe536fab061333a3ea960b7af93533992c993b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/git/commits/408fc276a8cd4ba755e6754c9e98a4184b543a5c","verification":{"payload":"tree c8fe536fab061333a3ea960b7af93533992c993b\nparent 00161abe91258a393816a4952035d561d67bfb70\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791193753 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791193753 -0300\n\nfix: ADR-conformance gaps (2026-10-04 audit): OCC+one-open-standard rollout, metrics coverage, docs drift, sweeper, DLQ writer (#114)\n\n* fix(standards): optimistic concurrency + one open standard per task type (ADR-0022)\n\n- migration 0006: labor_standards.version column + partial unique index\n  idx_labor_standards_one_open_per_task_type (task_type WHERE effective_to IS NULL)\n- StandardRepo.Save becomes a version-guarded upsert; RowsAffected()==0\n  maps to ports.ErrConcurrentModification; a 23505 on the partial index\n  maps to ports.ErrOpenStandardConflict\n- LaborStandard gains version/Version(); Rehydrate takes the row version\n- errors.go maps both sentinels to 409 concurrent-modification /\n  standard-conflict; openapi.yaml documents the header + 409 + /readyz\