d":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/labor-performance/commit/abc7dc2ddb1d98cd5a01f7d8fb73e9e3b763bb20","node_id":"C_kwDOUIGXYtoAKGFiYzdkYzJkZGIxZDk4Y2Q1YTAxZjdkOGZiNzNlOWUzYjc2M2JiMjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/labor-performance/commit/5473a676230b599e71fdff7f00206a7e2f9d0466","sha":"5473a676230b599e71fdff7f00206a7e2f9d0466","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/5473a676230b599e71fdff7f00206a7e2f9d0466"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/labor-performance/commit/99616b7aa7602a088da1338400f1f65409a9a7e8","sha":"99616b7aa7602a088da1338400f1f65409a9a7e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/99616b7aa7602a088da1338400f1f65409a9a7e8"}],"sha":"abc7dc2ddb1d98cd5a01f7d8fb73e9e3b763bb20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/abc7dc2ddb1d98cd5a01f7d8fb73e9e3b763bb20"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/5473a676230b599e71fdff7f00206a7e2f9d0466/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T13:22:25Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T13:22:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(migrations): run golang-migrate against a direct Postgres connection, not PgBouncer (ADR 0020) (#91)\n\ngolang-migrate''s postgres driver takes a session-scoped\npg_advisory_lock to serialize concurrent migration runs at boot.\nDATABASE_URL points this service''s cmd/labor and cmd/mcp at PgBouncer\nin transaction-pooling mode (warehouse-infra PR #43), which does not\npreserve session state across statements -- each statement can land\non a different physical backend connection. Two or more replicas\nstarting concurrently (an HPA scale-out per ADR-0019, or an ordinary\nrolling deploy) crash-loop with ''pq: unnamed prepared statement does\nnot exist'' for 1-2 minutes until one wins the advisory-lock race.\n\nPorts order-management PR #115 / ADR-0029 (the reference\nimplementation for this fleet-wide Phase-4 fix) into labor-performance:\n\n- cmd/labor/main.go and cmd/mcp/main.go (both run migrations at\n  startup) now read MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL for the migration step\n  only, falling back to DATABASE_URL when unset. The runtime pgxpool\n  built right after migrations complete is untouched -- still\n  PgBouncer, exactly as before.\n- charts/labor-performance: new database.migrationsExistingSecretKey\n  value (default \"MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\") renders the env var in\n  both the api and mcp Deployments, sourced from the same\n  existingSecret, with optional: true so a secret predating this key\n  still starts the pod.\n- docs/docs/adr/0020-migrations-direct-postgres-connection.md\n  documents the incompatibility, cross-references order-management''s\n  ADR-0029 and warehouse-infra PR #43/#44, and records local\n  verification evidence.\n- cmd/labor/wiring_test.go, cmd/mcp/wiring_test.go: new regression\n  tests proving the getenv fallback in both directions and that the\n  migration step actually receives migrationsDatabaseURL, not\n  databaseURL (not just the env-var read in isolation).\n\nwarehouse-infra PR #44 already provisions the MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\nsecret key for all 9 OLTP services including this one -- no\nwarehouse-infra changes needed here. cmd/labor-projector and\ncmd/labor-reports (the analytics binaries) are out of scope: their\nANALYTICS_DATABASE_URL was never routed through PgBouncer in the\nfirst place.\n\nLocal quality gate: make check, make check-all (coverage 99.4%,\ngate 90%), go test -tags=integration ./... -race (real Postgres +\nKafka Testcontainers), and helm lint/helm template all green.","tree":{"sha":"2af102978f5ce83c2607fdc9bbb5024063b11bb2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/git/trees/2af102978f5ce83c2607fdc9bbb5024063b11bb2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/git/commits/5473a676230b599e71fdff7f00206a7e2f9d0466","verification":{"payload":"tree 2af102978f5ce83c2607fdc9bbb5024063b11bb2\nparent c1cc4a72603d7d50ccad0d1c65de54d5f8fcb2c5\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790601745 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790601745 -0300\n\nfix(migrations): run golang-migrate against a direct Postgres connection, not PgBouncer (ADR 0020) (#91)\n\ngolang-migrate''s postgres driver takes a session-scoped\npg_advisory_lock to serialize concurrent migration runs at boot.\nDATABASE_URL points this service''s cmd/labor and cmd/mcp at PgBouncer\nin transaction-pooling mode (warehouse-infra PR #43), which does not\npreserve session state across statements -- each statement can land\non a different physical backend connection. Two or more replicas\nstarting concurrently (an HPA scale-out per ADR-0019, or an ordinary\nrolling deploy) crash-loop with ''pq: unnamed prepared statement does\nnot exist'' for 1-2 minutes until one wins the advisory-lock race.\n\nPorts order-management PR #115 / ADR-0029 (the reference\nimplementation for this fleet-wide Phase-4 fix) into labor-performance:\n\n- cmd/labor/main.go and cmd/mcp/main.go (both run migrations at\n  startup) now read MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL for the migration step\n  only, falling back to DATABASE_URL when unset. The runtime pgxpool\n  built right after migrations complete is untouched -- still\n  PgBouncer, exactly as before.\n- charts/labor-performance: new database.migrationsExistingSecretKey\n  value (default \"MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\") renders the env var in\n  both the api and mcp Deployments, sourced from the same\n  existingSecret, with optional: true so a secret predating this key\n  still starts the pod.\n- docs/docs/adr/0020-migrations-direct-postgres-connection.md\n  documents the incompatibility, cross-references order-management''s\n  ADR-0029 and warehouse-infra PR #43/#44, and records local\n  verification evidence.\n- cmd/labor/wiring_test.go, cmd/mcp/wiring_test.go: new regression\n  tests proving the getenv fallback in both directions and that the\n  migration step actually receives migrationsDatabaseURL, not\n  databaseURL (not just the env-var read in isolation).\n\nwarehouse-infra PR #44 already provisions the MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\nsecret key for all 9 OLTP services including this one -- no\nwarehouse-infra changes needed here. cmd/labor-projector and\ncmd/labor-reports (the analytics binaries) are out of scope: their\nANALYTICS_DATABASE_URL was never routed through PgBouncer in the\nfirst place.\n\nLocal quality gate: make check, make check-all (coverage 99.4%,\ngate 90%), go test -tags=integration ./... -race (real Postgres +\nKafka Testcontainers), and helm lint/helm template all green.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqumoRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuuAQAIci9HiIma87tE1NdEre8eP4\nUJMSmXCpU+/VYY4cpSxNOdWK19Y9p8Sq9n4VjL1J7WZva/ufJzkZ8ILDg1HpNunx\nWgrookYfnq48kbBvt6dBvd1OMxB9JNQII3OsqrbWNtmda7H2kctZdgFdSioQsRoZ\na3dFIpRQgeuTiPWLD313S9ExpJdBxthHgtgEyZoluTjA8VyqsBFFoTgaGCuvkt04\nDi54PkSzyQ2MDuWBSUgf22ZUysKbd1MWAHVosIQvtzXpEBX75gY9tWD3ml6nOafa\nn/uc1IpTuM+912E//z1aNEZobP1ah1M6poDGz/VAlmuUjs4rhfci8PA+A/K4/KsD\nJJwfXtqAzcFxRCnao2XCcQYXTOVBwVWN88Beh/M4pgBPMzaranp9IBY2IiwFEDBF\nXWInt1PBjPQ+DFMpwsCvQ9zx36f/Z6RTjW0jYj7BmiS5p+SyUZRKb2bxT21F33/C\nyloSeXmYJMUjsVQA/gFTvuPN+jj+7jIcyMKUKF0JiI3KiHkEeWrnrAUA05fyCb4S\nHnke4LQ5IirecvSkJys90aN8XPnIAJZfZ12/43HfgHExx5dfd2qWoZULHc++3CGo\npWgFWcf/2Ab/RnKgJZD7slTai34b74qU+vJEkTHf4xr/7kOLvYSQ2upc9sDPFlAD\nf9ykt978uUkfaIzkcNcm\n=P2F1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T13:22:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"h