tml_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/labor-performance/commit/c1cc4a72603d7d50ccad0d1c65de54d5f8fcb2c5","node_id":"C_kwDOUIGXYtoAKGMxY2M0YTcyNjAzZDdkNTBjY2FkMGQxYzY1ZGU1NGQ1ZjhmY2IyYzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/labor-performance/commit/fea811bd75e246907c52ff0c7a25a58f51a2fb44","sha":"fea811bd75e246907c52ff0c7a25a58f51a2fb44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/fea811bd75e246907c52ff0c7a25a58f51a2fb44"}],"sha":"c1cc4a72603d7d50ccad0d1c65de54d5f8fcb2c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/c1cc4a72603d7d50ccad0d1c65de54d5f8fcb2c5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/fea811bd75e246907c52ff0c7a25a58f51a2fb44/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T04:00:00Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T04:00:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(scalability): per-workload HPA + pgxpool MaxConns/statement_timeout tuning (ADR 0019) (#90)\n\nPort order-management''s Phase 3 scalability reference (PR #110, ADR 0026)\nto labor-performance.\n\nHPA (autoscaling/v2), one per independently-assessed workload, all\ndefault-disabled via values.yaml so this PR changes nothing on merge:\n\n- api (cmd/labor): min 1 / max 4 / 70% CPU. Stateless OLTP HTTP + Kafka\n  consumer under a stable shared consumer group; outbox relay uses\n  FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED, safe at N>1.\n- analytics-projector (cmd/labor-projector): min 1 / max 2 / 70% CPU.\n  Stable shared Kafka consumer group, idempotent upserts on event_id.\n- analytics-reports (cmd/labor-reports): min 1 / max 3 / 70% CPU.\n  Stateless read-only REST reader.\n- frontend: min 1 / max 3 / 70% CPU. Pure static-asset serving.\n- mcp: deliberately excluded, not just disabled. cmd/mcp wraps the MCP\n  SDK''s StreamableHTTPHandler, which keeps per-process in-memory session\n  state keyed by Mcp-Session-Id; the chart''s mcp Service has no\n  sessionAffinity, so >1 replica risks session-affinity breakage. Same\n  reasoning order-management''s ADR-0026 used to exclude its own cmd/mcp.\n\nEvery guarded Deployment''s spec.replicas is now wrapped in\n`{{- if not .Values.autoscaling.<x>.enabled }}` so an active HPA never\nfights a static replica count on helm upgrade. Verified with helm\ntemplate: default values render 0 HPAs and every static replicas field;\nall four autoscaling.*.enabled=true renders exactly 4 HPAs and drops\nreplicas on exactly those four Deployments.\n\npgxpool tuning, matching order-management''s numbers (PgBouncer,\nwarehouse-infra PR #43, already fronts every service''s OLTP DATABASE_URL\nin transaction-pooling mode; analytics DSNs stay direct per that PR''s\nreasoning):\n\n- OLTP pool (postgres.NewPool): MaxConns=10, statement_timeout=5s.\n- Analytics writer (analyticsstore.NewPool): MaxConns=5,\n  statement_timeout=10s.\n- Analytics reader (analyticsstore.NewReadOnlyPool): MaxConns=5,\n  statement_timeout=15s.\n\nAdded pool_limits_integration_test.go (testcontainers Postgres 16),\nported from order-management''s reference: proves statement_timeout is\nenforced server-side (a pg_sleep(2) against a 200ms timeout is actually\ncancelled, SQLSTATE 57014) and that MaxConns is a real, enforced\nceiling (an Acquire beyond MaxConns blocks until context deadline).\n\nADR 0019 records the full per-workload HPA table, the connection-budget\naccounting against the shared Postgres instance''s max_connections=100,\nand the residual fleet-wide risk already disclosed in order-management''s\nADR-0026.\n\nVerified: go build/vet (plain + -tags=integration), gofmt clean,\ngolangci-lint 0 issues, make check, make check-all (coverage 99.4%,\ngate 90%; arch-test including TestNoSiblingContextOutboundCalls; bdd),\ngo test -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1 (all green, including the\nnew pool tests against a real Postgres container), helm lint, helm\ntemplate default/all-enabled scenarios, and the existing chart-level\nrender-assertions.sh + test_service_selectors.py.","tree":{"sha":"da5fca923fc8acc82026ed8cc986fb6022aa9b1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/git/trees/da5fca923fc8acc82026ed8cc986fb6022aa9b1c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/git/commits/fea811bd75e246907c52ff0c7a25a58f51a2fb44","verification":{"payload":"tree da5fca923fc8acc82026ed8cc986fb6022aa9b1c\nparent ce59c340b7d76245233285b5f63faa5c38f3403e\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790568000 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790568000 -0300\n\nfeat(scalability): per-workload HPA + pgxpool MaxConns/statement_timeout tuning (ADR 0019) (#90)\n\nPort order-management''s Phase 3 scalability reference (PR #110, ADR 0026)\nto labor-performance.\n\nHPA (autoscaling/v2), one per independently-assessed workload, all\ndefault-disabled via values.yaml so this PR changes nothing on merge:\n\n- api (cmd/labor): min 1 / max 4 / 70% CPU. Stateless OLTP HTTP + Kafka\n  consumer under a stable shared consumer group; outbox relay uses\n  FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED, safe at N>1.\n- analytics-projector (cmd/labor-projector): min 1 / max 2 / 70% CPU.\n  Stable shared Kafka consumer group, idempotent upserts on event_id.\n- analytics-reports (cmd/labor-reports): min 1 / max 3 / 70% CPU.\n  Stateless read-only REST reader.\n- frontend: min 1 / max 3 / 70% CPU. Pure static-asset serving.\n- mcp: deliberately excluded, not just disabled. cmd/mcp wraps the MCP\n  SDK''s StreamableHTTPHandler, which keeps per-process in-memory session\n  state keyed by Mcp-Session-Id; the chart''s mcp Service has no\n  sessionAffinity, so >1 replica risks session-affinity breakage. Same\n  reasoning order-management''s ADR-0026 used to exclude its own cmd/mcp.\n\nEvery guarded Deployment''s spec.replicas is now wrapped in\n`{{- if not .Values.autoscaling.<x>.enabled }}` so an active HPA never\nfights a static replica count on helm upgrade. Verified with helm\ntemplate: default values render 0 HPAs and every static replicas field;\nall four autoscaling.*.enabled=true renders exactly 4 HPAs and drops\nreplicas on exactly those four Deployments.\n\npgxpool tuning, matching order-management''s numbers (PgBouncer,\nwarehouse-infra PR #43, already fronts every service''s OLTP DATABASE_URL\nin transaction-pooling mode; analytics DSNs stay direct per that PR''s\nreasoning):\n\n- OLTP pool (postgres.NewPool): MaxConns=10, statement_timeout=5s.\n- Analytics writer (analyticsstore.NewPool): MaxConns=5,\n  statement_timeout=10s.\n- Analytics reader (analyticsstore.NewReadOnlyPool): MaxConns=5,\n  statement_timeout=15s.\n\nAdded pool_limits_integration_test.go (testcontainers Postgres 16),\nported from order-management''s reference: proves statement_timeout is\nenforced server-side (a pg_sleep(2) against a 200ms timeout is actually\ncancelled, SQLSTATE 57014) and that MaxConns is a real, enforced\nceiling (an Acquire beyond MaxConns blocks until context deadline).\n\nADR 0019 records the full per-workload HPA table, the connection-budget\naccounting against the shared Postgres instance''s max_connections=100,\nand the residual fleet-wide risk already disclosed in order-management''s\nADR-0026.\n\nVerified: go build/vet (plain + -tags=integration), gofmt clean,\ngolangci-lint 0 issues, make check, make check-all (coverage 99.4%,\ngate 90%; arch-test including TestNoSiblingContextOutboundCalls; bdd),\ngo test -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1 (all green, including the\nnew pool tests against a real Postgres container), helm lint, helm\ntemplate default/all-enabled scenarios, and the existing chart-level\nrender-assertions.sh + test_service_selectors.py.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqueZACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxVwQAH7S/Nb79JZhEl1g/VxXeeur\n+/j6Mi68D3qAQrhdyP2FJJfKZ+Bk6xwfawVk/45kySqpnvHsqxsAwHcqVdVfhI/Z\nl1Y6vnxM981z3enC/7q+efMLVzMgznKz4Kl8hyZKveM7Rd+9DAWSpol6shBwaKi9\nlv2Vy4W4qt6cl5rxyS7+dpCJIF796IQuSCT2sslUumbrK6MFfevnLNhreBCNsdWH\nFEpKwBzodxAtKuKS36feavtf+Miq4SUo3PEGjes5K2CGlAm/MkbmIS/ZsosqXLKt\nSbpDGpq0pJmsMPedN1XZRMyQPbFx48AqZqM0VV5wa978sezA/aPKe3Zc6biLxWwL\nWN5IUD4lKAwnEJsMT8W9YkBeZ9efZPuFV3ZYESueTfY4qCERWPAWB1iM78f13H/H\nUV0eMIuxsIo2rIFAZv9ZMW+p2DovY/CAEDHDzWCsdy6v44F2A4tvaGDOSP782aFP\nT92VFIXVja0pWKjkfONxHnmVVaLJzzxxjCkO2RzLG9NQVHPGkKJ4Ou4LlnZZHqQH\nQRafSFpwFGAbcGoU5e962ipXTkPoqj+CdT9//sDwXnBT1kI71UblvzF1zPW/+Er5\nvohJd3aC/wfXdAKAOjXc8WQ4NmzbCdJ4ttLd3oqsBvGnw2dvUZI7wtOt1+S7f7YD\n72PcMXVcPk0hepDPRAVy\n=SDO6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T04:00:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/labor-performance/commit/fea811bd75e246907c52ff0c7a25a58f51a2fb44","node_id":"C_kwDOUIGXYtoAKGZlYTgxMWJkNzVlMjQ2OTA3YzUyZmYwYzdhMjVhNThmNTFhMmZiNDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/labor-performance/commit/ce59c340b7d76245233285b5f63faa5c38f3403e","sha":"ce59c340b7d76245233285b5f63faa5c38f3403e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/ce59c340b7d76245233285b5f63faa5c38f3403e"}],"sha":"fea811bd75e246907c52ff0c7a25a58f51a2fb44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/fea811bd75e246907c52ff0c7a25a58f51a2fb44"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/ce59c340b7d76245233285b5f63faa5c38f3403e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T03:35:05Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T03:35:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(kafka): switch every writer''s Balancer from LeastBytes to Hash (ADR 0018) (#89)\n\nEvery kafkago.Writer in internal/adapters/outbound/kafka\n(IntegrationPublisher, AnalyticsPublisher, RelaySink) was configured with\n&kafkago.LeastBytes{}, a balancer that ignores Message.Key entirely and\nroutes purely by cumulative byte volume written to each partition so far.\n\nMessage.Key has always been set correctly in this repo -- AssociateId on\nthe integration topic (integrationData), TaskType on the analytics topic\n(marshalData) -- but LeastBytes silently discarded that key for partition\nrouting. That was accidentally safe while every business topic ran at 1\npartition; warehouse-infra PR #42''s Phase 3 scaleup took every business\ntopic, including warehouse.labor-performance.events and\nwarehouse.labor-performance.analytics, to 8 partitions, which can now let\na consumer observe events for the same associate (or same task type) out\nof order if they land on different partitions.\n\nThis is the same class of bug already found and fixed fleet-wide in\norder-management (PR #111), inventory-storage (PR #102), and\nworkforce-management (PR #106): kafka-go''s Writer does not automatically\nhash Message.Key into a partition decision just because a message\ncarries one -- the Balancer field is an independent knob that must\nitself be key-aware.\n\nFix:\n- Switched Balancer to &kafkago.Hash{} (FNV-1a over Key) in\n  NewIntegrationPublisher, NewAnalyticsPublisher, and NewRelaySink. No\n  Key-setting logic changed -- it was already correct.\n- Updated the existing integration test''s inline Writer literal\n  (integration_publisher_integration_test.go) to match production wiring.\n\nTests:\n- Extended integration_publisher_integration_test.go with\n  TestIntegrationPublisher_KeysMessagesForSameAssociateOntoTheSamePartition,\n  a real-Kafka Testcontainers test against an 8-partition topic (mirroring\n  warehouse-infra PR #42''s actual scaleup): publishes 3\n  TaskPerformanceRecorded events for one AssociateId plus 1 for a\n  different associate, reads every partition back explicitly, and asserts\n  all 3 same-associate messages land on exactly one partition. Manually\n  verified this test fails (messages spread across 3 distinct partitions)\n  when the Balancer is reverted to LeastBytes, and passes with Hash --\n  proving the fake-writer unit tests alone would not catch this class of\n  bug.\n\nAdds ADR 0018 documenting the fix, referencing order-management PR #111\nand warehouse-infra PR #42.\n\nVerified: go build/vet, gofmt, make check, make check-all (coverage\n99.4%, gate 90%; arch-test; bdd), go test -tags=integration ./... -race\n-count=1.","tree":{"sha":"5db4723b0d51adc89015ea982067df88b1514916","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/git/trees/5db4723b0d51adc89015ea982067df88b1514916"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/git/commits/ce59c340b7d76245233285b5f63faa5c38f3403e","verification":{"payload":"tree 5db4723b0d51adc89015ea982067df88b1514916\nparent 592f3b3df88d38d3d3b9fab630b00ccb6a151ca8\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790566505 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790566505 -0300\n\nfix(kafka): switch every writer''s Balancer from LeastBytes to Hash (ADR 0018) (#89)\n\nEvery kafkago.Writer in internal/adapters/outbound/kafka\n(IntegrationPublisher, AnalyticsPublisher, RelaySink) was configured with\n&kafkago.LeastBytes{}, a balancer that ignores Message.Key entirely and\nroutes purely by cumulative byte volume written to each partition so far.\n\nMessage.Key has always been set correctly in this repo -- AssociateId on\nthe integration topic (integrationData), TaskType on the analytics topic\n(marshalData) -- but LeastBytes silently discarded that key for partition\nrouting. That was accidentally safe while every business topic ran at 1\npartition; warehouse-infra PR #42''s Phase 3 scaleup took every business\ntopic, including warehouse.labor-performance.events and\nwarehouse.labor-performance.analytics, to 8 partitions, which can now let\na consumer observe events for the same associate (or same task type) out\nof order if they land on different partitions.\n\nThis is the same class of bug already found and fixed fleet-wide in\norder-management (PR #111), inventory-storage (PR #102), and\nworkforce-management (PR #106): kafka-go''s Writer does not automatically\nhash Message.Key into a partition decision just because a message\ncarries one -- the Balancer field is an independent knob that must\nitself be key-aware.\n\nFix:\n- Switched Balancer to &kafkago.Hash{} (FNV-1a over Key) in\n  NewIntegrationPublisher, NewAnalyticsPublisher, and NewRelaySink. No\n  Key-setting logic changed -- it was already correct.\n- Updated the existing integration test''s inline Writer literal\n  (integration_publisher_integration_test.go) to match production wiring.\n\nTests:\n- Extended integration_publisher_integration_test.go with\n  TestIntegrationPublisher_KeysMessagesForSameAssociateOntoTheSamePartition,\n  a real-Kafka Testcontainers test against an 8-partition topic (mirroring\n  warehouse-infra PR #42''s actual scaleup): publishes 3\n  TaskPerformanceRecorded events for one AssociateId plus 1 for a\n  different associate, reads every partition back explicitly, and asserts\n  all 3 same-associate messages land on exactly one partition. Manually\n  verified this test fails (messages spread across 3 distinct partitions)\n  when the Balancer is reverted to LeastBytes, and passes with Hash --\n  proving the fake-writer unit tests alone would not catch this class of\n  bug.\n\nAdds ADR 0018 documenting the fix, referencing order-management PR #111\nand warehouse-infra PR #42.\n\nVerified: go build/vet, gofmt, make check, make check-all (coverage\n99.4%, gate 90%; arch-test; bdd), go test -tags=integration ./... -race\n-count=1.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqueBpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyKUQADswb/bJclUEjhltO+6of7Vl\n99vQuj4oM5+8JziWh/eZeTejcTn0QDgF1X5STBI1Hv5DEoAJIvaYFH5sc/To1B3G\n/WWMptvKbdkUhHpZUny9HDcVcU8/Rmt7+I585UQXDN82iMy3Qp8J+iMv6xCc0Zak\nJkmEbCIm2SgSXaChysUt34N2K8La2FQwCCw/nXJPSfw4kEUQ9I58g2DLfN9+JZ38\nfN1KQlA1tq5B5mjxPb0uc2eIdD2o4AHkcy1OpJRgCqNLUrDz/fhTDgAl7rTkyCmJ\n78g2SoU7owINUrK5ZpI7qS8Cu6PIE/Eye6kqNt9rcFPEeaRHYldcTYtQaO+i2E0y\nVVICK8dWnw2X0gUE8TASgkOS0YYtUwZk3vsNCcokOg0THcQpLVXzfu3pHFK2Y6Mf\nhZeSvHrQ5oOzj7vNcA0yERB8lYqcIX2iJBB+DfZ2R4heR8aHH47/DiV/kUqvEqRq\nj081faSCFi0MZSAKoL53fS03Hd9d/8v+qISye05wRAEKGw0dytRYzMt3aD2AmDb3\nakhzPL9JW1ryWyhOTKoKbMD2ZKYT2YQyvUj7TYdv006wKheXyOT9csrs2d/t4fxj\n8KTYKB6FzEpLu9a5aS0HLJhHB4+12FLiLuKmzxl8oiRCbHBQcln0FDLmYT7QPTRk\nGD79EvH/rc9RTZyFa7gS\n=u+cP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T03:35:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.