s://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/726f8d829300d0a7c1303d52305956eafa5f6a60/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T22:56:09Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T22:56:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(resilience): Kafka consumer DLQ + graceful shutdown hardening (ADR 0017) (#86)\n\nPhase 2 fan-out (resilience): DLQ + graceful-shutdown pieces only, ported\nfrom order-management''s reference implementation (PR #107, ADR 0025).\nNo circuit breaker work applies here -- this service makes zero sync\noutbound HTTP calls to any sibling bounded context (ADR 0002/0003/0015,\nenforced by internal/architecture''s TestNoSiblingContextOutboundCalls),\nso there is no dependency edge to wrap in a breaker.\n\n- internal/adapters/inbound/kafka/consumer.go: Consumer.handleMessage now\n  retries handleFulfillmentEvent in-process (cenkalti/backoff/v4, jittered\n  exponential backoff, up to 3 attempts total) before dead-lettering an\n  exhausted/poisoned message to warehouse.fulfillment.events.dlq (derived\n  as <source-topic>+\".dlq\", never a fixed constant) with\n  x-dlq-source-topic/x-dlq-error/x-dlq-failed-at headers, then commits the\n  offset so one poison message can never block the partition. Consumer\n  gains a dlqWriter (nil-safe, closed alongside the reader in Close) so\n  the several existing unit tests constructing a bare Consumer{} directly\n  keep compiling and passing unchanged.\n\n- Graceful shutdown (cmd/labor/main.go): readiness flips to not-ready\n  FIRST (new GET /readyz, backed by internal/adapters/inbound/http/\n  readiness.go, distinct from the pre-existing liveness-only GET\n  /healthz), then HTTP drain, then the outbox relay and the Kafka\n  consumer are stopped and awaited (bounded, \"final offset commit\"\n  guarantee), then persistence.close() (the pgx pool) runs LAST via\n  defer''s LIFO order.\n\n- charts/labor-performance: readinessProbe now targets /readyz (was\n  /healthz); startupProbe/livenessProbe stay /healthz, unchanged. Added\n  terminationGracePeriodSeconds: 30 (new chart value, previously absent).\n\n- go.mod: cenkalti/backoff/v4 promoted from indirect to direct dependency\n  (v4.3.0, same version order-management uses; no new transitive deps).\n\n- docs/docs/adr/0017: full design record, explicitly documenting why no\n  circuit breaker applies to this repo. Updated docs/docs/adr/about.md,\n  docs/sidebars.ts and .claude/rules/adrs-and-decisions.md (also backfills\n  the previously-missing ADR 0016 index entries).\n\nVerification (worktree labor-performance-resilience):\n- go build/vet (plain + -tags=integration): clean\n- gofmt -l .: clean\n- make check (fmt-check, vet, build, lint, test -race): clean, 0 lint\n  issues\n- make arch-test: all hexagonal/analytics/ports fitness tests pass,\n  including TestNoSiblingContextOutboundCalls (unaffected by this change)\n- make coverage: 99.4% (gate: 90%)\n- go test -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1: all packages pass\n  against real Testcontainers Kafka/Postgres, including the new\n  TestConsumer_PoisonMessage_GoesToDeadLetterTopicWithoutBlockingPartition\n  (poison message reaches .dlq after 3 attempts with full payload/error\n  context; a well-formed message published right after it is processed\n  without delay)\n- helm lint charts/labor-performance: 0 charts failed","tree":{"sha":"1d26d7e263795f7b37d2c15a12f8eb833b9d8925","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/git/trees/1d26d7e263795f7b37d2c15a12f8eb833b9d8925"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/git/commits/726f8d829300d0a7c1303d52305956eafa5f6a60","verification":{"payload":"tree 1d26d7e263795f7b37d2c15a12f8eb833b9d8925\nparent 53cb3a25b1c64e9abb098ab9ada9ab890dec0506\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790549769 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790549769 -0300\n\nfeat(resilience): Kafka consumer DLQ + graceful shutdown hardening (ADR 0017) (#86)\n\nPhase 2 fan-out (resilience): DLQ + graceful-shutdown pieces only, ported\nfrom order-management''s reference implementation (PR #107, ADR 0025).\nNo circuit breaker work applies here -- this service makes zero sync\noutbound HTTP calls to any sibling bounded context (ADR 0002/0003/0015,\nenforced by internal/architecture''s TestNoSiblingContextOutboundCalls),\nso there is no dependency edge to wrap in a breaker.\n\n- internal/adapters/inbound/kafka/consumer.go: Consumer.handleMessage now\n  retries handleFulfillmentEvent in-process (cenkalti/backoff/v4, jittered\n  exponential backoff, up to 3 attempts total) before dead-lettering an\n  exhausted/poisoned message to warehouse.fulfillment.events.dlq (derived\n  as <source-topic>+\".dlq\", never a fixed constant) with\n  x-dlq-source-topic/x-dlq-error/x-dlq-failed-at headers, then commits the\n  offset so one poison message can never block the partition. Consumer\n  gains a dlqWriter (nil-safe, closed alongside the reader in Close) so\n  the several existing unit tests constructing a bare Consumer{} directly\n  keep compiling and passing unchanged.\n\n- Graceful shutdown (cmd/labor/main.go): readiness flips to not-ready\n  FIRST (new GET /readyz, backed by internal/adapters/inbound/http/\n  readiness.go, distinct from the pre-existing liveness-only GET\n  /healthz), then HTTP drain, then the outbox relay and the Kafka\n  consumer are stopped and awaited (bounded, \"final offset commit\"\n  guarantee), then persistence.close() (the pgx pool) runs LAST via\n  defer''s LIFO order.\n\n- charts/labor-performance: readinessProbe now targets /readyz (was\n  /healthz); startupProbe/livenessProbe stay /healthz, unchanged. Added\n  terminationGracePeriodSeconds: 30 (new chart value, previously absent).\n\n- go.mod: cenkalti/backoff/v4 promoted from indirect to direct dependency\n  (v4.3.0, same version order-management uses; no new transitive deps).\n\n- docs/docs/adr/0017: full design record, explicitly documenting why no\n  circuit breaker applies to this repo. Updated docs/docs/adr/about.md,\n  docs/sidebars.ts and .claude/rules/adrs-and-decisions.md (also backfills\n  the previously-missing ADR 0016 index entries).\n\nVerification (worktree labor-performance-resilience):\n- go build/vet (plain + -tags=integration): clean\n- gofmt -l .: clean\n- make check (fmt-check, vet, build, lint, test -race): clean, 0 lint\n  issues\n- make arch-test: all hexagonal/analytics/ports fitness tests pass,\n  including TestNoSiblingContextOutboundCalls (unaffected by this change)\n- make coverage: 99.4% (gate: 90%)\n- go test -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1: all packages pass\n  against real Testcontainers Kafka/Postgres, including the new\n  TestConsumer_PoisonMessage_GoesToDeadLetterTopicWithoutBlockingPartition\n  (poison message reaches .dlq after 3 attempts with full payload/error\n  context; a well-formed message published right after it is processed\n  without delay)\n- helm lint charts/labor-performance: 0 charts failed","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquZ8JCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOmEQAAPft8tknlloqaM6Nf0SEtlh\nDj3TPtP7EvkC37NTXZp1z1ErJKC2WL4dyCxQD4kU6AKIOr7XoFBrgKCS0xt9pNRK\nyqdntJK2JmJi/PbZXlLrU4LvQJWe+djWTVXln8h6vEAgkOHBieq+AjODo5EKUQYl\naGIR2EiOwxVcAvExXSLdI30aqDrJhtH0XUUWr6Xkriq9KCYGYFtGim2lV1se7Dwf\n9q6iwQQxiKtRkDcaPtFU4gwA1ZGYRz4JMLZ3qYoB2/8OFTz+jveUmAadLlDYMUdP\njpBw3M2XTDTHeq/Lx3womLECijM3iuOeamGrSRRnI9sevInnUhTo8bhDWZ47Wc6z\n9NyBPvFKxfhLo33jQCsktLp5FdfmUNhVqOm9qTxF+C5eqOhTiSWfYZJhnB2C9W9G\n4vM56OkHHVT9oVz1JqHWNWQGe+GB2bNky52zSh8MsFoZKOQPBaOulX0XIaF8EzYm\nxNBaUp/QbEldPCImFXDtcaCuI2cOjIt9JXrTSiXtfYtLkWXaCzt8krTrwWf90mes\ndp7HC9pVMdHUd122j6cZaeNEyqsB5YS7b4dUI5UK1SfCjxwA3tmpN68W7aG8+S9t\n8Hvp1JM2B85ev1