b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/0b4d105e62d4cf757f022f5f6e82c2c16386c30b"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/labor-performance/commit/53cb3a25b1c64e9abb098ab9ada9ab890dec0506","sha":"53cb3a25b1c64e9abb098ab9ada9ab890dec0506","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/53cb3a25b1c64e9abb098ab9ada9ab890dec0506"}],"sha":"99616b7aa7602a088da1338400f1f65409a9a7e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/99616b7aa7602a088da1338400f1f65409a9a7e8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/53cb3a25b1c64e9abb098ab9ada9ab890dec0506/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T13:24:26Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T13:24:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(idempotency): transactional Idempotency-Key middleware for POST /standards (#85)\n\nAdds a route-scoped, transactional Idempotency-Key HTTP middleware\nprotecting POST /standards -- this service''s one true resource-creation\nendpoint (DefineStandard mints a server-generated StandardId, so a lost\n201 response and a client retry could otherwise double-define/close a\nstandard). Ported from order-management''s reference implementation\n(PR #105 / ADR 0023).\n\nResumed from a partially-drafted, uncommitted worktree. Already present\nand reviewed as correct, unchanged in substance:\n- internal/pgtx/pgtx.go -- the extracted WithTx/TxFrom pair\n- internal/adapters/inbound/http/idempotency.go -- the middleware itself\n- internal/adapters/outbound/postgres/unit_of_work.go''s refactor to\n  delegate to pgtx instead of its own private txKey\n- migrations/0005_idempotency_keys.{up,down}.sql -- matches the\n  reference schema exactly\n\nCompleted in this change:\n- Wired RequireIdempotencyKey onto POST /standards in server.go via\n  chi''s route-scoped r.With(...), gated on a new IdempotencyPool field\n  (nil in the in-memory dev configuration, mirroring every other\n  optional Postgres-backed capability''s convention in this service)\n- Wired IdempotencyPool from persistence.pool in cmd/labor/main.go\n- internal/adapters/inbound/http/idempotency_integration_test.go --\n  all 6 required scenarios (fresh key creates a standard; replay with\n  identical key+body returns the byte-identical response with exactly\n  one standard row created; same key + different body -> 422; missing\n  header -> 400; 5 real concurrent goroutines with the same key+body ->\n  exactly one standard created; a business-validation-error response\n  (422, non-positive ExpectedSeconds) is cached and replayed on retry)\n  against real testcontainers Postgres through the real chi router\n- docs/docs/adr/0016-idempotency-key-middleware.md\n- README''s endpoint table and curl examples\n\nDefineStandard already wrapped Save(s)+Publish in atomically()/\nUnitOfWork from the earlier outbox rollout (ADR 0010) -- no use case\nchanges were needed. The join between the middleware''s transaction and\nUnitOfWork.Execute''s own is verified for real (not assumed) by the\nintegration tests above.\n\nVerification (real output, not self-reported):\n- go build ./... and go build -tags=integration ./... both clean\n- go vet ./... and go vet -tags=integration ./... both clean\n- gofmt -l . empty\n- make check: fmt-check, vet, build, golangci-lint (0 issues), unit\n  tests all green\n- make arch-test: all fitness rules pass, including the\n  inbound-never-imports-outbound / outbound-never-imports-inbound rules\n  that internal/pgtx exists to satisfy\n- go test -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1: full repo integration\n  suite green, including the pre-existing outbox/Kafka/Postgres\n  integration tests, confirming the unit_of_work.go refactor changed no\n  observable behavior\n- make coverage: 99.4% before and after (gate 90%) -- unchanged,\n  because the middleware lives in the HTTP adapter package outside the\n  gated packages and is verified by the integration suite instead","tree":{"sha":"0e18df7de0b5bcd4df96151bf01f909ff4d04b1e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/git/trees/0e18df7de0b5bcd4df96151bf01f909ff4d04b1e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/git/commits/53cb3a25b1c64e9abb098ab9ada9ab890dec0506","verification":{"payload":"tree 0e18df7de0b5bcd4df96151bf01f909ff4d04b1e\nparent 611ff5323383c299ba466e4b6c97c8995cee8e17\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790515466 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790515466 -0300\n\nfeat(idempotency): transactional Idempotency-Key middleware for POST /standards (#85)\n\nAdds a route-scoped, transactional Idempotency-Key HTTP middleware\nprotecting POST /standards -- this service''s one true resource-creation\nendpoint (DefineStandard mints a server-generated StandardId, so a lost\n201 response and a client retry could otherwise double-define/close a\nstandard). Ported from order-management''s reference implementation\n(PR #105 / ADR 0023).\n\nResumed from a partially-drafted, uncommitted worktree. Already present\nand reviewed as correct, unchanged in substance:\n- internal/pgtx/pgtx.go -- the extracted WithTx/TxFrom pair\n- internal/adapters/inbound/http/idempotency.go -- the middleware itself\n- internal/adapters/outbound/postgres/unit_of_work.go''s refactor to\n  delegate to pgtx instead of its own private txKey\n- migrations/0005_idempotency_keys.{up,down}.sql -- matches the\n  reference schema exactly\n\nCompleted in this change:\n- Wired RequireIdempotencyKey onto POST /standards in server.go via\n  chi''s route-scoped r.With(...), gated on a new IdempotencyPool field\n  (nil in the in-memory dev configuration, mirroring every other\n  optional Postgres-backed capability''s convention in this service)\n- Wired IdempotencyPool from persistence.pool in cmd/labor/main.go\n- internal/adapters/inbound/http/idempotency_integration_test.go --\n  all 6 required scenarios (fresh key creates a standard; replay with\n  identical key+body returns the byte-identical response with exactly\n  one standard row created; same key + different body -> 422; missing\n  header -> 400; 5 real concurrent goroutines with the same key+body ->\n  exactly one standard created; a business-validation-error response\n  (422, non-positive ExpectedSeconds) is cached and replayed on retry)\n  against real testcontainers Postgres through the real chi router\n- docs/docs/adr/0016-idempotency-key-middleware.md\n- README''s endpoint table and curl examples\n\nDefineStandard already wrapped Save(s)+Publish in atomically()/\nUnitOfWork from the earlier outbox rollout (ADR 0010) -- no use case\nchanges were needed. The join between the middleware''s transaction and\nUnitOfWork.Execute''s own is verified for real (not assumed) by the\nintegration tests above.\n\nVerification (real output, not self-reported):\n- go build ./... and go build -tags=integration ./... both clean\n- go vet ./... and go vet -tags=integration ./... both clean\n- gofmt -l . empty\n- make check: fmt-check, vet, build, golangci-lint (0 issues), unit\n  tests all green\n- make arch-test: all fitness rules pass, including the\n  inbound-never-imports-outbound / outbound-never-imports-inbound rules\n  that internal/pgtx exists to satisfy\n- go test -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1: full repo integration\n  suite green, including the pre-existing outbox/Kafka/Postgres\n  integration tests, confirming the unit_of_work.go refactor changed no\n  observable behavior\n- make coverage: 99.4% before and after (gate 90%) -- unchanged,\n  because the middleware lives in the HTTP adapter package outside the\n  gated packages and is verified by the integration suite instead","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquRkLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEYQQADeFpa1SZJ5vJ7vfFOoOIglq\nOa3rlbIx1A/YHDXiFqa0ehs+XOBivfJXTbjqtlFgaHVyl5gfh/c0D79rywZjPGN2\nfAW0vxPN8M4W4qSj0CZmIK+qdtHrlZ26gAdXU2om2+tNdDc3y03CYHAWwAQBgRC1\nODGStoKm3Hk+hjPNJFDr8k1YHXEaZ+rH7DWUaQ2zUOZtr8UkQCLr0FPhIZ9v3/+U\n0mC2kmSSYLjxY9lmoZKWOx+NltUh6C04J2R2xeQy3SHAcfgXad2g4ZMdXzm6AQRz\nWHvveD36hABNVF5/ZLv/JqAAaCfG80J/0VEh/lVCPHolNU06fQxIzqdUOu3vsYa8\nyigu47S5hcD2+o9NmbEC9emJykh2XxiQMNYQ15xe7AtXxfm276ywB1E+9ka/AHDV\nvQuHmelQlFsM9DmzVY6sU027ViTEiHq9qhle7HPphUNxPYLdF3oGJGEvtQAohq1C\nHNHRt5JU1IOBpnMB4ySlbiHQQ/vU9DZp5Y0aKDTvcXRUQ/1P820oFzXzXzmgosda\noPyg0Q/VbAHFYZk+EjO4cOZ73BsHZMjGfJSjy9eO1z05Fdzg5wQknhqY9SL7lWL4\n0yZg+qkQ3QcEKXmP1fqhxSnDoPY17sAPNJJ6QhMJwfvntqW5HgIzsTotcyTVci/T\nJHA/TIGaVvY0v+Exu/NL\n=j++m\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T13:24:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/labor-performance/commit/53cb3a25b1c64e9abb098ab9ada9ab890dec0506","node_id":"C_kwDOUIGXYtoAKDUzY2IzYTI1YjFjNjRlOWFiYjA5OGFiOWFkYTlhYjg5MGRlYzA1MDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/labor-performance/commit/611ff5323383c299ba466e4b6c97c8995cee8e17","sha":"611ff5323383c299ba466e4b6c97c8995cee8e17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/611ff5323383c299ba466e4b6c97c8995cee8e17"}],"sha":"53cb3a25b1c64e9abb098ab9ada9ab890dec0506","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/53cb3a25b1c64e9abb098ab9ada9ab890dec0506"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/611ff5323383c299ba466e4b6c97c8995cee8e17/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T13:10:01Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T13:10:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(kafka): dual-read CloudEvents envelope for TaskCompleted (ADR-0027/0021 Phase 2 Task 2d) (#84)\n\nUpgrade the fulfillment-execution TaskCompleted consumer to dual-read\neither the legacy flat envelope (event_id/event_type/occurred_at/\nsource/data) or the CloudEvents 1.0 structured envelope\nfulfillment-execution''s apis/asyncapi.yaml already specifies\n(specversion/id/type/source/subject/time/data).\n\n- decodeEnvelope peeks the raw JSON for a specversion key to pick the\n  decode path, then normalizes either shape to the existing internal\n  envelope.Envelope before handing off to the unchanged\n  handleFulfillmentEvent logic — one business-logic path, never two.\n- bareEventType strips the reverse-DNS type prefix\n  (com.warehouse.wes.fulfillment-execution.task.TaskCompleted) back to\n  the bare \"TaskCompleted\" name the existing switch/case keys on.\n- An unrecognized/malformed specversion fails soft (returns an error),\n  mirroring this consumer''s existing unparseable-message posture: log,\n  skip, commit — never redelivered forever.\n- taskCompletedData is unchanged; this migration is envelope-only.\n\nNo env var: dual-read is unconditional and purely additive, read-side\nonly, per the ADR''s Phase 2 design.\n\nTests:\n- decode_envelope_test.go: flat-shape regression, CloudEvents-shape\n  (using the real type string from fulfillment-execution''s\n  apis/asyncapi.yaml) producing the identical normalized result and\n  identical use-case side effect, malformed-specversion fail-soft,\n  unparseable-JSON fail-soft.\n- consumer_integration_test.go: new\n  TestConsumer_DualReadSameEventIdFiresOnce runs the real consumer\n  against a testcontainers Kafka broker, publishes one flat-shaped and\n  one CloudEvents-shaped TaskCompleted message sharing the same\n  event_id/id key, and asserts the use case fires exactly once — the\n  idempotency safety this ADR''s later dual-write phase depends on.","tree":{"sha":"b30a1a33da186f98b9e11f7a86147545c4bbade2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/git/trees/b30a1a33da186f98b9e11f7a86147545c4bbade2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/git/commits/611ff5323383c299ba466e4b6c97c8995cee8e17","verification":{"payload":"tree b30a1a33da186f98b9e11f7a86147545c4bbade2\nparent 4bfebb17ac4608adf17f34cd90488db96f363903\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790514601 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790514601 -0300\n\nfeat(kafka): dual-read CloudEvents envelope for TaskCompleted (ADR-0027/0021 Phase 2 Task 2d) (#84)\n\nUpgrade the fulfillment-execution TaskCompleted consumer to dual-read\neither the legacy flat envelope (event_id/event_type/occurred_at/\nsource/data) or the CloudEvents 1.0 structured envelope\nfulfillment-execution''s apis/asyncapi.yaml already specifies\n(specversion/id/type/source/subject/time/data).\n\n- decodeEnvelope peeks the raw JSON for a specversion key to pick the\n  decode path, then normalizes either shape to the existing internal\n  envelope.Envelope before handing off to the unchanged\n  handleFulfillmentEvent logic — one business-logic path, never two.\n- bareEventType strips the reverse-DNS type prefix\n  (com.warehouse.wes.fulfillment-execution.task.TaskCompleted) back to\n  the bare \"TaskCompleted\" name the existing switch/case keys on.\n- An unrecognized/malformed specversion fails soft (returns an error),\n  mirroring this consumer''s existing unparseable-message posture: log,\n  skip, commit — never redelivered forever.\n- taskCompletedData is unchanged; this migration is envelope-only.\n\nNo env var: dual-read is unconditional and purely additive, read-side\nonly, per the ADR''s Phase 2 design.\n\nTests:\n- decode_envelope_test.go: flat-shape regression, CloudEvents-shape\n  (using the real type string from fulfillment-execution''s\n  apis/asyncapi.yaml) producing the identical normalized result and\n  identical use-case side effect, malformed-specversion fail-soft,\n  unparseable-JSON fail-soft.\n- consumer_integration_test.go: new\n  TestConsumer_DualReadSameEventIdFiresOnce runs the real consumer\n  against a testcontainers Kafka broker, publishes one flat-shaped and\n  one CloudEvents-shaped TaskCompleted message sharing the same\n  event_id/id key, and asserts the use case fires exactly once — the\n  idempotency safety this ADR''s later dual-write phase depends on.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquRWpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACAEQAAfyhC0u08GXoJlEwbaSlYb1\n4YVzroNCNTrA5CL/hgkSP/kZ00PmsW5GeQeXbK9Rd96qGZPQb5mi71A7pf9xaVxV\nsN0n3elvHyS0PYXuAiCt4aLC+nlHuKWOYk0cUFEOnG9MmSx8/9ovnC98UKD/xZZR\nF/drVF92QrzcKH1iMNAg9b2tEWcb4rATm/shOhO0LEX8X3ARX9z4GNoU/LLXmnQR\nsiXMQioMPDrSL59OLwycZgaoDpNfi8IA9IvQuGHrJ10XzHc0t62l5OpPycAQ2UyB\nScGCldIoSNXAMLQLE2RAYhGhkr9b3ey92dn08AD6Dpm2/ZSG/q9V0BdlWnA0N+Fa\nDrVKxFuQxtBeFF47ZL8+uWKAPTAE0jjNEZHUPycnXATBaeUuqewclbbi1ErjHFjs\nJ/NIjvTGL+lgbMHNSvkPUViAt83u8WJOX8Bzn3lkZRfU25uD6VEmjlAb8hEWGkLP\nqPrB/bU4ba/1N/hwIaA7MK8puapP1kzKA+LpQtV04e3+MhmvLogl5VYd/KR4tAUc\nj/hD6smWmmXrBQ4sZIyJleu8D5rMana7z/qNKkQwn5uRl9ipExbIb5YZqoPpI7g0\nej8F0uwAGFBe0DkT47XsAEmLOFYzjrtngLrTLj9wO8vOrla3jiV2ucUidpud4XRN\nVTSW+EAig/U5vuUh9oiW\n=YBmT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T13:10:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/use