oed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T23:24:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(boot): retry the first Postgres dial and add a startupProbe (#79)\n\nEvery injected pod''s first outbound TCP dial (Postgres, Kafka) in this\nfleet is reset ~10s after start (Istio 1.30 native sidecars). A single\nattempt turned that transient into CrashLoopBackOff in all 4 binaries.\n\n- Add internal/adapters/outbound/bootretry: one reusable retry helper\n  (5 attempts, 1s base, exponential backoff, ~31s budget), mirroring\n  the shipped network-fulfillment/inventory-storage/facility-layout\n  shape. Fails closed with the last real error once exhausted; stops\n  immediately on context cancellation.\n- Wire it into cmd/labor, cmd/labor-projector, cmd/labor-reports and\n  cmd/mcp''s Postgres RunMigrations/pool.Ping calls.\n- Kafka: traced kafka-go''s Reader/Writer — both dial lazily here (no\n  synchronous boot-time dial like inventory-storage''s\n  facilitycache.NewConsumer), so no Kafka-side wrap was needed.\n- Add a startupProbe (httpGet /healthz, periodSeconds 2,\n  failureThreshold 30) to charts/labor-performance''s deployment,\n  projector, reports and mcp templates, giving the retry budget room\n  before liveness/readiness probing begins.\n\nVerified: go build/vet/test -race, make check (fmt/vet/build/lint/\ntest) all green; helm lint + helm template render the new probe in\nall 4 deployments; render-assertions.sh and test_service_selectors.py\nboth pass. mutation-fast''s gremlins gate scopes only to\ninternal/domain/performance, untouched here.","tree":{"sha":"ae93147498d83e0cdf0d747f5c511649fd25392d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/git/trees/ae93147498d83e0cdf0d747f5c511649fd25392d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/git/commits/ee742773cea1e73540af78957e192f932cecf031","verification":{"payload":"tree ae93147498d83e0cdf0d747f5c511649fd25392d\nparent 8425e0829a2e5bc2795838ff7cff3a4228059ccd\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790465045 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790465045 -0300\n\nfix(boot): retry the first Postgres dial and add a startupProbe (#79)\n\nEvery injected pod''s first outbound TCP dial (Postgres, Kafka) in this\nfleet is reset ~10s after start (Istio 1.30 native sidecars). A single\nattempt turned that transient into CrashLoopBackOff in all 4 binaries.\n\n- Add internal/adapters/outbound/bootretry: one reusable retry helper\n  (5 attempts, 1s base, exponential backoff, ~31s budget), mirroring\n  the shipped network-fulfillment/inventory-storage/facility-layout\n  shape. Fails closed with the last real error once exhausted; stops\n  immediately on context cancellation.\n- Wire it into cmd/labor, cmd/labor-projector, cmd/labor-reports and\n  cmd/mcp''s Postgres RunMigrations/pool.Ping calls.\n- Kafka: traced kafka-go''s Reader/Writer — both dial lazily here (no\n  synchronous boot-time dial like inventory-storage''s\n  facilitycache.NewConsumer), so no Kafka-side wrap was needed.\n- Add a startupProbe (httpGet /healthz, periodSeconds 2,\n  failureThreshold 30) to charts/labor-performance''s deployment,\n  projector, reports and mcp templates, giving the retry budget room\n  before liveness/readiness probing begins.\n\nVerified: go build/vet/test -race, make check (fmt/vet/build/lint/\ntest) all green; helm lint + helm template render the new probe in\nall 4 deployments; render-assertions.sh and test_service_selectors.py\nboth pass. mutation-fast''s gremlins gate scopes only to\ninternal/domain/performance, untouched here.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquFQVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoQgQAHfN7GfFGc2dS7VPxQFLHutF\nsMpiRZIbHDcNBTOhqHFfMj2OEHJUy8HN4idEkE4hLsNioDNXGusTydB14wFP++py\ncP2V2+ugGhROJ3UExyyMsBWoTe48CyaS4AtcOeDo8CWQrwCy7h1iWzcMtIXmEJ0M\nrmdTVoRgBxz8rDWnT+Tcy/j+ESRx8ZUr6vNrInM/mZNIOucuyG