/api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/3269f01b8353237450fe6f7e6674b7ad0fe03d45/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T23:08:15Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T23:08:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(commands): add /code-review, /architecture-review, /domain-review (#54)\n\nLocal-only inferential review sensors, invoked by hand via Claude Code''s\n.claude/commands/ slash-command mechanism -- NOT a GitHub Action, never\nCI-blocking, never incurring per-PR API cost (explicit user decision:\n\"local-only for now, no CI cost, no API key needed\").\n\n- /code-review -- fast pre-commit semantic pass covering domain logic\n  leaking into the wrong layer, untested failing paths, domain types\n  carrying adapter concerns, non-interface ports, error-mapping gaps,\n  hardcoded Kafka consumer groups, reintroduced auth, sibling-context\n  boundary violations.\n- /architecture-review -- expensive, reasons across repo boundaries:\n  hexagonal dependency direction, Customer/Supplier direction per this\n  fleet''s context-mapping ADRs, the MCP additive-boundary rule\n  (ADR-0008), zero-write guardrails where applicable, analytics\n  isolation, Kafka consumer-group PATTERN correctness, and whether a\n  cross-repo contract change needs a (companion) ADR it doesn''t have\n  yet.\n- /domain-review -- ubiquitous-language drift against the repo''s own\n  domain-model doc: duplicate concepts under new names, implementation-\n  flavored naming in the domain layer, undocumented invariants, closed-\n  vs-open value-object mismatches, and new terminology that forks the\n  vocabulary between prose and code.\n\nAll three are advisory-only: they never modify files, never commit, and\nnever block a merge on their own -- output is a structured finding list\nthe author acts on by hand.\n\nPart of the harness-engineering coverage expansion plan\n(.hermes/plans/2026-09-13_234500-harness-coverage-expansion.md), Phase 4\nTask 4.2, fanned out from the reference implementation already merged in\ninventory-storage (PR #76).","tree":{"sha":"54a578bce1ef21d9d7ffeb3bba1efa2e55b7ec34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/git/trees/54a578bce1ef21d9d7ffeb3bba1efa2e55b7ec34"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/git/commits/3269f01b8353237450fe6f7e6674b7ad0fe03d45","verification":{"payload":"tree 54a578bce1ef21d9d7ffeb3bba1efa2e55b7ec34\nparent 21bf4d00df6544bfa6c407cda72d88dbf0b0fdf3\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1789427295 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789427295 -0300\n\ndocs(commands): add /code-review, /architecture-review, /domain-review (#54)\n\nLocal-only inferential review sensors, invoked by hand via Claude Code''s\n.claude/commands/ slash-command mechanism -- NOT a GitHub Action, never\nCI-blocking, never incurring per-PR API cost (explicit user decision:\n\"local-only for now, no CI cost, no API key needed\").\n\n- /code-review -- fast pre-commit semantic pass covering domain logic\n  leaking into the wrong layer, untested failing paths, domain types\n  carrying adapter concerns, non-interface ports, error-mapping gaps,\n  hardcoded Kafka consumer groups, reintroduced auth, sibling-context\n  boundary violations.\n- /architecture-review -- expensive, reasons across repo boundaries:\n  hexagonal dependency direction, Customer/Supplier direction per this\n  fleet''s context-mapping ADRs, the MCP additive-boundary rule\n  (ADR-0008), zero-write guardrails where applicable, analytics\n  isolation, Kafka consumer-group PATTERN correctness, and whether a\n  cross-repo contract change needs a (companion) ADR it doesn''t have\n  yet.\n- /domain-review -- ubiquitous-language drift against the repo''s own\n  domain-model doc: duplicate concepts under new names, implementation-\n  flavored naming in the domain layer, undocumented invariants, closed-\n  vs-open value-object mismatches, and new terminology that forks the\n  vocabulary between prose and code.\n\nAll three are advisory-only: they never modify files, never commit, and\nnever block a merge on their own -- output is a structured finding list\nthe author acts on by hand.\n\nPart of the harness-engineering coverage expansion plan\n(.hermes/plans/2026-09-13_234500-harness-coverage-expansion.md), Phase 4\nTask 4.2, fanned out from the reference implementation already merged in\ninventory-storage (PR #76).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqH5fCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAacoQAJvwDhybDrl3Ph+kOMEavcAp\n9yHgwPmGPK9OjqTQ17xizzTd03NUAnq7rGvXK/nYFEwkLHGJX4D1Yw9rnu+UEAL2\nVy/9bBJKCbyD1f7PqUGOS46zAh6BNpSgC03C6Cma7F3DaTmPOyYnMId9pr26N95A\nE14a8HELN0/pFq5Cbn0GPCs4To+0BMzh8Wp9zNCh4UWwgVSePLvYR4ug+VrVRppp\ndMamfpEzGDvmmYf6kLUsS9fMfbxO0u/UmYx2bb24jLoJYRqbEIjIbXH53cTVONQ8\nedAV5on4np5q8fQyv1IrKcGxUqKNQpK5/QylDM47id3zLWxYP3crQNs7ZIypFvlq\nLBAaC3v9kIAt0nwnj/6V/Ac0Ae8E+zo2B5Cg5vOB1M5c3akFV4Yu1YV2gmWuCpkX\ntcMCzcUV+pHO2b6V8xRtd44uQ6i2F5YNJ9NtRXdrVzUnSxUeXGJozhhulszufMpT\nLRn3rKhDBudjlHN/c/8L6GObKDVWSIv3WiNuUCEfYNsGjEVMdCGymMLssxb5GoG0\n2sd5ihqHzDCRalDmqtyQ0GqCndzLhcRkwhgXJ9U041lyOzNN5z6ZnAm6AYnK3PAC\nhemFcE/7QXOHfwTcYdD4tmzrUy1xOGaN7P1dDy7PCpu2XA4EE5ZMtIo9tfUoacfn\nkOCG