hub.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/21bf4d00df6544bfa6c407cda72d88dbf0b0fdf3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T11:54:28Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T11:54:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(claude): add .claude/skills/ how-to guides (Phase 4 Task 4.1) (#53)\n\nFan out from inventory-storage''s merged reference implementation\n(PR #75) into labor-performance, adapting every example to this\nrepo''s own, real codebase rather than copying verbatim:\n\n- how-to-add-a-rest-endpoint.md: worked example is the real\n  GetAssociateScorecard/GetUtilization use cases + server.go\n  handlers, including this repo''s own non-negotiable that\n  RecordTaskPerformance has NO REST handler (Kafka-consumer-only).\n- how-to-add-an-integration-event.md: worked example is this\n  repo''s real, live Kafka consumer of fulfillment-execution''s\n  TaskCompleted on warehouse.fulfillment.events\n  (internal/adapters/inbound/kafka/consumer.go, cmd/labor/main.go''s\n  KAFKA_CONSUMER_GROUP env var). Calls out AGENTS.md''s\n  non-negotiable #1 -- a stricter-than-fleet-norm ban on any\n  outbound REST/MCP call to fulfillment-execution or\n  workforce-management -- since it''s the sharpest version of this\n  rule in the fleet and belongs right in the consumer section.\n- how-to-write-an-adr.md: numbering/frontmatter grounded in this\n  repo''s real ADR sequence (0001-0015), citing ADR-0003 as the\n  Decision-section model and ADR-0012/0011 as the real\n  supersession example.\n- how-to-test.md: this repo''s real .gremlins.yaml thresholds (99/99),\n  its documented switch-statement mutation-coverage gap, the real\n  Makefile targets (check, check-all, mutation-fast, mutation, vuln,\n  api-lint) and their CI mapping.\n- how-to-add-a-frontend-remote.md: worked example is the real,\n  already-shipped labor-mfe remote (web/vite.config.ts,\n  web/package.json, web/Dockerfile, port 5187 matching this\n  service''s own CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS default).\n\nDocs-only change; no code touched.","tree":{"sha":"9a5d60e5706cea18169d6fddb175d2a6e0afd318","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/git/trees/9a5d60e5706cea18169d6fddb175d2a6e0afd318"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/git/commits/21bf4d00df6544bfa6c407cda72d88dbf0b0fdf3","verification":{"payload":"tree 9a5d60e5706cea18169d6fddb175d2a6e0afd318\nparent 838d73c7f6aeb2cc92b083c0d89ee148e389040d\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1789386868 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789386868 -0300\n\ndocs(claude): add .claude/skills/ how-to guides (Phase 4 Task 4.1) (#53)\n\nFan out from inventory-storage''s merged reference implementation\n(PR #75) into labor-performance, adapting every example to this\nrepo''s own, real codebase rather than copying verbatim:\n\n- how-to-add-a-rest-endpoint.md: worked example is the real\n  GetAssociateScorecard/GetUtilization use cases + server.go\n  handlers, including this repo''s own non-negotiable that\n  RecordTaskPerformance has NO REST handler (Kafka-consumer-only).\n- how-to-add-an-integration-event.md: worked example is this\n  repo''s real, live Kafka consumer of fulfillment-execution''s\n  TaskCompleted on warehouse.fulfillment.events\n  (internal/adapters/inbound/kafka/consumer.go, cmd/labor/main.go''s\n  KAFKA_CONSUMER_GROUP env var). Calls out AGENTS.md''s\n  non-negotiable #1 -- a stricter-than-fleet-norm ban on any\n  outbound REST/MCP call to fulfillment-execution or\n  workforce-management -- since it''s the sharpest version of this\n  rule in the fleet and belongs right in the consumer section.\n- how-to-write-an-adr.md: numbering/frontmatter grounded in this\n  repo''s real ADR sequence (0001-0015), citing ADR-0003 as the\n  Decision-section model and ADR-0012/0011 as the real\n  supersession example.\n- how-to-test.md: this repo''s real .gremlins.yaml thresholds (99/99),\n  its documented switch-statement mutation-coverage gap, the real\n  Makefile targets (check, check-all, mutation-fast, mutation, vuln,\n  api-lint) and their CI mapping.\n- how-to-add-a-frontend-remote.md: worked example is the real,\n  already-shipped labor-mfe remote (web/vite.config.ts,\n  web/package.json, web/Dockerfile, port 5187 matching this\n  service''s own CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS default).\n\nDocs-only change; no code touched.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqp+B0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvHgQAFovzEQx1gJX0Tuf49c6bWCT\nTdZo8iLd5opM8SdYuj7X9IKRR/9FOhL3WnWD/qG3Lgc7/YrYEapVtiG5myDHjHAi\nfxmGY2JLmwfDdlPbxBVjpv/sjiIBkmyYzc205yn2O47dDsICxSif6+BCTDIubqzQ\njWtISMaTpCWhouCXHugbmfMQNa/ovyfS08cCbGofCLr6+m+oGH3eqTjqoUdhqOny\nW3dp3SE2kninzea0kOWY9zF5a5EuVrW7zW/YlEg98m+aFSrHECnB0t4b0qDm4DXI\n8Hb29RlIfIeMrSGQBMYbXsFitn9nTAqIwLMoA3Jg7RDZYG1xBId2TwMHUw0DmXBw\n57f/vmFzs9ct0MG9NmoVu7oRNtQVOuzjvjMZVkRZgJLgbpTQfIgdA4wxrRH4OceQ\n0zCjAWfHOs0DmX8nlt8WDoPzGQQ1aQXlbPvzuapVvehvxKpF7V7wF/2hzKmys0NF\n06XTq9/50T67Eijo2jgzjPXb9Ifj8LzJDvp1TUYqXCVLh7sihlSjue3Mhqunen6o\nHGx5/9mueP+khEODW4DkveAulF27jjkbbG+AGw7sL8y2+z444W8kXT/vlNjQBw2q\nOcJRrPpkUveQJFMIOlmAOi340aQsWl4/3RwWpq+fdg8vckg+6cltjASwuwcbB9NN\n+YFs0vqHsn5Asd+l0LR+\n=Fz6x\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T11:54:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/labor-performance/commit/21bf4d00df6544bfa6c407cda72d88dbf0b0fdf3","node_id":"C_kwDOUIGXYtoAKDIxYmY0ZDAwZGY2NTQ0YmZhNmM0MDdjZGE3MmQ4OGRiZjBiMGZkZjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/labor-performance/commit/838d73c7f6aeb2cc92b083c0d89ee148e389040d","sha":"838d73c7f6aeb2cc92b083c0d89ee148e389040d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/838d73c7f6aeb2cc92b083c0d89ee148e389040d"}],"sha":"21bf4d00df6544bfa6c407cda72d88dbf0b0fdf3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/21bf4d00df6544bfa6c407cda72d88dbf0b0fdf3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/838d73c7f6aeb2cc92b083c0d89ee148e389040d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:16:40Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:16:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(arch): add MCP boundary, auth-revert, Kafka, and sibling-call fitness functions (#52)\n\nEncodes five fleet invariants plus one repo-specific rule as executable\narch-go/source-scanning fitness tests, extending internal/architecture\nbeyond the existing hexagonal-dependency-rule test. Each was already a\nrule paid for in incidents -- guarded only by prose in AGENTS.md or this\nfleet''s operational memory, never by a computational sensor.\n\n- TestMCPAdapterDependencyRule (ADR-0008): MCP inbound adapter depends\n  only on application+domain, and nothing else depends on it.\n- TestNoAuthMiddlewareReintroduced: fleet-wide static-bearer auth was\n  deliberately reverted 2026-09-11; scans internal/adapters/inbound for\n  a reintroduced Bearer/JWT pattern.\n- TestKafkaConsumerGroupNeverHardcodedInline: encodes the real incident\n  where wes-work-planning''s hardcoded OLTP consumer group made a\n  locally-run e2e-tests process join the SAME group as the live\n  in-cluster Deployment on the shared broker.\n- TestKafkaIntegrationTestsUseTestcontainers: a Kafka-touching\n  _integration_test.go must start its own broker via\n  testcontainers-go/modules/kafka, never skip-gate on KAFKA_BROKERS or\n  hardcode localhost:9092.\n- TestNoSiblingContextOutboundCalls (new, repo-specific): this repo''s\n  own AGENTS.md non-negotiable #1 is \"Pure Kafka consumer of\n  fulfillment-execution, nothing else\" -- no Go import from, no write\n  access to, fulfillment-execution or workforce-management; choreography,\n  not orchestration. Encodes it by banning net/http imports under\n  internal/adapters/outbound, where an outbound HTTP client package\n  would live if one were ever added.\n\nPart of the harness-engineering coverage expansion plan\n(.hermes/plans/2026-09-13_234500-harness-coverage-expansion.md), Phase 3\nTasks 3.1 (MCP boundary) + 3.2 (sibling-call ban) + 3.3 (Kafka\ntestcontainers) + 3.5 (auth guard) + 3.6 (consumer group), fanned out\nfrom the reference implementation already merged in inventory-storage\n(PR #69).\n\n## Verified locally\n\nAll 6 checks proven to actually fire on a deliberately introduced\nviolation, then reverted before committing (confirmed via `git status`\nshowing only the new test file as untracked):\n- MCP adapter importing an outbound package -> failed as expected\n- A `\"Bearer \"+\"secret\"` literal added to the HTTP adapter -> failed\n- analytics_consumer.go''s GroupID changed to an inline literal -> failed\n- consumer_integration_test.go''s testcontainers import removed -> failed\n- idle_period_repo.go given a bare `net/http` import under\n  internal/adapters/outbound -> failed, citing the sibling-call ban\n\n`go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `make check`, and the full\n`go test ./internal/architecture/... -v` all pass clean on the real\n(unmodified) codebase.","tree":{"sha":"5c2f84de680405b25b7040c73a816917c6f2406e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/git/trees/5c2f84de680405b25b7040c73a816917c6f2406e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/git/commits/838d73c7f6aeb2cc92b083c0d89ee148e389040d","verification":{"payload":"tree 5c2f84de680405b25b7040c73a816917c6f2406e\nparent 62b334833112f163ba37d6146574738685cdb266\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1789352200 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789352200 -0300\n\nfeat(arch): add MCP boundary, auth-revert, Kafka, and sibling-call fitness functions (#52)\n\nEncodes five fleet invariants plus one repo-specific rule as executable\narch-go/source-scanning fitness tests, extending internal/architecture\nbeyond the existing hexagonal-dependency-rule test. Each was already a\nrule paid for in incidents -- guarded only by prose in AGENTS.md or this\nfleet''s operational memory, never by a computational sensor.\n\n- TestMCPAdapterDependencyRule (ADR-0008): MCP inbound adapter depends\n  only on application+domain, and nothing else depends on it.\n- TestNoAuthMiddlewareReintroduced: fleet-wide static-bearer auth was\n  deliberately reverted 2026-09-11; scans internal/adapters/inbound for\n  a reintroduced Bearer/JWT pattern.\n- TestKafkaConsumerGroupNeverHardcodedInline: encodes the real incident\n  where wes-work-planning''s hardcoded OLTP consumer group made a\n  locally-run e2e-tests process join the SAME group as the live\n  in-cluster Deployment on the shared broker.\n- TestKafkaIntegrationTestsUseTestcontainers: a Kafka-touching\n  _integration_test.go must start its own broker via\n  testcontainers-go/modules/kafka, never skip-gate on KAFKA_BROKERS or\n  hardcode localhost:9092.\n- TestNoSiblingContextOutboundCalls (new, repo-specific): this repo''s\n  own AGENTS.md non-negotiable #1 is \"Pure Kafka consumer of\n  fulfillment-execution, nothing else\" -- no Go import from, no write\n  access to, fulfillment-execution or workforce-management; choreography,\n  not orchestration. Encodes it by banning net/http imports under\n  internal/adapters/outbound, where an outbound HTTP client package\n  would live if one were ever added.\n\nPart of the harness-engineering coverage expansion plan\n(.hermes/plans/2026-09-13_234500-harness-coverage-expansion.md), Phase 3\nTasks 3.1 (MCP boundary) + 3.2 (sibling-call ban) + 3.3 (Kafka\ntestcontainers) + 3.5 (auth guard) + 3.6 (consumer group), fanned out\nfrom the reference implementation already merged in inventory-storage\n(PR #69).\n\n## Verified locally\n\nAll 6 checks proven to actually fire on a deliberately introduced\nviolation, then reverted before committing (confirmed via `git status`\nshowing only the new test file as untracked):\n- MCP adapter importing an outbound package -> failed as expected\n- A `\"Bearer \"+\"secret\"` literal added to the HTTP adapter -> failed\n- analytics_consumer.go''s GroupID changed to an inline literal -> failed\n- consumer_integration_test.go''s testcontainers import removed -> failed\n- idle_period_repo.go given a bare `net/http` import under\n  internal/adapters/outbound -> failed, citing the sibling-call ban\n\n`go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `make check`, and the full\n`go test ./internal/architecture/... -v` all pass clean on the real\n(unmodified) codebase.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqp1kICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFKcQABYPUnOkKkeV0I5/a9w9nsvt\naGpC/brU1/IMa5iKCOznhBKeDnGRnhd/vy7tSlW+GGrXIM1uzU8iQwepEGdCOM0l\n0J/T/achEqsPW3hR9/J+enaFcPHeVReL7KOmb2/teaufaD4oSPUWRV6yN1LR3JPP\ndriEaGjyeUl6Wi0IFybzBfZeM4JwuNZBxHvINTJK5YvJ5DtqmCHrb8LGtT3lK0yz\nyBJVfk9WSHp7YyOzabtC4CoTqCPzWYaiY+cp2ZeG8/hxk24m0bXaRN8TGgAPx0dm\npDom03PsW/mc3gekk9x6zLPhZChzsIgoAQioynvfQNnNE+Ruao8ICTHPjDWwo0Jb\nNqLs2Eki82i0LxWXwv0/lBioXtxdstaUbOFgM+Zq4tFOpST6vK2zjcOtYIbE0nfH\nejOZ3TReyamufzEpqnoMFWojzYs/w8w7eL4rSh18KI4oQW2ojwpb9SMZs6CBcV7K\nof+lQn85DVQgLKIDYK1YCdXlHPdrpufcIIIMXodHIxvFm/0GSL3t1JmEI6aVYqui\nDeAQiAQbzzfL5NUyCJ+1Oexw2boCwYuOkCCMgumA4MxphX8nq5m/VtbrVB2+ktcZ\n0X/L6JbQrIxgsMWGe33Ovm8KNmels5BuO/bySj9AmoW6vH7wY/+pACOp9eT0PndA\nYArIEhQtomY+XX9fKYk5\n=teS6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T02:16:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/labor-performance/commit/838d73c7f6aeb2cc92b083c0d89ee148e389040d","node_id":"C_kwDOUIGXYtoAKDgzOGQ3M2M3ZjZhZWIyY2M5MmIwODNjMGQ4OWVlMTQ4ZTM4OTA0MGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/labor-performance/commit/62b334833112f163ba37d6146574738685cdb266","sha":"62b334833112f163ba37d6146574738685cdb266","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/62b334833112f163ba37d6146574738685cdb266"}],"sha":"838d73c7f6aeb2cc92b083c0d89ee148e389040d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/838d73c7f6aeb2cc92b083c0d89ee148e389040d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/62b334833112f163ba37d6146574738685cdb266/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T01:26:30Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T01:26:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ci): add docs-api-drift job — guard against OpenAPI/generated-docs skew (#51)\n\nOnly wes-work-planning had a docs-api-drift job across the fleet. Every\nother repo''s Docusaurus REST reference (docs/docs/api-reference/rest/) is a\ncommitted, hand-regenerated artifact that can silently diverge from\napis/openapi.yaml -- this fleet has already lived that exact failure once\n(a PR removing security:[]/securitySchemes.bearerAuth from\norder-management''s spec did not regenerate the .api.mdx files, caught only\nby manually decoding the embedded payload).\n\nAdds the same job wes-work-planning already runs: npm run clean-api-docs\n&& npm run gen-api-docs from docs/, then fail the PR if that produces any\ndiff against docs/api-reference/rest.\n\nPart of the harness-engineering coverage expansion plan\n(.hermes/plans/2026-09-13_234500-harness-coverage-expansion.md), Phase 2\nTask 2.1.\n\nVerified locally: clean-api-docs + gen-api-docs against current\napis/openapi.yaml produces zero diff -- no pre-existing drift found.","tree":{"sha":"e908666f303ee261c321baf1429c7e43d6cbc268","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/git/trees/e908666f303ee261c321baf1429c7e43d6cbc268"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/git/commits/62b334833112f163ba37d6146574738685cdb266","verification":{"payload":"tree e908666f303ee261c321baf1429c7e43d6cbc268\nparent 35340e1a36f01e40818944d8e6db3086f5834092\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1789349190 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789349190 -0300\n\nfeat(ci): add docs-api-drift job — guard against OpenAPI/generated-docs skew (#51)\n\nOnly wes-work-planning had a docs-api-drift job across the fleet. Every\nother repo''s Docusaurus REST reference (docs/docs/api-reference/rest/) is a\ncommitted, hand-regenerated artifact that can silently diverge from\napis/openapi.yaml -- this fleet has already lived that exact failure once\n(a PR removing security:[]/securitySchemes.bearerAuth from\norder-management''s spec did not regenerate the .api.mdx files, caught only\nby manually decoding the embedded payload).\n\nAdds the same job wes-work-planning already runs: npm run clean-api-docs\n&& npm run gen-api-docs from docs/, then fail the PR if that produces any\ndiff against docs/api-reference/rest.\n\nPart of the harness-engineering coverage expansion plan\n(.hermes/plans/2026-09-13_234500-harness-coverage-expansion.md), Phase 2\nTask 2.1.\n\nVerified locally: clean-api-docs + gen-api-docs against current\napis/openapi.yaml produces zero diff -- no pre-existing drift found.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqp01GCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoY8QADZPCFeIgMAi9mw3ADAQO+OR\nl8DMzdeh/XFxZc3TUtuYtEcz/MxHWa8/yAQM3dtSxYpXGhNA1rfjUa3j9kDb5CWQ\nCrWrF1q9j+Q6pStpmMXY5cFNfUvk+rE3shN3k2vwlWwgEJlUR+9JkhPXbfoTRWjm\nMWoMGdJ61sEMZxdwHx3u+GRu3YQsBZyq2UEP9vEc8+E3h3Nex+3DJPn/X5DkFDnm\nqo+mmyK8g0NNNyA4Ii7zUFaBGVDBCiaqx5dfS1fEJc5nPf0+JhLjBB4ss4l8XDo7\nG7oIdRSHFoc2lb8RHtFKZGY/pwuX16WeyYSYbNbhHw4XBr6lrIohJ4