 web job exactly: dual checkout of this repo +\nclaudioed/warehouse-ui-kit@develop, build ui-kit, npm ci, oxlint, tsc -b,\nvitest run, vite build.\n\nVerified locally before opening this PR: lint clean, tsc clean, vitest\npassing, vite build succeeds.\n\nPart of the harness-engineering coverage expansion plan\n(.hermes/plans/2026-09-13_234500-harness-coverage-expansion.md), Phase 1\nTask 1.2.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqp0GmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKaoQACIMXAI3ZBgGNi6Zd6Janfvg\nZl7yDB0w9piytfsQu1juI3gxniozSsEfMkJpdluvKlNkbIBQjA5yNNv2VGDg3FVt\ncd55wd1geg+oH7IS/yb1yo/56on+5p7jJGJOY9P3igNZ7NBQS7zagAWIlW4mU270\nRJbPJ+6KJsGrIcndQYaviieQR16gYei/+bVWCFevC5Rff8S5IlCj1//3BP6Dq9Ki\nSPotdWj/bSocwcWt8aqNEkMrAyOenwXEsWTVb0151kxJSzJ98EeNzWxVkA9/3lF0\nfxAeH8q2TnKOlCVcJ/Gjl//MXAT95NkJi5bjLZpfsQjinMB9cVL6f2kIVsqivvvZ\nmEYnR8AQ6trajadPslVeurMd9gnVsz54Pd0HOZlUPrDXu/WHAZDJ+NbL1qXPsfh4\nLfxqHf7ldg4O2d1AL2HfuhhIS9WHi4BRU6unayi60mQ1+FY/wmw9myjF+WgNP5Ue\n4UzMoekdsA6ZyypMx2HMLFZDb7WLZCMD/6Fdbec9rLVW8/TlIQnT6aayrQYV2Jay\nAd1Pvjg8CtmZRtJBwGQnclQn99CmQt6zMNE2ht5mhY2PlVoanFwGGmTvQb/KF7nX\nx8nL32/xiEC2UMcXANF7hukNGKxqszeaxLRxM9M3nv7btYWpwr99UzIMKmgdgODP\nWWU/RJrwjVxcST9e3A/S\n=Iqjv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T00:36:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/labor-performance/commit/04fab43b8d228019bbd27325d75d02ed26728736","node_id":"C_kwDOUIGXYtoAKDA0ZmFiNDNiOGQyMjgwMTliYmQyNzMyNWQ3NWQwMmVkMjY3Mjg3MzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/labor-performance/commit/445eaf08b55cbf3170c3f541c0c91e5bd6954008","sha":"445eaf08b55cbf3170c3f541c0c91e5bd6954008","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/445eaf08b55cbf3170c3f541c0c91e5bd6954008"}],"sha":"04fab43b8d228019bbd27325d75d02ed26728736","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/04fab43b8d228019bbd27325d75d02ed26728736"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/commits/445eaf08b55cbf3170c3f541c0c91e5bd6954008/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T14:23:01Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T14:23:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(standard): optional travel-time component on a LaborStandard (ADR-0015, Phase B3) (#48)\n\nImplements the labor-performance half of facility-layout''s Phase B3\nfollow-on: \"travel component of engineered standards from real distance\ninstead of a constant.\" This service''s own v1 boundary is stricter than\nthe fleet-wide pattern -- \"no REST dependency in either direction with\nany sibling context\" is a BLANKET rule here, not scoped to specific\nsiblings the way wes-work-planning''s or fulfillment-execution''s own\nboundary promises are. So unlike those two prior B3 items (which added a\nlive TravelDistanceLookup port calling facility-layout directly), this\nfield is entirely caller-supplied and this service never calls out to\ncompute or validate it -- mirroring process-path-management''s own ADR\n0009 precedent for the identical constraint.\n\n- internal/domain/standard: LaborStandard gains an optional\n  TravelComponentSeconds (*int64, nil = \"not declared\", the default).\n  New invariant enforced purely in-process: 0 <= travel <= expected\n  (ErrNegativeTravelComponentSeconds,\n  ErrTravelComponentExceedsExpectedSeconds) -- travel can be the WHOLE\n  standard (a water-spider run is arguably all travel) but never more.\n- internal/domain/shared/events.go: LaborStandardDefined/\n  LaborStandardRevised carry the field through; a revision declares its\n  OWN value, never inheriting the closed prior standard''s.\n- internal/application/usecases: DefineStandard.Execute takes the new\n  parameter and passes it straight through to New/the published event --\n  no resolution, no lookup, no I/O beyond the existing Save/Publish.\n- internal/adapters/inbound/http: optional on the request, omitted\n  entirely (never defaulted to 0) on the response when unset; new 422\n  mapping for both new domain errors.\n- internal/adapters/inbound/mcp: get_labor_standard''s output DTO mirrors\n  the same omit-when-unset discipline.\n- internal/adapters/outbound/postgres: additive nullable\n  travel_component_seconds column (migration 0004, CHECK-constrained to\n  [0, expected_seconds]).\n- internal/adapters/outbound/kafka: the analytics wire payload for both\n  LaborStandardDefined and LaborStandardRevised includes the field only\n  when declared.\n- apis/openapi.yaml + apis/asyncapi.yaml: new TravelComponentSeconds\n  schema wired into DefineStandardRequest/Standard (REST) and both\n  envelope schemas (AsyncAPI); Spectral-clean on both.\n- docs/docs/adr/0015: full ADR explaining why the live-lookup pattern\n  used twice already in this fleet is architecturally unavailable here.\n  Docusaurus REST reference regenerated surgically (deleted+regenerated\n  only define-standard''s and get-standard''s own generated files, per\n  this fleet''s documented docusaurus-plugin-openapi-docs staleness\n  pitfall).\n\nTests: new unit tests at every layer -- domain (valid range, both\ninvariant violations, Rehydrate round-trip), application (persisted +\npublished, a revision''s own value never inherited, invalid value\nrejected with no event published), HTTP (echoed on 201, omitted when\nunset, both 422s, GetStandard reads it back), Kafka (present on the wire\nwhen declared, omitted when not, for both event types).\n\nVerified: go build/vet/test -race (default AND -tags integration against\nreal testcontainers Postgres+Kafka), gofmt, golangci-lint (0 issues),\nmake check-all (90% coverage gate -- actual 94.8%; arch-test; BDD) all\ngreen. gremlins unleash ./internal/domain (this repo''s actual CI mutation\nscope, no separate make target) -- 100% efficacy, 100% mutator coverage,\nzero survivors including the new validateTravelComponentSeconds code.","tree":{"sha":"75fd55e09d93ab27c4aa488854fa4d09f82cf3e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/git/trees/75fd55e09d93ab27c4aa488854fa4d09f82cf3e7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/labor-performance/git/commits/445eaf08b55cbf3170c3f541c0c91e5bd6954008","verification":{"payload":"tree 75fd55e09d93ab27c4aa488854fa4d09f82cf3e7\nparent 23369e310510eca19c507858faa6d17ff58a7557\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1789309381 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789309381 -0300\n\nfeat(standard): optional travel-time component on a LaborStandard (ADR-0015, Phase B3) (#48)\n\nImplements the labor-performance half of facility-layout''s Phase B3\nfollow-on: \"travel component of engineered standards from real distance\ninstead of a constant.\" This service''s own v1 boundary is stricter than\nthe fleet-wide pattern -- \"no REST dependency in either direction with\nany sibling context\" is a BLANKET rule here, not scoped to specific\nsiblings the way wes-work-planning''s or fulfillment-execution''s own\nboundary promises are. So unlike those two prior B3 items (which added a\nlive TravelDistanceLookup port calling facility-layout directly), this\nfield is entirely caller-supplied and this service never calls out to\ncompute or validate it -- mirroring process-path-management''s own ADR\n0009 precedent for the identical constraint.\n\n- internal/domain/standard: LaborStandard gains an optional\n  TravelComponentSeconds (*int64, nil = \"not declared\", the default).\n  New invariant enforced purely in-process: 0 <= travel <= expected\n  (ErrNegativeTravelComponentSeconds,\n  ErrTravelComponentExceedsExpectedSeconds) -- travel can be the WHOLE\n  standard (a water-spider run is arguably all travel) but never more.\n- internal/domain/shared/events.go: LaborStandardDefined/\n  LaborStandardRevised carry the field through; a revision declares its\n  OWN value, never inheriting the closed prior standard''s.\n- internal/application/usecases: DefineStandard.Execute takes the new\n  parameter and passes it straight through to New/the published event --\n  no resolution, no lookup, no I/O beyond the existing Save/Publish.\n- internal/adapters/inbound/http: optional on the request, omitted\n  entirely (never defaulted to 0) on the response when unset; new 422\n  mapping for both new domain errors.\n- internal/adapters/inbound/mcp: get_labor_standard''s output DTO mirrors\n  the same omit-when-unset discipline.\n- internal/adapters/outbound/postgres: additive nullable\n  travel_component_seconds column (migration 0004, CHECK-constrained to\n  [0, expected_seconds]).\n- internal/adapters/outbound/kafka: the analytics wire payload for both\n  LaborStandardDefined and LaborStandardRevised includes the field only\n  when declared.\n- apis/openapi.yaml + apis/asyncapi.yaml: new TravelComponentSeconds\n  schema wired into DefineStandardRequest/Standard (REST) and both\n  envelope schemas (AsyncAPI); Spectral-clean on both.\n- docs/docs/adr/0015: full ADR explaining why the live-lookup pattern\n  used twice already in this fleet is architecturally unavailable here.\n  Docusaurus REST reference regenerated surgically (deleted+regenerated\n  only define-standard''s and get-standard''s own generated files, per\n  this fleet''s documented docusaurus-plugin-openapi-docs staleness\n  pitfall).\n\nTests: new unit tests at every layer -- domain (valid range, both\ninvariant violations, Rehydrate round-trip), application (persisted +\npublished, a revision''s own value never inherited, invalid value\nrejected with no event published), HTTP (echoed on 201, omitted when\nunset, both 422s, GetStandard reads it back), Kafka (present on the wire\nwhen declared, omitted when not, for both event types).\n\nVerified: go build/vet/test -race (default AND -tags integration against\nreal testcontainers Postgres+Kafka), gofmt, golangci-lint (0 issues),\nmake check-all (90% coverage gate -- actual 94.8%; arch-test; BDD) all\ngreen. gremlins unleash ./internal/domain (this repo''s actual CI mutation\nscope, no separate make target) -- 100% efficacy, 100% mutator coverage,\nzero survivors including the new validateTravelComponentSeconds code.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqprHFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApo8QAIyzlXRjYByN/MB6S5dYnsJt\n0TnYyaps2/i5Z1xfv30wYHLf6SuyEjNw4BCBzC/NPNvPtMxK2zDBrJmAhG74yyDD\nIbcCnBleMXxC7RiEFSgkLRRGzrPYREs+V/3CSd7lBid4qGDemHDw5tuNVS82vsHU\nCcGEuqOiqI+5zJx0yiJVlkCzkMpXFd2jh/YkPGymtOHWktzhTDAhTeyGw/BUBdBF\nqiJbywwnsKDoeR9+M6Qb+YY7Y8tPiaXktsy96Jnme17DQ/ezM6CadzEnfFzK3uUg\nBDRzq1vTLXstZWmZ2C8Lt9MLH1B+cdtm98H3ABW9Uv3NVJFZcwfGQQI7jv4i8+Rr\nUgI/w3mtJY5OY5/NaH7pM+UMJkD+z+eaKcQUNUMKdySGfGpgiuoyB0CQ8s+s5Iea\nzOyar+ioefqOEar7nxZD15CVWWJhG6+NpXYu0LoXsEUpEsMJdFTdFmtD7jN+TYP7\neKn6aLBTtaGmpMJv1p8j9cV+ZaxzLiF0BjOtaxpfebGAjUwawUTMsDDONBhSv0Xk\nBLXm/SIgCVTWRNqJ8O9KlGSksxcw+vxdkSxlNyCcra70klnHHfAm9BUvEgwQxefh\nlRVTINShlNLBWtjJ9HRsGIGIYK8c5msaCq/UJWf82ntx9b2PVoXYzWDLsfvhx6E3\nRT01ixm9HzHCoopGbpVn\n=s9Qd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-13T14:23:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO